"arcade_the-brain-washing-game","The Brain Washing Game","arcade","Arcade","Arcade","Ýmsir (Namco, Sega, Capcom, Konami, Taito, SNK, Atari, o.fl.)","Arcade (Öll tímabil)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","Toaplan","Toaplan","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Teki-Paki is Toaplan's take on the classic falling block puzzle game genre. Players control L-shaped sets of three coloured blocks as they fall from the top of the screen. As in most falling-block puzzle games, players can rotate the set of blocks as it falls using the game button. Players can eliminate blocks and earn coins by connecting together a set of five of them. Unlike in most similar games, the placement of blocks is quite flexible; as long as a block is diagonal to another block of the same colour, it qualifies as part of a combo, allowing for some complex combos. There are also two special block types: a bomb, which when chained with at least four other bombs, clears the screen; and a smiling face, which counts as any colour in part of a chain. Players can play solo, or alongside a second player.","tekipaki.zip","ZIP","0.31","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/arcade/tekipaki.png","miximages/arcade/tekipaki.png","screenshots/arcade/tekipaki.png","titlescreens/arcade/tekipaki.png","3dboxes/arcade/tekipaki.png","backcovers/arcade/tekipaki.png","marquees/arcade/tekipaki.png"
