"arcade_vasara","Vasara","arcade","Arcade","Arcade","Ýmsir (Namco, Sega, Capcom, Konami, Taito, SNK, Atari, o.fl.)","Arcade (Öll tímabil)","2000-01-01","2000","2000s","Visco","Visco","Shoot'em Up / Vertical","Shooter","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Vasara is a 2D arcade vertical scrolling shoot'em up, taking place in an alternative 1600s Japan, featuring ahistorical elements such as giant robots normally found in sci-fi shooters. The game follows the typical manic shooter/bullet hell concept - players (up to two in co-op) fly forward on hover bikes and shoot enemies while trying to avoid many projectiles fired at them. Vasara has three playable characters: Yukimura Sanada, Keiji Maeda, and Saiga Magoichi - each specializing in a different weapon. Besides the standard shot, screen clearing bombs and charge attacks are available. Defeating or damaging enemies with the charge attacks makes red gems appear. Picking these up fills a ""Vasara"" meter, turning the charge attack into a super attack. Another unique feature is that players (and enemies) don't die after collisions. The game features six stages and several bosses to kill.","vasara.zip","ZIP","15.49","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/arcade/vasara.png","miximages/arcade/vasara.png","screenshots/arcade/vasara.png","titlescreens/arcade/vasara.png","3dboxes/arcade/vasara.png","","marquees/arcade/vasara.png"
