"nes_exciting-basket","Exciting Basket","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-07-24","1987","1980s","Konami","Konami","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Exciting Basket (Known in the US as Double Dribble) was a basketball arcade game developed and released in 1987 by Konami. Much of the game's popularity came from its animation sequences showing basketball players performing slam dunks.Players can choose from one of four teams: Boston, Chicago, Los Angeles and New York. There is no difference in skill level or abilities between the teams. Since there is no NBA license, no team names or player names are used, however, the teams wear the same color of their NBA counterparts (Boston wears green, Chicago red, etc.).","Exciting Basket (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","miximages/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png","marquees/nes/Exciting Basket (JP).png"
"nes_exciting-billiard","Exciting Billiard","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-06-26","1987","1980s","Konami","Konami","Sports / Pool","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","Exciting Billiard is a billiard simulation game developed and published by Konami for the Family Computer Disk System in 1987. It was the first of Konami's ""Exciting Sports"" series produced for the Nintendo Famicom, similar to Namco's own ""Family Sports"" label. Exciting Billiard offers players four modes of play. Break Shot is a single player only mode, where the player competes against other pool hustlers for money, attempting to earn enough money to graduate to higher and more impressive venues with increasing amounts of money on each bet. The remaining three modes can be played with one to four players at a time (human or computer controlled), with each players' progress capable of being saved to disk.","Exciting Billiard (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","miximages/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png","marquees/nes/Exciting Billiard (JP).png"
"nes_exciting-soccer-konami-cup","Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1988-02-16","1988","1980s","Konami","Konami","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Players select one of the various soccer teams, and aim to become the best team in the league. Each team possesses different levels of kick strength, endurance, dribbling technique, defensive skill, and luck. They are set at the beginning of the game, but can be enhanced through training. During play, the view of the field is a bird's eye view, with either goal located at the far top and bottom sections of the field. Although this game is considered a relatively minor release, it's ending BGM entitled ""Seaside Memory"" is highly revered.","Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","miximages/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png","marquees/nes/Exciting Soccer - Konami Cup (JP).png"
