"nes_famimaga-disk-vol-2-panic-space","Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-10-19","1990","1990s","Tokuma Shoten Intermedia","Tokuma Shoten Intermedia","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Panic Space, or Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 Panic Space, is a puzzle game in which the goal is to reflect a laser to an exit panel in order to open the way to the next stage. The laser cannot hit any of the stage's surrounding wall: were it do so, it would cause the level to explode and the player to lose a life (from an initial allotment of five, though this can be increased while playing the game). Much of the time the various reflectors (which send the beam off at a 90 degree angle) and blocks (which simply stop the laser in its tracks) must be maneuvered into place before the laser should be tested on them.","Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","miximages/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png","marquees/nes/Famimaga Disk Vol. 2 - Panic Space (JP).png"
