""The fate of the country hangs by a thread. It may be possible to save the country with Gladrif's magic, but he is nowhere to be found. Therefore, I want you to search for him! Find Gladrif, defeat the monsters, and restore peace to this land once again!""","Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","miximages/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","screenshots/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","titlescreens/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","3dboxes/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","backcovers/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","marquees/nes/Kalin no Tsurugi (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png"
"nes_kamen-rider-black-taiketsu-shadow-moon","Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1988-04-15","1988","1980s","Human Entertainment","Bandai","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","","","The game is based on the Kamen Rider Black television series, which was the eight installment of the Kamen Rider superhero series.In the game, players take control of Kamen Rider Black, who must defeat numerous Gorgom mutants. There are five levels of four stages each. In the first four levels, players must complete three side scrolling stages with a boss at the end. In the fourth stage, the player must fight against a final level boss using a zoomed in perspective with larger sprites. The player gets to ride Battle Hopper motorcycle throughout the second and fourth levels. The fifth level is composed entirely of boss fights, first against three Evil Lords, and then against Shadow Moon. If the player loses against Shadow Moon, the bad ending is shown before the game ends.","Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","miximages/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","screenshots/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","titlescreens/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","3dboxes/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","backcovers/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png","marquees/nes/Kamen Rider Black - Taiketsu Shadow Moon (English Translated by BlackPaladin).png"
"nes_karate-champ","Karate Champ","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1988-07-22","1988","1980s","Data East","Data East","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","","","The player assumes the role of a karate competitor and fights against another player or the computer. Using two joysticks, players can execute a number of moves.

Gameplay consists of a two dimensional fight between Karate characters wearing white and red gi, followed by various bonus rounds for the successful player. This pattern repeats itself in the next, more challenging round set against a new background. Unlike most later fighter-type games, there are no health bar or hit points. A hit successfully landed ends the round and earns the player or his opponent either one point or half point (along with a numeric score for the top ten but this has no effect on winning a match per se). The first to score two points is the winner. If the player loses a battle, the game ends. The game also featured some early speech synthesis, in which the judge would call out such phrases as ""Fight!"" or ""Winner!"" It's also spoken in Japanese in the Japanese version.","Karate Champ (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","miximages/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png","marquees/nes/Karate Champ (JP).png"
