"nes_pro-golfer-saru-kage-no-tournament","Pro Golfer Saru - Kage No Tournament","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-05-25","1987","1980s","TOSE","Bandai","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Pro Golfer Saru: Kage no Tournament is a golf game with fantasy elements thrown in, developed by Bandai and published on the Family Computer Disk System in 1987. The game is based on a manga (Japanese comic book) known as Pro Golfer Saru published by Fujiko Fujio (also responsible for Doraemon) about a young cave man or neanderthal-like boy who desires to become the greatest golfer in history. To accomplish this goal, he trains in the most desolate of locations, driving golf balls over giant chasms in an effort to hit greens several hundred meters away.

The game is composed of a training mode as well as the tournament challenge. The first nine holes replicate the desolate, and almost prehistoric locations that Saru normally trains in. Balls must be driven over wide spaces in order to stay in bounds and continue play. The back nine holes take place is a more modern, and even slightly futuristic locale, where Saru must sink balls from across rooftops. The game will save one players performance to disk. It was never released outside of Japan.","Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","miximages/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png","marquees/nes/Pro Golfer Saru - Kage no Tournament (JP).png"
"nes_pro-wrestling","Pro Wrestling","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1986-10-13","1986","1980s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Sports","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","The player chooses a wrestler with unique skills and presses various combinations of buttons to use different wrestling moves. It is possible to leave the ring; however, a player who does so must re-enter the ring before the referee's 20-count. Failure to do so results in a loss (via count-out) or a draw (double count-out), if both wrestlers fail to re-enter in time. (Note: The referee's count is broken only after both wrestlers have re-entered the ring. That is, as long as at least one wrestler is outside the ring, the referee's count continues. Moreover, it is possible for a wrestler to be counted out while executing a ""plancha"" if he has crossed the ring ropes by the count of 20.","Pro Wres (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","miximages/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png","marquees/nes/Pro Wres (JP).png"
"nes_putt-putt-golf","Putt Putt Golf","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-03-30","1989","1980s","Pack In Video","Pack In Video","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","Putt Putt Golf by Pack-In-Video is one of many golf games for the Famicom and the Famicom Disk System, but one of the few to take players through an abstract world rather than an approximation of a real golf course. The goal of each stage is to reach the hole on the green and pot the ball in as few strokes as possible, but each of the courses are covered with various obstacles - some animated, some stationary. The player must navigate around them (or use them to their advantage, in some cases) in order to achieve the best score.","Putt Putt Golf (JP).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","miximages/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","screenshots/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","titlescreens/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","3dboxes/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","backcovers/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png","marquees/nes/Putt Putt Golf (JP).png"
