"nes_super-mario-brothers-2","Super Mario Brothers 2","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1986-06-03","1986","1980s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Originally released in Japan as Super Mario Bros.® 2, this game has previously made only brief cameo appearances in the Western hemisphere. Mario fans will appreciate the familiar look and feel of the game, while finding that its updated game play creates an entirely new challenge. No longer content just to wear different-colored overalls, Mario and Luigi also possess different skill sets (Mario can stop quicker, while Luigi can jump higher). In addition to the classic enemies already known to fans worldwide, there are also Poison Mushrooms, backward Warp Zones, and the occasional wind gust (which can help or hinder your progress) to take into account. And if that?s somehow not enough, expert players can go looking for the game?s secret worlds. So get ready to put your Mario skills to the ultimate test, and save the Princess again. Just don?t be surprised if she?s in another castle!","Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).fds","FDS","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","miximages/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","screenshots/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","titlescreens/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","3dboxes/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","backcovers/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png","marquees/nes/Super Mario Bros. 2 (JP, Rev 2).png"
"nes_tama-and-friends-3-choume-daibouken","Tama And Friends - 3 Choume Daibouken","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-02-23","1989","1980s","Advance Communication Company","Bandai","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","The game is based on a manga and anime for children of the same name that concerns the cats and dogs of a close-knit neighborhood. 



