"nes_bokosuka-wars","Bokosuka Wars","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1985-12-14","1985","1980s","ASCII","ASCII","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","50","2.5","King Ogreth of the Basam Empire has invaded your country and either captured or turned into rocks and trees all your soldiers. You, king Suren, are left completely alone. In a desperate attempt, you decide to walk to king Ogreth's castle and to defeat him. You hope you'll be able to find some way to bring your soldiers back to you...

In this strategy game, your goal sounds simple – just walk a distance of 600 meters and defeat king Ogreth. But to do that is not simple at all. Bumping into trees and rocks, king Suren can bring his soldiers to life. Once there are some knights in his small army, he will also be able to free imprisoned soldiers. King Ogreth's units will constantly attack you on the way. The results of the battles are calculated automatically, according to the strength of your units. So before you engage in a battle, you have to be sure you have the upper hand.","Bokosuka Wars (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Bokosuka Wars (Japan).png"
"nes_bomberman","Bomberman","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-01-02","1989","1980s","Hudson Soft","Hudson Soft","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1","1","1","70","3.5","Bomberman was a robot in a bomb making factory who longed for his freedom. Rumors circulated that escaping to the surface would allow the robot to become human. Getting out would be the trick. Each room is inhabited by monsters that must be neutralized and the exit itself hidden underneath bricks.

The first of the Bomberman series. Bomberman is a single player game with a top down view and simplistic controls. In fact, in addition to movement, you only have a single ability: placing bombs. Each bomb explodes into a cross-shaped blast (4 directions) which can destroy either enemies or blocks. Power-ups may be found to increase the size of the blast, place additional bombs, increase the speed of the Bomberman or to walk through walls. Your goal on each level is to destroy all enemies and escape through the exit before the time limit is up.. Hitting the exit with a bomb blast releases more enemies which must also be destroyed.","Bomberman (USA).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","miximages/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Bomberman (USA).png","marquees/nes/Bomberman (USA).png"
"nes_dynablaster","Dynablaster","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Hudson Soft","Hudson Soft","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-3","1","3","90","4.5","Our hero Bomberman Shiro was walking down the street one day when he witnessed a robbery. It was Bomberman Kuro who was the robber. But Kuro knocked Shiro to the ground, and then left the money so that he would be framed. Now Shiro has been taken to jail and must fight his way out of this place using the only method he knows: explosive bombs.

Dynablaster is the second Bomberman game in the series and plays similar to the first, only all gameplay has been reduced to a single screen. Your goal however remains the same on a smaller playing area. You are to destroy all enemies on a level and then find the exit to the next one. Bombing the exit is always a bad idea. The occasional power-up will increase your bomb blast, number of bombs on the screen at one time, player speed or give you the ability to walk through walls.

This game introduces a Versus Mode for 2 players and a Battle Mode for 3. Your goal in these is to destroy the other players while staying alive yourself.","Bomberman II (USA).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","miximages/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png","marquees/nes/Bomberman II (USA).png"
