"nes_cyber-stadium-series-base-wars","Cyber Stadium SerieS : Base Wars","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-06-01","1991","1990s","Konami","Ultra Games","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","In the 24th century, the game of Baseball is very different. Tired of paying huge players salaries, the team owners got together one weekend and came up with a bold new idea, Robots. Indeed they renamed their league the Cyber League and stocked it with four robot types; Cyborg, Tank, Floater or Motorcycle, to play.  On an orbital stadium in space, these robots all play a slightly different variation of the baseball rules. Hitting the ball and catching pop-flys and making home runs are all the same, but when the call of a play is in dispute, there are no base referees; the robots engage in a one-on-one battle using any weaponry they're carrying.  Of course to make things interesting, weaponry (and other robot parts and equipment) can only be purchased with team funds during a tournament game, and team funds can only be obtained by wins. Thus the series closer is always sure to be a sold out game.","Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","miximages/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png","marquees/nes/Cyber Stadium Series - Base Wars (USA).png"
