"nes_datach-yu-yu-hakusho-bakutou-ankoku-bujutsukai","Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-10-22","1993","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Fighting / 2D","Fighting","1-2","1","2","","","Yu Yu Hakusho inspired fighting game on the Famicom, developed by TOSE and published by Bandai, which was released in Japan in 1993. Based on the YuYu Hakusho manga and anime series created by Yoshihiro Togashi. The protagonist is Yusuke Urameshi, a delinquent junior high school student who is killed while trying to save a young boy from being hit by a car. Yusuke is brought back to life and is promptly given the task of participating in the martial arts tournament to defeat the demon Rando. One of seven games released for the Datach Joint ROM System, an aftermarket enhancement accessory by Bandai for the Famicom, allowing the system to play select compatible games. Its main feature is the card reading / barcode slot on the front used for adding characters or items to the game.","Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Datach - Yu Yu Hakusho - Bakutou Ankoku Bujutsukai (Japan).png"
