"nes_days-of-thunder","Days of Thunder","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-04-25","1991","1990s","Beam Software","Mindscape International","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","30","1.5","Tom Cruise's film brought NASCAR racing to the masses, and Mindscape did the same for games players with this license. If you mentally change the driver names, it can be thought of as a recreation of real NASCAR racing rather than a direct recreation of the film. 

You play Cruise's Cole Trickle character (his name, like many of the others, is slightly different to that of a real NASCAR racer of the day) against your rivals on 8 tracks, based on real-life counterparts. The races are all on ovals, although the exact lengths, corner types and gradients are varied.  This means that the ideal racing line on one track can put you into the wall on another. Qualifying is incorporated alongside the races themselves.

From times to times you'll have to pull into the pit stop area. When doing so, you control the five members of the pit crew. Loosing time on pit will make you loose positions at the race. The other racers, however, never pit.

The NES version has 3rd-Person perspective only.","Days of Thunder (USA).zip","ZIP","0.17","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","miximages/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png","marquees/nes/Days of Thunder (USA).png"
"nes_de-block","De-block","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-08-09","1991","1990s","Athena","Athena","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-2","1","2","","","De-Block is a puzzle game that can be most easily explained as a 4-way Tetris. The player controls a block in the center of the screen which can move and rotate freely. Larger blocks move inward from each side of the screen and attach to the center block, then change color depending on their distance from the center. If the player completes a colored ring, that layer and all the blocks inside of it are cleared, and all the ones outside are moved inward. Play ends if a newly-appearing block overlaps with the player's structure.","De-Block (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","miximages/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/De-Block (Japan).png","marquees/nes/De-Block (Japan).png"
