You are a group of repairman, who are superheroes now because of coca-cola produced by evil Doctor Mayhem. Doctor wants to mutate all people proposing to them his cola, but you want to prevent this plan killing his robots and finally stopping the Doctor. 
When the game starts you choose your character and some others join you in your case. If your character will be captured you can choose another one, while nobody is left.","Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","miximages/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png","marquees/nes/Defenders of Dynatron City (USA).png"
"nes_demon-sword","Demon Sword","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","TOSE","Taito","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","In Demon Sword you play the part of the noble fighter Victar. Victar carries with him a sword which was used long ago to defeat the evil Dark Fiend who took over the land. Now he is back, and Victar must use the sword to defeat him once again.  The game is an arcade style platform game. You begin with just part of the demon sword, and after defeating a large monster at the end of each level an additional section of the sword is restored. After all six missing parts of the sword are found, you can attempt the final level to defeat the Dark Fiend. In addition to the sword pieces, there are other items which can be found during the levels to help out; these include keys to open mystic doors, spheres to restore life, and different types of weapons.","Demon Sword (USA).zip","ZIP","0.1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","miximages/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png","marquees/nes/Demon Sword (USA).png"
"nes_derby-stallion-zenkoku-ban","Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-08-29","1992","1990s","ASCII","ASCII","Horse racing","Racing","1","1","1","","","The Derby Stallion also known in Japan by the portmanteau abbreviation DerbyStal - The game is a genre-merging horse-racing and business simulation game originally created by ASCII Entertainment, and released by Nintendo. The series is the best-selling horse racing series of all.","Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Derby Stallion - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png"
"nes_desert-commander","Desert Commander","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-06-02","1989","1980s","Kemco Limited","Kemco Limited","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Somewhere in a nameless desert, two opposing nameless armies take to the battlefield to destroy the other. Through the strategy of their commanders and the diversity of their units, each side seeks to gain the advantage over the other. There are 5 campaigns total and can be played either VS the computer or a second player.

The game is is a top-view turn-based strategy games with animated battle sequences between units. Each unit can move a certain value across the battlefield on different types of terrain and must keep track of it's ammunition and fuel consumption. Towns are scattered around the map for resupply and other special icons (Position, Oasis, Airfield) confer other special advantages. Players may choose any combination of choices of 2 types of air units and 2 styles of cannon, 4 types of land vehicles and an infantry unit to customize their specific strategy. The side that loses their Headquarters unit first loses.","Desert Commander (USA).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","miximages/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png","marquees/nes/Desert Commander (USA).png"
"nes_destination-earthstar","Destination Earthstar","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-02-01","1990","1990s","Imagineer","Acclaim Entertainment","Simulation","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","30","1.5","Two centuries ago, an alien species known as the Kojans kidnapped the people of Earth and made them their slaves. But the Earthlings never gave hope of returning to their homeland. So they sent you, a brave space ship pilot, to travel through the galaxy in search of the Earth. But beware, as the Kojans won't let you pass without a fight!

The gameplay is divided into two parts. You begin in the simulation mode, controlling your ship from first-person perspective. You can change your altitude, speed, and weapons, at the same time paying attention to the fuel you have left. Once you have defeated enough enemies and landed on a planet, the game turns into a side-scrolling shooter in which you must navigate your ship through arcade sequences.","Destination Earthstar (USA).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","miximages/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png","marquees/nes/Destination Earthstar (USA).png"
"nes_destiny-of-an-emperor","Destiny of an Emperor","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-09-01","1990","1990s","Capcom","Capcom USA","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","A role-playing game for the NES set within the Romance of the Three Kingdoms mythos that has spawned games on nearly every platform imaginable.  A party is formed by selecting up to five officers from a huge pool, many of whom would only join you after be bribed or defeated in combat.  Officers in turn each had a certain amount of soldiers, which essentially acted as hit points (i.e. Si Ma Ye leads 40000 men, and when he is hit by Zhang Bao, he loses 5000 men, so his manpower is now at 35000).  One of the first games on the NES to attempt to simulate large scale combat between different forces, although obviously in a very limited way.","Destiny of an Emperor (USA).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","miximages/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png","marquees/nes/Destiny of an Emperor (USA).png"
