"nes_devil-man","Devil Man","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-04-25","1989","1980s","ISCO","Namcot","Action / Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Go Nagai's Devilman comes to life in this graphic and text action-adventure game for the Famicom/NES. High atop the Himalayas, ancient devils are stirring beneath the ice after ten thousand years of imprisonment. Archdemon Xenon, their four-faced master unleashes them upon the Earth much to the chagrin of humanity. You are Akira Fudo who combines with a powerful ancient demon named Amon to become Devilman! Six levels of fire, ice, water, secret demon research labs, Tokyo ruins, and much more to explore as Devilman, Akira, his friends, or girlfriend Miki!","Devil Man (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Devil Man (Japan).png"
"nes_devil-world","Devil World","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-07-15","1987","1980s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Devil World is a scrolling maze game, strikingly similar to the classic Pac-Man, only with an undeniable religious bent. Collect dots in an automatically-scrolling maze directed by the devil himself, use crosses to power up and destroy his minions, and be careful not to get crushed by the walls. After collecting all the dots, you must collect bibles to seal up the source of the enemies and make the devil temporarily retreat. After this, there is a timed bonus stage where the player can control the scrolling, then the next round starts the cycle over from the beginning.","Devil World (Europe).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","miximages/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","screenshots/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","titlescreens/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","3dboxes/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","backcovers/nes/Devil World (Europe).png","marquees/nes/Devil World (Europe).png"
"nes_dick-tracy","Dick Tracy","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-12-02","1991","1990s","Realtime Associates","Bandai","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","You play as square-jawed detective Dick Tracy as he tries to solve five different crimes that vary in difficulty. This game is mostly a platform game with some overhead driving to get to the different buildings in search of clues.

There are five different weapons in the game: hand gun, tommy gun, super punch, tear gas and Tracy's plain fists. There are also medical kits that can be found. Enemies can be armed or unarmed. If Tracy shoots an unarmed thug, he loses health.

The main goal of the game is to collect five clues; enough to be able to arrest the culprit. Clues are scattered all over town in various buildings, usually full of Tracy-hating thugs. You start by viewing the mug shots of known criminals, going to there last whereabouts and interrogating them.","Dick Tracy (USA).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","miximages/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png","marquees/nes/Dick Tracy (USA).png"
"nes_die-hard","Die Hard","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-12-15","1992","1990s","Pack In Video","Activision","Shooter","Shooter","1","1","1","70","3.5","John McClain decides to visit his wife Holly in Nakatomi Plaza, only to discover that she is taken hostage on 30th floor, along with a bunch of other hostages. The main terrorist, Hans, is after the money locked away in a safe on the 30th floor. His hacker, Theo, is slowly breaking the locks into the vault. It's up to McClain to stop them. Die Hard for the Nintendo Entertainment System is a lot different to its other counterparts. The game is played from a top-down perspective, rather than the 1st-/3rd-person perspective.

There are 40 terrorists scattered throughout the building, and the task is to clear each floor of terrorists. The stairwell, air duct or the express elevator is used to travel only to Floors 31 – 35. These are freely accessible at any time, doing away with linearity, and more floors are unlocked in ""Advanced"" mode). At the start of the game, John can only use a pistol or his fists to deal with foes, but after bringing down some terrorists, several weapons become available, including the submachine gun, C-4 explosives, rocket launcher, and flashbangs, using their weapons against them. When hit by these terrorists, John loses some life, but it can be restored by collecting soda cans and med-kits. The game ends when all life is lost.","Die Hard (USA).zip","ZIP","0.12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","miximages/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Die Hard (USA).png","marquees/nes/Die Hard (USA).png"
"nes_dig-dug","Dig Dug","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1985-06-04","1985","1980s","Namco","Namcot","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Dig Dug is a 1-2 player arcade game in which you have to use your shovel to dig your way through the earth. Stopping you from doing this are two monsters, called Pooka and Fygar, who will continually chase you around. The only weapon that you carry is an air pump, which you can use to inflate the monsters to the point where they explode. (if you start to inflate them but stop doing so, the monsters will get turned back to their normal selves.) Furthermore, rocks are scattered throughout the earth, and you can use these rocks to squash them. If the monsters do not find you for several seconds, they will eventually get turned into ghosts, which are able to walk through the earth. They are invincible and cannot be killed. From time to time, vegetables will appear in the center, and you can get these for points.","Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).zip","ZIP","0.01","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","miximages/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","screenshots/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","titlescreens/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","3dboxes/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","backcovers/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","marquees/nes/Dig Dug (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png"
"nes_dig-dug-ii-trouble-in-paradise","Dig Dug II : Trouble in Paradise","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-12-01","1989","1980s","Namco","Bandai","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","It is Dig Dug's job to protect 72 different tropical islands from his arch rivals, Pooka and the fire breathing Fygar. Played from an overhead point of view, Dig Dug now has two weapons at his disposal; the first is an air pump and the second is a drill. The pump can be used to inflate and destroy the enemies the same as in the original Dig Dug. At various locations on the islands are stakes, and when the drill is used near a stake a crack will form. If enough cracks become connected that section of the island will fall into the ocean, hopefully taking an enemy (and not Dig Dug!) with it. When all of the Pookas and Fygars have been destroyed, the game moves on to the next, more difficult level.","Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","miximages/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","screenshots/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","titlescreens/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","3dboxes/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","backcovers/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","marquees/nes/Dig Dug II (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png"
