"nes_f-15-strike-eagle","F-15 Strike Eagle","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-02-18","1993","1990s","MicroProse","MicroProse","Shooter / Plane, FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","70","3.5","The seven missions featured in this simulation of F-15 flight are all real-life missions the plane was originally used in. They take in the Middle East and Asia in the 1970s and early 1980s, and have air and ground targets to destroy. You have machine guns, guided missiles and bombs at your disposal. There is an arcade mode and 3 further difficulty levels. The game features 3 enemy aircraft and 3 types of enemy SAMs.","F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).zip","ZIP","0.23","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","miximages/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","screenshots/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","backcovers/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png","marquees/nes/F-15 Strike Eagle (USA).png"
"nes_f1-circus","F1 Circus","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-02-07","1992","1990s","Nichibutsu","Nichibutsu","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","F1 Circus is a Formula 1 simulation racing game. Unlike later entries in the series, this version does not feature an official license, and so only features generic teams and drivers. Races are viewed from a top-down perspective, and there are a variety of machine settings as well as basic vehicle damage.

A total of 15 courses are on offer, and there is a World Championship mode, as well as a ""Constructors"" mode for one or two players where the player can take the role of team manager while the computer does the actual racing. The Famicom release also adds a Time Attack mode for practicing and perfecting each course.","F1 Circus (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","miximages/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png","marquees/nes/F1 Circus (Japan).png"
"nes_f1-race","F1 Race","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1984-11-02","1984","1980s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","80","4","In this game, which is similar to Pole Position, the player takes control of an F1 car. The player can race the vehicle on one of three different skill levels. Each skill level contains five different tracks for the player to race on. On each of these tracks, the player must complete 2 laps before a countdown timer expires. The player must also try not to crash into other racers and obstacles on the sides of the road. The vehicle has a manual transmission, so the player has to switch between low and hi gear while racing.","F1 Race (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.01","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","miximages/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png","marquees/nes/F1 Race (Japan).png"
"nes_famicom-doubutsu-seitai-zukan-katte-ni-shirokuma-mori-o-sukue-no-maki","Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte Ni Shirokuma - Mori O Sukue No Maki!","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-12-15","1989","1980s","Graphic Research","CBS Sony Group","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Katte ni Shirokuma, or Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! Katte ni Shirokuma: Mori o Sukue no Maki!, is a menu-based adventure game for the Famicom based on a manga and anime about a group of forest animals, the main protagonist of which is an albino Japanese black bear commonly mistaken as a polar bear.
Unusual for adventure games of this era, the player traverses the world via a top-down perspective more common to RPGs. The characters also have their own HP and ""IQ"" stats, which play a greater role towards the end of the game.","Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Famicom Doubutsu Seitai Zukan! - Katte ni Shirokuma - Mori o Sukue no Maki! (Japan).png"
