"nes_gorby-no-pipeline-daisakusen","Gorby No Pipeline Daisakusen","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-04-12","1991","1990s","Compile","Tokuma Shoten Intermedia","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Gorby's Pipeline is a variation on the classic Tetris game, with elements of Pipe Dream / Pipe Mania and its bonus game..

While in the classic Tetris game you 'll have to fit the falling geometric shaped pieces together to make a row disappear in Gorby's Pipeline the geometric shapes are replaced with pieces that contain different forms and shapes of pipelines.

The game starts with a water leak at the bottom right of the screen and it's you goal to put the various pipeline pieces together in such a way that the water runs from the bottom-right to the left and disappears in one of the pipelines on the left side of the screen. If you succeed a row will disappear.","Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Gorby no Pipeline Daisakusen (Japan).png"
