"nes_keiba-simulation-honmei","Keiba Simulation - Honmei","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-04-28","1989","1980s","Nichibutsu","Nichibutsu","Horse racing","Racing","1","1","1","","","Keiba Simulation: Honmei (""keiba"" is the Japanese word for horse-racing, and ""honmei"" is a term meaning a favorite to win) is a Famicom horse-racing simulation game from Nichibutsu, often known as Nihon Bussan. In fact, the box art states the former as developer and the title screen states the latter. As a true simulation game, there is no racing (at least that the player can control) or gambling. The player instead can fiddle with the parameters for each race and the horses competing, changing their stats such as fatigue, age and the weight of the jockey. Then players can watch a race with these settings play out and observe the winner. It is possible the goal of this game is to recreate the likely output of an actual race based on as much information as the player is able to muster in order to assist them with their gambling, though its more likely the game is for racing enthusiasts.","Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Keiba Simulation - Honmei (Japan).png"
"nes_kekkyoku-nankyoku-daibouken","Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1985-04-22","1985","1980s","Konami","Konami","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","As a penguin, you must travel around Antarctica, making your way between bases before time runs out. This sounds easy, right? Wrong. Hindering your progress will be ice crevices and leopard seals. You can jump over the crevices, but jumping over the leopard seals may be difficult. You can speed up or slow down the penguin to avoid both of these hazards. The bases include Australia, France, New Zealand, USA, Argentina, UK, and Japan. You can collect flags and eat fish for points. Collecting a flashing flag will allow you to wear a propeller that enable you to fly over those hazards.","Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","miximages/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","screenshots/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","titlescreens/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","3dboxes/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","backcovers/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png","marquees/nes/Kekkyoku Nankyoku Daibouken (Japan) (Rev 1).png"
"nes_kero-kero-keroppi-no-daibouken","Kero Kero Keroppi No Daibouken","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-03-29","1991","1990s","Pax Softnica","Character Soft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Keroppi's Big Adventure) is based on the popular Sanrio character Keroppi. It is a children's puzzle game where Keroppi must rescue his girlfriend Keroleen who is locked up in a castle. To do so, he must solve the action based puzzles in seven differently themed worlds with four different types of stages (the surface of the maze, flying a plane, a Reversi-like level, and through a field of lava). All the items in the game are pre-determined; there is a need to memorize the pattern for each playthrough so that a player may advance through the levels more quickly once they have achieved a degree of expertise in the game.","Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Kero Kero Keroppi no Daibouken (Japan).png"
