"nes_the-mafat-conspiracy","The Mafat Conspiracy","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-06-01","1990","1990s","Vic Tokai","Vic Tokai","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","60","3","You play as Golgo 13 aka Duke Togo, ace sharpshooter and assassin. Based off a character of various manga comics, Golgo is a down-to-business man at the end of a gun. Stuck in the world of espionage among such groups as the FBI and the CIA, Golgo is constantly in mortal danger, and a lethal weapon in his own right. 

The Mafat Conspiracy is the sequel to the NES game Top Secret Episode. In this chapter, Golgo must track down a missing satellite from the SDI laser defense system, as well as rescue a top scientist and stop those who would use the satellite for blackmail and terror on the world's nations. 

While Golgo is outdoors, the game is a side-scrolling romp where the player can fire and jump. This changes when Golgo enters a building, at which point the game switches to a first person 3D maze. Navigating past soldiers and between floors, Golgo collects various clues to advance the storyline. There is also a driving sequence, and several sniper sequences in which precision aiming is required.","Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","miximages/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png","marquees/nes/Mafat Conspiracy, The (USA).png"
