"nes_mappy","Mappy","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1984-01-01","1984","1980s","Namco","Namcot","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","40","2","You control Mappy a police-mouse whose job is to collect valuables (consumer electronics)from a cat's house. You are being pursued by a gang of five pink cats. Doors are your only defense against the cats. You get from floor to floor by jumping on one of the trampolines.
Points are earned by recovering stolen goods. Other ways of earning points are bouncing on a trampoline, putting cats in the microwave, striking a cat with a door, striking cats with a bell, retrieving a treasures from the Boss cat Goro or dropping cats through a hole in the floor.","Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).zip","ZIP","0.01","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","miximages/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","screenshots/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","titlescreens/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","3dboxes/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","backcovers/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png","marquees/nes/Mappy (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 1).png"
"nes_mappy-kids","Mappy Kids","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-12-22","1989","1980s","Namco","Namcot","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","","","Mappy the mouse had a son named Happy. Happy has grown up and now wants to settle down with a wife. However, the girl he wants to marry won't agree to marriage until Happy can prove that he can provide for a family. So now it's up to Happy to collect a small fortune so he can please his would be spouse. Of course, the boss cat Nyamco and his legion of mukies stand in the way of making this an easy endeavor.

The game is a basic sidescrolling platformer. Happy can defeat his enemies by kicking them. He can also perform a jump, and while he's up in the air, he can spin his tail so he can glide in the air for a short period of time, which is useful for clearing large chasms. Littered throughout the levels are treasure boxes and coins which earn money for Happy, which in turn can be spent on items for domestic living. On the other hand, every time Happy is hit by an enemy, he loses some money, though a money bag will appear allowing Happy to recollect some of the lost money.

After each stage, Happy is presented with a slot machine ran by Nyamco. First, Happy spins the wheel to see a prize. Prizes range from extra lives to domestic items. Now, to actually win these  prizes, Happy must go up against one of the Mukies in a minigame. If he fails to win the minigame, he can be penalized by losing some money, domestic items, or even a life. Minigames include waving flags by following Nyamco's orders. There's also a  minigame where Happy stands back to back with a mukie and they try to push each other off a platform.  The other minigame involves trying to spot more differences in a picture than the opponent can.

After the minigame is over, Happy goes to a shop, where he can purchase items for his house. Buying these items will prove to the bride to be that Happy is worth marrying.

The two player game has both players, (one playing as Happy, the other as his brother Rappy), competing against each other to collect the most assets to prove their worth as a suitable husband.","Mappy Kids (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Mappy Kids (Japan).png"
"nes_mappy-land","Mappy-Land","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-04-01","1989","1980s","TOSE","Taxan","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","Mappy the mouse has a girlfriend named Mapica. In order to please his girlfriend, Mappy goes on a mission to collect gifts for his significant other. Unfortunately the boss cat Nyamco and his legion of pink cats want to track Mappy down so they can make a meal out of him. The goal of the game is to collect 6 of 1 item in each stage without getting eaten by a cat. The items you collect (either pieces of cheese, wedding rings, christmas trees, or baseballs) vary depending on what stage your playing.  There are also stage specific items in the background that will help you defeat your feline adversaries.","Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).zip","ZIP","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","miximages/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","screenshots/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","titlescreens/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","3dboxes/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","backcovers/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","marquees/nes/Mappy-Land (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png"
"nes_marble-madness","Marble Madness","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-01-01","1989","1980s","Rare Limited","Milton Bradley Co.","Unknown","Unknown","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","A port of the arcade game. The idea is deceptively simple: Guide a marble down a path without hitting any obstacles or straying off the course. The game is viewed from an isometric perspective, which makes it harder to stay focused on the direction the ball is to follow. There are tight corridors to follow and enemies to avoid. There is a 2-player mode in which players must race to the finish; otherwise you're racing against the clock.","Marble Madness (USA).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","miximages/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png","marquees/nes/Marble Madness (USA).png"
"nes_mario-bros","Mario Bros.","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1986-01-01","1986","1980s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Mario and Luigi are doing some underground plumbing when all sorts of weird creatures come flying out of the pipes. Turtles, crabs - even fighterflies - attack the helpless Mario Bros. It's up to you to kick, punch, and knock out these sewer pests before time runs out! But beware. Just when you think you got rid of them, they come back for more! Play against the computer, or with a friend - either way, this is one underground classic you'll want to play time and time again!","Mario Bros. (World).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","miximages/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","screenshots/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","titlescreens/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","3dboxes/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","backcovers/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png","marquees/nes/Mario Bros. (World).png"
"nes_mario-is-missing","Mario Is Missing!","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-07-01","1993","1990s","Radical Entertainment","Mindscape","Educational","Action","1","1","1","50","2.5","Bowser, the token bad guy from the Mario Bros. series, is up to no good again in this educational game designed to teach children geography. This time he's set up his headquarters in Antarctica and created portals to 25 famous cities around the world, so that his Koopas can wreak havoc in our own world. He's also kidnapped Mario, hence the title of this game. You play as Luigi who must foil Bowser's plans by entering through each of the portals, tracking down the Koopas who have stolen famous artifacts, and looking for clues about your location. Once you've set everything right and determined where you are, you call Yoshi on your Globulator so he can track you down. You need Yoshi's help to eat the Pokey (a cactus-like creature) that's guarding the return portal, and when Luigi returns he can close the portal forever.

