"nes_mezase-pachi-pro-pachio-kun","Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-12-18","1987","1980s","Marionette","Coconuts Japan","Casino","Board / Casual","1","1","1","","","The first game to feature Pachio-kun, the mascot for a series of pachinko-themed games by Coconuts Japan, Mezase Pachi Pro: Pachio-kun (""Aiming For Pachinko Pro: Pachio-kun"") is simply a virtual pachinko hall with 72 different machines on which the player may try their luck.

The game rewards attentive pachinko veterans by having several of the machines possess quirks, such as the frequency of payouts, certain pins being bent that will favor a ball's route to the bottom and the like. Pachio-kun simply has to lean in to examine the machines closer to ascertain how to make the machine pay out. The overall goal is to keep playing each machine, winning either through a determined strategy or simple perseverance, until all the machines have been emptied of their contents. Doing so will win the game.","Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Mezase Pachi Pro - Pachio-kun (Japan).png"
"nes_mezase-top-pro-green-ni-kakeru-yume","Mezase Top Pro - Green Ni Kakeru Yume","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-03-05","1993","1990s","Jaleco","Jaleco","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Mezase! Top Pro: Green ni Kakeru Yume is Jaleco's  first golf game, released exclusively in Japan in 1993. It was developed by TOSE and published by Jaleco.

There are four modes in the game: stroke, course, challenge and train. When the game start, one can change the club then the golf stance. After these choices are done, a screen with the golf player swinging the club is shown, and the player must press the button A at an exact time to select the force that the club will impact the ball. There is also a caddy menu that can be accessed with the button B. In this menu, one can get hints for the current hole, ask for and mulligan and even can be consoled by the caddy if the player misses many strokes. As the player progress in the challenge mode, he can use the money won to buy new clubs and hire new caddies.

The game simulates many terrains, such as grass and sand, and also takes account the effect of the wind, which velocity and direction is shown to the player before his making the stroke. Besides that, the game has also a two player mode, where each player takes a turn to stroke.","Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.17","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Mezase! Top Pro - Green ni Kakeru Yume (Japan).png"
