"nes_mississippi-satsujin-jiken","Mississippi Satsujin Jiken","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1986-10-31","1986","1980s","Activision","Jaleco","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Murder on the Mississippi, fully titled as Murder on the Mississippi: The Adventures of Sir Charles Foxworth, is a 1986 detective adventure game developed and published by Activision for the Commodore 64, Commodore 128 and the Apple II computers. It was also licensed for release exclusively in Japan by Jaleco, who ported the game to the Nintendo Famicom and the MSX2 as Mississippi Satsujin Jiken. It is an adventure game in which the player must solve a murder mystery on the luxury ship ""Delta Princess"". While heading to New Orleans from St. Louis on the ship ""Delta Princess"", detective Sir Charles and Watson are caught up in the midst of a murder case by chance, that they must solve.","Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).zip","ZIP","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png","miximages/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png","screenshots/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).jpg","titlescreens/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png","3dboxes/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png","backcovers/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png","marquees/nes/Mississippi Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev A).png"
"nes_mito-koumon-sekai-manyuu-ki","Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1988-08-11","1988","1980s","TOSE","Sunsoft","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","","","Mito Koumon II: Sekai Manyuuki (lit. Mito Koumon's World Tour Chronicle) is an adventure game. It is the sequel to Tenka no Goikenban: Mito Koumon and is very similar in appearance and gameplay. As in that game, the player controls one of Mitsukini Tokugawa's retainers as they gather clues and evidence of crimes in the area while either avoiding or fighting off hostile NPCs. Unlike the first game, which was set entirely within Japan, Tokugawa crosses the world solving problems instead. The first stage is America (specifically the Wild West, as would be chronologically accurate for the 17th century) though there are plenty of other locations to visit across the world as well, including Transylvania.","Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Mito Koumon - Sekai Manyuu Ki (Japan).png"
