"nes_pac-land","Pac-Land","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1985-11-21","1985","1980s","Namco","Namcot","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","40","2","Pac-Land is a side-scrolling 1-2 player game with a cartoony feel to it. Now equipped with arms, face, and legs, Pac must guide a fairy back to her home in Fairy Land, but this task will not be easy because Inky, Blinky, Pinky, Clyde, and Sue will pursue Pac-Man as he travels through Pac-Land. When he finally transports the fairy back to her home, Pac is given some magic shoes, which will help him get to his own home, where he will be greeted by his family: Ms. Pac-Man, Baby Pac-Man, Chomp Chomp, and Sourpuss. 

There are sixteen rounds to complete, with four trips each. During each round, he can grab a power pellet, which cause ghosts to turn blue, allowing Pac-Man to eat them for points. Points are also awarded by collecting fruit that appear, like cherries and strawberries. In some rounds, Pac must use a springboard to jump over a lake. He must also make it to the end of each round before time runs out, otherwise a ghost will chase him.","Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).zip","ZIP","0.02","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","miximages/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","screenshots/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","titlescreens/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","3dboxes/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","backcovers/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png","marquees/nes/Pac-Land (World) (Namcot Collection, Namco Museum Archives Vol 2).png"
"nes_pac-man","Pac-Man","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Namco","Namco","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","80","4","One of the most popular and influential games of the 1980's, Pac-Man stars a little, yellow dot-muncher who works his way around to clear a maze of the various dots and fruit which inhabit the board.

Pac-Man's goal is continually challenged by four ghosts: The shy blue ghost Bashful (Inky), the trailing red ghost Shadow (Blinky), the fast pink ghost Speedy (Pinky), and the forgetful orange ghost Pokey (Clyde).  One touch from any of these ghosts means a loss of life for Pac-Man.

Pac-Man can turn the tables on his pursuers by eating of the four Energizers located within the maze.  During this time, the ghosts turn blue, and Pac-Man can eat them for bonus points.  This only lasts for a limited amount of time, as the ghost's eyes float back to their center box, and regenerate to chase after Pac-Man again.

Survive a few rounds of gameplay, and be treated to humorous intermissions between Pac-Man and the ghosts.","Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).zip","ZIP","0.01","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","miximages/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","screenshots/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","titlescreens/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","3dboxes/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","backcovers/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png","marquees/nes/Pac-Man (USA) (Virtual Console).png"
"nes_pac-man-championship-edition","Pac-Man Championship Edition","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","2020-06-18","2020","2020s","M2","Bandai Namco","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Like the original Pac-Man, the basic game play of Pac-Man Championship Edition consists entirely of navigating Pac-Man through a maze, eating dots, power pellets and bonus items (such as fruits, keys, and other objects), and avoiding the four ghosts that roam the maze as well. If Pac-Man is caught by a ghost, the player loses a life. Eating a power pellet causes the ghosts to turn blue, allowing Pac-Man to eat them and send them back to their home, where they re-emerge in their original form.
However, there are several major differences from its original counterpart, making Pac-Man C.E. a faster paced game. Each maze is divided into two halves. Eating all the dots on one half causes a bonus item to appear on the other side, and eating the item causes a new maze to appear on the other half. Players can also collect additional power pellets to increase their powered up time and continue earning maximum points for eating ghosts.","Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png","miximages/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png","screenshots/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png","titlescreens/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png","3dboxes/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png","","marquees/nes/Pac-Man Championship Edition (USA, Europe) (Namco Museum Archives Vol 1) (Aftermarket).png"
