"nes_puzslot","Puzslot","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-02-28","1992","1990s","Sammy Corporation","Sammy USA Corporation","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","","","Puzslot is a falling blocks puzzle game with a unique slot machine mechanic. Blocks fall in pairs and can be rotated with the A button (similar to Puyo Puyo), and a line of 3 or more matching blocks in any direction will vanish (similar to Columns). The unique element is that the falling blocks cycle through every picture, stopping when the block lands or the player presses the B button. Points are awarded based on which picture is matched (7 and BAR are worth much more), the number of blocks in a cleared line, and for chain combos. Each level has a score goal that the player must clear before the block counter reaches 0.","Puzslot (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Puzslot (Japan).png"
"nes_puzzle","Puzzle","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","American Video Entertainment","American Video Entertainment","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","40","2","The object of Puzzle is to reassemble a picture which has been scrambled. The picture is broken into a number of pieces with one or more open spaces. Slide the pieces into the open spaces to rearrange them back into the proper order. If you're stuck, you have the option of challenging the computer to a game of chance like rock, paper, scissors or roll the dice. This will subtract 60 seconds from your time, but if won allows any two pieces on the board to be swapped. If you forget what the picture looks like, you can pause the game and see the completed version, but this can only be done five times per puzzle. There are eight different levels, plus two additional expert levels.","Puzzle (USA) (Unl).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","miximages/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","screenshots/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","titlescreens/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","3dboxes/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","backcovers/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png","marquees/nes/Puzzle (USA) (Unl).png"
"nes_puzznic","Puzznic","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","Taito","Taito","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","70","3.5","The challenge in each level of Puzznic is to maneuvre a selection of blocks into place so as to clear them all, by making them make contact with blocks of the same design. You control a cross-hair, which can move a block left or right, which can cause it to fall if there is no block under the space it would occupy.

There are many complications in terms of solving the levels. Moving platforms meaning that you need to move a block at a particular time, or in particular order, to prevent them being blockaded. In some situations there are an odd number of a certain type of block - solving these requires positioning two of the blocks one space apart, such that a move will result in a piece making contact with 2 others, and immediately removing all 3. You will also encounter blocks positioned on platforms suspended in space and gaps in level arrangements meaning that a certain number of blocks must be in place to make a certain move possible (by forming a stack, for example)

The game structure is slightly unusual, as after you complete each batch of four levels you get a choice of 2 sets of levels - you are progressing through an expanding matrix of levels, which means there are 2 sets on level 2, 3 on level 3, 4 on level 4, and so on. This means that there are a total of 220 screens in the game. Each screen is played against a time limit, and losing a level (either by running out of time, or by making a poor move and leaving an impossible position) loses one of your 3 lives.","Puzznic (USA).zip","ZIP","0.04","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Puzznic (USA).png","miximages/nes/Puzznic (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Puzznic (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Puzznic (USA).jpg","3dboxes/nes/Puzznic (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Puzznic (USA).png","marquees/nes/Puzznic (USA).png"
