"nes_sd-gundam-gachapon-senshi-3-eiyuu-senki","Sd Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1990-12-22","1990","1990s","TOSE","Yutaka","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","It is a video game adaptation of the series based on the anime Mobile Suit Gundam including Super Deformed Gundam. This is the third installment in a series of five video games.

There are two main game modes, simulation mode and battle mode.
The first one allows to produce units, to move these, and to occupy zones.
The second allows you to launch your units to attack enemy units.

There are 4 types of units which also correspond to stages: that of the ground, the space ones, Sengokuden and Gaiden. There are 10 scenarios for each stage.","SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","miximages/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png","marquees/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 3 - Eiyuu Senki (Japan).png"
"nes_sd-gundam-gachapon-senshi-4-newtype-story","Sd Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - Newtype Story","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-12-21","1991","1990s","TOSE","Yutaka","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","SD Gundam World Gachapon Senshi 4 is based on the popular SD Gundam series. It's a standard turn-based game where you have to take over the opponent's base to win. You have many types of fighting robots at your disposal to achieve this goal. The interesting part about this game is the level of customization; before each game, you can set options such as how much money each player has, if they start with a small / large number of units on the battlefield, and if the players are human or computer controlled. This game improves upon previous games in the series, as there are now set campaign battles to participate in, as well as the usual matchmaking maps that you can select from.","SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.23","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","miximages/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png","marquees/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 4 - NewType Story (Japan).png"
"nes_sd-gundam-gachapon-senshi-5-battle-of-universal-century","Sd Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle Of Universal Century","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-12-22","1992","1990s","TOSE","Yutaka","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","This is the final installment of the SD Gundam World series to be released on the Famicom. The objective of the game is to conquer both Earth and space, by leading your army into battle against groups of rival armies. There are 10 preset scenarios in the game, each with a specified number of teams and a time limit to get the objectives done. (The player can also choose a Free Scenario.) Once a scenario is chosen, and game settings are set (all settings can be changed in Free Scenario mode), the player and computer take turns navigating units through a series of menus, in the hopes of gaining enough force to occupy a locale. Once a locale is captured, the player who took it over gains money which can be used to bolster their units. The first player to capture all 21 areas (or the player further ahead when time is up) wins the scenario. A battery-backed memory allows players to save their progress and return to the game at a later time.","SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","miximages/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png","marquees/nes/SD Gundam - Gachapon Senshi 5 - Battle of Universal Century (Japan).png"
