"nes_shin-moero-pro-yakyuu","Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-07-13","1989","1980s","TOSE","Jaleco","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (New Burning!! Pro Baseball) is the sixth of Jaleco/TOSE's Moero!! series of sports games (it's occasionally referred to as Moero 6!! Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu) and the third in the series to be associated with baseball. The first two Moero!! Pro Yakyuu games saw localizations in the US as Bases Loaded and Bases Loaded 2, but Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu was skipped. What eventually became Bases Loaded 3 was instead the fourth Moero!! Pro Yakyuu game, Moero 8!! Pro Yakyuu '90 Kandouhen.

A curious addition to this version is that of the biorhythms, which tells the player how each athlete is feeling: If the athlete is having an off-game, one or more of these biorhythms will be low and the player will need to strategize around these dips. Though big in 70s sports punditry, the idea of mathematical biorhythms predicting an athlete's prowess in any upcoming game was all but discredited as pseudoscience by the time when this game came out.","Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.13","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Shin Moero!! Pro Yakyuu (Japan).png"
"nes_shin-satomi-hakken-den-hikari-to-yami-no-tatakai","Shin Satomi Hakken-den - Hikari To Yami No Tatakai","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-12-08","1989","1980s","Micronics","Toei Animation","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","Shin Satomi Hakkenden: Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (""New Eight Dog Chronicles: Battle of Light and Darkness"") is a traditional Japanese RPG that follows the story of the 19th century historical novel Nansou Satomi Hakkenden, or Eight Dog Chronicles, based on eight half-brother samurai who were all descended from a dog and team up for various adventures across Sengoku period Japan. In particular, the game is based on the 1983 live-action movie, localized in the west as Legend of the Eight Samurai which in turn was based on a 1982 reworking of the epic novel named Shin Satomi Hakkenden.

The game has a then-distinct feature of being able to start the game as any of the eight samurai, each of which begins the game in a different location. Their goal is to meet up and recruit their brothers, eventually forming a group of eight. The game is otherwise standard for the genre: the player splits their time between exploring towns and talking to NPCs, and fighting monsters and enemy soldiers in dungeons and the overworld map via a turn-based combat system.","Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Shin Satomi Hakken-Den - Hikari to Yami no Tatakai (Japan).png"
