"nes_stick-hunter-exciting-ice-hockey","Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-12-18","1987","1980s","Micronics","K. Amusement Leasing","Sports / Hockey","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Stick Hunter: Exciting Ice Hockey is a game for the Famicom released only in Japan in 1987. It was never released in North America. Stick Hunter was the first actual ice hockey game created for a Nintendo gaming system.

The game was designed so that 1 player could play against the computer, or 2 players could play simultaneously against each other. The length of the periods and difficulty level could both be adjusted.

Playing as a character who has possession of the puck, the character could not only skate faster, but could only shoot the puck forward. So if the player wanted to pass to a teammate, the character on screen would have to be facing the person to which he's passing. The same applied to shooting at the net and attempting to score a goal. The character would have to be facing the opposing net. A player without the puck could only skate faster. If the goalie had control of the puck, he could only pass to a teammate.

As in the real-world sport of hockey, the object is to score more goals than the opposing team.","Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Stick Hunter - Exciting Ice Hockey (Japan).png"
