"nes_tashiro-masashi-no-princess-ga-ippai","Tashiro Masashi No Princess Ga Ippai","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-10-27","1989","1980s","HAL Laboratory","Epic - Sony Records","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai is a Japanese video game for the Nintendo Famicom (NES) by former comedian Masashi Tashiro released in time for October, 1989.

The story is about the hero Masashi Tashiro who has to rescue the four princesses in distress. One happy ending and four unhappy endings were used in the game; becoming one of the first video games to have multiple endings. The game was not very successful, but it started appearing frequently and getting high prices on online auction sites like Yahoo! after 2000, when Masashi Tashiro was arrested and convicted several times in connection with voyeurism and drug abuse.","Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Tashiro Masashi no Princess ga Ippai (Japan).png"
"nes_transformers-convoy-no-nazo","Transformers - Convoy no Nazo","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1986-12-05","1986","1980s","ISCO","Takara","Platform / Shooter Scrolling","Shooter","1-2","1","2","20","1","Probably the first game to be based on the Transformers toys, Convoy no nazo pits the player as Ultra Magnus, who must find out the secret of Convoy (known as Optimus Prime in most of the world). To find it out, Ultra Magnus must travel through a set of platform-style worlds and fight a range of bosses, ranging from the Megatron, through the combiner series to a flying Decepticon emblem(!).

Ultra Magnus starts out in robot mode, where he can jump far but his shots travel only halfway across the screen. Press down, and Magnus transforms into a trailer. In trailer mode, he can pass below the planes as well as shoot upwards. When a plane is shot down, it transforms into a robot, which must be killed with the forward-pointing shot. Later on, the game becomes more platform-oriented.","Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Tatakae! Chou Robot Seimeitai Transformers - Convoy no Nazo (Japan).png"
"nes_tatakae-rahmen-man-sakuretsu-choujin-102-gei","Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1988-08-10","1988","1980s","Human Entertainment","Bandai","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Tatakae!! Ramen-Man: Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei is an adventure game developed by Human Entertainment for the Famicom and published by Bandai in 1988. It is based off the Tatakae!! Ramenman series, which itself is a spin-off of the Kinnikuman series, known in the US as M.U.S.C.L.E.. Ramenman is a popular character in the Kinnikuman universe.

The game follows the eponymous warrior Ramenman as he attempts to track down his father's killers and bring them to justice with his many years of martial arts training. Notably, this game is the first true point-and-click adventure game for the system. While there had been many adventure games made for the NES, such as Portopia Renzoku Satsujin Jiken or Princess Tomato in the Salad Kingdom, they are largely driven by menus. Ramenman is directed by using the cursor to select an area to walk to or interact with instead much like classic Sierra adventure games such as King's Quest.","Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","miximages/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","screenshots/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","titlescreens/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","3dboxes/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","backcovers/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png","marquees/nes/Tatakae!! Rahmen Man - Sakuretsu Choujin 102 Gei (Japan).png"
"nes_tecmo-baseball","Tecmo Baseball","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-01-02","1989","1980s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Tecmo Baseball is one of the many baseball games released for the Nintendo Entertainment Systems. There are five modes in Tecmo Baseball: One Player, Two Player, One Player Allstar, Two Player Allstar, and a watch mode. In One Player mode you pick from one of the fourteen teams and challenge each of the other teams. A password feature allows you to continue from where you left off. You also have the option of using the DH rule.

Gameplay is similar to the many other baseball released for the NES. The camera angle when batting or pitching is from behind the pitcher. The pitcher can pitch the ball high and low, as well as curve it. Tecmo Baseball includes digitized voices for the umpire.","Tecmo Baseball (USA).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","miximages/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png","marquees/nes/Tecmo Baseball (USA).png"
"nes_tecmo-bowl","Tecmo Bowl","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1989-02-02","1989","1980s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Tecmo Bowl pits the player vs. the computer in 11 game single-elimination playoff action, or you can go head-to-head with a human opponent in action or coach mode. There are 12 teams of real NFL players (circa 1988) to choose from, but don't look for official NFL team logos or mascots.

There are four plays to choose from on offense--usually two runs and two passes. The player takes control of the quarterback before the snap and then either hands off to the running back or works through his receiver progression from the top to the bottom of the screen. Defense consists of trying to guess which offensive play the opponent will select and then taking control of one of the defensive players before the snap. A very simple power meter system is used for kicking field goals, extra points, and punts.

There are no game or season stats and there is no way to save your season, but there is a password feature allowing you to resume tournament play where you left off.","Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).zip","ZIP","0.1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","miximages/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","screenshots/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","titlescreens/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","3dboxes/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","backcovers/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png","marquees/nes/Tecmo Bowl (USA) (Rev 1).png"
"nes_tecmo-cup-football-game","Tecmo Cup : Football Game","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1","1","1","100","5","Robin Field loves soccer. He aims to be the best player in the world with the help of his dad (who was former top player) and his little brother Cecil. After successful domestic league campaign, Robin continues his career in the ""Tops"", which consist of best players seen in the domestic league. Tops participate in the Tecmo Cup, the youth World Cup with best players from around the world. 

Tecmo Cup is a soccer simulator combined with RPG-elements. As the game progress, Robin and his teammates will get better. The matches itself consists of numerous choices what to do at each moment. If you are attacking, you have options to pass, shoot or to dribble. And when you are defending, you can either tackle, cut pass/shoot, or mark the opposition player with ball.","Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).zip","ZIP","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png","miximages/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).jpg","3dboxes/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png","marquees/nes/Tecmo Cup - Soccer Game (USA).png"
"nes_tecmo-nba-basketball","Tecmo NBA Basketball","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1992-11-01","1992","1990s","Sculptured Software","Tecmo","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","This basketball game is very similar to Tecmo Super NBA Basketball with the main difference being their rosters. The game has 27 NBA teams with a roster of 324 Players. Each player has a rating for his shooting ability, stamina, jumping power, running speed, stealing ability, and blocking ability. The game allows for pre-season and season modes. In the season modes the game tracks team &amp; player statistics throughout the season.

