"nes_tetris-2","Tetris 2","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","TOSE","Nintendo","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Unlike the original Tetris, Tetris 2 has you clearing the field of blocks in a different way. Each play field starts with different colored dots (in this case black, gray and white), with one of each color flashing. The blocks are made up of the same three colors, and by matching blocks of the same color over the top or to the side of the dot will clear the dot and those blocks from the screen. If you clear a flashing dot, all the corresponding dots of the same color will be cleared. To complete the round just clear the dots, not the blocks themselves.","Tetris 2 (USA).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","miximages/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","screenshots/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","titlescreens/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","3dboxes/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","backcovers/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png","marquees/nes/Tetris 2 (USA).png"
"nes_tetris-2-bombliss","Tetris 2 + Bombliss","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1991-12-13","1991","1990s","Chunsoft","Bullet Proof Software","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","","","Tetris 2 + BomBliss is one of the many versions of the famous soviet puzzle game. There are, naturally, two variations featured on this cartridge: regular Tetris with several modes, as well as a new game called BomBliss. Also included is a two-player battle version of regular Tetris.

Tetris mode includes three game types. First is A-Type, which is a standard endless mode that continually increases pace until the player loses. Next is B-Type, which is a race to 25 lines under increasingly tough conditions. Last is C-Type, which is similar to A-Type, but adds a continually-rising stack of garbage appearing from the bottom of the well.

BomBliss is slightly different from regular Tetris. In each stage, the well is filled with a preset pattern of blocks and bombs. Completing a line will, unlike Tetris, not clear it. It will, however, activate any bombs within the completed line, which can then destroy the blocks. The goal is to clear the entire well of blocks.

BomBliss also includes three different modes of play. Contest mode tasks the player with clearing out a preset field in as few blocks as possible; the top three scores for each stage are saved. Puzzle mode tasks the player with clearing a preset field with a preset sequence of pieces. Last, there is Construction mode, which allows the player to build their own puzzle stages.","Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png","miximages/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png","screenshots/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png","titlescreens/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).jpg","3dboxes/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png","backcovers/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png","marquees/nes/Tetris 2 + Bombliss (Japan) (Rev 1).png"
"nes_tetsudou-ou-famicom-boardgame","Tetsudou Ou - Famicom Boardgame","nes","Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) / Famicom","NES","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit)","1987-12-12","1987","1980s","DB Soft","DB Soft","Board game","Board / Casual","1-4","1","4","","","This is a board-game title in which 4 players play as rail road cars. The goal of the game is to acquire the most assets and cross the destination points as much as possible in competition with your other players.

Here is a full English translation for the game, Tetsudou Ou: Famicom Boardgame for the famicom system!

