"fds_bakutoushi-patton-kun","Bakutoushi Patton-kun","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1988-08-05","1988","1980s","Soft Pro International","Soft Pro International","Shooter","Shooter","1-4","1","4","","","Bakutoushi Patton-Kun is an overhead tank combat game similar in style to Atari's Combat game. It was the first FDS title to allow for four players to play simultaneously. In the game, players attempt to destroy each others tanks. If a tank is destroyed, the driver of the tank will exit the vehicle, and must try to stay alive long enough for a replacement tank to parachute down from the sky. Game play continues until only one tank is the sole survivor. Then players advance to a new stage with different terrain. There are 56 stages in total. Tank stats can also be changed in an Editor mode. Despite referencing the name of American General George S. Patton in the title, there is no mention of him anywhere else throughout the game. Although the game was only release in Japan, the loading screen instructions contain English profanity.","Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.04","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Bakutoushi Patton-kun (Japan).png"
