"fds_maerchen-veil","Maerchen Veil","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1987-03-03","1987","1980s","System Sacom","Sunsoft","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","A long time ago, people from Ferikusu could communicate with the gods and divine spirits. The king of the kingdom is now looking for a young man to marry his daughter, the royal princess. Many contestants are selected and a tournament is organized to decide of the new prince. However, before the end or the ceremony, an evil magician sends the last hero, the one the princess has fallen in love with, to an unknown and desolated world. He also quickly realizes that he fell under a terrible curse, and he has been turned into a weird creature. The only item he has left is a magic bracelet the princess gave him. The player takes control of the lost prince and his journey will take him back to where he came from, confront the evil magician and marry the princess he loves. Each stage starts with a short animation (called a ""visual stage"") which unfolds the story as the game progresses. The rest of the game follows a classic top-view action formula, where the hero defeats all kind of enemies with the help of his magic powers. Sometimes, special items can be found under tree logs or rocks.","Maerchen Veil (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Maerchen Veil (Japan).png"
"fds_magma-project-hacker","Magma Project - Hacker","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1989-08-10","1989","1980s","Bits Laboratory","Tokuma Shoten","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","Magma Project Hacker is a sci-fi themed RPG and an adaptation of the 1985 PC/Amiga/Atari ST strategy game Hacker. As with the Famicom Disk System adaptation of Monty on the Run, a considerable number of liberties were taken with the game's themes practically transforming it into a completely different game. Ironically, the story more closely resembles another western PC game, Captive, with its plot.
The player character witnesses a murder and is told to seek information on a shadowy organization known as the Magma Project by the dying victim. In order to effectively hunt for clues, the player character uses a device to activate a robot on the other side of the planet and employs the robot's various combat and exploration functions to track down the Magma Project.","Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Magma Project - Hacker (Japan).png"
