"fds_mahjong-kazoku","Mahjong Kazoku","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1987-08-04","1987","1980s","Irem","Irem","Asiatic board game","Board / Casual","1","1","1","","","Mahjong Kazoku (""Mahjong Family"") is a standard Mahjong simulation game for Nintendo's Famicom Disk System. It is a one-on-one version of the game, rather than the standard four-player board game arrangement, and it incorporates many of the various and byzantine scoring rules of the game.
