Irem created four Arcade versions of the original Lode Runner, each with a unique set of levels as well as added features like a co-operative mode for two players. For the FDS home versions, Irem compiled several levels from each of these Arcade versions onto one disk. Super Lode Runner II has fewer single-player levels than its predecessor, but contains more co-op levels to make up for it.","Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).zip","ZIP","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png","miximages/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png","screenshots/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png","titlescreens/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png","3dboxes/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png","","marquees/fds/Super Lode Runner II (Japan) (Disk Writer).png"
