"fds_tantei-jinguuji-saburou-kiken-na-futari-kouhen","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken Na Futari - Kouhen","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1989-02-10","1989","1980s","SAS Sakata","Data East","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","The second chapter of the series. Detective Hunter and his assistant Yulia have been invited to watch Yulia's friend Sabin participate in a motorcycle race. It doesn't all go too well when he crashes in the race, but when the racing team checks up on him it turns out to be Thomas, Sabin's apprentice, under the helmet. The mystery deepens as another friend of Yulia is found murdered in a hotel room.","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Kouhen (Japan).png"
"fds_tantei-jinguuji-saburou-kiken-na-futari-zenpen","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken Na Futari - Zenpen","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1988-12-09","1988","1980s","SAS Sakata","Data East","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen  (Detective Saburou Jinguuji: Danger For Two, Part 1) is a mystery-adventure game developed by Data East for the Famicom Disk System in 1988. It is the third game of the long standing Tantei Jinguuji Saburou series, following Tantei Jinguuji Saburou: Yokohama-kou Renzoku Satsujin Jiken. In the third mystery, the detective visits a race circuit at the invitation of one of Yulia's friends. A motorcycle racer, Sabin Olsen, crashes at the circuit, but a different racer's body is recovered from the crash site. At the same time, Sabin Olsen, at a hotel, is found where a man he was supposed to meet was killed causing Olsen to be framed as he fled the hotel. Due to memory constraints on the size of the disks, this game was broken up into two parts. This is the first part, while the second part, Tantei Jinguuji Saburo: Kiken na Futari Kouhen, was release a few months later.","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Kiken na Futari - Zenpen (Japan).png"
"fds_tantei-jinguuji-saburou-shinjuku-chuuou-kouen-satsujin-jiken","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1987-04-27","1987","1980s","SAS Sakata","Data East","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken  (""Detective Saburo Jinguuji: Shinjuku Central Park Murder Mystery"") is the first in a long-running series of crime-themed adventure games from Data East regarding the detective Saburo Jinguuji, or Jake Hunter as he is known in the West.

As with all the games that follow, the goal of the game is to discover the perpetrator behind a murder by talking to witnesses and suspects, gathering clues and deducing facts about the case. The player can use a menu of options with which to control Detective Jinguuji's investigation, such as ""Talk"" and ""Look"" commands to get a better sense of the world of the game.","Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).zip","ZIP","0.06","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","miximages/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","screenshots/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","titlescreens/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","3dboxes/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","backcovers/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png","marquees/fds/Tantei Jinguuji Saburou - Shinjuku Chuuou Kouen Satsujin Jiken (Japan) (Rev 1) (Disk Writer).png"
"fds_tarot-uranai","Tarot Uranai","fds","Famicom Disk System","FDS","Nintendo","3. kynslóð (8-bit viðbót)","1988-12-23","1988","1980s","Scorpion Soft","Scorpion Soft","Simulation","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","","","Tarot Uranai (Lit. Tarot fortune telling) is a fortune telling simulation developed and published by Scorpion Soft for the Famicom Disk System in 1988. During play, the game predicts the player's future in several areas, including love, finance, and education. It followed a series of other astrological ""utility"" programs for the platform, including Chuugoku Senseijutsu and '89 Dennou Kyuusei Uranai.

The game focuses on the Tarot deck and their supposed clairvoyant properties. The game will randomly shuffle a deck and lay them out in a formation of the player's choosing - each formation is meant to predict a different aspect of the player's life. The game will then reveal cards that the player chooses and decipher the meaning behind them.","Tarot Uranai (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","miximages/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","screenshots/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","titlescreens/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","3dboxes/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","backcovers/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png","marquees/fds/Tarot Uranai (Japan).png"
