"megadrive_aerobiz","Aerobiz","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Koei","Koei","Build And Management","Action","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","You are the CEO of an airline company. Your goal is to become the most successful airline in the world by connecting all 22 cities with air routes, maintain a profit, and meet the required quota of passengers. If you cannot turn a profit for a year or meet the victory conditions in 32 years you lose. Some strategic decisions you must make include negotiating for open air routes, purchasing or selling aircraft, invest in branch offices and hotels, advertise your airline and set budgets. You must also pay attention to statistics like quarterly and annual sales reports, as well as city data. World events also affect your airline, from natural disasters to war and even the Olympic games, all of which will affect how many passengers you get. All the planes in the game are based on real-life aircraft, such as the Boeing 747 and the Concorde.","Aerobiz (USA).7z","7Z","0.34","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).jpg","titlescreens/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Aerobiz (USA).png"
"megadrive_aerobiz-supersonic","Aerobiz Supersonic","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Koei","Koei","Build And Management","Action","1-4","1","4","60","3","It's the beginning of the 21st century and competition in the airline industry is heating up. As a young, ambitious CEO, it's up to you to make sure your airline is a survivor and not just another casualty. To succeed, you will have to make some tough decisions including where to fly, which planes to purchase and how to attract visitors to the cities you service. Your goal: to differentiate your airline from the rest while still turning a profit. Get ready to make some tough decisions! If you make the right ones, your planes will dominate the skies of the 21st century!","Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).7z","7Z","0.42","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Aerobiz Supersonic (USA).png"
"megadrive_after-burner-ii","After Burner II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-04-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Shooter / Plane, TPV","Shooter","1","1","1","70","3.5","Similar to its predecessor, the premise of After Burner II is to get on the F-14 Tomcat and fly mission after mission of shooting planes out of the sky. At your disposal is a vulcan cannon (basically a machine gun) and a limited number of missiles. In some versions of the game the guns fire automatically all the time. Sometimes you come across a friendly supply plane and if you dock with it you can replenish your missiles. The game is viewed from behind the plane with you fighting wave after wave of enemy fighters. But at heart it offers the usual shooter mechanics, meaning you spend most of your time dodging and shooting. You also can speed up and slow down to deal with enemies which appear behind you.","After Burner II (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/After Burner II (Japan) (En).png"
"megadrive_after-burner-ii","After Burner II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-04-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Shooter / Plane, TPV","Shooter","1","1","1","70","3.5","Similar to its predecessor, the premise of After Burner II is to get on the F-14 Tomcat and fly mission after mission of shooting planes out of the sky. At your disposal is a vulcan cannon (basically a machine gun) and a limited number of missiles. In some versions of the game the guns fire automatically all the time. Sometimes you come across a friendly supply plane and if you dock with it you can replenish your missiles. The game is viewed from behind the plane with you fighting wave after wave of enemy fighters. But at heart it offers the usual shooter mechanics, meaning you spend most of your time dodging and shooting. You also can speed up and slow down to deal with enemies which appear behind you.","After Burner II (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/After Burner II (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_aq-renkan-awa","Aq Renkan Awa","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","C&amp;E","C&amp;E","Quiz","Board / Casual","1","1","1","","","Aq Renkan Awa is an unlicensed educational game for the Sega Mega Drive by C&amp;E Inc. released in 1995. There are five game modes. The first three are some variants of the normal gameplay: you are a student on a game board-like path. You roll a die to see how many spaces you move. At most spaces there is a building where you are asked five questions. If you get a certain number correct, you can stay at the spot you were in; otherwise you go back to the previous position. Play continues with the next player.","Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).7z","7Z","0.54","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).png","miximages/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).jpg","titlescreens/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).jpg","3dboxes/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).png","marquees/megadrive/Ah Q Lianhuan Pao (Taiwan) (Unl).png"
"megadrive_air-buster","Air Buster","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-02-01","1991","1990s","Inter State","Kaneko","Shoot'em Up / Horizontal","Shooter","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Air Buster is a fast side-scrolling shooter. The player controls a small craft through different levels with many enemies. Every level ends with a boss and some section speed up the gameplay, offering fast obstacle courses both horizontally and vertically scrolling. Flying orange pods release many power-ups at once, enhancing the ships with new or more powerful lasers, wing men and shields. The player can also hold the fire key to charge a blast that removes all enemy bullets from the screen and deals damage to all enemies. With an unforgiving difficulty, every hit is fatal, but the game can be continued from any points as long as there are lives and credits left. The game can be played with two players cooperatively.","Air Buster (USA).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Air Buster (USA).png"
"megadrive_air-diver","Air Diver","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","Copya System","Seismic","Shooter / FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","40","2","A terrorist organization led by a fanatic in the Middle East has brought together a military force able to hold the world hostage, backed by hostile governments. The player boards an F-119 stealth fighter and must stay undetected while taking out all opposition.

Although technically a stealth fighter, no stealth elements are involved. After choosing a one of the many locations, the player flies from a realistic cockpit view, with enemies trying to destroy your aircraft. In solo missions the player takes out all opposition using bullets and lock-on missiles. All stats, including time before you are out of fuel and enemies on the radar, are shown in the HUD. The craft can move left and right, and use a boost to do sideways rolls or loops to get behind enemies. Some shots can be taken, causing body damage, but incoming missiles are fatal and must be shot down or avoided. Alongside regular enemies, there are boss planes too and missions take place worldwide at different times of day.","Air Diver (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Air Diver (Japan) (En).png"
