"megadrive_streets-of-rage-ii","Streets of Rage II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-04","1993","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","80","4","After Axel Stone, Blaze Fielding and Adam Hunter destroyed the evil Syndicate leader, Mr. X, the city became a peaceful place to live, and each one of them followed their own paths. One year later, after their reunion, Adam's brother Sammy returned from school to find their apartment in a mess, and Adam nowhere to be seen, and after calling his two friends, one of them notices a photo of Adam chained to a wall, next to someone they knew very well - Mr. X, who returned to turn the peaceful city once again into a war zone. Now, Axel, Blaze, Sammy, and Axel's good friend Max, a pro wrestler, must head out to stop Mr. X once again...hopefully for good...

Streets of Rage 2 differs from the previous title in several ways. There are changes in both graphics (characters now are bigger, more detailed and with more animation frames, and scenarios are less grainy) and gameplay (the rocket move was replaced by a special move that doubles in offense and defense along several new moves), along other new features such as life bars (and names) for all enemies and the radically different new characters.","Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","miximages/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png","marquees/megadrive/Bare Knuckle II (Japan) (En) (Beta).png"
"megadrive_streets-of-rage-3","Streets of Rage 3","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-01","1994","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","80","4","Streets of Rage 3 takes the series to the next level – faster, more complex, and more brutal than ever. With longer stages, branching storylines, and interactive environments featuring deadly traps, the game packs serious variety. New dash and dodge moves add speed, weapons break after use, and can now be integrated into combos. Team attacks return, and enemies use them too, showing smarter behavior – some even steal your health pickups! Blitz moves are now upgradeable but reset on death, though holding a button allows access at a cost. Special attacks no longer drain health but use a regenerating bar. Secret characters await those who meet hidden conditions. It's an intense street brawler with serious depth.","Bare Knuckle III (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Bare Knuckle III (Japan).png"
