"megadrive_bill-bolha","Bill Bolha","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Devworks Game Technology","Tectoy","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Bil Bolha and his brothers have been trapped in a mysterious machine. Your objective is to free them all. The problem is that the machine possesses a strange rule: when you free or imprison one of them, those on their left, right, up and down change their own state. If they were free, they are imprisoned. If they were imprisoned, they are free. There are many initial configurations to be solved, including ""Draw"", where a random pattern is created. To release or imprison, press the buttons A, B, or C when the selection is over the chosen spot. Now play, they need your help! A puzzle game, it wasn't sold on physical media, only on the memory of certain models of Mega Drive sold in Brazil, like the Sega TecToy Super Mega Drive 3 with 71 games in memory. Later, the game began to appear in models by AtGames throughout the world.","Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).7z","7Z","0.05","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","miximages/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","marquees/megadrive/Bil Bolha (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png"
"megadrive_bill-walsh-college-football","Bill Walsh College Football","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-24","1993","1990s","EA Sports","Visual Concepts","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","The game features 24 college football teams from the 1993 season and 24 of the all-time college teams since 1978. Play modes include exhibition, playoffs and all-time playoffs and the SNES version also has an eleven week season mode.with the National Championship as the ultimate goal. 

The playbook consists of 56 offensive plays and 52 defensive plays.
On offense, running backs can dive, spin and hurdle. Also, passing is dealt with by having the receivers in their own windowed boxes . When on defense, defenders can dive at the ball carrier, and raise hands to block kicks or intercept passes.

