"megadrive_championship-bowling","Championship Bowling","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-02-14","1993","1990s","Soft Machine","Visco","Sports","Sports","1","1","1","50","2.5","Championship Bowling is a standard bowling game for one or two players, and the only one available for the Genesis. The player picks one of four different bowlers and the ball they want to use, then heads out to the lanes. The player controls the throw, spin, and power by stopping bars at the right time.

The game includes three different play modes: standard bowling; spare mode, where a handful of pins are placed with the goal being to pick up a spare; and bonus mode, where specific pins are worth different amounts of points. Each mode can be played against either the computer or a friend, and there are three different lane types available. There is also a practice mode for each of the game types.

The Japanese version, Boogie Woogie Bowling, is largely the same but features different, more anime-style characters to play as (including a robot for no explained reason), as well as minor tweaks to the timing for throws.","Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Boogie Woogie Bowling (Japan).png"
"megadrive_bottle-taps-race","Bottle Taps Race","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2008-01-01","2008","2000s","Devworks Game Technology","Tec Toy","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","The game itself is based on the traditional Polish game of same name, but adapted for Brazilian aesthetics. In this game, the player is competing alongside three CPU opponents in a race from the start to the finish. Similar to a golf game, a growing bar is available to measure the distance for the player to throw the bottle cap further; the more power is on it, farther the bottle cap will go. However, if the bottle cap itself does a move that goes outside of the course's boundaries, it counts as a miss and another CPU player takes over your turn.","Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).7z","7Z","0.04","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).png","miximages/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).jpg","titlescreens/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).jpg","3dboxes/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).png","marquees/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (Europe) (Sega Reactor).png"
"megadrive_bottle-taps-race","Bottle Taps Race","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2008-01-01","2008","2000s","Devworks Game Technology","Tec Toy","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","The game itself is based on the traditional Polish game of same name, but adapted for Brazilian aesthetics. In this game, the player is competing alongside three CPU opponents in a race from the start to the finish. Similar to a golf game, a growing bar is available to measure the distance for the player to throw the bottle cap further; the more power is on it, farther the bottle cap will go. However, if the bottle cap itself does a move that goes outside of the course's boundaries, it counts as a miss and another CPU player takes over your turn.","Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).png","miximages/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).jpg","titlescreens/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).jpg","3dboxes/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).png","marquees/megadrive/Bottle Taps Race (USA) (Unl).png"
"megadrive_boxing-legends-of-the-ring","Boxing Legends of the Ring","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Sculptured Software","Electro Brain","Sports / Boxing","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","In Boxing Legends of the Ring, you step into the ring with eight middleweight legends — including Roberto Durán, Jake LaMotta, Sugar Ray Leonard, Marvin Hagler, and James Toney. You can fight in exhibition matches or rise through the ranks in career mode to become the greatest of all time. Use jabs, hooks, uppercuts, and even the occasional illegal low blow to wear down your opponent. Every knockdown earns you a Super Punch — a devastating strike that can end the fight if it connects but is lost if you miss. Two indicators track the action: glove-shaped hit meters and a damage display showing fighters' faces bruising and bleeding over time. A neat twist is that the camera alternates each round, switching between your view and your opponent's shoulder for a more cinematic experience.","Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).7z","7Z","0.47","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Boxing Legends of the Ring (USA).png"
"megadrive_bram-stoker-s-dracula","Bram Stoker's Dracula","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Traveller's Tales","Sony Imagesoft","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","40","2","The player controls Jonathan Harker, who, on his quest to destroy the Transylvanian vampire, must make his way through nine levels, starting at a tavern near Dracula's castle and then the castle itself. Back in England, Dracula and his minions must be driven out of a convent, an abbey and the house of Jonathan's fiancée Mina, among others. nnnnA primary task in each level is to find and destroy several coffins of Transylvanian earth. Hindering Jonathan on his way are henchmen as well as critters under the vampire's control: bats, rats, snakes and more. The last coffin in each location is usually guarded by one of Dracula's stronger minions, which include his three brides, the madman Renfield, and Mina's friend Lucy, now turned undead.","Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Bram Stoker's Dracula (Europe).png"
