"megadrive_college-football-s-national-championship-ii","College Football's National Championship II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","BlueSky Software","SEGA","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-4","1","4","60","3","This is the follow-up to College Football's National Championship with the same game engine as before which is essentially a clone of NFL Football starring Joe Montana.

It still has the standard set of modes such as Exhibition, Tournament and Season and updated rosters for the top schools of the time, reflecting the 1994 season.

There are 32 teams with 5 added ones to this version (Wisconsin, North Carolina, Colorado State, Oregon and Washington State). However to add these schools, 5 others were taken out that were in the previous game (San Diego State, Pitt, LSU, Arkansas and Houston). It also keeps track of 19 different stats along with authentic offensive and defensive plays attributed to each team.

It also features a battery backup to keep track of stats and save games along with the ability to let 4 different players compete utilizing multi-tap. There are also new sound effects added to this version with the announcer from the previous version removed from this one.","College Football's National Championship II (USA).7z","7Z","0.61","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/College Football's National Championship II (USA).png"
"megadrive_college-slam","College Slam","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-02-01","1996","1990s","Iguana Entertainment","Acclaim Entertainment","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Part of the NBA Jam series of basketball games, College Slam allows you to choose from over 40 real college teams and take part in head-to-head games, tournament games, and season-long play. The gameplay is arcade-style two-on-two fast action featuring backboard shattering wild dunks, power-ups and other crazy moves. The game also features fight songs from all the available teams.","College Slam (USA).7z","7Z","1.71","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/College Slam (USA).png"
"megadrive_columns","Columns","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-02-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Columns is loosely derived from Tetris, as it involves arranging falling blocks in such a way as to clear them. However, in columns they are groups of 3 same-size but varying color blocks, which must be arranged into sequences of 3 or more, either horizontally, vertically or diagonally. Sequences of 4 or 5 count for double or triple points, and diagonal sequences score the most. The real trick is to set up 'combos' - where one line causes other blocks to drop so as to create other lines.

As well as the normal game mode, there is also a 'flash' mode, in which the aim is simply to remove a particular block from the base of the pre-formed pile of bricks. The difficulty of this can be determined by increasing the number of complete rows which are already in place.","Columns (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Columns (Japan) (En).png"
