"megadrive_bottle-taps-race","Bottle Taps Race","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2008-01-01","2008","2000s","Devworks Game Technology","Tec Toy","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","The game itself is based on the traditional Polish game of same name, but adapted for Brazilian aesthetics. In this game, the player is competing alongside three CPU opponents in a race from the start to the finish. Similar to a golf game, a growing bar is available to measure the distance for the player to throw the bottle cap further; the more power is on it, farther the bottle cap will go. However, if the bottle cap itself does a move that goes outside of the course's boundaries, it counts as a miss and another CPU player takes over your turn.","Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","miximages/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","screenshots/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).jpg","titlescreens/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).jpg","3dboxes/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","backcovers/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","marquees/megadrive/Corrida de Tampinhas (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png"
"megadrive_cosmic-spacehead","Cosmic Spacehead","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Codemasters","Codemasters","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Linus had crash landed on a distant planet called Earth, and made his way back home again. Trouble is, no one believes his tale of the planet he discovered! Your job is to help Linus make his way back to planet Earth so he can take some pictures to convince his friends. Gameplay consists of two parts, an adventure and arcade action. In adventure mode you can explore lands, find objects, and talk to people. Sentences can be constructed by using the pointer to select actions or objects on the screen (This is similar to the interface LucasArts used in games such as Maniac Mansion.) To reach many new locations involves the action mode, where you will need to cross treacherous landscapes and evade dangerous creatures. This portion resembles a side scrolling platform game. Once you've cleared an action sequence, you will not need to do so again if you decide to revisit a location. Whenever you wish you can receive a password allowing you to continue the game later from the same point.","Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","miximages/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","screenshots/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","backcovers/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png","marquees/megadrive/Cosmic Spacehead (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es) (Rev 1).png"
