"megadrive_eswat-city-under-siege","ESWAT : City Under Siege","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-12-01","1990","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","The city is besieged by wanted criminals, and as a police officer it is your duty to stop them. The first criminals in the wanted list can be stopped with your service weapon an some fast reactions, but once you're facing the toughest criminals in town you'll need to use the cyber suit, which provides additional protection and higher firepower.

Unlike other versions of this game, this Genesis cartridge doesn't follow the layout of the arcade game. The levels, rather than being linear, feature some platform elements, and the enemies in the first levels are no longer bank robbers or hit-men, but soldiers and robots instead. And the setting is no longer your typical American city, but a futuristic megalopolis.","Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Cyber Police - ESWAT (Japan) (En).png"
"megadrive_corporation","Corporation","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-09-01","1992","1990s","Core Design","Virgin","Shooter / FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","30","1.5","A first person shooter that requires you to think things through rather than just attack anything that moves.  This game preceded Wolfenstein 3D by a number of years, and while the walls were not ray cast, but solid fill polygons, it was still one of the earliest simulations to tackle a human viewpoint with complete, 360 degree freedom of movement.","Cyber-Cop (USA).7z","7Z","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Cyber-Cop (USA).png"
"megadrive_cyberball","Cyberball","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","Atari","SEGA","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","After American Football players started cheating by using bionic parts, the game was forced to change its rules. By 2022, the game was played not by humans, but two teams of seven robots. To spice things up, the usual pig skin ball was replaced with a 350 pound bomb.

Cyberball brings this fast and furious action to life. Gameplay is essentially the same as the real sport, although the 'downs' are replaced by the bomb's heat gradually increasing towards 'critical'. After this it will explode and possession will be swapped. This is prevented when you cross the 50-yard line, lose possession or score a touchdown, in which cases it resets to 'cool'. Field goals and punts are not featured - the only kick is the initial kick-off you receive.

Control passes from the quarterback (thrower) to the intended catcher as soon as a pass is released. The two-player game is co-operative - on offense one player passes and the other receives","Cyberball (World).7z","7Z","0.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","miximages/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","screenshots/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","backcovers/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png","marquees/megadrive/Cyberball (World).png"
"megadrive_cyborg-justice","Cyborg Justice","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Novotrade","SEGA","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","80","4","In the near future, anarchy reigns supreme and nobody is safe. Cyborgs control the streets and they enforce their rules the only way they know how:  Through CYBORG JUSTICE. Now's your chance to create your very own cyborg and enter it in the ultimate fighting competition. You can mix and match parts for your cyborg to form a fighting machine that matches your fighting style.

