"megadrive_uncharted-waters","Uncharted Waters","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Koei","Koei","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","","","The Franco family used to be one of the influential houses of Portugal. That is until the head of the family sailed out of a disastrous voyage to find the kingdom of Prester John. The disarray that followed brought about an end to the nobility of the Franco name. 100 years have passed and Portugal has prospered through it's sailing and trading empires. Young Leon Fanco wishes to restore his family's good name and make a name for himself as a sailor. At the heart of his ambition is the fair lady, Christiana, who is desired by the likely heir to the kingdom. Towards that end, Leon has been working hard to secure finances for his first ship. With the first step of his dream complete, Franco sails out with his father's good friend as first mate, you're off to find fame, adventure and fortunes out on the sea and in uncharted waters.","Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/Da Hanghai Shidai (Taiwan) (Pirate).png"
"megadrive_new-horizons","New Horizons","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Koei","Koei","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","Set in the early 16th century during the age of exploration, Uncharted Waters: New Horizons allows players to choose from 6 distinct adventurers, each with unique intertwining storylines ranging from seeking Atlantis and clearing family debts to pursuing revenge or serving as a privateer.

As a top-down sailing simulation, the game requires managing ship direction, crew health and weather conditions to navigate the seas, discover new ports and engage in trade or conflict. Upon docking, players access various port services like shipyards, inns and guilds to earn gold through trade, missions or gambling.

