"megadrive_dark-castle","Dark Castle","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-11-01","1991","1990s","Silicon Beach Software","Electronic Arts","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","40","2","The Black Knight has brought misery to the land, and the end way to end this is to enter his haunted house to slay him. You are the brave adventurer taking on this quest through 14 increasingly-tough zones.

The bulk of the game is side-viewed, involving single screens to pass through, which incorporate ropes, cages and trapdoor. There are enemies walking, flying and hovering through this, and many of them respawn. Unusually your weapon to take them on (rocks) can be thrown through 360 degrees, which aims to make the gameplay more realistic and methodical. The screens were linked by hub screens, which the player passes through simply by clicking on a door.","Dark Castle (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.34","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Dark Castle (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_darwin-4081","Darwin 4081","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-04-07","1990","1990s","Data East","SEGA","Shoot'em Up / Vertical","Shooter","1","1","1","60","3","Lakya is a technologically-advanced civilization on a planet far from our own galaxy. The planet's inhabitants have unknowingly unleashed the planet's life force, Evol. As the Evol drifts from Lakya, it reaches a planet called Cokyo, whose inhabitants use it to attack and invade Lakya. Now, fighters from Lakya must fight back against the invading army by using the Evol themselves.

