"megadrive_espn-baseball-tonight","ESPN Baseball Tonight","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Park Place Productions","Sony Imagesoft","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","ESPN Baseball Tonight is a baseball game with both exhibition and playoff modes. Other modes included are both practice (both pitching and batting) and Home Run Derby modes. The game contains 28 real MLB teams but no actual players. Gameplay options include being able to turn errors on or off and to have assisted fielding on or off.

Gameplay has the behind the batter viewpoint, whether pitching or batting. One thing to note when fielding, the player must manually throw the ball back to the pitcher for the game to continue.

The Sega CD version is an update which includes the option for an 162 game season and has over 10 minutes of video highlights.","ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).7z","7Z","0.76","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/ESPN Baseball Tonight (USA).png"
"megadrive_espn-national-hockey-night","ESPN National Hockey Night","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-01","1994","1990s","Park Place Productions","Sony Imagesoft","Sports / Hockey","Sports","1-4","1","4","60","3","ESPN National Hockey Night was one of the many hockey games released back in the day.  This one featured all the NHL teams for its time, but lacked an official players license.

