"megadrive_fastest-1","Fastest 1","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-06-28","1991","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","40","2","Fastest 1 is a Formula One racing game. The game doesn't have an official FIA license, but much like Human's Fire Pro Wrestling series, includes a number of recognizable fictionalized drivers, such as Ayrton Sesna and Satoru Inakajima. The game includes a world championship mode, where the player must start from the lowest rankings and win races to become the F1 world champion. There is also a battle mode where one or two players can race each other or against computer opponents, as well as a test run mode where the player can learn each course and try to set course records. There are a total of 16 different courses, which can be played in either dry, wet, or half-wet conditions, as well as a wide variety of vehicle settings that can be tweaked.","Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0.17","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Fastest 1 (Japan) (En).png"
