"megadrive_checker","Checker","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Devworks Game Technology","Tectoy","Board game","Board / Casual","1","1","1","","","The game Fica 1 consists of 1 board and 32 pieces. It's a single-player game, that aims to leave just one piece on the board. There are several starting positions for the pieces, the most common being one in which all the squares are occupied by pieces, with the exception of the central square. Captures are made by jumping, as long as the next square is free. Each time a piece jumps over another, the latter is removed from the game. You only capture pieces in a straight line, i.e. you don't capture them in curves or diagonally. The game continues with repeated jumps until no more pieces can be captured. To select the piece you want to move or to cancel the selected piece, press any of the buttons: A, B or C. Good luck!
Puzzle game. The game was not sold on physical media, but only released in the memory of some Mega Drive console models sold in Brazil, such as the Sega TecToy Super Mega Drive 3 with 71 games in memory. Later, the game also began to appear on AtGames models released around the world. Game released exclusively on the Mega Drive.","Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).7z","7Z","0.12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","miximages/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","screenshots/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","backcovers/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png","marquees/megadrive/Fica 1 (Brazil) (Mega Drive 4).png"
