"megadrive_from-tv-animation-slam-dunk-kyougou-makkou-taiketsu","From Tv Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu!","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-04-28","1995","1990s","Bandai","Bandai","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Hanamichi Sakuragi is a typical delinquent high school student: sporting a bright red pompadour and consistently rejected by every girl he approaches, he seizes the opportunity to impress a pretty girl named Haruko by joining his school's basketball team.

Initially a bit lost, he gradually becomes an important member of the Shohoku High School team, which fights against all odds to reach the regional championships.

Slam Dunk: Kyogo Makko Taiketsu! (Clash of Champions!) is a 5-on-5 basketball game based on the anime and manga by Takehiko Inoue. Following the story, from the very first exhibition matches, the player can control a single player or the entire Shohoku team in an arcade-style basketball game.

The game uses a side view for the center of the court and zooms in near the basket. There is also an exhibition mode for up to 5 players, where 6 different school teams from the series are available.","From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).7z","7Z","0.79","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/From TV Animation Slam Dunk - Kyougou Makkou Taiketsu! (Japan).png"
"megadrive_fun-n-games","Fun 'n Games","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Leland Interactive Media","Tradewest","Casual Game","Action","1","1","1","40","2","Fun 'N Games presents a mixture of games and ""applications"". The main menu is divided into four sections:

1. Paint: 

A paint program that offers different tools and brushes, a few pre-made backgrounds and objects as well as the option to import figures that were created in the sub-games 'Stylin' Stuff' and 'mix 'n match'.

Games: 

Mouse Maze: A Pac-Man-clone in which the player guides a mouse through a top-down labyrinth. To complete a level, all cheese symbol have to be collected while cats have to be avoided. Collecting a bone temporarily transforms the mouse into a dog that can kill the cats.

Space Lazer: A  shooter seen from the cockpit of a space-ship. The player controls a crosshair and has to shoot increasingly difficult enemies.

Whack a Clown: This game is exclusive to the Genesis Version and plays like 'Whac-a-Mole' only with clowns instead of moles.

Music: 

Songs can be composed by choosing from several instruments and putting notes onto a stave. It is also possible to add sound effects (animal noises and others) or edit provided songs.

Style: 

This section contains two mini-games:

Stylin' Stuff: Here, the player can edit the sprite of a woman by selecting different clothes, hats or haircuts.

mix 'n match: Sprites can be created by putting together different heads, torsi and legs.","Fun 'n Games (Europe).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Fun 'n Games (Europe).png"
