"megadrive_gambler-jiko-chuushinha-katayama-masayuki-no-mahjong-doujou","Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki No Mahjong Doujou","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-12-14","1990","1990s","Game Arts","Game Arts","Mahjong","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Gambler Jiko Chushinha: Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Dojo is a traditional 4-player mahjong game based on the manga by Masayuki Katayama, one of many produced by Game Arts over the years. The game offers both a free play mode and a lighthearted story mode which follows Katayama's characters, a group of students who play mahjong to settle their differences. There is also a ""Mahjong Dojo"" mode which quizzes you on aspects of the game in order to help you learn how to play better.","Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).7z","7Z","0.28","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Gambler Jiko Chuushinha - Katayama Masayuki no Mahjong Doujou (Japan).png"
"megadrive_shove-it-the-warehouse-game","Shove It! ...The Warehouse Game","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-05-01","1990","1990s","Masaya Games","DreamWorks","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","50","2.5","Shove It! The Warehouse Game is a top-down puzzle game based on the original gameplay of Soko-Ban Hiroyuki Imabayashi wrote for Thinking Rabbit. The player controls Stevedore, a warehouse keeper, from a top-down view. Shoving boxes will earn him money to make his dreams come true, a lovely girlfriend and a fiery red sports car.

The game consists of 16 stages with 10 rounds each. At a certain stage, any of the 10 rounds can be selected while playing but a new stage will only be opened up when all rounds have been successfully completed.

To complete a round, Stevedore needs to push all boxes on the marked spots. This is no easy task as the level design will obstruct many moves and cornered boxes can no longer be moved. While playing it is possible to restart the round, undo the last step and the game keeps track of the number of steps taken.

The game supports passwords and includes an edit mode where new levels can be designed and played.","Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","miximages/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","screenshots/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","backcovers/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png","marquees/megadrive/Game no Kanzume Otokuyou (Japan) (Sega Channel).png"
"megadrive_traysia","Traysia","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-04-01","1992","1990s","Renovation Products","Telenet","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","50","2.5","In ""Traysia"", you control a young man named Roy, who lives in the town Johanna. All his life Roy has been dreaming about leaving the town and going to explore faraway lands. Now, finally, his chance has come. His uncle, a travelling merchant, is going on a journey, and Roy decides to leave with him. His girlfriend Traysia gives him a pendant, to remind him of her... will Roy be able to escape from all the dangers that await him on his long journey and to see Traysia again?

The game is a party-based RPG with randomly encountered enemies. The combat is somewhat similar to early  Ultima games. When an enemy appears, you enter a battle screen on which your party is positioned in the lower part, the enemies in the upper part. You can attack if you are close enough to the enemy, otherwise you'll just move towards him. Magic spells should be cast to an appropriate direction to hurt the enemy.","Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/Gang Du Shaonian (China) (Pirate).png"
