"megadrive_gensou-senki-kokou-no-ryuu-crying-dragon","Gensou Senki Kokou no Ryuu - Crying Dragon","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2019-11-20","2019","2010s","SEGA","Unreleased","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","Gensou Senki Kokou no Ryuu: Crying Dragon is an unreleased action RPG originally announced by Sega as part of a line-up of early Sega Mega-CD games given to Famitsu and listed in the 28 June 1991 issue, on page 14. It was cancelled for unknown reasons.

On November 20th, 2019, a very early prototype of the game was acquired by Andlabs and subsequently dumped. As a sign that the prototype is from very early in development, it is a Sega Mega Drive on a standard Sega development cartridge.

