"megadrive_hit-the-ice-the-video-hockey-league","Hit the Ice : The Video Hockey League","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Taito","Taito","Sports / Hockey","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Hit the Ice is a fast-paced, high-impact hockey game based on the 1990 arcade game from Williams. Having more in common with Midway's Arch Rivals than any sane hockey simulation, this arena is no place for penalties, and no place for wimps. While the idea is still to somehow put the puck into the opposing team's goal, each team only has three players, there is a heavy focus on checking, and it is possible to do a ""super shot"" which is strong enough to send the goalie into the net along with the puck.

Available are exhibition and tournament modes for one or two players. Two players can even team up to take on the computer. The TurboGrafx-16 release also adds a four-player mode, while the Gameboy version adds a ""shot race"" mode where the player must get a certain number of goals as quickly as possible.","Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).7z","7Z","0.2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Hit the Ice - VHL - The Official Video Hockey League (USA).png"
"megadrive_last-battle","Last Battle","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-09-01","1990","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","40","2","Last Battle (known in Japan as Fist of the North Star: Legend of the New Era Savior) is a 2D side-scrolling brawler developed and published by Sega for the Sega Genesis on July 1, 1989 (in Japan) and August 14, 1989 (in North America as a launch title).

Set in the war-torn future, players take on the role of wandering Jet-Kwon-Do fighter Aarzak as he fights to reclaim his homeland from the empire of the evil Duke, only to journey to the land of the unknown to rescue one of his traveling companions, Alyssa, from three seemingly-invincible rebel generals (Gromm, Gross, and Garokk).

The original Japanese version of the game is the sequel to the 1986 Sega Master System brawler Fist of the North Star (based on the post-apocalyptic martial arts manga and anime of the same name) and details the events of the second anime series (itself the last half of the manga series). Like its predecessor, the international version of the game was localized to remove both the series's trademark extreme violence and all direct references to the source material (though its post-apocalyptic setting and plot elements remained).","Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Hokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuuseishu Densetsu (Japan).png"
