"megadrive_jack-nicklaus-power-challenge-golf","Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Accolade","Accolade","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","Power Challenge Golf is a golf simulation game, based on Accolade's own Golf &amp; Course Design from the year prior, and featuring both of the courses from that title (Sherwood and English Turn) as well as one additional new course (Baltusrol). The game offers stroke and skins play for up to four players, as well as a driving range and a practice mode. The course editor from the PC version, however, has been removed.","Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.53","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Jack Nicklaus' Power Challenge Golf (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_james-buster-douglas-knockout-boxing","James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-06-01","1991","1990s","Taito","SEGA","Sports / Boxing","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","Final Blow is an action game based around the sport of boxing. You can play the fighters in a sequence of knock-out competitions, (the computer versions also include a round-robin league). Rounds last one minute, with a short break in between them. As in the real sport, your aim is to knock your opponent down for 10 seconds, by gradually weakening him with a series of punches. You can block punches, to avoid them inflicting damage onto you. The ring is of a limited size, so players can be cornered, although the referee will intervene to break the boxers up if they become entangled in a stalemate position.

The genesis version is not to be confused with the Master System game of the same name, which is entirely different.","James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.17","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/James 'Buster' Douglas Knockout Boxing (USA, Europe).png"
