"megadrive_jerry-glanville-s-pigskin-footbrawl","Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","Developer Resources","Midway","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","The NFL meets medieval times as you are the captain of a squad of medieval footbrawl players as you compete in a dangerous game involving swords, maces, nooses and traps.  For the first half you play on an open field with rocks and water puddles to trip you up and an assortment of weapons laying around, as for the second half you play in a dungeon with weapons laying around, but trap doors to make things interesting. Based on the arcade game made by Midway and actually endorsed by then Atlanta's Falcons head coach Jerry Glanville.","Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).7z","7Z","0.3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Jerry Glanville's Pigskin Footbrawl (USA).png"
"megadrive_jesse-the-body-ventura-wrestling-superstars","Jesse ""The Body"" Ventura : Wrestling Superstars","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Human Entertainment","DreamWorks","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","Jesse ""The Body"" Ventura Wrestling Superstars is an unreleased wrestling game set to be published by DreamWorks for the Sega Mega Drive. It was sponsored by professional wrestler Jesse Ventura.

Little is known about the history of Jesse Ventura Wrestling Superstars. DreamWorks announced the game at Winter CES 1991, began advertising it in the Spring of 1991, and also took it to Summer CES 1991, but each time only released a couple of screenshots. The game was developed by Human, authors of the long-running Fire Pro Wrestling series, and much of the game's content was recycled for the 1992 release of Thunder Pro Wrestling Retsuden, a Japanese exclusive.","Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).7z","7Z","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","miximages/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","screenshots/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","backcovers/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png","marquees/megadrive/Jesse 'The Body' Ventura - Wrestling Superstars (USA) (Proto) (1992-03-02).png"
"megadrive_jewel-master","Jewel Master","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-12-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","As the peaceful kingdom Mythgard came close to being overthrown by the evil demon king Jardine the Mad, the Elemental Masters of the realm gathered to do battle. They fought Jardine until there was no more than four remaining. The four combined their powers to form the Elemental Blade with which the demon king could be slain. At this time the Jewel Master was summoned to wield the blade, however the blade has been lost and the rings of the elemental masters have been scattered across Mythgard, all save two. The Jewel Master must gather the other ten rings of the Elemental Masters and reclaim the blade and ultimately do battle with the demon king.

The gameplay is based on fighting a lot of monsters in classic arcade platform kind of way. To do this you have at your disposal rings, two which you begin with and further more that you gain along the way. Each ring is of one of the four elements and by combining them you gain different effects. Rings of opposite elements cancel each other but you have to hands and two attack buttons so you can use say water on the one and fire on the other. The rings are also different in strength which further adds some complexity.","Jewel Master (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Jewel Master (Japan) (En).png"
