"megadrive_strider-ii","Strider II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Tiertex","Capcom","Platform / Fighter Scrolling","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Strider has been called into action to save the people of the planet Magenta, armed with a Gyro laser and matter converter. He must fight his way through a forest, a ruined city, underground colonies, a roof-top battle, and finally the prison ship in which the Megantan leader is held.

The gameplay is similar to the original, consisting of running, jumping and attacking, with a very dynamic central character. The laser gun can be used while standing still; moving attacks with the sword are still possible, with the two weapons combining similarly to the Switchblade games. Tokens can be collected, which will turn you into a robot to face the end-of-level enemies if enough are collected.","Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).7z","7Z","0.51","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Journey from Darkness - Strider Returns (USA).png"
