"megadrive_decapattack","DEcapAttack","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-11-01","1991","1990s","Vic Tokai Corporation","Vic Tokai","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","In this game you play as Chuck D. Head, the product of a mad, but benevolent, scientist.  Chuck looks a lot like a mummy, except he is missing an important part: a head.  Fortunately, he is equipped with a set of eyes and a weird punching appendage in the middle of his chest. 

Chuck's weird features come in handy when, one day, this evil guy named Max D. Cap emerges from the underworld.  Max quickly takes over our world, and only Chuck can stop him.

The gameplay in Decapattack is of the side-scrolling platformer variety.  You play through several colorful worlds, collect useful power up potions, and deliver a beat down to the ugly bosses.","Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Magical Hat no Buttobi Turbo! Daibouken (Japan).png"
"megadrive_magical-taruruuto-kun","Magical Taruruuto-kun","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-04-24","1992","1990s","Game Freak","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Based on a popular manga comedy published in Shonen Jump, Magical Taruruuto-kun is about a boy named Edojou Honmaru who is constantly being bullied at school until he calls the titular hero Taruruuto from another world to help him. It is a cutesy platform game that plays similarly to most other games of its genre. There are many hazards to jump over and end of level boss fights, Taruruuto can hit enemies with his wand or pick up items and throw them.","Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).7z","7Z","0.36","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Magical Taruruuto-kun (Japan).png"
"megadrive_mahjong-cop-ryuu-shiro-ookami-no-yabou","Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1989-12-14","1989","1980s","Whiteboard","SEGA","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","Mahjong Cop Ryuu? Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Ambition of the White Wolf) is a cross between a visual novel and a game of Mahjong featuring a detective named Ryuu, endowed with psychic power.","Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).7z","7Z","0.14","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Mahjong Cop Ryuu - Shiro Ookami no Yabou (Japan).png"
"megadrive_mamono-hunter-youko-dai-7-no-keishou","Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 No Keishou","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-03-22","1991","1990s","Klon","Masaya Games","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","From NCS (the makers of Assault Suit Leynos, Assault Suit Valken, Gynoug, and Shubibinman) comes Mamono Hunter Yoko: Dai 7 no Keisho (or Devil Hunter Yoko: The Seven Bells), one of the only games based on the anime/manga devil slayer of the same name. Devil Hunter Yoko is about Yoko Mano, who was a regular girl making her way through high school--until she learned that she is the 108th successor to a line of warriors charged with defending the earth against demons. 

Every woman born into the Mano family has taken up the role of the legendary Devil Hunters, warriors who battle demons and other forces of darkness who threaten Earth. The realm of the demons (which is parallel to our world) is in cross-dimensional alignment with our own, which could cause a portal to open, allowing the demons to cross over, and launch an all-out attack. The demons are trying to destroy Yoko before she can take her rightful place as the 108th generation Devil Hunter. She must stop the demons before they can perform the ritual that will mean the end of the human race.

Mamono Hunter Yoko: Dai 7 no Keisho is a side scrolling action/platformer game along the lines of Valis. You control Yoko who is equipped with a sword, which you use to slash your enemies. Also if you hold the attack button you can create a shield which will block weak attacks. The shield can also then be thrown to attack enemies. You play through various different worlds, such as a plant type stage, a water stage, a cave stage, a snow stage, etc.","Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).7z","7Z","0.24","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Mamono Hunter Youko - Dai 7 no Keishou (Japan).png"
