"megadrive_menacer-6-game-cartridge","Menacer 6-Game Cartridge","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Western Technologies","Western Technologies","Lightgun Shooter","Shooter","1","1","1","50","2.5","The Menacer 6-Game Cartridge is the bundled title for the Menacer light gun, delivering 6 distinct shooting games.

In Pest Control, players use a spotlight to eliminate bugs swarming a pizza, balancing visibility against insecticide depletion as pests multiply when struck.

Space Station Defender tasks players with destroying aliens spawning, forcing periodic reloads and precise timing.

In the Toejam &amp; Earl universe, Ready, Aim, Tomatoes! challenges players to fend off foes by hurling tomatoes, collecting power-ups, and racking up points.

Whack Ball reimagines Breakout by letting players change the color of an brick wall while special blocks modify gameplay rules.

Front Line challenges players to destroy military vehicles and aircraft using unlimited cannon fire and limited missiles.

In Rockman's Zone, players must target cardboard targets while avoiding civilians. Accuracy can be enhanced by activating the Accu-Sight crosshair or  the Menacer's Binocular Module.","Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.36","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Menacer - 6-Game Cartridge (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_langrisser-2","Langrisser 2","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-26","1994","1990s","Masaya Games","Nippon Computer Systems (NCS)","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","""Langrisser II"" is a sequel to  Warsong (whose original title is Langrisser). The events of the game take place several years after those described in ""Warsong"". Gone is the benevolent kingdom of Baltia, and a new power has risen - the Rayguard Empire, led by Emperor Bernhart and his four generals. Recently, Bernhart ordered his army to attack the neighboring countries, obviously searching for something. This ""something"" might be none else but a legendary evil sword, that makes the one who wields undefeated. It is up to the noble knight Elwin and his friends to stop the Emperor!

""Langrisser II"" is a strategy RPG. The army is divided into soldier units and generals, who fight alone and who are usually stronger than a whole unit. Before the scenario begins, you must hire soldiers, buy weapons and items, etc. During the battle, if you come into contact with an enemy unit, an automatic battle sequence occurs. You can also cast healing spells on your units or offensive spells to hurt the enemy.

