"megadrive_mr-nutz-hoppin-mad","Mr. Nutz Hoppin' Mad","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","NEON Software","Ocean","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Mr. Nutz 2 is a Sega Genesis port of Mr. Nutz Hoppin' Mad for the Amiga. It was developed by Neon and was to be released in 1995 by Ocean but the Genesis market began to die around that time and so Ocean decided not to release it. Someone related to Neon released the source code of this port during the late 2000s and some pictures of the ROM as well (which couldn't be released due to copyright problems). Compiling the source code into a ROM was hard at first but it was eventually done, and the compiled ROM was released in the Sonic Retro forum.
This ROM (which is the one played in the video) is apparently a near final beta because there are no Neon or Ocean logos at the beggining and the title of the ROM is ""Mr. Nutz Hoppin' Mad"" like in the original Amiga version instead of ""Mr. Nutz 2"" like in the screenshots that were released before. Other than that, the game looks complete and is playable.","Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).7z","7Z","0.67","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","miximages/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","screenshots/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","backcovers/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png","marquees/megadrive/Mr. Nutz - Hoppin' Mad (Europe) (Proto).png"
"megadrive_ms-pac-man","Ms. Pac-Man","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Innerprise Software","Time Warner Interactive","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-2","1","2","80","4","In 1982, a sequel to the  incredibly popular Pac-Man was introduced in the form of his girlfriend, Ms. Pac-Man.  This sequel continued on the ""eat the dots/avoid the ghosts"" gameplay of the original game, but added new features to keep the title fresh.

Like her boyfriend, Ms. Pac-Man attempts to clear four various and challenging mazes filled with dots and ever-moving bouncing fruit  while avoiding Inky, Blinky, Pinky and Sue, each with their own personalities and tactics.  One touch from any of these ghosts means a loss of life for Ms. Pac-Man.

Ms. Pac-Man can turn the tables on her pursuers by eating one of the four Energizers located within the maze. During this time, the ghosts turn blue, and Ms. Pac-Man can eat them for bonus points (ranging from 200, 400, 800 and 1600, progressively). The Energizer power only lasts for a limited amount of time, as the ghost's eyes float back to their center box, and regenerate to chase after Ms. Pac-Man again.

Survive a few rounds of gameplay, and the player will be treated to humorous intermissions showing the growing romantic relationship between Pac-Man and Ms. Pac-Man, leading all the way up to the arrival of ""Junior"".","Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.07","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Ms. Pac-Man (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_valis","Valis","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","Riot","Renovation Products","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","Yuko Asou is an ordinary Japanese teenager with an ordinary life - until one day she is attacked by a monster on the street. Out of nowhere, a sword appears in her hands. She fights the monsters who have suddenly invaded the city, and is summoned to the parallel world known as Vecanti, which is ruled by a cruel tyrant named Rogles, whose actions disrupt the balance of the the worlds. Wielding the legendary Valis sword, Yuko must defeat Rogles and restore the balance.

Valis has the same story and basic genre (platform action) as the  original first game in the  series; however, it is a different game with different locations, regular enemies and bosses, new cut scenes, etc.  Defeating the numerous enemies populating the game world requires precise usage of jumping and ducking abilities, and attack timing. Yuko can jump very high and attack while jumping. Various power-ups are scattered through the game, many of which enhance the performance of Yuko's sword. Acting as a melee weapon in the beginning, it can be customized with power-ups and turn into a medium-range weapon, firing shots at the enemies - with proper power-ups, also in different directions. Boss enemies typically have different attack patterns and require different strategies to defeat them.","Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Mugen Senshi Valis (Japan).png"
