"megadrive_ferrari-grand-prix-challenge","Ferrari Grand Prix Challenge","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-09-01","1992","1990s","Aisystem Tokyo","Flying Edge","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","60","3","Ferrari Grand Prix Challenge puts you behind the wheel in a first-person racing sim spanning a full F1 season with qualifying and races across 20 tracks, including all 16 from 1992. In Grand Prix mode, you're limited to one of the four weakest teams, with weather randomized. In Time Attack, you can race as top teams like McLaren or Williams, customize weather, and go for lap records. Car setup can be adjusted before races, and the blend of cockpit view and strategic tuning delivers an immersive racing experience.","Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu - F-1 Hero MD (Japan).png"
"megadrive_nakajima-satoru-kanshuu-f1-grand-prix","Nakajima Satoru Kanshuu F1 Grand Prix","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-12-20","1991","1990s","Varie","Varie","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","60","3","Satoru Nakajima, the first Japanese driver to race full-time in Formula 1, licensed this racing game which combines arcade and simulation elements. The full 1991 season is recreated, with the chance to do individual races or a full season. Before the race you can modify several areas of the car set-up, including engine performance (configurations with higher top speed have slower acceleration), wing downforce (higher top speed means lower grip), tyres (better grip means lower durability) and so on.

