"megadrive_nba-showdown-94","NBA Showdown '94","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-03-29","1994","1990s","Electronic Arts","Electronic Arts","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","The game could be played in various ways: players could play against each other, or against the computer. Games against the computer were divided into two levels, ""exhibition"" or ""playoffs"". Players could pick from any of the NBA teams for the first time, including non-playoff teams. Games could be configured for 2, 5, 8 or 12 minute quarters.","NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.68","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/NBA Showdown '94 (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_ncaa-final-four-basketball","NCAA Final Four Basketball","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Bitmasters","Mindscape","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-4","1","4","50","2.5","NCAA Final Four Basketball is a standard basketball-sim with a full NCAA license with 64 of the top Division 1-A teams including North Carolina, Florida State, Boston College, and Maryland to name a few.

There are three modes of play to choose from: two Practice modes, one which shows the player the basic in's and outs of the game and another for free throw shooting, Exhibition and Tournament.  Along with these modes are the ability to change around options to play a game to the player's liking including changing the length of the game. A battery-backup lets the player save their games, stats and rosters.","NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).7z","7Z","0.36","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/NCAA Final Four Basketball (USA).png"
"megadrive_ncaa-football","NCAA Football","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","The Software Toolworks","Mindscape","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","NCAA Football lets you play as one of sixteen college football teams in either an exhibition game or in tournament play. The tournament pits you against all the other teams which you must win in order to proceed; the game will automatically save after each game won so you can pick up the tournament where you left off. Team rosters are unique in that you can choose players from different decades from the 60's up to the 90's, and you can mix players from different decades if you want.","NCAA Football (USA).7z","7Z","0.39","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/NCAA Football (USA).png"
"megadrive_high-school-soccer-kunio-kun","High School Soccer - Kunio Kun","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-08-07","1992","1990s","Technos Japan","PALSOFT","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Nekketsu FC is referred to as a weak team, but now we were finally supposed to play the national tournament. To celebrate the national competition, the team went to eat sushi. However, a series of unfortunate incidents began to happen. Wow, who would have thought the whole team would come down with food poisoning from eating sushi!?

At this rate it looked like we would have to give up our dream of entering the nationals, but just then our coach Misako had a bright idea!

