"megadrive_pebble-beach-golf-links","Pebble Beach Golf Links","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-01","1994","1990s","T&amp;E Soft","SEGA","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Pebble Beach Golf Links is a golf simulator that recreates all eighteen holes of the famous course of the same name. One of the most well regarded golf courses in America is now open for play in the comfort of your own home on your Sega Mega Drive.","New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Pebble Beach no Hatou (Japan).png"
"megadrive_new-3d-golf-simulation-waialae-no-kiseki","New 3d Golf Simulation - Waialae No Kiseki","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-25","1994","1990s","T&amp;E Soft","T&amp;E Soft","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","The mechanics are simple to understand with options to select your club, stance, direction, and a circular meter for selecting the power of your shot. Like with many golf games, this will require good timing. Once the power level is selected, a ball with a dot tracing along its surface is shown and a button push selects where the ball will be hit. There are some customizations for your character including the ability to select a caddie and name your player. Your name, as well as records and progress, can be saved via battery backup.","New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).7z","7Z","0.6","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/New 3D Golf Simulation - Waialae no Kiseki (Japan).png"
"megadrive_new-horizons","New Horizons","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Koei","Koei","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","Set in the early 16th century during the age of exploration, Uncharted Waters: New Horizons allows players to choose from 6 distinct adventurers, each with unique intertwining storylines ranging from seeking Atlantis and clearing family debts to pursuing revenge or serving as a privateer.

As a top-down sailing simulation, the game requires managing ship direction, crew health and weather conditions to navigate the seas, discover new ports and engage in trade or conflict. Upon docking, players access various port services like shipyards, inns and guilds to earn gold through trade, missions or gambling.

Naval combat shifts to a turn-based strategy where players position ships for cannon fire or boarding and if opposing flagships clash, the captains face off in a side-view duel using specific fighting maneuvers.","New Horizons (USA).7z","7Z","0.85","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/New Horizons (USA).png"
"megadrive_newman-haas-indycar-featuring-nigel-mansell","Newman-Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-02","1994","1990s","Gremlin Interactive","Acclaim Entertainment","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","40","2","Newman Haas Indy Car is a racing game endorsed by the CART racing team of the same name and their top driver at the time: Nigel Mansell.

The player has the option to drive a single race (where the option to practice is hidden) or go for the crown against 12 other drivers in 15 tracks (with some variety, not only ovals) across North America, with the season opener in Queensland, Australia.

It is possible play solo, with a friend in split screen or with split screen against the computer, and if music or engine sounds are played in the race.

A key choice in the game is selecting between Arcade and Simulation mode - in the later, the car can take a lot less damage before giving up, fine-tuning must be done by the driver and rules are enforced, under the risk of a disqualification.

Graphically, the game is less sterile than most driving games of the platform thanks to the inclusion of several polygonal buildings scattered around the circuits.","Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).7z","7Z","0.59","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","miximages/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","screenshots/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","backcovers/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png","marquees/megadrive/Newman Haas IndyCar Featuring Nigel Mansell (World).png"
"megadrive_newzealand-story-the","Newzealand Story, The","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-03-03","1990","1990s","Taito","Taito","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","One day, a kiwi tribe was having fun and games outside the zoo, only to be kidnapped by the evil-minded Leopard Seal, who plans to sell them at the black market. Fortunately, during the kidnapping process, Tiki, leader of the tribe, managed to escape the sack, and her job is to rescue Phee-Phee and the other kiwis scattered around New Zealand, and are held in cages in various locations that include Auckland, Rotorua, Waitomo Caves, Strait Cook, and Mt. Cook. 

If Tiki doesn't rescue a kiwi in a limited amount of time, the devil will appear and try to kill her. When Tiki reaches the outskirts of each city, except Strait Cook, there is a boss waiting to meet Tiki, and kill her by using their own choice of weapons. Also making the rescue mission difficult are several nasties that attempt to throw their own weapons, like bombs and arrows, at her. To defeat these enemies, Tiki shoots at them using her crossbow and arrows. More often than not, when Tiki shoots at enemies, they will leave behind pieces of fruit that she can pick up for points. However, it is likely that Tiki may get other weapons or the letters E, X, T, E, N, and D. Collecting all these letters will result in an extra life, and as for the weapons, they include laser shots, bombs, and fireballs. 

In some levels, a few areas are located further up than just left or right, and the only way that Tiki can go up is by snatching something off the enemy that gives her the ability to fly up. Other areas are underwater, and when Tiki goes underwater, her oxygen  meter decreases, so she has to rise up to the surface again to restore her oxygen levels. Apart from her own weapons, Tiki is able to squirt water at enemies if she gets to the top of the water.","NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0.19","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/NewZealand Story, The (Japan) (En).png"
