"megadrive_ninja-gaiden","Ninja Gaiden","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-12-12","1992","1990s","Tecmo","SEGA","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","40","2","Sega developed a third, unreleased title for the Mega Drive through the obscure studio Opus, evidenced by the game's sound engine and visual assets. This project was likely abandoned due to significant quality problems, though a beta version eventually leaked and is now playable via emulation.

Rather than faithfully adapting the original arcade experience, the game resembles a poorly executed beat-'em-up similar to Streets of Rage. It includes numerous cutscenes plagued by broken English, while chapter titles remain in Japanese, contributing to a disjointed and nonsensical narrative where the protagonist unexpectedly meets familiar characters and learns mid-game that the true objective was to rescue Ryu's girlfriend.","Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).7z","7Z","0.34","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","miximages/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png","marquees/megadrive/Ninja Gaiden (Japan) (En) (Proto).png"
"megadrive_no-escape","No Escape","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Bit","Bits Studios","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","30","1.5","Based on the 1994 movie of the same name starring Ray Liotta, the player takes control of Liotta's character, Capt. J.T. Robbins, whose only objective of the game is to escape an island. After shooting his commanding officer, Robbins is imprisoned and eventually sent to the island Absolom as a war criminal, from where there is no escape possible. To do this still, the player must explore the island with side-scrolling platform gameplay for clues, finding items and combining them to make weapons and traps.  

