"megadrive_nobunaga-no-yabou-bushou-fuuunroku","Nobunaga No Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-12-20","1991","1990s","Koei","Koei","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-8","1","8","","","Nobunaga no Yabou: Bushou Fuuunroku (ä¿¡é•·ã®é‡Žæœ› æ­¦å°†é¢¨é›²éŒ²) is a simulation game by Koei as part of a series of games based on the life of Nobunaga which itself is part of their Historical Simulation Series. It was first released in 1990 on the NEC PC-88 and then was ported to several other platforms released in Japan, including a port to the Sega Mega Drive in 1991 which was not released outside Japan.","Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).7z","7Z","0.33","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Bushou Fuuunroku (Japan).png"
"megadrive_nobunaga-no-yabou-haouden","Nobunaga No Yabou - Haouden","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-25","1994","1990s","Koei","Koei","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-8","1","8","","","Nobunaga no Yabou: Haouden (Nobunaga's Ambition: Tale of the Conquerer) is a strategy-sim from Koei and the fifth in their flagship Nobunaga's Ambition series of Sengoku-era feudal sims. Once again, the player assumes one of a number of daimyos, including Oda Nobunaga himself and tries to take over the rest of Japan.

Among the tweaks to the gameplay was the addition of castles, which are now the locations that players must conquer in order to take over new territory. Haouden was also the first game in the series to be given an expansion pack though this pack would not be available to all versions of the game.

The game was the first flagship Nobunaga's Ambition game to never receive a US localization. It sits between the fourth game, Nobunaga's Ambition: Lord of Darkness (Nobunaga no Yabou: Bushou Fuuunroku) from 1990 and the sixth game, Nobunaga no Yabou: Tenshouki from 1994.","Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).7z","7Z","0.84","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Haouden (Japan).png"
"megadrive_nobunaga-s-ambition","Nobunaga's Ambition","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Koei","Koei","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-8","1","8","90","4.5","In the 16th century, Japan's Sengoku period divided the nation into numerous feudal states, each ruled by a daimyo. Many dreamt of conquering the land, becoming the Shogun and ruling the entire country. One of those daimyos was the ambitious Nobunaga Oda, a merciless ruler and a renowned strategist. Players take on the role of Nobunaga Oda or one of many other daimyos to try to conquer Japan.

Nobunaga's Ambition is a turn-based strategy game which can be played in different modes.  Players begin by selecting either a 17 regions scenario or a larger 50 scenario. Then, the player must select a daimyo, each of which is rated attributes in several categories; Age, Health, Ambition, Luck, Charm and IQ. As the game progresses, these values change depending on events in the game. The age value represents a time limit of sorts, as an elderly daimyo becomes increasingly likely to die of old age or sickness.","Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Nobunaga no Yabou - Zenkoku Ban (Japan).png"
