"megadrive_outback-joey","Outback Joey","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-24","1993","1990s","Western Technologies","HeartBeat","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Joey, a kangaroo, lives with his family in northern Australia. Their peaceful life is interrupted by the invasion of a group of poachers who take away several of his family members, so Joey sets out on a journey to bring them back.

Outback Joey is the only game released for the HeartBeat Personal Trainer, a Sega Genesis-based fitness system. Using a pulse sensor and game control pads mounted to an exercise bike, stairclimer, treadmill or ski machine, players have to exercise while playing an otherwise traditional 2D platformer. The player's heartbeat is directly tied to the player character's in-game speed, with a healthy heartbeat allowing him to move faster and a resting heartbeat slowing him down to a slog. Players can create a profile with their name, age, and gender, and their health data is tracked persistently over time to let them track their progress.","Outback Joey (USA).7z","7Z","0.55","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Outback Joey (USA).png"
"megadrive_outlander","Outlander","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Mindscape","Mindscape","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","80","4","Mindscape developed this game hoping to secure an official Mad Max license but Warner Bros. never followed through. Regardless, the game is very similar to Mad Max 2: The Road Warrior. Your goal is to traverse the Wasteland in your car, trying to survive biker gang attacks and avoid running out of gas.

The gameplay is divided into 2 genres: Racing and side-scrolling. During the racing sections, you must eliminate enemies such as bikers, gyroplane pilots, red trucks and more.

Your car is equipped with a machine gun on the front and if an opponent gets too close, a window appears, allowing you to take them down with your shotgun.

The road is dotted with several towns and each time you pass through one, an alarm sounds. When your gas level drops, you must stop in these towns to refuel and replenish your ammunition.

