"megadrive_outworld-2375-a-d","Outworld 2375 A.D.","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Western Technologies","HeartBeat","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","Outworld 2375 A.D. is a racing game that was in development for the Sega Mega Drive in 1993. The game was designed to be used with the Heartbeat Catalyst device, a body-worn fitness sensor that connected to the console. This device monitored the player's heart rate and responded based on whether the heart rate was within a target threshold. The game was never completed or officially released, but there appears to have been a limited production run, and some copies are in collectors' hands. Recently, the Video Game History Foundation acquired a copy of the game.","Outworld 2375 A.D. (USA) (HeartBeat Catalyst).7z","7Z","0.46","false","true","true","true","false","false","true","false","","miximages/megadrive/Outworld 2375 A.D. (USA) (HeartBeat Catalyst).png","screenshots/megadrive/Outworld 2375 A.D. (USA) (HeartBeat Catalyst).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Outworld 2375 A.D. (USA) (HeartBeat Catalyst).png","","","marquees/megadrive/Outworld 2375 A.D. (USA) (HeartBeat Catalyst).png"
"megadrive_arnold-palmer-tournament-golf","Arnold Palmer Tournament Golf","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","Select your level of play, and then head for the pro shop to choose between Black Carbon, Glass Fiber, and Ceramic Clubs.

Tee off by yourself or play 18 holes with a friend. Besides the One and Two Player modes there's also a practice mode, match play (head to head), and a full-blown international tournament, where you'll stroke it out against 15 competitors.

Tournament play lasts 12 rounds, 18 holes of golf each. Most rounds are standard ""stroke"" play but the seventh and eighth rounds are ""match"" games. Things really get serious when match game ends in a tie, and players move into a sudden death play-off.

During the tournament players earn higher skill levels, more knowledgeable caddies, and more power. You'll earn a password at the end of each round of the tournament.

The game let's you play on three different courses; Japan, the United States, and Great Britain.","Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Ozaki Naomichi no Super Masters (Japan).png"
"megadrive_p-t-o-pacific-theater-of-operations","P.T.O. : Pacific Theater of Operations","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Koei","Koei","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-2","1","2","80","4","P.T.O is another military sim from KOEI.  In this game you can choose to be either Japan or the Allies.  By managing your fleets and ordering new warships you can control many different sides of the conflict.  (ship development, Base defense, Fleet arrangement, Direct battle control, Economic decisions)  There are many different options of play in PTO, you can choose to play from one of many different famous battles or you can play the campaign.  You can control one side or both.  There are also limited controls on victory conditions.","P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).7z","7Z","0.43","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/P.T.O. - Pacific Theater of Operations (USA).png"
