"megadrive_pepenga-pengo","Pepenga Pengo","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-22","1995","1990s","JSH","SEGA","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","The Sno-Bees are back! One day in Antarctica, an asteroid crashes into the crystal that protects the penguins, shattering it into many pieces and freeing the Sno-Bees who had been frozen in ice. In order to rescue his people, the blue penguin (along with a pink penguin in two-player mode) goes after the Sno-Bees and to recover the missing pieces of the crystal. The game takes the basic template of the 1982 original and expands on it, offering a greater variety of enemies, various environmental hazards, and power-ups, along with of course updated 16-bit graphics and sound. The goal is still to push blocks and crush enemies. Enemies now appear from generators, which must be destroyed to stop new enemies from appearing, and all enemies must then be eliminated to complete each stage.

In addition to the main story mode, the game also features a competitive battle mode for up to four players, as well as a conversion of the original arcade game.","Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0.27","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Pepenga Pengo (Japan) (En).png"
"megadrive_pete-sampras-tennis","Pete Sampras Tennis","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-06","1994","1990s","Codemasters","Codemasters","Sports / Tennis","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Play singles and doubles exhibition games, knockout tournaments or go on a world tour. Choose from 30 different players including world seed #1, Pete Sampras.

The actions is viewed from the traditional third-person viewpoint. A tutorial mode is provided to help you get used to the forehand, lob and drop shots on offer. Several venues from all over the world can be played on, on Hard, Grass and Clay courts.

This was the first and one of the very few Genesis / Mega Drive games to be released with a J-Cart, which meant that four-way gameplay was possible without the need for special adapters. The J cartridge had two built-in joypad connectors. The Game Gear version was equally inventive, allowing two players to share one Game Gear, or four players to play doubles by linking two handhelds.","Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","miximages/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","screenshots/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","backcovers/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png","marquees/megadrive/Pete Sampras Tennis (Europe) (Rev 2) (MDSTEE13).png"
