"megadrive_pga-tour-golf-ii","PGA Tour Golf II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Polygames","Electronic Arts","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","The sequel to PGA Tour, this game was released solely for the Sega Genesis / Mega Drive along with an alternative version for the Game Gear, as was getting more common for EA sports titles at the time, helping to drive the sales of the 2nd choice console.

This update sees the series add ten professional players to the roster (60 in total) and have the ability to play against them on seven courses and across five tournaments. There is also a new graphics engine in place and new sounds to boot. Statistics became more detailed and the ball physics were improved through a Draw and Fade meter. Game data can be backed up through the built-in battery. Other features include different ball lies, dynamic wind conditions, digitized sounds, an improved automatic caddy and special shots such as chips, punches and fringe putts.","PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/PGA Tour Golf II (Japan).png"
