"megadrive_phantasy-star-fukkokuban","Phantasy Star Fukkokuban","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","In 1994, Sega released a version for the Sega Mega Drive, Phantasy Star Fukkokuban. This version is merely the Master System version on a Mega Drive cartridge PCB with the appropriate connector pin to signal Master System mode changed accordingly (which is how passthrough devices like the Power Base Converter work). The situation behind this release is unknown; the most prominent rumor is that it was a contest giveaway.","Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).7z","7Z","0.28","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Phantasy Star Fukkokuban (Japan).png"
"megadrive_phantasy-star-ii","Phantasy Star II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","The people on a technically advanced planet Mota make experiments to create biomechanical creatures. But one day, a creature was created that appeared to be dangerous to the humans themselves. No signal came to the capital city from the experimental labs... You, a nameless young man living in Paleo, Mota's capital, are commanded to go to the labs and check the issue. Your friend Nei, a semi-human girl, goes with you, and other brave adventurers join you on what starts with a simple mission but develops into saving the entire world...

