"megadrive_pocket-monsters","Pocket Monsters","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Gametec","X BOY","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Like the Famicom pirate, the player controls Pikachu through numerous sidescrolling levels. There are 5 levels in total, with a boss at the end of each, as well a mini-boss in the first level of the Mega Drive version. Pikachu can jump on enemies and use a special move which clears all of the enemies on the screen, although the latter can only be done when the charge meter is full (indicated by a power bar at the top of the screen of the SNES version, or a numeric counter in the Mega Drive version, which is full when it hits 20.) The player can start either 3 and 5 lives and continues each, and there's a difficulty setting in the options menu.","Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).7z","7Z","0.7","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","miximages/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","screenshots/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","backcovers/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","marquees/megadrive/Pikachu - Pocket Monster (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png"
