"megadrive_prince-of-persia-2-the-shadow-and-the-flame","Prince of Persia 2 : The Shadow and the Flame","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-20","1995","1990s","Brøderbund Software","Brøderbund Software","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Prince of Persia 2: The Shadow and the Flame is the sequel to the 1989 hit Prince of Persia. Released for DOS computers in 1993, ports were made to the Apple Macintosh in 1994 and the Super Nintendo in 1995.

A port to the Sega Mega Drive was planned for a 1996 release, but ultimately cancelled. Development of this port was handled by Microïds, and the game was to be published by Psygnosis. A prototype was dumped and released on 11 August 2006 by drx of Hidden-Palace.org, which dates back to 20 February 1995.

Though more graphically accurate to the DOS original than the SNES port, it has poorer sound quality and various bugs. There is also less time to complete the game (75 minutes) and the HUD uses different colours.","Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).7z","7Z","1.1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","miximages/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","screenshots/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","backcovers/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png","marquees/megadrive/Prince of Persia 2 (Europe) (Proto) (1995-02-20).png"
"megadrive_pro-moves-soccer","Pro Moves Soccer","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","ASCII","ASCII","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","If anyone is wondering what the AWS in this title means, it is an acronym for Asciiware World Sports. Now with that out of the way, this is a soccer game with training, exhibition, and tournament modes.

Training lets the players team practice without an opposing team on the field. Exhibition is the basic one team versus another for one game. The tournament mode is divided into two different modes; 8 Nations and World Cup. 8 Nations is just a shorter version of the World Cup tournament mode because it involves only 8 teams instead of all 32 of them like it does in the World Cup mode.

The player can choose to play as one of these 32 International teams or can choose to create their own team that has its own shirt, stripe, and shorts colors.

The game has options that allow the player to choose to have light or heavy wind, a dry, soggy, or snowy field, and to have fouls turned on or off.","Pro Moves Soccer (USA).7z","7Z","0.28","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Pro Moves Soccer (USA).png"
"megadrive_pro-quarterback","Pro Quarterback","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Leland Interactive Media","Tradewest","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Pro Quarterback is a football game featuring 27 different teams. Since this game doesn't have an NFL or NFLPA license, there aren't any real NFL teams or players here, although the teams included in the game represent the cities of their real life NFL counterparts and also mimic the colors of their team's uniforms.

The games options allow the player to choose to play on 6 different field surfaces (grass, mud, dirt, snow, rain and artificial turf) and to choose how long the game will last (2, 5, 10 or 15 minute quarters). There are also no penalties in this game whatsoever. 

