"megadrive_richard-scarry-s-busytown","Richard Scarry's Busytown","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Novotrade","SEGA","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","80","4","This early version distinguishes itself from the PC release by offering 6 unique stages, each with distinct gameplay mechanics.

- In Bruno's Deli, players control Huckle the Cat to assist Bruno by grabbing requested items from a conveyor belt.

- Captain Salty stage tasks Huckle with operating a crane to assemble a ship by dropping pieces into marked spots.

- The Building House stage follows a similar crane-based format but focuses on constructing a house instead.

- Delivery Truck: Players guide Huckle and Lowly Worm to deliver goods to various shops while dodging obstacles like trash cans, crossing chickens, and furniture.

- The Fire Station stage shifts control to a pig firefighter driving a truck through BusyTown to collect equipment. After each pickup, the player must extinguish a house fire and rescue trapped animals.

- The Wind: Players view a top-down map of BusyTown and manipulate objects with a whirlwind to trigger animations.","Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).7z","7Z","1.29","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Richard Scarry's Busytown (USA).png"
