"megadrive_riddle-wired-quiz-dokusen-kigy-no-hkai","Riddle Wired - Quiz Dokusen Kigy No Hkai","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-08-28","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Quiz / Japanese","Board / Casual","1-2","1","2","","","A terrorist group has taken control of an armed satellite and is attacking all the nations of the Earth. Your mission: infiltrate and recapture the satellite...by answering trivia questions. Riddle Wired is a Japanese-style quiz game, and despite the scenario, the entirety of the game consists of answering general knowledge questions. The player will face a series of different opponents during the mission, and each one will ask the player a series of questions in a so-called ""Quiz Battle"". If the player answers correctly, the enemy will lose HP; if not, then the player will lose HP. If the enemy's HP is drained, the player moves on to the next stage, but if all HP is lost then the game is over. One or two players can play simultaneously.","Riddle Wired (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).7z","7Z","0.11","false","true","true","true","false","false","true","false","","miximages/megadrive/Riddle Wired (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Riddle Wired (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Riddle Wired (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","","","marquees/megadrive/Riddle Wired (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png"
"megadrive_rings-of-power","Rings of Power","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-02-01","1992","1990s","Naughty Dog","Electronic Arts","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","For ages, humanity lived in spiritual darkness until the holy Nexus arrived with his Rod of Creation, blessing the world with 6 magical Arts and establishing an era of prosperity under the Red Priests.

This golden age ended when the demon Void stole the Rod, triggering a cosmic battle that shattered the artifact into 11 Rings of Power and plunged the world back into chaos. Now, a young sorcerer named Buc, must journey to recover these rings, reforge the Rod and finally defeat Void.

Rings of Power distinguishes itself from traditional console RPGs by offering a free-roaming, isometric world reminiscent of the Ultima series, where players can ignore side plots to focus on the main quest.

The game features a dynamic day-night cycle affecting NPC behavior and unique turn-based combat driven entirely by magic spells as there are no weapons or armor. Along the way, Buc can recruit members from various magical guilds to join his party.","Rings of Power (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.53","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Rings of Power (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_rise-of-the-robots","Rise of the Robots","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-01","1995","1990s","Data Design","Acclaim Entertainment","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Rise of the Robots is a 2.5D fighting game. You play as the cyborg Eco35-2, half-man half-robot, created by the Electrocorp company, in order to counter the mutiny that is brewing in their Metropolis 4 factory, following the reprogramming of certain robots by injecting them with the EGO virus, making them aware of their situation and therefore aggressive. You will have to fight them one by one in duel battles to stop this rebellion.
The title was intended to be graphically revolutionary. But although the fighting robots are quite nice (with 3D sprites transcribed in a 2D universe), the scenery is only in dull static 2D. Also, the in-game animation is slow, even quite ""heavy"", directly impacting the handling. 
The slowness of your robot and the varying power of the enemies (to the point that some robots are ultra powerful and atomize you in two shots) quickly make the fights unbalanced.","Rise of the Robots (Europe).7z","7Z","1.53","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Rise of the Robots (Europe).png"
"megadrive_risk","Risk","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Parker Brothers","Parker Brothers","Board game","Board / Casual","1-6","1","6","80","4","Players attempt to capture territories from other players by rolling higher die numbers. The game is won when one player has managed to occupy every territory.","Risk (USA).7z","7Z","0.28","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Risk (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Risk (USA).png"
"megadrive_risky-woods","Risky Woods","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-12-14","1992","1990s","Dinamic Software","Electronic Arts","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Unusually for Electronic Arts in the early 90s, this was a platform -shooter game with little or no adventuring or strategy elements. The game scrolls sideways, and has sections where precision jumps are required, either to clear rivers or collect bonuses. You carry a dagger to deal with the enemies, and must avoid contact with them. When killed, they leave coins to be collected - these are spent in the shop sections. Death loses you most of your coins, but they can usually be retrieved if they land on solid ground - making it better to be killed in combat than by drowning.","Risky Woods (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.39","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Risky Woods (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_ristar","Ristar","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-17","1995","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","90","4.5","An evil tyrant with a silly name (Greedy) has arisen to control a solar system full of sentient beings. He Corrupts the leaders of each world and thereby enslaves the populace. He has sent his minions in the disguise of planet natives into the worlds to enforce his rule...

A lush forest planet, the last planet in the tyrants agenda manages to send a call of help to the solar systems ancient hero before being over run. However Greedy even has managed to remove the great hero. Yet he did not count on the interference of the hero's sun... Ristar!

You control Ristar in his attempt to liberate the solar system. You will stretch his arms to grab enemies and summarily head-but them. Your long limbs will be used to climb various surfaces. Being a star adds even more to the unique gameplay, already chock-full of action and puzzles.","Ristar (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","1.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Ristar (USA, Europe).png"
