"megadrive_robocop-3","RoboCop 3","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Eden Entertainment Software","Flying Edge","Platform / Shooter Scrolling","Shooter","1","1","1","40","2","RoboCop 3 is a side-scrolling platform shooter. You get missions (such as rescuing your colleagues who are being kept hostages), which are divided into several smaller levels. The levels usually consist of several platforms, and are heavily populated by enemies who shoot at you. You can gather special repair kits, which will be used to restore your health after you've completed a level. ""RoboCop 3"" is more of a shooter than its predecessors, having more and tougher enemies.","RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.26","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/RoboCop 3 (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_robocop-versus-the-terminator","RoboCop versus The Terminator","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Virgin","Virgin","Shooter / Run and Gun","Shooter","1","1","1","80","4","The Genesis game RoboCop versus The Terminator, inspired by a Dark Horse comic, is a platformer with heavy shooting elements that spans ten levels across present-day Detroit and a post-apocalyptic future.

Players control RoboCop, who is tricked by future Terminators into uploading his consciousness to create Skynet before being reactivated years later to help the human resistance destroy it.

The game features 8 weapons with unlimited ammo, though only 2 can be carried at once and death results in losing the current firearm.

Enemies range from street criminals in the present to advanced machines like Terminators and robotic beasts in the future, with each level concluding in a boss battle against foes such as ED-209 and Cain. Optional objectives, including hostage rescue and camera destruction, add extra challenges throughout the mission.","RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/RoboCop Versus The Terminator (China) (En) (Pirate).png"
