"megadrive_shadow-dancer-the-secret-of-shinobi","Shadow Dancer : The Secret of Shinobi","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-05-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","90","4.5","A.D. 1997, New York City

After defeating the Neo Zeed crime empire, the ninja master Shinobi disappeared until a new, instinct-driven reptilian monster emerged. This colossal creature attacked relentlessly, taking hostages and causing mass panic across the streets.

It remained only for Shinobi to take action. His weapons were stealth and quickness of attack, his only allies facing overwhelming forces. Relying on Ninja weapons and magic, Shinobi fought on, assisted by his faithful dog.

Shadow Dancer: The Secret of Shinobi on the Sega Genesis features 5 missions with 3 stages each, distinct from its home computer counterpart. Instead of disarming bombs, players rescue hostages and face a boss at the end of each mission. Defeating the first 4 bosses unlocks a bonus stage where you shoot incoming flying ninjas.

Some of the enemies are also quite different. Some of the lizards, which appear in later missions, leave a lizard coin which you can collect for bonus lives.","Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/Shadow Dancer (China) (En) (Pirate).png"
