"megadrive_shining-force-ii","Shining Force II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Camelot Software Planning","SEGA","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Shining Force II blends strategy and RPG elements with cartoon-style graphics, alternating between exploration and tactical battles. Players explore new lands and interact with NPCs to advance the story, while combat shifts to a close-up, turn-based view for individual engagements.

The hero embarks on quests to rescue a princess, rebuild his hometown, and unite forces against his nemesis, aided along the way by many allies.

Several of these characters can only be obtained by completing side quests. In addition, random battles can occur between the programmed scenarios, giving the hero's party a chance to obtain experience and gain levels outside of the set scenarios.

