"megadrive_snake-rattle-n-roll","Snake Rattle n Roll","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Rareware","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Rattle and Roll are 2 snakes racing to the moon. Play solo or with a friend to out-eat and out-score your opponent then head to the next level.

In Snake, Rattle 'n Roll, an isometric 3D platformer, players eat colorful Nibbley Pibblies to increase their snake's weight. Once heavy enough to trigger the scales, the exit door opens, allowing progression to the next level.

Like many platformers of its time, Snake, Rattle 'n Roll is notoriously difficult. Players face deadly foes such as Jaws, a toothy water monster and Bigfoots, which require multiple attacks to defeat. The game also features various Nibblies, including jumping Pibblesplats, high-jumping Pibbleboings, and flying Pibblewings.

The 2-player mode offers both co-op and competitive gameplay where players race to eat more Nibblies than their opponent. Standing on the scale together combines your weights, allowing both players to exit the level faster.","Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).7z","7Z","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Snake Rattle n Roll (Europe).png"
"megadrive_snow-bros-nick-amp-tom","Snow Bros. Nick &amp; Tom","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","Toaplan","Tengen","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Nick and Tom are two Princes living the dream with two beautiful princesses. When suddenly the evil King Scorch freezes Prince Nick and Tom and kidnaps the Princesses. Now Nick and Tom find themselves with abilities dealing with snow and ice. These two Snow Brothers will need to hunt down the evil King Scorch and rescue the princesses.

Snow Bros. is a fixed-screen platform game where players must defeat all enemies on each level (screen), 50 altogether. The Snow Bros use  snow as their weapon, throwing it at the enemies to stun them. When lots of snow is thrown at an enemy, it becomes covered in a flurry and unable to move. These can be rolled into  giant snowballs and pushed or kicked into other enemies. If left alone, enemies will eventually  defrost and become angry at the player. The enemy filled snowballs are a much stronger weapon then the regular handful of snow and are the only effective weapon Nick and Tom have against the bosses.","Snow Bros. - Nick &amp; Tom (Japan) (En).7z","7Z","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
"megadrive_socket","Socket","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Vic Tokai Corporation","Tokai Engineering","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","In this fast-paced platformer inspired by Sonic the Hedgehog, the evil Time Dominator steals treasures from the past, disrupting the timeline. Socket, a time-traveling duck from the Time Warp Patrol, races through warped eras to restore history and stop the overlord.

Socket is a robot who can jump, kick and run fast but his energy constantly drains: He must collect scattered electric bolts to replenish his health which also decreases when hit by enemies.

The game features 7 themed zones, each divided into 4 parts. Players start in the High Speed Zone for fast-paced action then progress to the Athletic Zone with its jumping challenges, and the Labyrinth Zone focused on exploration. Each Labyrinth Zone concludes with a boss battle against Time Dominator before advancing to the next High Speed Zone.

The game also features a sound test mode and a time trial mode, where the High Speed Zone stages can be played without any enemies present with times being recorded.","Socket (USA).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Socket (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Socket (USA).png"
