"megadrive_sonic-3","Sonic 3","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-24","1994","1990s","Sonic Team","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Sonic the Hedgehog 3 is the third in the Sonic series of games. As with the previous games, it is a side-scrolling platformer based around speed. The basic game remains the same - players collect rings to earn extra lives, which are also used for protection, and scatter everywhere when Sonic is hurt. Sonic can jump on enemies to defeat them, and Spin Dash by holding down and the jump button, then letting go of down. Dr. Robotnik's Death Egg has crash-landed on Floating Island, so called because it harnesses the power of the Chaos Emeralds to float in the air. Robotnik needs them to repair the Death Egg, so he tells the guardian of Floating Island, Knuckles the Echidna, that Sonic and Tails are there to steal them. With Knuckles tricked and trying to stop the heroes at every turn, will they be able to stop Robotnik in time? New to Sonic 3 are three different types of shields; the Fire Shield (which protects you from fire but disappears if you enter water), the Water Shield (which lets you breathe underwater infinitely), and the Electric Shield (which pulls nearby rings towards you).","Sonic 3 (Europe).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Sonic 3 (Europe).png"
"megadrive_sonic-3d-flickies-island","Sonic 3D Flickies' Island","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-11-05","1996","1990s","Traveller's Tales","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Sonic 3D is the last Sonic game for the Mega Drive, his only platform outing on the Sega Saturn, and one of his rare PC appearances. Despite its name, it isn't truly 3D but rather an isometric adventure where Sonic can move freely in all directions. On Flicky Island, he discovers that Dr. Robotnik has turned his bird friends into Badniks to hunt for the Chaos Emeralds. Across seven large levels, Sonic must destroy Badniks, free the Flickies, and guide them through interdimensional rings. The pace is slower than previous games, but exploration is rewarded — collecting all Flickies unlocks hidden bonus tokens. There's no time pressure, and to obtain the Chaos Emeralds, Sonic must find Tails or Knuckles while carrying at least 50 rings.","Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).7z","7Z","2.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","miximages/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","screenshots/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","backcovers/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png","marquees/megadrive/Sonic 3D Blast (USA, Europe, Korea) (En).png"
