"megadrive_sonic-eraser","Sonic Eraser","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-01-01","1991","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","20","1","Sonic Eraser is a puzzle game similar to Columns where matching pieces disappear and trigger chain reactions. It features four distinct single-player modes.

1. Round: Each stage starts with pieces in the well already. There are several spinning green pieces which must all be destroyed to finish the stage.

2. Normal: A standard endless mode in which the game speed continually rises as matches are made.

3. Doubt: No white-colored blocks will appear in the drop formations but often a random block in the formation will change to a white block after it is placed.

4. Block: Similar to Normal mode but blocks will not fall out of formation until a match is made, allowing for impressive clear combos.

These modes support single-player or two-player simultaneous play plus a versus mode where clearing combos of 3 or more disrupts the opponent's control temporarily.","Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).7z","7Z","0.09","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","miximages/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","marquees/megadrive/Sonic Eraser (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png"
"megadrive_sonic-jam-6","Sonic Jam 6","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Gamtec","Gamtec","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Sonic Jam 6, called Super 1998 Sonic 6 on the original box, is a hack of Super Mario 2 1998 made later in 1998, an unlicensed clone of Super Mario Bros. for the Sega Mega Drive that uses tiles appropriated from Super Mario All-Stars.

The Mario sprite of Super 1998 Mario 2 was replaced by Sonic the Hedgehog, who is red without a mushroom and blue with one. The title screen was also changed to feature Sonic, as well as the ""intermission"" screens that show you the remaining lives and the ""Game Over"" screen. Mario's name above the score readout was also changed to Sonic's. Curiously, the large Mario head in the underground bonus areas still remains. Controls are also modified; only the C button allows Sonic to jump and A shoots fireballs (if Sonic has grabbed a Fire Flower.)","Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/Sonic Jam 6 (Taiwan) (En) (Pirate).png"
