"megadrive_star-trek-the-next-generation-echoes-from-the-past","Star Trek, The Next Generation : Echoes from the Past","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","80","4","The Romulans' attempt to enter the Neutral Zone to find missing researchers prompts the USS Enterprise to monitor their true intentions.

The game offers 3 core modes: Commanding the ship from the bridge, leading away teams on planetary missions and engaging in ship-to-ship combat.

From the bridge, players handle navigation, communications and sensor monitoring, while accessing the computer for data, engineering for repairs, the briefing room for orders and the tactical station for battles.

Away missions require recruiting a 4-person crew with unique abilities to tackle real-time combat, puzzles involving and strategic item use.

Space battles feature a top-down perspective where players fire phasers and torpedoes while managing shields and dodging enemy attacks with the option to surrender if heavily damaged.

Although the SNES and Genesis versions share the same gameplay, the Genesis edition runs faster and features distinct graphics and a different map layout.","Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","miximages/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","screenshots/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","backcovers/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png","marquees/megadrive/Star Trek - The Next Generation (USA) (Beta) (1993-12-28).png"
