"megadrive_super-smash-t-v","Super Smash T.V.","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-11-01","1992","1990s","Probe Entertainment","Probe Entertainment","Shooter / Run and Gun","Shooter","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","The year is 1999. The world's most popular television show is Smash T.V., an ultra-violent contest between two armed-to-the-teeth combatants, set loose in a series of deadly arenas that are filled to bursting with hordes of mindless beasts and killer robots. The aim of the game is to blast everything in sight and try to grab more cash and prizes than the other guy. Toaster ovens, VCRs, fancy cars and luxury holidays are there for the taking... for anyone who can survive long enough to enjoy them.

Smash T.V. is an insane shoot-em-up from the brain of Eugene Jarvis, creator of Robotron: 2084. It retains that game's frantic style of play and two-joystick control method, but adds plenty of gore, violence, a hint of satire and that all-important two player mode.","Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).7z","7Z","0.28","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Super Smash T.V. (USA, Europe).png"
"megadrive_super-street-fighter-ii","Super Street Fighter II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Capcom","Capcom","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","This is the sequel to the super hit Street Fighter II Turbo and Street Fighter II Championship games for the SNES and Genesis. This port of the arcade game featured all 4 new characters and stages making a total of 16 playable. The game was packed into massive 32Meg and 40Meg cartridges for the SNES and Genesis. Featured many multiplayer modes in addition to the single player mode. There was the returning elimination group battle where you and a group of people played until one person was the champ. The Point Battle where the person with the most points wins. Newer modes included Tournament where you had an 8 man double elimination tournament. Finally the Challenge mode, where you tried to get the most points on a CPU opponent or beat them real fast trying to surpass records.","Super Street Fighter II (Europe).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Super Street Fighter II (Europe).png"
