"megadrive_teddy-boy-blues","Teddy Boy Blues","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1990-01-01","1990","1990s","SEGA","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Teddy Boy Blues is an updated conversion of the 1985 Sega coin-op action platformer. While the basic premise is similar to the Master System version -- each stage contains a number of enemy generators, and enemies must be shot and collected before they take a portion of the time meter -- this version of the game has several differences. The graphics have been redrawn to take advantage of the more powerful hardware and the Yohko Ishino tie-in has been removed. There are also several new stages throughout the game, though many of the original game's stages are also present.","Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).7z","7Z","0.11","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","miximages/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png","","marquees/megadrive/Teddy Boy Blues (Japan) (Sega Game Toshokan).png"
