"megadrive_tiny-toon-adventures-3","Tiny Toon Adventures 3","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Gamtec","Gamtec","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","The game consists of five stages, each usually composed of four screens each and then a boss. Following with the story, you free different types of animals each stage, trapped in what appear to be either little cages or trash bins, jumping on the cages will release them and will destroy all enemies currently as well as adding to your score. In the game, the graphics in stages three and four are based off those from Super Mario World. Stage three appears to outright lift level graphics straight from the SNES game, while stage four uses what appear to be original graphics based on the Super Mario World style. Unlike stage three though, stage four also has enemy sprites that are based off of Super Mario World enemies, including Koopas and Chargin' Chuck, and pigs that fly with parachutes, much like Para-bombs.","Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).7z","7Z","0.16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","miximages/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","screenshots/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","backcovers/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png","marquees/megadrive/Tiny Toon Adventures 3 (Taiwan) (En) (Unl).png"
"megadrive_tnn-bass-tournament-of-champions","TNN Bass Tournament of Champions","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Imagitec Design","American Softworks","Fishing","Action","1","1","1","70","3.5","Starting at 7.30 in the morning, the player has until 4PM to take a boat on the lake and fish for bass to beat competitors. The boat can be steered freely using a top-down view until an appropriate spot has been found by checking the lowrance monitor. The game then switches to a first-person view, also showing the fisher from a side-view on a separate part of the screen, and it is possible to look around in the environment.

Casting is done using a power meter to determine the distance. As the bait sinks, a monitor can be checked for nearby fish. There are also visual clues through splashing water. The player can check the depth and reel in when needed. When a fish has been caught, it becomes a sensitive play with the line tension to make sure it does not snap shown through the side-view of the fisher. At the end of the day the boat can go back to the weighing area to determine the results. Money earned in the tournaments can be used to acquire new spin reels, bait reels, boats, lines and lures.","TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).7z","7Z","0.64","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","miximages/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","screenshots/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","titlescreens/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","3dboxes/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","backcovers/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png","marquees/megadrive/TNN Bass Tournament of Champions (USA) (Rev 1).png"
"megadrive_tnn-outdoors-bass-tournament-96","TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-01","1996","1990s","Imagitec Design","American Softworks","Fishing","Action","1","1","1","","","TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 is the sequel to TNN Bass Tournament of Champions. It shares many elements with the PC game of the same name, but that version has an isometric-style map and a full 3D view for the fishing sequences. Just like the original game it is a fishing simulator that allows the player to access a free fishing mode or to participate in a fishing tournament. First, equipment needs to be bought. It consists of lures, rods, reels, lines and boats. Better items can only be acquired by winning money in tournaments.","TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).7z","7Z","0.37","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/TNN Outdoors Bass Tournament '96 (USA).png"
"megadrive_todd-s-adventures-in-slime-world","Todd's Adventures in Slime World","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-09-02","1991","1990s","Micro World","Renovation Products","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","60","3","While flying your spaceship, you crash land on a planet covered entirely in slime.  You and a friend explore the labyrinthine planet of slime, armed with a water pistol and all manner of gadgets you find along the way in an effort to find your way back out.  The game world is a giant maze with quirky hidden areas and plenty of original layout ideas.  Depending on the game mode, you are either cooperating or competing with your ""friend"" to find and get to an exit first.  Due to the massive sizes of the slime worlds (about 6 entries to choose from), games often take several hours to complete.

The basis of the game is exploration, with varying game modes further focusing on competition, puzzle solving, speed, exploration, or cooperation.","Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","miximages/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","screenshots/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","backcovers/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png","marquees/megadrive/Todd's Adventures in Slime World (USA).png"
"megadrive_toejam-amp-earl","ToeJam &amp; Earl","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-11-01","1991","1990s","ToeJam &amp; Earl Productions","SEGA","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Toejam and Earl are two hip aliens from the planet Funkotron. One day, they are cruisin' their galaxy in the sweet spaceship ride. Unfortunately, Earl wasn't paying enough attention to where he was driving, and ran the ship into an asteroid.  The ship crash landed onto the most bizarre planet in the galaxy: Earth.

Toejam and Earl must travel from level to level on Earth and collect the 10 scattered pieces of the ship. But the various Earthlings, such as Nerd Herds, Giant Hamsters, Phantom Ice Cream Trucks and the Bogeyman will make that difficult.

The power up items that TJ and E can pick up come in the form of wrapped presents. You never really know what a power up is until you open it. What's more, randomized levels and item locations make it a different game every time.

The game features a dynamic screen splitting - screen joining 2-player mode.
Players start the game close to each other. If one gets away from the other, the screen vertically splits to allow each player to move freely. When players are close again, the screens join together to become one single screen.","ToeJam &amp; Earl (Japan, Europe) (En) (Rev A).7z","7Z","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
