"megadrive_shining-force-ii","Shining Force II","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Camelot Software Planning","SEGA","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Shining Force II blends strategy and RPG elements with cartoon-style graphics, alternating between exploration and tactical battles. Players explore new lands and interact with NPCs to advance the story, while combat shifts to a close-up, turn-based view for individual engagements.

The hero embarks on quests to rescue a princess, rebuild his hometown, and unite forces against his nemesis, aided along the way by many allies.

Several of these characters can only be obtained by completing side quests. In addition, random battles can occur between the programmed scenarios, giving the hero's party a chance to obtain experience and gain levels outside of the set scenarios.

There are several difficulty levels in the game, selectable when starting a new game. In addition, there is a configuration code that allows cheats to be activated, including the ability to control the enemy units.","Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","miximages/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","screenshots/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","backcovers/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png","marquees/megadrive/Xin Guangming Yu Heian III - Gudai Fengyin (China) (Pirate).png"
"megadrive_xin-qi-gai-wang-zi","Xin Qi Gai Wang Zi","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Computer &amp; Entertainment","C&amp;E","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","Xin Qigai Wangzi is a Chinese-made RPG loosely based on the famous novel by Mark Twain, Prince and the Pauper. A young prince is bored with the life in the palace, and one day manages to go outside the gate, distracting the guards. In the town he meets a young boy who looks very similar to him. The prince offers him to switch their clothes, because he wants to spend the day as an ordinary boy. But when he comes back to the palace, the guards don't recognize him in his beggar's clothes and refuse to let him in. A new life, full of danger and adventures, begins for the young prince...","Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","miximages/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","screenshots/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","backcovers/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png","marquees/megadrive/Xin Qigai Wangzi (Taiwan) (Beta) (Unl).png"
