"megadrive_yogi-bear-cartoon-capers","Yogi Bear : Cartoon Capers","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Blue Turtle","Empire Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","60","3","When Yogi Bear catches wind of a plan to turn Jellystone Park into a Chemical plant he sets out on a mission to stop it. Play as Yogi in this side-scrolling Action/Adventure that is fit for all ages. Work your way through the five park areas collecting ""Pic-i-nic"" baskets by bouncing on top of them. In many cases you bounce from one basket to the next raising you into the air where no ""average bear"" could ever go. There are a variety of enemies such as weasels and skunks. There are also some action parts where you ride a mine cart or go ""beaver surfing"".","Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).7z","7Z","0.41","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","miximages/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","screenshots/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","backcovers/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png","marquees/megadrive/Yogi Bear - Cartoon Capers (Europe).png"
"megadrive_instruments-of-chaos-starring-young-indiana-jones","Instruments of Chaos Starring Young Indiana Jones","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Brian A. Rice","LucasArts","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Germany is growing its war machine to overtake the world. To reach this goal quickly, their evil leaders sent spies around the world with instructions to buy the finest military weapon technologies. The player is young Indiana Jones and he is informed by agent Rolf that friendly French agents know about such tasks and the countries the spies will visit. The spies need to be stopped in each country before the technology sale takes place.

The mission takes young Indy to India, Tibet, Egypt, and England before come finally arriving in Germany. In 2d side-scrolling levels Indy uses his whip, revolver, grenades, and ability to walk/jumpto progress through the levels with small puzzle elements. Enemies can be attacked or avoided and actions can be performed in eight directions. There are different mini-goals such as whipping key stones to open the door to the temple from Indian marketplace, or bombing a bridge gearbox.

There are three difficulty levels. The number of lives can be adjusted.","Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","miximages/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","screenshots/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","backcovers/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png","marquees/megadrive/Young Indiana Jones Chronicles, The (USA) (Beta).png"
"megadrive_ys-iii","Ys III","megadrive","Sega Mega Drive / Genesis","Mega Drive","Sega","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-12-01","1991","1990s","Nihon Falcom","Nihon Falcom","Action RPG","RPG","1","1","1","100","5","Adol's long time friend, Dogi wishes to return to his home town of Redmont after hearing about strange disturbances that are happening there.  Always looking for an adventure, Adol joins him and soon finds out the cause of this new evil.

Ys III breaks away from the ""bumping into enemies"" battle system of the first two games and allows Adol to control his sword in a variety of directions.  As well as changing the battle system, the game is now side scrolling instead of the previous games top-down view. Adol also now has the ability to jump.  Not new to the series is the use of magical rings which give Adol different powering up abilities such as healing and shielding.  The game also uses various key items found along the way to solve minor puzzles and progress the story.","Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).7z","7Z","0","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","miximages/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","screenshots/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","titlescreens/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","3dboxes/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","backcovers/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png","marquees/megadrive/Ys - Wanderers from Ys (Japan).png"
