To accomplish the ultimate goal of defeating the Zarak army, players venture out on numerous missions (called ""sorties"") that have varied and specific objectives. Typically, various installations such as radar sites, air bases or ground units are the target. Other missions include disabling an oil-pipeline and destroying SCUD launchers before they fire.","A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","miximages/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","screenshots/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","backcovers/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png","marquees/snes/A.S.P. - Air Strike Patrol (NA).png"
