"snes_arcana","Arcana","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-05-01","1992","1990s","HAL Laboratory","HAL America","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","In this game you play as a young boy named Rooks.  He's the only one that can save the world from the evil Galneon.  With the power of the cards he begins his adventure.

All of the people you fight with and against are displayed on cards.  They can have an elemental attribute or not.  Rooks is able to summon an elemental to aid him.  He can only summon one type at a time, and he must find them before being able to summon them.","Arcana (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Arcana (NA).png","miximages/snes/Arcana (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Arcana (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Arcana (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Arcana (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Arcana (NA).png","marquees/snes/Arcana (NA).png"
"snes_archer-maclean-s-super-dropzone","Archer MacLean's Super Dropzone","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-01","1995","1990s","Eurocom","Psygnosis","Shoot'em Up","Shooter","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Dropzone was the first game to propel Archer Maclean to stardom. The game, originally written for the 8-bit Ataris, is basically a Defender clone, but popular because it so closely recreates the gameplay of the original Defender, with its speedy scrolling and frantic gameplay.

The player is a spaceman with a jet-pack, flying across a barren landscape whose skies are inhabited by a number of different aliens; from the simple Planter to the slowly advancing Blunder Storm or the quick, aggressive Nemesite. 

Planters and Nemesites will try to pickup the small men walking on the surface, who must then be rescued. You must shoot down the alien, while avoiding to hit the man. Sometimes, the aliens will carry an android, which is similar to the human but deadly. Care must be taken so as to not pick up the androids. All men must be transported to a surface base, where they are put in safety. This is the Dropzone.","Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Archer Maclean's Super Dropzone (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_arcus-spirits","Arcus Spirits","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-10-22","1993","1990s","Wolf Team","Sammy USA Corporation","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Long time ago, an evil sorceress Castomira decided to conquer the world. But a good princess revolted against her, and in a great fight defeated the sorceress. But in order to completely seal the sorceress' powers, the princess had to forge a magic sword. For a long time this sword guarded the peace of the citizens of Arcus. But now the followers of Castomira stole it, and the world is facing a great peril...

This is a  Gauntlet-like game: lots of action and magic, with items to collects, and many dungeons to free from monsters. The game is also viewed from an isometric perspective, typical for the genre. Choose one of four characters to battle your way through dungeons and castles, or play with a friend in a 2-player mode.","Arcus Spirits (Prototype).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","miximages/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","screenshots/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","titlescreens/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","3dboxes/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","backcovers/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png","marquees/snes/Arcus Spirits (Prototype).png"
"snes_ardy-lightfoot","Ardy Lightfoot","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-31","1994","1990s","ASCII","Titus","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","In this 2D platform game, you play as Ardy Lightfoot - a cat-like creature - with your friend Pec, a blue penguin that can be used to defeat the enemies. Your goal is to find the Seven Pieces of the Sacred Rainbow. Each piece is widespread in various colorful worlds with strange and funny enemies and bosses. You'll have to find all the pieces in order to face a terrible enemy in the last stage. At some parts of the game, you will receive a little help from your friends, such as Nina and a mysterious adventurer named Don Jacoby.","Ardy Lightfoot (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","miximages/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png","marquees/snes/Ardy Lightfoot (NA).png"
"snes_aretha","Aretha","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-26","1993","1990s","Japan Art Media","Yanoman Games","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","In a far away land, war was raging, as an evil ruler sent his troops to invade the castle of a mighty king. His minions stormed the castle and burnt it down. The king could not escape his fate, and the villain thought no one was spared by his wrath. You are Ariel, a little girl who lives with her old wise grandmother in a small house near a mountain range, north to the forest. She just turned ten, and the grandmother sends her on a seemingly simple quest: to go through the forest to Nineveh, the nearby town, and to meet there a certain person. But what starts as a simple assignment soon develops into the quest for magic powers of Aretha, the ultimate battle against the evil, and the discovery of Ariel's own true identity. The game is a console-style RPG, where Ariel and her party travel on the world map, through forests, mountain paths, and caves, occasionally visiting towns and fighting monsters in turn-based combat viewed from first-person perspective, using a variety of physical and special attacks.","Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).sfc","SFC","2.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","miximages/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","screenshots/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","titlescreens/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","3dboxes/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","backcovers/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","marquees/snes/Aretha (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png"
"snes_aretha-2-ariel-no-fushigi-na-tabi","Aretha 2 - Ariel No Fushigi Na Tabi","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-02","1994","1990s","Yanoman Games","Japan Art Media","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","The game continues the story of the young princess Ariel. After she rightfully regained her throne, people enjoyed a peaceful life under her benevolent reign. But this peaceful existence did not last long... Two adventurers who were wandering through mountains met a mysterious evil being, who threatened to ruin Ariel's kingdom. After that, the two men disappeared without a trace. Ariel's servants reported to her about the matter. After consulting her wise grandmother, Ariel decided to go out herself, to meet up with her old trusty companions and to find out the origin of the new threat.

The game is a console-style RPG - you fight random enemies in turn-based combat viewed from first-person perspective. Enemies may attack you from the sides, and you should pay attention which enemy you face. A unique feature the game uses is the ability to get special items called ""souls"" after battles, and then to use them to forge your own armor.","Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","miximages/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","screenshots/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","titlescreens/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","3dboxes/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","backcovers/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png","marquees/snes/Aretha II - Ariel no Fushigi na Tabi (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 0.91).png"
"snes_arkanoid","Arkanoid","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1997-01-01","1997","1990s","Taito","Nintendo","Action / Breakout games","Action","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","A sequel to the arcade game Arkanoid. Use your paddle to move the ball around and hit bricks to clear the level. Once all the bricks are gone in the current level, you go on to the next level. Power-ups, like lasers and paddle lengthening will help you during the levels. Unlike the arcade version, the sequel has boss battles and somewhat of a storyline.","Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","miximages/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png","marquees/snes/Arkanoid - Doh It Again (NA).png"
"snes_art-of-fighting","Art of Fighting","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","SNK","Takara","Fighting / Versus","Fighting","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Yuri Sakazaki has been kidnapped! Her big brother Ryo Sakazaki and Robert Garcia, his best friend, go search for her on the streets of South Town. As they go deeper and deeper they will find clues as to who ordered the kidnapping, the Sakazaki family's relation to the mob, and a person from their past.

This fighting game is a coin-op conversion of the Neo-Geo hit of the same name, and has all characters, stages, and moves featured in the arcade unit. Unlike the original arcade version, players can now play as Mr. Big and the elusive Mr. Karate.

The gameplay differs from most fighting games. In this game, you have a Spirit meter. A Spirit meter is in the game and will decrease as you perform special moves. It can be recharged, but doing so leaves you open to attack. When your health is almost gone, you can perform a secret combination that will unleash a deadly attack on your opponent - provided you have a full Spirit meter.","Art of Fighting (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","miximages/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png","marquees/snes/Art of Fighting (NA).png"
"snes_ashita-no-joe","Ashita No Joe","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-11-27","1992","1990s","Wave","K. Amusement Leasing","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Ashita no Joe started as a manga in the late 60s and since that time has become a very popular property with fans all over the world. Joe Yabuki, the protagonist of this story, is an everyday man who was orphaned at at a young age. With no hope for the future, Joe becomes a delinquent with no direction in life. While walking around the slums of Tokyo, Joe helps a kid who is being bullied by a gangster. By fate, a down and out boxing trainer named Danpei Tange sees the fight between Joe and the gangster. Danpei believes Joe has what it takes to be a professional boxer. With the help of Danpei and others, Joe will achieve growth not only as a boxer, but as a human being as well.
The game consists of 8 opponents which Joe must defeat in succession to move on. Each one must be knocked out in the first round or Joe must begin the fight again if any continues are left (You get 3 continues regardless of difficulty setting). The characters Joe fights all come from the manga so they should be familiar to Tomorrow?s Joe fans. Most involve using a certain strategy to defeat them and herein lies the challenge and fun.","Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","miximages/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","screenshots/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","titlescreens/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","3dboxes/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","backcovers/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png","marquees/snes/Ashita no Joe (English Translated by Vice Translations, Rev 0.99 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu).png"
