"snes_bebe-s-kids","Bebe's Kids","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-04-01","1994","1990s","Radical Entertainment","Motown Software","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","30","1.5","This side-scrolling beat em' up game is based on a 1992 Paramount Pictures animated movie which was the first ever to feature an all-Black main cast. The characters were originally from comedian Robin Harris' ""Bébé's Kids"" (pronounced Bay-Bay) stand-up comedy act. They're described as little hellions and bad-ass troublemaker kids.  In this game, someone has taken control of the Fun World amusement park, and you've got to help Kahlil, LaShawn, and PeeWee make things right.","Bebe's Kids (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","miximages/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png","marquees/snes/Bebe's Kids (NA).png"
"snes_beethoven-the-ultimate-canine-caper","Beethoven : The Ultimate Canine Caper!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-01","1993","1990s","RSP","Hi Tech Expressions","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","Beethoven's 2nd is a platform game where you get a chance to wear the metaphorical shoes of Beethoven - that lovable, big dog from the movie.

Your four puppies need to be rescued and brought back to their mom. As a responsible father and guardian you'll first need to find the puppy, avoiding dangers such as bad-tempered cats, mean dogcatchers, acorns which have a habit to drop down just when you pass underneath, and careless skateboarders. You can bark at these opponents to scare them away. And if you'll find a source of water (such as a rubber hose), you can make yourself wet and then - in a tense situation - shake off the water, eliminating everyone in the vicinity. 

Once you find your pup, you'll find out that getting him back to his mom is no easy task. While your puppy can - thankfully - walk on his own accord when you put him down, you'll still have to carry it over obstacles, and you'll be forced to fight all the enemies again while doing it.","Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","miximages/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png","marquees/snes/Beethoven - The Ultimate Canine Caper! (NA).png"
"snes_best-of-the-best-championship-karate","Best of the Best : Championship Karate","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-05-27","1993","1990s","Loriciel","Electro Brain","Sports / Boxing","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","Best of the Best Championship Karate is a realistic fighting game.
After you choose your fighter for his parameters (strength, stamina and resistance), you can choose from 55 different moves.
You can now train your fighter at a gym before the real fights.
To master the game, one must alternate training and fights, as training improves stamina, strength and resistance.
Be careful, loosing a fight reduces those parameters, so you have to be ready before getting on the ring !","Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","miximages/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png","marquees/snes/Best of the Best - Championship Karate (NA).png"
"snes_big-ichigeki-pachi-slot-daikouryaku","Big Ichigeki! Pachi-slot Daikouryaku","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-16","1994","1990s","Syscom","ASK Kodansha","Casino","Board / Casual","1","1","1","60","3","Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (""Big Blow! Great Pachi-Slot Tips"") is a pachi-slot game for the Super Famicom. The player has a selection of pachi-slot machines to choose from and then attempt to win the jackpot. The idea is to play the machines enough times to get a sense of how its payouts work and then take that knowledge to real-life pachi-slot parlors.The game was developed by Syscom, which had previously developed and would develop a number of mahjong and pachi-slot games, and published by media corporation Ask Kodansha. It was followed by Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku 2: Universal Collection in 1995.","Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","miximages/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png","marquees/snes/Big Ichigeki! Pachi-Slot Daikouryaku (JP).png"
"snes_big-sky-trooper","Big Sky Trooper","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-01","1995","1990s","LucasArts","JVC","Shooter","Shooter","1","1","1","50","2.5","It's Jack Spudtop to the rescue! As a 21-star general in the Big Sky Troopers, it's your job to stop the dastardly Sultan of Slime and his alien armada of slippery slugs from taking over the universe. Navigate your way across the interstellar Skyway with the help of your sidekick FIDO, a Flexible Interactive Digital Omnicomputer, and then, battle through each and every wacky world to collect an arsenal of weapons.","Big Sky Trooper (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","miximages/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png","marquees/snes/Big Sky Trooper (NA).png"
"snes_bike-daisuki-hashiriya-tamashii","Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-30","1994","1990s","Nippon Computer Systems (NCS)","Masaya Games","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","80","4","The challenge of bike racing heats up and players choose their favorite machine. In five courses, aim to win the Grand Prix or go for a Chicken Run or time trial. There are four modes, including endurance race. Two players can go head to head in a split screen race.","Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","miximages/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","screenshots/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","titlescreens/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","3dboxes/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","backcovers/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","marquees/snes/Bike Daisuki! Hashiriya Tamashii - Rider's Spirits (English Translated by MrRichard999).png"
"snes_biker-mice-from-mars","Biker Mice from Mars","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-01","1994","1990s","Konami","Konami","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","80","4","Based on the cartoon of the same name, Biker Mice From Mars is a racing game very similar to Rock 'n Roll Racing. Races are shown from an isometric perspective and you can choose between six different drivers that differ in acceleration, top speed and grip. During the races, you can use weapons such as mines or missiles to slow down your opponents and pick up random bonuses ranging from money to making you temporarily invincible. After each race, you will receive money that can be spent on better tires, armor, engines or weapons. There's also a two-player mode that lets you play the main race with a friend or compete in a one on one race.","Biker Mice from Mars (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","miximages/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png","marquees/snes/Biker Mice from Mars (NA).png"
"snes_bill-laimbeer-s-combat-basketball","Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-11-01","1991","1990s","Hudson Soft","Hudson Soft","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-2","1","2","40","2","This futuristic basketball game is endorsed by none other than Bill Laimbeer of the Bad Boys Detroit Pistons.  The game is 5-on-5 with no rules except for out-of-bound and backcourt.  The storyline is that in the year 2023 Bill Laimbeer, the most physical player to ever play in the NBA, becomes the new commisioner of the NBA.  As new commisioner of the League he throws away all the old rules and make the game plays more to his liking which means basketball is to be an extremely physical game.  The new League is only for those who aren't scare of contact and are tough enough to endure constant physical pain.  The new NBA is extreme enough for players to wear armor to protect themselves from the new style of basketball that include hitting, shoving, punching and tackling.  It's an all-new basketball game that plays like the style of extreme football.  This game is contact basketball to the max.  There are even  weapons on the court such as bombs and saw blades that make this game one of the most violent basketball games of all time.","Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","miximages/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png","marquees/snes/Bill Laimbeer's Combat Basketball (NA).png"
"snes_bill-walsh-college-football","Bill Walsh College Football","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-06-02","1993","1990s","High Score Productions","Electronic Arts","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-5","1","5","80","4","The game features 24 college football teams from the 1993 season and 24 of the all-time college teams since 1978. Play modes include exhibition, playoffs and all-time playoffs and the SNES version also has an eleven week season mode.with the National Championship as the ultimate goal. 

The playbook consists of 56 offensive plays and 52 defensive plays.
On offense, running backs can dive, spin and hurdle. Also, passing is dealt with by having the receivers in their own windowed boxes . When on defense, defenders can dive at the ball carrier, and raise hands to block kicks or intercept passes.

The game also features four weather conditions (fair, windy, rain and snow), and three different quarter lengths (20, 40 and 60 minutes).","Bill Walsh College Football (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","miximages/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png","marquees/snes/Bill Walsh College Football (NA).png"
"snes_bing-bing-bingo","Bing Bing! Bingo","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-22","1993","1990s","Copya System","KSS","Casino","Board / Casual","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","The basic concept of Bing Bing! Bingo is that the player is on a vacation to a private island somewhere in the world that is known for their Bingo-oriented lifestyle.

He can either play Bingo through a slot machine, while skydiving, aplay a game of Bingo with Santa Claus, and an option to play Bingo on a pirate ship. There is also arm wrestling and a mode where players get to make imaginary wagers on the horses in case the player does not like Bingo. However, the numbers are announced in Japanese rather than English, so knowledge of Japanese numbers is vital for multiplayer action. Full card Bingo is mandatory for single player games but party games can use any variation of Bingo that the players consent to.

A party mode is present for two players.","Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","miximages/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","screenshots/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","titlescreens/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","3dboxes/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","backcovers/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png","marquees/snes/Bing Bing! Bingo (English Translated by MrRichard999).png"
"snes_biometal","BioMetal","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Athena","Activision","Shoot'em Up / Horizontal","Shooter","1","1","1","60","3","BioMetal is a side-scrolling shooter game. Their are two pairs, one for lasers and the other for missiles, of three upgrades for your weapons. 

The war that divided the galaxy and used all it's resources has ended. A fleet was sent on a mission to find more natural resources. They never returned. Their last transmission reveals that the enemy' created one last experiment. This experiment is a combination of the aggressive nature of animals combined with the efficiency of machines. These creatures were named BioMetal.

The MF-92GX Halbard mothership has been assigned to destroy the threat before they can not be stopped. You are piloting the MF-92GX Halbard fighter that is equipped with the experimental Gel Analog Mutant weapon. The Gel is charged up on the ship and can be used to surround the ship as a protective shield or be thrown at the enemy forces.","BioMetal (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","miximages/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","screenshots/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","backcovers/snes/BioMetal (NA).png","marquees/snes/BioMetal (NA).png"
"snes_bishin-densetsu-zoku","Bishin Densetsu Zoku","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-25","1993","1990s","Toho Company","Magifact","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","60","3","The game takes place in and around Neo Tokyo after Mount Fuji erupts in a catastrophic manner in the year 2020.While Tokyo survives and the people managed to repair the areas where the volcano destroyed their property, it becomes marginalized and become infested with street gangs. In a wasteland type environment far away from Neo Tokyo, a player must drive an automobile through a labyrinth-like series of roadways using either the male character Koji or the female character Risa.","Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","miximages/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png","marquees/snes/Bishin Densetsu Zoku (JP).png"
"snes_sailor-moon","Sailor Moon","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Angel","Bandai","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","The game is based on the popular manga/animé series of the same name. The heroine of the series is a 14-year-old schoolgirl named Serena (Usagi in the Japanese version). One day she encounters a magical talking cat named Luna, who tells her she has been chosen to be a Sailor Moon fighter, to find the lost Princess of the Moon Kingdom and to fight the forces of darkness lead by the evil Queen Beryl. 

This adaptation of the story is a beat-'em-up game. You can control either Serena herself or one of her Sailor Moon companions. Each girl has different strengths and special attacks. You advance in the game by moving on a platform and defeating the enemies you encounter. You can't move on if you haven't defeated all the enemies that keep coming at you.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon (English Translated by Flamepurge and Mziab, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-another-story","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-22","1995","1990s","Angel","Bandai","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","The game is based on the Japanese manga and animé series Bishoujo Senshi: Sailor Moon - ""Bishoujo Senshi"" roughly meaning ""Pretty Young Girl Warrior"". It is set in the 30th century, in a futuristic city Crystal Tokyo. In this city lives a totally ordinary (at first) fourteen-year old girl Usagi. When she meets a magical cat named Luna, she finds out that she is in fact a princess sent to the future in order to fight the minions of Darkness. She discovers within herself the power to transform into the hero of darkness, Sailor Moon, meets other warriors who help her on her quest, and fights the evil Queen Beryl, hostile aliens, and other foes.

The events of this game take place shortly after Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S, the fourth volume of the long-running series. A global peace is established in the universe, but lately suspicious things are happening. A strange meteorite is seen approaching the Earth. Street gangs and spies who work for a mysterious person called Apsu are seen in Crystal Tokyo. And the Mystic Silver Crystal, the Ginzuishou, which protects the city, is shaking! Usagi and her friends must now investigate the strange events and face the forces of Darkness once again.

The game is a console-style RPG in  Final Fantasy style (battles with your party to the right and the enemies to the left), with a battle system somewhat similar to that of  Chrono Trigger: you must form a party out of several available characters, make them participate in battles together, and learn powerful combo attacks.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon - Another Story (English Translated by BST, Rev 2.08).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-r","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-29","1993","1990s","Angel","Bandai","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","The game is based on the events of the animé that follow the victory of Usagi and her friends over the Queen Beryl. Peace has returned to the Moon Kingdom. But suddenly, a little girl named Chibiusa arrives from the future and says the future kingdom is threatened by the forces of the evil Prince Diamond. Looks like you are the only ones who can defeat him, and save the future Sailor Moon, Chibiusa's mother.

This is a beat-'em up game. You can play as either Usagi or any of her girlfriends, including Chibiusa. You move on a platform and fight the enemies by punching, kicking, and throwing them, and by using special abilities unique to each character. You can advance only after you have cleared an area from enemies.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon R (English Translated by FuSoYa).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-s-jougai-rantou-shuyaku-soudatsusen","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-16","1994","1990s","Arc System Works","Angel","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","The game is based on the animé series Sailor Moon. The heroine of the series is Tsukino Usagi, a 14-year-old schoolgirl. She meets a talking cat named Luna, who tells her she is in fact the powerful fighter Sailor Moon who can save the Moon Kingdom from an assault of the forces of darkness. Later, other Sailor fighters join Usagi on her quest.

This is a fighting game in which you can play as Usagi or any of her Sailor companions (named after planets). The girls fight against each other, using punches, kicks, and special attacks. There is also a tournament mode and a two-player mode.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).sfc","SFC","2.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Jougai Rantou! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-s-kondo-wa-puzzle-de-oshioki-yo","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo Wa Puzzle De Oshioki Yo!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-15","1994","1990s","Tom Create","Bandai","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","60","3","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S: Kondoha Puzzle de Oshiokiyo is a falling block competitive puzzle game. Players begin by choosing from a selection of Sailor Moon licensed characters, each with a unique special attack. The player is presented with a board filled with colored blocks in three colors: red, blue and green. The goal is to remove all the blocks from play. Clicking on a block that touches several adjacent blocks of the same color will remove them all from play. As each player successfully clears blocks, they drop ""black blocks"" on their opponent as well as increase their power bar. Black blocks cannot be removed by normal means and disappear only when large ammounts of blocks are removed adjacent to them. As the power bar charges, players can unleash their special ability, often an attack on the other player.

This puzzle game is based on the ""S"" series of Sailor Moon and includes characters from there: Sailor Moon, Sailor Mars, Sailor Venus, Sailor Mercury, Sailor Jupiter, Chibiusa, Tuxedo Mask, Sailor Uranus, Sailor Neptune and Sailor Pluto.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kondo wa Puzzle de Oshioki yo! (JP).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-s-kurukkurin","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-24","1995","1990s","Tom Create","Bandai","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S: Kurukkurin is a competitive puzzle game featuring Sailor Moon licensed characters. Upon choosing a character (each with unique ""special moves""), the player competes against an opponent. Each player controls a grid of 10x6 sections (represented by hearts) initially made up of clear hearts. The player moves their cursor over the clear hearts to turn them into one of four colors: red, yellow, blue and green. Sometimes ""treasures"" will show up on the board. When several hearts of the same color are adjacent to one another, the player can clear them... which pushes all the hearts (and treasures) down towards the bottom. The goal is to be the player with the most treasures to end the round.

Sailor Moon characters featured are primarily from the ""S"" Series and includes: Sailor Moon, Sailor Mars, Sailor Mercury, Sailor Venus, Sailor Jupiter, Chibius, Tuxedo Mask, Sailor Neptune, Sailor Uranus and Sailor Pluto.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S - Kurukkurin (JP).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-super-s-fuwa-fuwa-panic","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon Super S - Fuwa Fuwa Panic","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-08","1995","1990s","Tom Create","Bandai","Puzzle / Throw","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS: Fuwa Fuwa Panic (""Pretty Soldier Sailor Moon SuperS: Floating Panic"") is a puzzle game licensed by Bandai that features the various Sailor Guardians, including the new ""super"" transformations of Usagi Tsukino (Sailor Moon) and Chibi-usa (Sailor Chibi Moon) that debuted in the ""SuperS"" season, which was the name of the fourth season of the anime adaptation.

The goal of the game is to fire at the balloons that appear at the top of the screen to pop them. By shooting a balloon adjacent to another of the same color, the player pops both simultaneously. By popping a large number of balloons simultaneously, they can create trash for the other player to clear - these appear as gray balloons that can't easily be popped directly but disappear when multiple balloons are popped near them.

The player can select between nine Sailor Guardians in the vs. mode (all except Saturn), but is restricted to Sailors Moon, Chibi Moon, Mars, Mercury, Jupiter and Venus for the single-player story mode. Sailor Saturn appears in-game as an advisor, but is not playable. The game was followed by a sequel the following year: Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon Sailor Stars: Fuwa Fuwa Panic 2. It also received a fan translation in 2016.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Fuwa Fuwa Panic (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01 With Westernized Names).png"
"snes_bishoujo-senshi-sailor-moon-super-s-zenin-sanka-shuyaku-soudatsusen","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon Super S - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-03-29","1996","1990s","Monolith","Angel","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","The game is based on the manga/animÃ© series Sailor Moon. It tells the story of Pretty Sailor Fighters, teenage girls who were summoned to protect the futuristic Moon Kingdom and to fight the forces of darkness, led by the evil Queen Beryl and Prince Diamond. The main heroine is a girl named Tsukino Usagi, who was contacted by the magical talking cat Luna to become Sailor Moon, the leader of the group.

This fighting game is an enhanced version of  Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon S: Jougai Ranto!? Shuyaku Soudatsusen. Girls compete against each other in tournament mode, story mode, player-vs.-computer mode, and two players mode. They can use physical attacks and magical spells. In story mode you can also upgrade your fighter's attributes (strength, defense power, etc.) New in this expanded version: additional playable characters (hence the title Zen'in Sanka - ""Everyone Participates""), different scenes in story mode, additional backgrounds for battles.","Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","miximages/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png","marquees/snes/Bishoujo Senshi Sailor Moon SuperS - Zenin Sanka!! Shuyaku Soudatsusen (JP).png"
