"snes_boogerman-a-pick-and-flick-adventure","Boogerman : A Pick and Flick Adventure","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-25","1996","1990s","Interplay","Interplay","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","He thinks he's a hero, but he's snot! He's mean. He's green. And he nose how to pick a fight!

He's BOOGERMAN, as slick as he is deep, and he's on a pick 'n' flick adventure to save the world. He's stretched to the limit of blowing away the vile slimebags who are bent on sticking it to Planet Earth, any way, every way, and everywhere they can.

You're his first pick to help him rescue the whole world before it's flushed down the toilet. Join the flick-or-be-flicked race to pull the plug on the Booger Meister and his gang of filthy stinkers who aren't afraid to fight dirty... because yours is the only finger which can wipe 'em out!","Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","miximages/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png","marquees/snes/Boogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure (NA).png"
"snes_boxing-legends-of-the-ring","Boxing Legends of the Ring","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Sculptured Software","Electro Brain","Sports / Boxing","Sports","1","1","1","60","3","In Boxing Legends of the Ring, you step into the ring with eight middleweight legends — including Roberto Durán, Jake LaMotta, Sugar Ray Leonard, Marvin Hagler, and James Toney. You can fight in exhibition matches or rise through the ranks in career mode to become the greatest of all time. Use jabs, hooks, uppercuts, and even the occasional illegal low blow to wear down your opponent. Every knockdown earns you a Super Punch — a devastating strike that can end the fight if it connects but is lost if you miss. Two indicators track the action: glove-shaped hit meters and a damage display showing fighters' faces bruising and bleeding over time. A neat twist is that the camera alternates each round, switching between your view and your opponent's shoulder for a more cinematic experience.","Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","miximages/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png","marquees/snes/Boxing Legends of the Ring (NA).png"
"snes_brain-lord","Brain Lord","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-02","1994","1990s","Produce","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","In ""Brain Lord"", you play a young traveler and warrior who is searching for his long lost father. Long ago, when you were a mere child, your father told you about the great legacy of your village. Once your people were Dragon Warriors, who could control and fly on dragons. But the dragons had disappeared, and your father was determined to find the legendary Tower of Light, where, according to rumors, the last dragons might be hiding. You father went to search the Tower of Light and never came back. Years have passed, and now you finally found the Tower of Light. But your adventure doesn't end there, as you had thought - it begins there...

""Brain Lord"" is an action RPG with a heavy emphasis on dungeon exploring. You fight enemies in real time, using various weapons with different ranges - swords, axes, etc. You can equip different kinds of armor and shields. On your quest you will find magical jades that summon fairies who would fight at your side. The fairies have special attacks and level up after fighting just like you, but are controlled by the AI. There are also puzzles to solve in the dungeons, and the hero has the ability to jump.","Brain Lord (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","miximages/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png","marquees/snes/Brain Lord (NA).png"
"snes_bram-stoker-s-dracula","Bram Stoker's Dracula","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Psygnosis","Sony Imagesoft","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","Bram Stoker's Dracula is the title given to a number of games based on the 1992 film of the same name. Gameplay for each game varies greatly from platform to platform, but they all retain a similar plot based on the movie. The 16-bit console versions are side-scrolling hack-and-slash games.

The player controls a young lawyer named Jonathan Harker. Harker must free himself from Dracula's capture, follow him to London, and end his reign of terror.","Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","miximages/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png","marquees/snes/Bram Stoker's Dracula (NA).png"
"snes_brandish","Brandish","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-01","1995","1990s","Falcom","Koei","Action RPG","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","The game is an action RPG, a dungeon crawler with plenty of creatures to defeat and many weapons, armor, and other treasure to collect. Once there was a prosperous kingdom, which was protected by a tower, where a mighty dragon was living. The people of the kingdom were secure with such a guardian. But one man wanted the dragon's power for something else, and this man was the king. He went to the tower and tried to kill the dragon, in order to rob his power.","Brandish (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brandish (NA).png","miximages/snes/Brandish (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Brandish (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Brandish (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Brandish (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Brandish (NA).png","marquees/snes/Brandish (NA).png"
"snes_brandish-2-the-planet-buster","Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-08-11","1995","1990s","Nihon Falcom","Koei","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","The Planet Buster continues the story that was told in the first Brandish game, and depicts the events that happened three years after the evil demonic king was defeated in his lost kingdom, sunken deep underground. You take control of a young warrior named Ares, who wields a magical weapon, a powerful sword called the Planet Buster. One day, while traveling through a desert, Ares is captured by a warlock named Karl, who is after the powers hidden within the magical sword. Suspecting Ares might have some valuable information, Karl doesn't execute him, but takes away the Planet Buster and throws Ares into his underground prison. Now your primary goal is to guide Ares out of the huge prison full of various dangers, and to get your mighty weapon back.

The game is an action RPG with a heavy emphasis on dungeon crawling. You guide Ares through rotating dungeons, fighting enemies in real-time combat, casting spells, and solving an occasional puzzle. You have the ability to jump forwards and to attack inanimate objects such as doors to cause damage and to break the object.","Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","miximages/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","screenshots/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","titlescreens/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","3dboxes/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","backcovers/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png","marquees/snes/Brandish 2 - The Planet Buster (English Translated by Synchronicity).png"
"snes_brawl-brothers-rival-turf-2","Brawl Brothers : Rival Turf! 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Jaleco","Jaleco","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","The Brawl Brothers are two guys, not actually brothers, named Rick and Doug (or, Hack and Slash, respectively) who run a self-defense gym in Bayside City. Three of the gym's best fighters are also characters in this game: there is Lord J., a karate and judo master; Kazan, a ninja; and Wendy, a pro wrestler. You choose which two characters you want to control, and Dieter, the psycho bad guy who's got his secret Air Fortress outside the city, kidnaps the other three. Dieter wants these fighters so he can clone them and develop his own army for evil purposes, and it is up to whatever two characters you choose to fight your way through these clones to reach Dieter.","Brawl Brothers (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png","miximages/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).jpg","3dboxes/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png","marquees/snes/Brawl Brothers (NA).png"
"snes_breakthru","BreakThru!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-01","1994","1990s","Zoo","Spectrum Holobyte","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","60","3","BreakThru is a frenetic-paced puzzle that forces you to think fast. The fun starts with a clock and a solid wall of colored bricks. Eliminate the bricks by clicking on two or more neighboring bricks of the same color. Tear down wall after wall through six cities as you race the clock to raise your score. Watch out! Pesky spiders, annoying soda cans and obnoxious boulders are out to make life rough. Knock them out of action with rockets and dynamite before time runs out, so you can break throw h to the next wall.","BreakThru! (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","miximages/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","screenshots/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","backcovers/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png","marquees/snes/BreakThru! (NA).png"
"snes_breath-of-fire","Breath of Fire","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-08-01","1994","1990s","Capcom","Squaresoft","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","In a distant land, peace was maintained for thousands of years by a fearful dragon clan who could transform into powerful monsters. One day they discovered a goddess who could fulfill their every wish. Greed split the clan into Dark and Light Dragons, each battling the other to win her magic.

One member of the Light Dragons, along with seven of his companions, emerged to keep the opposing forces from destroying their world. Using six magical keys, they sealed the goddess into another realm.

Centuries have passed. The Dark Dragons are destroying the land in search of the keys. When they find the keys, they will once again release the magic goddess. Light Dragon... the time has come to draw your sword and fight for the future of your people.","Breath of Fire (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","miximages/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png","marquees/snes/Breath of Fire (NA).png"
"snes_breath-of-fire-ii","Breath of Fire II","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-04-25","1996","1990s","Capcom","Capcom","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","Ryu was a young boy who has memories of a strange village far away and a magical doorway which sucked him through. However those are only distant memories. Ryu and his best friend Bow are apprentices in the Ranger's Guild. As adventurers they take on posted jobs needed by the townspeople. However it isn't long before one job goes awry and Bow is accused of stealing a valuable item. In order to clear his friend's name and find the meaning of his dreams, Ryu will explore the world, eventually discovering the meaning of his dreams and hidden abilities inside himself.

Breath of Fire II is a role playing game. The majority of game is played from a top-down map, however battles are seen from an isometric view. Ryu will form parties from among 8 other characters, each with their own set of skills and powers that will help him discover the truth behind the mystery.","Breath of Fire II (NA).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","miximages/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png","marquees/snes/Breath of Fire II (NA).png"
"snes_brett-hull-hockey-95","Brett Hull Hockey 95","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Radical Entertainment","Accolade","Sports / Hockey","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","All the hard-hitting NHLPA players. True NHL-style stats. Real ice-grinding hockey action. In this game you're playing for keeps. Control the blue-line with guys like Leetch and Bourque. Blank-'em in the crease with guys like Richter and Irbe. Take it down the wing and into the slot behind scoring legends like Modano, Yzerman, Bure, and of course, Brett Hull. Can you make the cut? Only the stats will tell. Shots, checks, penalties, and passing percentages. Make it or miss, it's crunch time. And this time, it's for real.","Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Brett Hull Hockey '95 (NA).png"
"snes_brett-hull-hockey","Brett Hull Hockey","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Radical Entertainment","Sony Imagesoft","Sports / Hockey","Sports","1","1","1","50","2.5","Brett Hull Hockey lets the player take control of NHL great Brett Hull along with 600 NHLPA players and all of the NHL teams of the time including their respective names and logos.  The player can choose to play in an Exhibition mode either against the computer A.I. or a friend, Playoffs or in Season mode with three different length options (a full season, half a season or an 11-game season).  The game simulates hockey action including slap shots, body checks, hat tricks among many other real-life hockey moves.  Al Michaels also lends his voice talents to the game for in-game commentary.","Brett Hull Hockey (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","miximages/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png","marquees/snes/Brett Hull Hockey (NA).png"
"snes_bronkie-the-bronchiasaurus","Bronkie the Bronchiasaurus","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-01","1995","1990s","WaveQuest","Raya Systems","Adventure","Adventure","1-2","1","2","40","2","Years ago, meteors struck San Saurian, filling the air with thick and filthy dust. So a mighty wind machine was made to help everyone breathe. But Mr. Rexo has stolen the parts for the machine, forcing other dinosaurs to guard the pieces!

