"snes_clay-fighter","Clay Fighter","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-05-26","1994","1990s","Visual Concepts","Interplay","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Clay Fighter is a 2D fighting game released in which the characters, as the name suggests, are made completely out of clay.  This allows for interesting moves and stylized graphics.  The zany roster includes: Bad Mr. Frosty, a snowman; Taffy, a piece of stretchable candy; Blob, a character who can morph into different shapes; Blue Suede Goo, an Elvis knock-off; Ickybod Clay, a pumpkin-headed ghost; Helga, an opera singer; and Bonker, the crazed clown. Each character also has their own level and individual taunts.","Clay Fighter (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","miximages/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png","marquees/snes/Clay Fighter (NA).png"
"snes_clay-fighter-tournament-edition","Clay Fighter : Tournament Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-22","1994","1990s","Visual Concepts","Interplay","Fighting","Fighting","1-8","1","8","50","2.5","The Tournament Edition of Clay Fighter fixes some glitches and adds new features to the original 2D fighting game. Most scenarios were changed or redone, the graphics are brighter and the gameplay is faster. The characters can now perform three and four-hit combos. More voice-overs and a new introduction cut-scene were added.

