"snes_clay-fighter-2-judgment-clay","Clay Fighter 2 : Judgment Clay","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-05-23","1995","1990s","Interplay","Interplay","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Bad Mister Frosty is buffed up and faster than greased lightning. This surly snowman has mayhem on his mind... but there's some bunny new in town with a hare-trigger temper. You can bet the fur will fly as this wild hare unleashes a barrage of blistering rabbit punches on Bad Mister Frosty. Could there be a new top bunny in town, or will he get his cottontail kicked?","Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","miximages/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png","marquees/snes/Clay Fighter 2 - Judgment Clay (NA).png"
"snes_claymates","Claymates","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-20","1993","1990s","Visual Concepts","Interplay","Platform","Platformer","1-8","1","8","70","3.5","From the creators of Clay Fighter comes a game about a shape-shifting ball of clay.  You play as a boy named Clayton, whose father has developed a serum to turn humans into animals.  However, an evil shaman desires this serum, and when he is denied ownership of it, he kidnaps Clayton's father and turns Clayton into a ball of clay.  It's up to the unlikely hero to rescue his father, the serum, and the world!

The game is a side-scrolling platformer where you gain power-ups that let you transform into various forms to help you reach the end of the level.  After each level, you are placed on the world map and given several robots who blindly walk forward until they hit an obstacle, then turn at a right angle and continue on their way.  It's up to you to manipulate them to help you clear a way to the next level, where more challenges await.","Claymates (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Claymates (NA).png","miximages/snes/Claymates (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Claymates (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Claymates (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Claymates (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Claymates (NA).png","marquees/snes/Claymates (NA).png"
"snes_cliffhanger","Cliffhanger","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-10","1993","1990s","Malibu Games","Sony Imagesoft","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","40","2","Standard side-scrolling fighter based off of the Stallone film of the same name. Sly must fight thugs and the elements as he tracks down suitcases of stolen cash dropped around the peaks of the Rockies. Combat follows the Final Fight standard, broken up by some mountain climbing and running (or 3-D snowboarding on the Sega CD) from avalanches. 

Enemies are the standard brawler crooks, occasionally carrying guns and knives the player can pick up. The game tends to follow a pattern of having you deal with a natural hazard (scaling a cliff, leaping over gaps), then locking the screen down for a fighting segment, nature again, fighting again, etc. The available fighting moves is limited, compared to other games of this type, and the ability to hit an enemy character is noticeably less accurate.

The plot is identical to the film, with levels based off of, or inspired by, scenes in the movie. Animated cutscenes move the story along on the cartridge systems, while brief clips from the film play between levels on the Sega CD.","Cliffhanger (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","miximages/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png","marquees/snes/Cliffhanger (NA).png"
"snes_clock-tower","Clock Tower","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-14","1995","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Adventure / Survival Horror","Adventure","1","1","1","90","4.5","Jennifer and her friends are adopted by a nice lady named Mary one day. They expect to be going to a wonderful new home, at the Barrows Mansion. There they will live with Mary and Mr. Barrows. Unfortunately, something goes terribly wrong and Jennifer's friends are showing up dead one by one.  While this is happening, Mary is missing and Jennifer ends up being chased by a crazed psychopath known only as...Scissorman. 

Now she must survive and get out of the mansion in this point-and-click horror adventure... Being a teenage girl, you have no special abilities at all, just your wits and your will to survive, there are a few enemies that can kill you instantly, but Scissorman is the true horror that will give you trouble.","Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","3.13","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Clock Tower (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_clockwerx","Clockwerx","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-08","1995","1990s","Axes Art Amuse","Tokuma Shoten","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","70","3.5","The goal of the game is to navigate a screen full of nodes to reach a specific point. Along the way are various traps that have a fixed patrol around the screen. The player walks clockwise or anti-clockwise around each node, and can move to another at the moment when their head is touching the node in question. They can also switch direction. By using these two abilities, the player can move across each screen, carefully avoiding obstacles and reaching the end.","Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","miximages/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","screenshots/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","titlescreens/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","3dboxes/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","backcovers/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png","marquees/snes/Clockwerx (English Translated by MrRichard999, Rev 0.75).png"
"snes_clue","Clue","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-07-01","1992","1990s","Sculptured Software","Parker Brothers","Board game","Board / Casual","1-6","1","6","50","2.5","Who killed Mr. Boddy? Was it Colonel Mustard, in the Kitchen, with the Lead Pipe? All the deductive fun of the classic mystery game comes to life with hundreds of animated vignettes, crisp graphics, bright colors, and refined sound effects and music of advanced 16-bit technology. Playing alone or with up to five human or computer opponents, you'll solve a new CLUEÂ® mystery every time you play, as you choose one of five ""ranks"" and work up from Amateur to Detective.

So enter Mr. Boddy's mansion and start collecting evidence from the animated vignettes that show Suspects skulking through Rooms and leaving fingerprints on Weapons. When you've collected enough clues, make your Accusation of Whodunit? Where? With which Weapon? If you're right, you'll see the murder reenacted before your very eyes!","Clue (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Clue (NA).png","miximages/snes/Clue (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Clue (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Clue (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Clue (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Clue (NA).png","marquees/snes/Clue (NA).png"
