"snes_cu-on-pa-sfc","Cu-On-Pa SFC","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-12-20","1996","1990s","T&amp;E Soft","T&amp;E Soft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","80","4","Cu-On-Pa is a puzzle game in which the player takes control of a cube, the object being to roll this cube over squares of a particular color. If the top face of the cube matches the colour of the square, it is collected; claim enough squares to move onto the next level.

Essentially, this is a Super Famicom port of the 1995 PC game Endorfun - in fact, Cu-On-Pa is licensed from Endorfun. Cu-On-Pa features none of the new-age stylings of the earlier game, instead opting for a more traditional puzzle game aesthetic. This version offers a couple of new features over Endorfun: there is an Easy Mode, which reduces the available colors from six down to three; and there is also a Puzzle Mode which gives the player predefined boards to solve, and a limited number of moves to do so.","Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Cu-On-Pa SFC (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1).png"
"snes_cutthroat-island","Cutthroat Island","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-02-22","1996","1990s","Software Creations","Acclaim Entertainment","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","40","2","In this game you play the role of a pirate lady called Morgan who was given a piece of a map by her father before he died. In the game you set out to find more pieces of the map so that you can find the hidden treasure buried on Cutthroat Island. The gameplay involves you scrolling along the screen and sword fighting pirates and other scoundrels one on one with various different attacks. As you progress you unlock more combos. This game is based on the film by the same name.","CutThroat Island (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","miximages/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","screenshots/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","backcovers/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png","marquees/snes/CutThroat Island (NA).png"
"snes_cyber-knight","Cyber Knight","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-10-30","1992","1990s","Advance Communication Company","Tonkin House","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","60","3","Cyber Knight is an RPG with a science-fiction theme of being lost in an alien galaxy. The game takes place in a top-down view for movement on planets and areas, a side-view for combat sequences and a first person menu system when aboard the Swordfish starship. The Swordfish can travel between stars, scanning worlds for information. If the ship is able to land on a planet, three crew members piloting three Modules (giant robots) can be selected to debark and explore the planet. Many planets will have towns or people living on them which can be talked to in order to uncover information. Different quests are assigned in order to find the items necessary to progress. There is no system of currency or buying items. Instead, many defeated Berserkers leave behind ""NeoParts"", which can be brought back to the Swordfish's lab. Analysis of these Neo parts unlocks enhances statistics (endurance, agility, accuracy, etc) for the Modules and new weapons for them to carry","Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Cyber Knight (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_cyber-knight-2-chikyuu-teikoku-no-yabou","Cyber Knight 2 - Chikyuu Teikoku No Yabou","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-08-26","1994","1990s","Group SNE","Tonkin House","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","80","4","Cyber Knight II is an RPG with science-fiction themes. As in the first game, much of the game takes place in a top-down view for movement on planets and areas, a side-view for combat sequences and a first person menu system when aboard the Galvodirge starship. The Galvodirge can travel between stars, scanning worlds for information. If the ship is able to land on a planet, the crew can debark either on foot or using combat modules (mechs). Some areas are only accessible using modules and others (such as towns) do not allow the use of these war machines. Many planets will have towns or people living on them which can be talked to in order to uncover information. Different quests are assigned in order to find the items necessary to progress. There is no system of currency or buying items. Instead, many defeated enemies leave behind ""NeoParts"", which can be brought back to the Swordfish's lab.","Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","miximages/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","screenshots/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","titlescreens/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","3dboxes/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","backcovers/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","marquees/snes/Cyber Knight II - Chikyuu Teikoku no Yabou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png"
