"snes_dolucky-no-a-league-soccer","Dolucky No A.league Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-08","1994","1990s","Zoom","Imagineer","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","","","This game features a cat called Dolucky (the main character of the video game series) and other cartoonish animals such as dogs, rabbits and bears. The game structure has similarities with Battle Soccer: Field no Hasha, Rockman's Soccer or Nintendo World Cup.","Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","miximages/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png","marquees/snes/Dolucky no A.League Soccer (JP).png"
"snes_dolucky-no-kusayakiu","Dolucky No Kusayakiu","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-17","1993","1990s","Zoom","Imagineer","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Neco Dolucky is a cool cat from New York City. He enjoys soul music and dancing, and loves nothing more than a cool, refreshing Coca Cola Classic. One day he and his other animal friends were bored, so they decided to start a baseball league. One can assume their sponsor is the Coca Cola Corporation... Suddenly, they receive a challenge via telegram from the ""Tab Clear Empire Hellthunder Destroyers!"" Of course they can't back down, that wouldn't be TOUGH. Fight on through baseball, boys!

Lead The Coca Cola Doluckies to victory!","Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","miximages/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png","marquees/snes/Dolucky no Kusayakiu (JP).png"
"snes_dolucky-no-puzzle-tour-94","Dolucky No Puzzle Tour '94","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-28","1994","1990s","Zoom","Imagineer","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 is a puzzle game featuring Zoom Inc.'s mascot character Dolucky the cat. It was released for the Super Famicom in 1994 and would be the last ever game featuring Dolucky. The game is a mix of Bust-a-Move and Tetris, where the goal is to fire colored blocks at an encroaching wave of same. If five blocks of the same color are touching, they vanish. Certain blocks, gray in color, cannot be removed unless they're touching five colored blocks as they vanish: the goal is to quickly fire five blocks to remove these before they reach the player character at the bottom of the screen. There are also random power-ups that can be acquired. The blocks have facial expressions that change depending on the number of similar blocks they're touching, allowing the player to see how close they are to clearing them if the top of the screen cuts it off. Smiling or grinning suggests that there's three or four in contact.","Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Dolucky no Puzzle Tour '94 (JP).png"
"snes_donald-duck-no-mahou-no-boushi","Donald Duck No Mahou No Boushi","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-08-11","1995","1990s","SAS Sakata","Epoch","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (""Donald Duck's The Magic Hat"" or ""Donald Duck in The Magic Hat"") is a Super Famicom platformer that features the irascible Disney character Donald Duck as he first attempts to raise money to buy the eponymous magic hat for his girlfriend Daisy, and then gets involved in more misadventures due to the headwear.

The game has an open structure where the player can tackle stages in any order: the first group include a bunch of oddjobs that Donald can perform to raise cash, from taking a paper delivery job to washing windows to taking part in an obstacle course for prize money.

The game is one of a handful published by Epoch that was compatible with their Barcode Battler II device via a special cable. Scanning in barcodes adds new content to the game.","Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","miximages/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","screenshots/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","titlescreens/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","3dboxes/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","backcovers/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png","marquees/snes/Donald Duck no Mahou no Boushi (English Translated by Gorgyrip).png"
"snes_donkey-kong-country","Donkey Kong Country","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-18","1994","1990s","Rareware","Nintendo","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Help Donkey Kong and Diddy Kong get back those stolen bananas!After a dark and stormy night, Donkey Kong finds all of his bananas stolen by K. Rool and his reptilian crew of Kremlings! Armed with chest-pounding muscle, mighty barrel rolls, and awesome vine-swinging skills, Donkey Kong and Diddy Kong set out to face their adversaries! Play solo, compete with a friend, or play cooperatively with a friend in over 100 levels filled with collectibles and hidden bonus levels. With the help of Donkey Kong's quirky family, animal friends, and your fast reflexes, our dynamic duo will prove to be an unstoppable force. Time to save those bananas!","Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","miximages/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","screenshots/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","titlescreens/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","3dboxes/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","backcovers/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png","marquees/snes/Donkey Kong Country (NA, Rev 2).png"
"snes_donkey-kong-country-2-diddy-s-kong-quest","Donkey Kong Country 2 : Diddy's Kong Quest","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-11-14","1995","1990s","Rareware","Nintendo","Platform / Run &amp; Jump","Platformer","1-2","1","2","100","5","Donkey Kong has been kong-napped by the nasty K.Rool and the Kremlings, and it is up to Diddy Kong and his girl-friend Dixie Kong to save him.

All the familiar enemies and helpful friends return, along with some new characters, including the wise Wrinkly Kong who will teach you some important lessons in gameplay. Again the emphasis is on banana collecting, where as every 100 bananas makes one extra life. Apart from beating K. Rool and rescuing Donkey Kong, there are extra missions that can be completed. Collect enough K. Rool Krem Coins to open up the routes to the Lost World, while every level has a hidden Hero Coin to collect.","Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Donkey Kong Country 2 - Diddy's Kong Quest (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_donkey-kong-country-3-dixie-kong-s-double-trouble","Donkey Kong Country 3 : Dixie Kong's Double Trouble!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-12-19","1996","1990s","Rareware","Nintendo","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","This time both Donkey Kong and Diddy Kong have been kong-napped by a mysterious new leader of the Kremlings, and it's up to Dixie and new team mate Kiddy Kong to save the day.

