"snes_doom","Doom","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-10-25","1995","1990s","Sculptured Software","Ocean","Shooter / FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","60","3","The Union Aerospace Corporation has been experimenting with teleportation technology on the moons of Mars, Phobos and Deimos. After the initial breakthroughs, something goes wrong. It seems the scientists have opened a direct gateway to hell. The Phobos base is overrun with demonic creatures, and Deimos simply vanishes. A squad of marines is sent to Phobos, but all except one are quickly annihilated. The surviving marine must face the demons alone.","Doom (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Doom (NA).png","miximages/snes/Doom (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Doom (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Doom (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Doom (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Doom (NA).png","marquees/snes/Doom (NA).png"
"snes_doom-troopers-mutant-chronicles","Doom Troopers : Mutant Chronicles","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-11-01","1995","1990s","Adrenalin Interactive","Playmates Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","40","2","Based on the popular role-playing and card game, DOOM TROOPERS casts you as a fearless commando who's been commissioned to save the world from an invading force of mutants. Play as either Mitch Hunter or Max Steiner as you embark on the most important mission of your life--the complete annihilation of the Dark Legion. Work your way through eight detailed levels filled with all kinds of evil and dangerous mutants, as you unload with a barrage of high-powered weapons that are readily available. If the pressure is a little too much for you to handle alone, recruit a friend and try to eliminate the Dark Legion together. The world is in grave danger, and only the Doom Troopers can make things right.","Doom Troopers (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","miximages/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png","marquees/snes/Doom Troopers (NA).png"
"snes_doomsday-warrior","Doomsday Warrior","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Laser Soft","Renovation Products","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","40","2","The Doom Squad is a group of fighters under the control of an evil wizard. They threaten earth and bring destruction. One of the Doom Squad members betrays his group and becomes the Doomsday Warrior. This warrior must then defeat the other members of the Squad and finally the wizard controlling it all.

Doomsday Warrior is a fighting game. Choosing one of the Doom Squad members to become to the Doomsday warriors, you must defeat your opponents. Each character has the ability to punch, kick, jump and unleash a special move (usually by being close to the enemy and using either jump, kick or punch). The better the skill in fighting, the more ability points are earned. These ability points can be used to improve various areas of the fighter after battle.","Doomsday Warrior (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","miximages/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png","marquees/snes/Doomsday Warrior (NA).png"
"snes_doraemon-4-nobita-to-tsuki-no-oukoku","Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-15","1995","1990s","Agenda","Epoch","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","This is a platform action game that is somewhat similar to  Super Mario World. You travel on a world map and enter various platform locations. Before each level, you can choose to play as either Doraemon, Nobita, or other four available characters. You can jump on enemies' heads or shoot at them with various weapons to eliminate them. There are many items and upgrades scattered around the levels, and sometimes it is possible to power-up by using two characters simultaneously.","Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","miximages/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","screenshots/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","titlescreens/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","3dboxes/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","backcovers/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png","marquees/snes/Doraemon 4 - Nobita to Tsuki no Oukoku (English Translated by Sgt. Bowhack, Rev 0.94b).png"
"snes_do-re-mi-fantasy-milon-no-dokidoki-daibouken","Do-re-mi Fantasy - Milon No Dokidoki Daibouken","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-03-22","1996","1990s","Hudson Soft","Hudson Soft","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","A young boy named Milon sets off to save Alis, his fairy friend, after she was captured by the evil sorcerer Amon. He later learns that the only way to defeat Amon is by collecting five legendary instruments which Amon has stolen.  The sorcerer placed a curse on these instruments so that their true powers cannot be used and then left them in the hands of his minions.  The only way to lift the curse is by collecting five stars.

Armed with only his bubble shooter, Milon must retrieve the legendary instruments, lift their curses and use their powers to defeat Amon and rescue Alis.

Traveling through many different worlds starting with the forest, Milon will be confronted by many enemies. Milon can either shoot bubbles to trap and send his enemies away, or he can jump and flatten his enemies temporarily turning them into a platform for him to walk across.  

Milon has three different ""outfits"": red, blue, and green.  With the green outfit, Milon can withstand three hits.  Each time he gets hit, he will be downgraded a color - green to blue, blue to red.  If he gets hit with the red outfit, he will die and have to start the level over.

By collecting 100 music notes, Milon will get an extra life.  There are also other useful items to get like bubble gum that will save Milon once if he were to fall, a special bubble shooter that let's him shoot multiple bubbles at once and a star that makes Milon temporarily invincible so that he can defeat enemies simply by running at them.","DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).sfc","SFC","2.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","miximages/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","screenshots/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","titlescreens/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","3dboxes/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","backcovers/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png","marquees/snes/DoReMi Fantasy - Milon no DokiDoki Daibouken (English Translated by Gaijin Productions and RPGOne, Rev 1.3).png"
"snes_dorke-amp-ymp","Dorke &amp; Ymp","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2015-08-06","2015","2010s","Norsehelm Production","Piko Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","","","Dorke &amp; Ymp will be an elegant platformer with 4 worlds, a plethora of items and countless enemies. The clever Dorke is an apprentice of a rather sketchy wizard, and a showdown between the two is inevitable.","Dorke &amp; Ymp (NA).sfc","SFC","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
"snes_dossun-ganseki-battle","Dossun ! Ganseki Battle","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-16","1994","1990s","I'Max","I'Max","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","A falling block puzzle game  in a pseudo-medieval fantasy setting that pits two characters against each other in an abstract form of combat that is quite similar to games like Columns. Combining at least three matching symbols in a vertical, horizontal or diagonal line does not only clear them off the screen, but also deals damage to an opponent. This means that players do not only have to keep their game area clear, but also pay attention to their characters health bar. Once a block touches the top of the screen or the health bar is diminished the game ends.

There are four different icons that have different effects when combined:
Books, swords and rocks deal damage to an opponent by attacking with fireballs, dragons or swords.
Bottles heal a certain amount of health.
Purple blocks have no effect, but clog up the screen nonetheless.

Chain reactions result in particularly powerful attacks or place one or more grey blocks inside the opponents area. They can be destroyed just like ordinary blocks, but they always stay in the same spot and do not fall down.

More complex chain reactions give access to special attacks, up to three of which can be held and activated with the shoulder buttons. Special attacks have different effects that include clearing all purple blocks, using all potions and clearing the bottom three lines.","Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","miximages/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","screenshots/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","titlescreens/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","3dboxes/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","backcovers/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","marquees/snes/Dossun! Ganseki Battle (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png"
