"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-butouden","Dragon Ball Z : Super Butouden","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-30","1993","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","60","3","Dragon Ball Z: Super Butōden was the first fighting game based on the Dragon Ball Z franchise and the first to introduce the split-screen mode to the games, where the screen is split in two whenever one of the two combatants moves away too far to keep them both shown in a single screen. This title features the adventures of Goku from the battle against Piccolo in the martial arts tournament to the conclusion of the Cell Games.","Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.98).png"
"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-butouden-2","Dragon Ball Z Super Butouden 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-01","1994","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Dragon Ball Z: Super Butouden 2 is a fighting game that chronicles the events that take place during the battle against Perfect Cell, and includes a side story about Bojack and his henchmen (who Gohan, Trunks, Piccolo and Vegita fought in the ""Bojack Unbound"" movie), and Broli, the Legendary Super Saiyan. You can play as SSJ2 Gohan, Piccolo, Vegeta, Future Trunks, Perfect Cell, Cell Jr., Bojack or Zangya. Goku and Broli will be also available after you enter a secret code.","Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 2 (English Translated by Commando Ginyu).png"
"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-butouden-3","Dragon Ball Z Super Butouden 3","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-25","1995","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","60","3","Dragon Ball Z: Super Butouden 3 (known as Dragon Ball Z: Ultime Menace in France) is the last installment to the Super Butoden series for the SNES, which in this occasion is based on the Majin Buu saga. Avaliable charachers are Goku, Goten, Kid Trunks, Majin Vegita, Junior Gohan, Kaiohshin, Majin Boo, Darbura and C-18, plus another one available as a secret character: Future Trunks.

Split screen mode is maintained, but now you can now fly up or down while on the same screen as your opponent. You can also struggle with your rival pushing with your arms together to test your button smashing abilities, or execute new Meteor Combos. Scenarios will also be different (mainly based on Buu saga) and will include alternative versions of themselves with different times of the day as well.","Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Butouden 3 (English Translated by DragonBallZ Translations and Vice Translations, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-gokuden-kakusei-hen","Dragon Ball Z Super Gokuden - Kakusei-Hen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-22","1995","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","This is a direct sequel to the  first ""interactive fighter"" for SNES, based on the popular manga/animé series Dragon Ball. The game picks up the story where it ended in the previous game, and continues through Piccolo, Saiyajin, and Freezer sagas of the manga. After the battle with the Demon King (Daimaou) Piccolo, the twenty-third World Martial Arts Tournament is about to begin. But to the amazement of the hero Son Goku and his friends, their archrival Piccolo appears during the tournament, so that it quickly turns into a genuine battle.","Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Kakusei Hen (English Translated by Commando Ginew).png"
"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-gokuden-totsugeki-hen","Dragon Ball Z Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-03-24","1995","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","The first of the two ""interactive fighters"" for SNES based on the famous manga series Dragon Ball. ""Totsugeki Hen"" tells the story of the hero, Son Goku, following the first volume of the manga. The boy Son Goku meets a mysterious girl named Bulma, and she sends him on a mission to obtain the magical Dragon Balls. Naturally, Bulma is not the only one needing those Balls, so that the young hero will soon have to face and defeat some bad guys, including his first true rival Piccolo.","Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Gokuden - Totsugeki Hen (English Translated by Kakkoii Translations, Rev 0.98 With Anime Names).png"
"snes_dragon-ball-z-super-saiya-densetsu","Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-25","1992","1990s","TOSE","Bandai","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","50","2.5","Cho Saiya Densetsu is based on the popular manga/animé series Dragon Ball. It follows the events described in the beginning of Dragon Ball Z, the second story block, which tells about the connection of the hero Son Goku with a powerful alien race, and new mighty foes from far away planets. The game starts just where the tale of Dragon Ball begins. Son Goku goes to meet his friends, but is stopped by a mysterious stranger named Raditz who tells Son Goku they are relatives. Raditz demands from him to destroy humanity, and as Son Goku refuses, takes his son Son Gohan hostage. To rescue his son, Son Goku joins forces with his arch-rival, the Demon King Piccolo, who obviously has his own plans concerning Raditz. And thus begins the story during which Son Goku will learn of his true origin...","Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Ball Z - Super Saiya Densetsu (English Translated by Klepto Software, Rev 1.02).png"
"snes_dragon-quest-1-and-2","Dragon Quest 1 And 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-18","1993","1990s","Chunsoft","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","This is a remake of two classic NES RPGs - an exclusively Japanese release of the two first Dragon Quest titles on one cartridge.

