"snes_dragon-quest-3-soshite-densetsu-e","Dragon Quest 3 - Soshite Densetsu E...","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-12-06","1996","1990s","Heart Beat","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","Dragon Warrior III is the concluding game of the first Dragon Quest/Dragon Warrior trilogy, and its story takes us back to the time period of the legendary Erdrick (also known as Loto), the ancestor of the first game's hero. You are the son of a powerful warrior Ortega, skillful in physical combat and spellcasting. Your father went out to fight the evil Baramos, who is responsible for the appearance of monsters in your region, and never returned. You are sent by the king on a quest to continue your father's brave deeds and to defeat Baramos.","Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).sfc","SFC","6","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Quest III - Soshite Densetsu e... (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1 With Bugfixes by Rod Merida, Rev 1c).png"
"snes_dragon-quest-5-tenkuu-no-hanayome","Dragon Quest 5 - Tenkuu No Hanayome","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-09-27","1992","1990s","Chunsoft","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","""Dragon Quest V"" is a party RPG with turn-based combat, and battles viewed from 1st person perspective, just like all its predecessors. Your party roams about the world, fighting random enemies, performing quests, and defeating bosses. The novelty is in the game's unusual story, which spans almost a lifetime of the hero.","Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Quest V - Tenkuu no Hanayome (English Translated by DeJap and Partial Translations, Rev 2.01 Final).png"
"snes_dragon-quest-6-maboroshi-no-daichi","Dragon Quest 6 - Maboroshi No Daichi","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-09","1995","1990s","Heart Beat","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","You and two of your friends decide to attack the Archenemy - the evil Mudo - in his castle. But as you reach his throne, he attacks you and send the three friends into three different places...

Was this just a dream? You have just fallen out of your bed dreaming! It's time to go to the village elder, to get a seemingly simple assignment - to sell some goods at a bazaar in the nearest town. But soon the hero will discover his dream was not so far away from reality...

""Dragon Quest VI"" is the last SNES game of the Dragon Quest series (called ""Dragon Warrior"" in US). It is a party RPG with turn-based combat and battles viewed from 1st person perspective. Not much has changed since the NES days of Dragon Quest - gameplay style, setting, and even menu layout seem almost identical to those of the early classics. Like its immediate predecessor  Dragon Quest V, this game was never released outside Japan.","Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","miximages/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","screenshots/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","titlescreens/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","3dboxes/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","backcovers/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png","marquees/snes/Dragon Quest VI - Maboroshi no Daichi (English Translated by NoPrgress, Rev 0.90b2).png"
