"snes_dynamic-stadium","Dynamic Stadium","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-26","1993","1990s","Electronics Application","Sammy Corporation","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Dynamic Stadium is a baseball game from Eleca/Electronics Application released exclusively for the Super Famicom. While adopting the same behind-the-batter perspective as Namco's Famista series, Dynamic Stadium presents its athletes as comic book heroes rather than chibi figures, making them absurdly buff and frequently featuring action shots of them catching fly-balls and narrowly making it to base before being caught out. ""Safe!"" and ""Out!"" calls are presented as spiky word balloons.

