"snes_fifa-international-soccer","FIFA International Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","EA Sports","EA Sports","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-5","1","5","70","3.5","The game that started the best-selling series licensed by football's world governing body, this first installment in the long running series used a dimetric (colloquially known as ""isometric"") viewpoint, previously unusual in football games but quickly imitated by several titles. The televisual presentation, one of the unique points of the early EA Sports titles, with hosts introducing the matches, was another thing making the game stand out from a market dominated by Sensible Soccer and Kick Off games.","FIFA International Soccer (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","miximages/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","screenshots/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","backcovers/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png","marquees/snes/FIFA International Soccer (NA).png"
