"snes_fire-emblem-monsh-no-nazo","Fire Emblem - Monshô No Nazo","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-21","1994","1990s","Intelligent Systems","Nintendo","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","A remake and expansion of the first NES/Famicom Fire Emblem, Marth must face the betrayal if Hardin and an old enemy he thought long vanquished, the Dragon King Medeus.

Book 1 of the game is essentially a remake of the first NES game. Book 2 continues the story with the same characters.

This game expands the series, however it drops explorable towns and the navigation through a world map which was introduced in Fire Emblem: Gaiden. New features include the ability to dismount the horse and pegasus mounted units, to allow the riders to fight indoors if needed.","Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","miximages/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","screenshots/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","titlescreens/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","3dboxes/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","backcovers/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png","marquees/snes/Fire Emblem - Monshou no Nazo (English Translated by RPGuy96 and VincentASM, Rev 0.98 With Updates by Quirino, Rev 0.14 and Fixes by RobertTheSable, Rev 0.22).png"
"snes_fire-emblem-seisen-no-keifu","Fire Emblem - Seisen No Keifu","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-05-14","1996","1990s","Intelligent Systems","Nintendo","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","100","5","The fourth installment in the popular strategy series, set in the continent of Jugdral, southeast of Akaneia. The game's first fifth chapters follow the Prince of Chalphy, Sigurd -- from there, his son Celis becomes the protagonist. The game uses the same turn-based strategy gameplay as its predecessors, but changes up the promotion system by making it entirely level-based, adds RPG-style status effects, and introduces the concept of the weapons triangle, in that a sword is strong against an axe, spear against the sword, and axe against the spear. Seisen no Keifu also featured much larger maps than previous titles (though a lower number of them -- 12 in all) and a handful of new units, such as the Troubadour, Dragon Master, and Falcon Knight. The game was released late in the Super Famicom's lifecycle in Japan and never published internationally.","Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).sfc","SFC","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","miximages/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","screenshots/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","titlescreens/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","3dboxes/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","backcovers/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png","marquees/snes/Fire Emblem - Seisen no Keifu (English Translated by Fire Emblem 4 Translation Team, Rev 20160707 Beta 7).png"
"snes_fire-emblem-thracia-776","Fire Emblem - Thracia 776","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2000-01-21","2000","2000s","Intelligent Systems","Nintendo","Tactical RPG","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Thracia 776 continues the Fire Emblem story with a midquel or a ""meanwhile"" setting. The events transpire during  Fire Emblem: Seisen no Keifu and the game contains many of the same characters from that game, while featuring cameos of many more. 

At its most simple the story is of Prince Leaf of Lenster's struggle to free his native land from two forces, the Grandbell Empire and the Loptus religion.

Features introduced into this part of the series include fog of war and night maps with limited vision, this requires characters to use torches and wands to light their way. Also the capture command which allowed enemies to be subdued and their weapons taken.","Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).sfc","SFC","6","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","miximages/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","screenshots/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","titlescreens/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","3dboxes/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","backcovers/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png","marquees/snes/Fire Emblem - Thracia 776 (English Translated by Cirosan, Rev 1.04 - Lil' Manster Version by Miacis, Rev 1.08).png"
"snes_fire-pro-joshi-all-star-dream-slam","Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-22","1994","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Fire Pro Joshi All-Star Dream Slam (also known as Zen-Nippon Joshi Pro Wrestling Kounin: Fire Pro Joshi All-Star Dream Slam) is an all-female wrestling game from Human Entertainment and uses their 16-bit isometric Fire Pro Wrestling engine. The wrestlers are all taken from the Zen-Nippon Joshi Pro Wrestling (""All Japan Women's Pro Wrestling"") circuit, an exclusively female wrestling promotion that lasted for many years in Japan.

As with prior Fire Pro Wrestling games, the mechanics behind the moves, pins and submissions rely more on timing and rhythm than button-mashing. Each bout is depicted with an isometric perspective, and various configurations of single-player and two-player controls are available for one-on-one matches and tag teams. The game features 18 pre-generated wrestlers and six create-a-wrestler slots.","Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","miximages/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png","marquees/snes/Fire Pro Joshi - All Star Dream Slam (JP).png"
