"snes_super-battletank","Super Battletank","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-03-18","1993","1990s","Imagineering","Absolute Entertainment","Unknown","Unknown","1-2","1","2","60","3","Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank puts you inside the cockpit of an M1 Abrams during the Gulf War. As part of Operation Desert Storm, you navigate wide mission areas in Kuwait from a first-person view. Your goal is to locate and destroy enemy targets. Realistic controls let you accelerate, rotate the tank and turret, fire weapons, and consult the map. In addition to the main cannon, you can use a powerful laser or deploy a smoke screen to escape. Precision, navigation, and tactics are key to mission success.","Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Garry Kitchen's Super Battletank - War in the Gulf (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_gegege-no-kitarou-fukkatsu-tenma-daiou","Gegege No Kitarou - Fukkatsu! Tenma Daiou","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-02-05","1993","1990s","Bandai","Bandai","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","GeGeGe no Kitarou: Fukkatsu! Tenma Daiou (""GeGeGe no Kitarou: Revival! Great King Tenma"") is a side-scrolling action game based on the GeGeGe no Kitarou license. Kitarou, a youkai boy and the last surviving member of the Ghost Tribe, is tasked with defeating the cocoon form of the dormant Great King Tenma before he can revive and destroy the world of humans.


Each stage is set up as a series of boss fights against notable youkai from the franchise. The player must learn their tactics and defeat them while preserving as much of their health as possible, as they will often have to fight several bosses in a row without being able to heal. There's also the occasional action sequence, such as a vaguely shoot 'em up part that leads to a tough fight against a colossal enemy.


