"snes_go-go-ackman","Go Go Ackman","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-23","1994","1990s","Banpresto","Banpresto","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","Ackman is not what one would call a good person. His job is to murder and steal souls for the Demon Lord. The angel Tenshi has taken it upon himself to put an end to Ackman's nefarious ways, and sends an army of angels and hired assassins to take out Ackman for good. It's just as well, because Ackman was getting bored without anyone to kill.

Go Go Ackman is a scrolling platformer starring the titular Ackman. Ackman can punch and charge up a ranged wave of energy, and he can also jump on some enemies to stun them before running into them and turning them into a sliding projectile. Ackman can hold up to three bombs that can clear the screen of enemies, and can also hold a weapon, either a sword, boomerang, or pistol, but it will be lost if Ackman is hit. Levels are linear, but do allow some exploration to find weapons and items hidden off the beaten road.","Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","miximages/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","screenshots/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","titlescreens/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","3dboxes/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","backcovers/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png","marquees/snes/Go Go Ackman (English Translated by Ackman Translations).png"
"snes_go-go-ackman-2","Go Go Ackman 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-07-21","1995","1990s","Banpresto","Banpresto","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","Go Go Ackman 2 is mostly the same as its predecessor, with a few small tweaks. The angel Tenshi is still determined to end Ackman's nefarious ways, and this time he has enlisted the help of the angelic rock band Metal Angel. Ackman still murders at whim and has his companion Godon collect the souls of his slain, but this time Ackman can keep the weapons he finds, either sword, boomerang, or gun. Each weapon can be upgraded twice, but upgrades will be lost if Ackman is hit or finds a new weapon. Ackman can also now throw smaller enemies, although he can't move while holding them.

Ackman 2 takes place over 5 stages filled with new bosses and enemies.","Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Go Go Ackman 2 (English Translated by Anime_World, Bunkai, and Retroman, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_go-go-ackman-3","Go Go Ackman 3","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-15","1995","1990s","Banpresto","Banpresto","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","90","4.5","Yet again Tenshi is hard at work on finding a way to kill off Ackman for good. But, what's this, it seems there's been a shake up in the chain of command, and now Tenshi is wanted by the Angel Police! Will Tenshi be able to clear his good name? Who's really pulling the strings here? And, most importantly, does Ackman care about any of this at all?

The last of the Ackman games, Go Go Ackman 3 makes very few changes from Go Go Ackman 2, although Tenshi is now a playable character. Both Ackman and Tenshi can be switched between at special points in a level, but they share the same health meter and weapon. Unlike Ackman Tenshi can fly, but as he is an angel he can not collect the souls of enemies he kills. Souls have changed too, and are now used as currency in shops where Ackman can buy temporary powerups or healing. Finally Ackman has lost the ability to slide enemies along the ground, but he can now move while holding a stunned enemy.","Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","miximages/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","screenshots/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","titlescreens/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","3dboxes/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","backcovers/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png","marquees/snes/Go Go Ackman 3 (English Translated by Reld, Rev 20200105).png"
