"snes_hagane-the-final-conflict","Hagane : The Final Conflict","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-06-01","1995","1990s","CAProduction","Hudson Soft","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Hagane: The Final Conflict pulls you into a hidden war between two ancient ninja clans whose power goes far beyond the human. The Fuma clan has long guarded the Holy Grail – an artifact capable of wiping out the entire world. When the rival Koma clan steals it and destroys an entire Fuma faction, only one warrior survives: Hagane. His body is gone, but a mysterious master saves his brain and rebuilds him as a near-superhuman cyborg. Armed with incredible strength, blistering speed, and a vow of vengeance, you hunt the Koma clan to reclaim the Grail and prevent the world from falling into ruin.","Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","miximages/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png","marquees/snes/Hagane - The Final Conflict (NA).png"
"snes_hakunetsu-pro-yakyuu-93-ganba-league","Hakunetsu Pro Yakyuu '93 - Ganba League","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-12-11","1992","1990s","Sting Entertainment","Epic - Sony Records","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Hakunetsu Pro Yakyuu Ganba League '93 is the sequel to Hakunetsu Pro Yakyuu Ganba League, otherwise known as Extra Innings. As with the original, Ganba League '93 has a cartoony presentation and emphasizes arcade-style fast gameplay over more serious sim elements. All the included teams are fictional and the player can even edit their own teams. The player can choose between playing a one-off game or entering a pennant race, as well as selecting one or two human players or letting the CPU play against itself with the Watch mode.

