"snes_hal-s-hole-in-one-golf","HAL's Hole in One Golf","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-10-22","1992","1990s","HAL Laboratory","HAL Laboratory","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","HAL's Hole in One is a standard 18-hole golf game, played from a top-down perspective. You can compete in stroke play with up to four players, or match play against a friend or the computer. When playing against the computer, you will play against an opponent that uses metal clubs, which hit farther than the standard wooden clubs.

In addition to stroke and match play, you can obtain passwords that allow you to replay any spectacular shots that you make (eagles, holes-in-one, and double-eagles).","HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","miximages/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","screenshots/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","backcovers/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png","marquees/snes/HAL's Hole in One Golf (NA).png"
"snes_hameln-no-violin-hiki","Hameln No Violin Hiki","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-29","1995","1990s","Daft","Enix","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","In Violinist of Hameln you play the role of Hamel, a sort of wanderer / adventurer whose weapon is… a violin. His music can cover enemies in fear, or even control their minds. Hamel and his mascot Oboe arrives at Staccato, a small town attacked by monsters, and drives them away with his power. Impressed, a cute little girl named Flute decides to go with Hamel in order to find and destroy the evil power behind the attacks.

The game is typical platform. You play as Hamel, and with your violin can shoot musical notes to beat your enemies. However, you count with Flute’s aid. Flute follows you (although you can order her to stop and stay), but also can be grabbed and thrown at the enemies (yes, thrown at the enemies). Flute can also collect through all the stages some costumes that, when worn, give her special abilities, such as flying, leaping, breaking walls or even explode and kill all in screen. At the end of each stage, of course, you’ll find the typical boss, all named as musical instruments.","Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","miximages/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","screenshots/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","titlescreens/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","3dboxes/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","backcovers/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png","marquees/snes/Hamelin no Violin Hiki (English Translated by J2e Translations).png"
"snes_hammerlock-wrestling","HammerLock Wrestling","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-01","1994","1990s","Jaleco","Jaleco","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-8","1","8","50","2.5","Hammerlock Wrestling is Jaleco's take on wrestling with a style geared towards Saturday Night Slam Masters.  The player can choose from 12 fictional wrestlers and compete in four different modes of play.  There is also 60 different moves to choose from as well as unique finishers for each wrestler.

The Exhibition mode allows up to four different players to compete either against each other in singles match or in tag team format.  Champion League Match is a round robin-type tournament with six different wrestlers competing for the league championship.  Tournament is the standard tournament format with eight different wrestlers involved and Top Ranking Match where the player must battle through the other eleven wrestlers and defeat each one to become champion.","Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","miximages/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png","marquees/snes/Hammer Lock Wrestling (NA).png"
"snes_hardball-iii","HardBall III","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-01","1994","1990s","MindSpan","Accolade","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Welcome to the big leagues. 28 teams. 28 authentically-rendered big league ballparks. And over 650 of baseball's best from the Major League Baseball Players Association. Like Barry Bonds, John Olerud and Kirby Puckett Hardball III captures the total baseball experience - from the first pitch to the last out. So pick your ballclub, and pick your opponent. Then sit back and enjoy The Show.","HardBall III (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","miximages/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","screenshots/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","backcovers/snes/HardBall III (NA).png","marquees/snes/HardBall III (NA).png"
"snes_harley-s-humongous-adventure","Harley's Humongous Adventure","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Visual Concepts","Hi Tech Expressions","Adventure","Adventure","1-2","1","2","80","4","Harley is a hip, young scientist who happens to have an IQ the size of Mt. Rushmore. While experimenting with a shrinking machine, something goes terribly wrong--the machine explodes and Harley is now the size of a bug! Harley has to find the missing pieces of his machine and reassemble it in order to return to his regular size. You'll guide him through all kinds of crazy capers, commandeering a tank, parachuting, using a jet pack, and fighting a giant rat, that will lead him to the parts he needs. When you're the size of an insect everything looks humongous, but even normal-sized people will agree that Harley's adventure is humongous.","Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","miximages/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png","marquees/snes/Harley's Humongous Adventure (NA).png"
"snes_harvest-moon","Harvest Moon","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1998-01-29","1998","1990s","Amccus","Nintendo","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","80","4","Ever wanted to live life on a farm, with nothing but the sun, the fresh scent of your crops, the muddy fields underneath, and cows and chickens to keep you company? Well, you're in luck, because you have just inherited your grandfather's ranch, but it's in a terrible state of disrepair! What ever can you do?

You're going to do like the farmers do; roll up your sleeves, get down in that dirt, fix that farm up and make it the best farm anyone has ever seen! It sure gets lonely on that farm...but not to worry! There are plenty of girls in the village, and if you treat them right and manage to win their love, you've got yourself a wife!

So let's go, farmer! You've got 2 years to make a name for yourself on that farm! Work hard, and the rewards will be great!","Harvest Moon (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","miximages/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png","marquees/snes/Harvest Moon (NA).png"
"snes_hashire-hebereke","Hashire Hebereke","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-22","1994","1990s","Sunsoft","Sunsoft","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Hashire Hebereke (""Run Hebereke"") is an isometric racing game from SunSoft that features Hebereke, Sukezaemon, O-Chan and the rest of Hebereke's friends. The player must race across a course hitting three checkpoints before returning to the starting line to move onto the next lap. The courses all have different layouts and the player must use the D-pad to turn their character mid-sprint, often causing them to veer strongly from one side to the other. In the single-player the player, as Hebereke, has to challenge every other character on their respective courses. Characters have distinctive strengths and weaknesses that the player needs to ascertain in order to defeat them.

Players can also acquire items that can help them out by running over certain spots on the course, similar to Super Mario Kart, and can collect multiple items and switch between them. The game also includes a tag mode and bonus rounds that involve getting chased in a circle by a giant boulder.","Hashire Hebereke (JP).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","miximages/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png","marquees/snes/Hashire Hebereke (JP).png"
"snes_hat-trick-hero-2","Hat Trick Hero 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-29","1994","1990s","Neverland","Taito","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Hat Trick Hero 2 is a soccer game released exclusively in Japan in 1994. An American version was originally planned under the name Super Soccer Champ 2, but was cancelled.
The game allows you to choose the different international teams present during the 94 World Cup. At the beginning of the game, you will have to choose the captain of the team among 8 possible choices, as well as the type of formation. You can choose between Exhibition, World League (similar to a world tournament), Taito Cup (24 teams to beat), Shootout, Option and Password modes. Note that in Taito Cup mode, after beating all 23 teams, there is a final match against the team with the abbreviation ""NLC"". Mode 7 gives a special perspective to the game.","Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Hat Trick Hero 2 (JP).png"
"snes_hatayama-hatch-no-pro-yakyuu-news-jitsumei-ban","Hatayama Hatch No Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-10-29","1993","1990s","Agenda","Epoch","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1","1","1","70","3.5","Hatayama Hacchi no Pro Yakyuu News! Jitsumeiban is a baseball game from Agenda and Epoch, with a comedic cartoonish theme. The title roughly translates as ""Pro Baseball News by Hatayama Hacchi! Real Name Version"" (the ""Real Name Version"" refers to the game's license to use actual athlete/team names from the Nippon Professional Baseball league). It looks and plays like Namco's Famista/Family Stadium series.

Like many Epoch games released around this time, the game is compatible with the Barcode Battler. Players can scan barcodes through the device, which can be read by the Super Famicom via a peripheral sold separately. These unlock additional athletes for use.","Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","miximages/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png","marquees/snes/Hatayama Hatch no Pro Yakyuu News! - Jitsumei Ban (JP).png"
"snes_havoc","Havoc","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Argonaut Software","Unknown","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","","","Havoc is an early version of King Arthur's World, a Lemmings style puzzle game by Argonaut. According to the label on the prototype, it had the original working title of ""Castles"". The name ""Havoc"" made it into the final game as the title of the main theme song. The prototype is in a standard US cart, indicating that this was likely given out in the US (despite Argonaut being a British company).","Havoc (Prototype).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","miximages/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","screenshots/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","titlescreens/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","3dboxes/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","backcovers/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png","marquees/snes/Havoc (Prototype).png"
"snes_fever-pitch-soccer","Fever Pitch Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","U.S. Gold","U.S. Gold","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-4","1","4","50","2.5","Experience intense hi-speed soccer action as you compete boot-to-boot against the world's greatest teams. Recruit star players like Barger, Tricky and Striker and use their arsenal of awesome special moves to destroy your opponents.","Head-On Soccer (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","miximages/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png","marquees/snes/Head-On Soccer (NA).png"
"snes_hebereke-s-popoitto","Hebereke's Popoitto","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-30","1995","1990s","Sunsoft","Sunsoft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Wowwww! Wheeee! The ultimate puzzle game, starring the eight unique Hebereke characters! Play against the computer or take on a friend for non-stop Hebereke fun!

Line up four or more Popoons and Poroporo characters of the same color to make them disappear. Use the special color combo attacks to make Popoons and Poroporos pour into your opponent's area! Be the first to get rid of all your Poroporos to win!","Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","miximages/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","screenshots/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","titlescreens/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","3dboxes/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","backcovers/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png","marquees/snes/Hebereke's Popoitto (NTSC-U Conversion Patch by CF).png"
"snes_hebereke-s-popoon","Hebereke's Popoon","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-01","1994","1990s","Sunsoft","Sunsoft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","80","4","Hebereke's Popoon is a block-grouping game closer in style to Dr. Mario than Tetris. There are eight playable characters, each having different abilities. In one-player mode, the player is forced to choose Hebereke and must play against Oh-Chan. After defeating Oh-Chan, the player is allowed to choose between Hebereke and Oh-Chan in the next match against Sukezaemon, and so on, until the player has ""unlocked"" all the characters. Each match consists of a single-round. A defeated player may elect to resume play by using a continue. In two-player mode, all characters are immediately available to either player and each match is the best of three rounds. Players can also select a handicap level (from 1 - 5) to increase or decrease the difficulty of the game.","Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Hebereke's Popoon (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_heisei-inu-monogatari-bow-pop-n-smash","Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-04-28","1994","1990s","Takara","Takara","Sports","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow: Pop'n Smash!! (""Heisei-era Dog Tales Bow: Pop'n Smash"") is a video game adaptation of a 1993 comedic anime series (which in turn is based on a manga) about a bull terrier, Bow Wow, who is adopted into a Yakuza family. The game is a competitive two-player action sports game that plays similarly to a vertically-oriented version of Pong. The player takes on various opponents, taking advantage of the arena and power-ups spread around.","Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","miximages/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png","marquees/snes/Heisei Inu Monogatari Bow - Pop'n Smash!! (JP).png"
"snes_heracles-no-eikou-3-kamigami-no-chinmoku","Heracles No Eikou 3  Kamigami No Chinmoku","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-04-24","1992","1990s","Data East","Data East","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","In this third installment of The Glory of Hercules series, you once again visit the world of ancient Greek mythology. Cast into the role of a young boy from a remote village, you live a peaceful life until one day the pigs in your village go crazy, and as a result you are thrown underground, only to be saved by mysterious fairies. Something goes wrong, and the world as you knew it doesn't exist any more. You must establish contact to the great gods and other famous characters from the Greek mythology in order to restore the balance.

Like the previous games of the series, this is a standard console-style RPG with turn-based combat viewed from first-person perspective. There is a day/night cycle, which influences not only the appearance of the world map and the towns, but also the schedules of the world's inhabitants.","Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","miximages/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","screenshots/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","titlescreens/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","3dboxes/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","backcovers/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png","marquees/snes/Heracles no Eikou III - Kamigami no Chinmoku (English Translated by DQ Translations, Rev 1.1a).png"
"snes_heracles-no-eik-4-kamigami-no-okurimono","Heracles no Eikō 4 - Kamigami no Okurimono","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-21","1994","1990s","Data East","Data East","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-4","1","4","80","4","In this installment of the  Glory of Hercules RPG series, you are a young man who lives in Atlantis, an ancient land with advanced civilization, which is surrounded by a huge wall. He studies the wisdom of Atlantis together with his best friend Platon and his sweetheart Epipha. One day, he and Platon visit Epipha on the wall tower, but at this moment barbarian soldiers attack Atlantis. The young heroes have to flee and to find a way to protect their land from the invasion. Of course, none other but the great hero Hercules will help them on their quest!

Like other Glory of Hercules games, this is a traditional console-style RPG. You travel on the world map, visiting towns and villages, descending into dungeons, and fighting random enemies in first person perspective turn-based battles, Dragon Warrior-style.","Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Heracles no Eikou IV - Kamigami Kara no Okurimono (English Translated by Translation Corporation, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_hercules","Hercules","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Unknown","Unknown","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","","","Hercules is an unofficial/unlicensed (bootleg) Super Nintendo game. It's an action-adventure title with four stages inspired by the original PlayStation game. The graphics try to mimic the PS1 version, but they're simpler and miss many details, including the forest atmosphere in the first level. The first three stages are platforming-based, while the fourth and final stage plays more like a shooter, with the player riding Pegasus. Most stages end with a boss that must be defeated to continue; the exception is the final stage, which has no boss and simply shows Zeus being freed from the rocks. The sound effects are reused from Street Fighter II on the SNES.","Hercules (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Hercules (NA).png","miximages/snes/Hercules (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Hercules (NA).jpg","titlescreens/snes/Hercules (NA).jpg","3dboxes/snes/Hercules (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Hercules (NA).png","marquees/snes/Hercules (NA).png"
"snes_hero-senki-project-olympus","Hero Senki - Project Olympus","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-11-20","1992","1990s","Winky Soft","Banpresto","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Part of the Compati Hero Series of games that feature cameos from the Gundam, Kamen Rider and Ultraman franchises as super deformed characters of relative size. The series also ties in with the Super Robot Taisen (Super Robot Wars) series of crossover anime mecha RPGs. The game introduces the Gespenst and other narrative elements of the game are frequently referenced by modern Super Robot Taisen games.The game is a traditional turn-based RPG. The party of playable characters consists of Amuro Ray, Dan Moroboshi and Kotaro Minami (Kamen Rider Black) of the Gundam, Ultraman and Kamen Rider franchises respectively. The characters can attack normally with weapons or fists or, instead of magic, the characters use some of their ""technical power"" to perform stronger laser attacks.","Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","miximages/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","screenshots/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","titlescreens/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","3dboxes/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","backcovers/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png","marquees/snes/Hero Senki - Project Olympus (English Translated by Aeon Genesis).png"
"snes_higashio-osamu-kanshuu-super-pro-yakyuu-stadium","Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-09-30","1993","1990s","C-Lab","Tokuma Shoten Intermedia","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1","1","1","70","3.5","A baseball game sponsored by Osamu Higashio, a former pitcher for the Nippon Professional Baseball League who has his own entry in the Japanese Baseball Hall of Fame. The game takes the vertically-aligned batter/pitcher angle favored by series like Namco's Famista series (from which RBI Baseball spun off), but mixes it up by changing the perspective depending on whether the player is pitching or batting: the player's team is always closer to the screen. Osamu Higashio also sponsored some Game Boy baseball games published by Tokuma Shoten prior to this game: Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Pro Yakyuu Stadium '91 and Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Pro Yakyuu Stadium '92.","Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","miximages/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png","marquees/snes/Higashio Osamu Kanshuu Super Pro Yakyuu Stadium (JP).png"
