"snes_human-grand-prix-3-f1-triple-battle","Human Grand Prix 3 - F1 Triple Battle","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-30","1994","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Human Grand Prix III: F1 Triple Battle is a Formula One racing game for the Super Famicom. It is the third of four Human Grand Prix games for the system. It has the licenses of FOCA and Fuji TV: the former allows the game to use actual driver/team names while the latter is the official Japanese TV carrier of the Formula One races. Like its precedents, F1 Triple Battle uses Mode 7 and a low perspective for its racing.

