"snes_hungry-dinosaurs","Hungry Dinosaurs","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-03","1995","1990s","Magical Company","Sunsoft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-4","1","4","60","3","Hungry Dinosaurs is a variant of the board game Othello with a dinosaur setting. In each turn, one player gets to lay an egg into one grid of the 9x9 playfield. When a player manages to trap a row (horizontally, vertically or diagonally) of an opponent's eggs, i.e. having an one egg at each end of the row, they change colour. A round is over after a certain amount of time and whoever has the most eggs on the field, wins. One match consists of several rounds. In contrast to the real board game, up to four player can participate.","Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","0.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Hungry Dinosaurs (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_hurricanes","Hurricanes","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Probe Software","U.S. Gold","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Featuring in a children's TV cartoon, The Hurricanes are the most revered team in the World Soccer League. The Gorgons are desperate to beat them in a key match - so desperate that they have made it hard for the team to even get to the stadium. Taking control of one of their star players, you must trek through the jungle, mines and a temple to get them to the stadium on time.","Hurricanes (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","miximages/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png","marquees/snes/Hurricanes (NA).png"
"snes_hyper-iria","Hyper Iria","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-10-13","1995","1990s","Banpresto","Banpresto","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","Hyper Iria is based on the anime prequel to the sci-fi movie Zeiram. As in the anime and movie Iria is a space traveling bounty hunter who keeps running into the immortal villain Zeiram. In the game Iria can select one of four missions with a fifth selectable after the other four are completed. On the way to a mission Iria will discuss the mission with her AI companion Bob, and sometimes will be ambushed, requiring her to defend herself in a scrolling shooter type level. Upon reaching her destination Iria will proceed on foot, making her way through a maze-like level with several paths to her goal. Iria has powerful physical attacks, and can also carry firearms and grenades with limited ammunition. Money is rewarded based on your performance in a mission, and can be used to buy new firearms and more grenades.","Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","miximages/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","screenshots/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","titlescreens/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","3dboxes/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","backcovers/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png","marquees/snes/Hyper Iria (English Translated by Dynamic Designs and Matt's Messy Room, Rev 1.03).png"
"snes_hyper-v-ball","Hyper V-Ball","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Video System","Ubi Soft Entertainment Software","Sports / Volleyball","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","A volleyball simulation seen from a side-view perspective, meaning it is only possible to move players to the left or right. The player can choose between three different leagues: Men's League, Woman's League and Hyper League, which is a league for robots. Two buttons are used to control the ball, one for normal actions and one for ""Hyper Plays"", special attacks that can only be learned and used in the Hyper League. How a player will block or attack depends on the ball's speed and the players position. Team members who aren't under the player's direct control will also act on their own by positioning themselves or preparing spikes. They will, however, not block spikes on their own but it is possible to let players not under direct control block spikes by pressing one of the action buttons at the right moment.","Hyper V-Ball (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","miximages/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png","marquees/snes/Hyper V-Ball (NA).png"
"snes_hyperzone","HyperZone","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-09-01","1991","1990s","HAL Laboratory","HAL Laboratory","Shoot'em Up","Shooter","1","1","1","60","3","A 3D shooter similar to Space Harrier. Control different futuristic flying vehicles and blast your way through numerous enemies and obstacles. If your ship is getting too fast, you can use the brakes, however flying too slow damages your ship. Apart from the standard weapons, most ships have a special attack that can be charged by holding down the fire button. The action takes place on set tracks; leaving those tacks will cause heavy damage to your ship. You can repair your ship by flying over certain areas. At the end of end of each level, a boss has to be defeated.","HyperZone (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","miximages/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","screenshots/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","backcovers/snes/HyperZone (NA).png","marquees/snes/HyperZone (NA).png"
"snes_ihatovo-monogatari","Ihatovo Monogatari","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-03-05","1993","1990s","HectorSoft","HectorSoft","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","80","4","Ihatovo is a magical land created by the Japanese author Kenji Miyazawa. In the game, you are a stranger who arrives at Ihatovo and has to find seven missing notebooks by Miyazawa, to complete his stories, such as for example The Fire Stone, and others.

This is an adventure game in which you can freely navigate your character through the top-down world, in a console RPG-like fashion. There are no battles in the game and also no puzzles, although at some points you'll have to collect and to use items. The game mainly progresses thanks to conversations with various characters you encounter in Ihatovo.","Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","miximages/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","screenshots/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","titlescreens/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","3dboxes/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","backcovers/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png","marquees/snes/Ihatovo Monogatari (English Translated by Tom, FlashPV, and DDSTranslation, Rev 2).png"
"snes_illusion-of-time","Illusion of Time","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-04-27","1995","1990s","Quintet","Nintendo","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","Will is a young boy whose father disappeared long time ago. Now Will lives in a small town with his grandparents. He possesses unusual abilities of pushing and pulling things without touching them. One day, he finds in his house a girl, who soon turns out to be the princess Kara. Kara's father, king Edward, wants her to marry a mysterious person called the Jackal. Kara asks Will to help her to escape the palace, and soon they both get involved in a string of mystery and conspiracies...

