"snes_international-sensible-soccer-world-champions-limited-edition","International Sensible Soccer - World Champions : Limited Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Sensible Software","Sony Electronic Publishing","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1","1","1","70","3.5","Released alongside the 1994 World Cup, this was the first version of Sensible Soccer to feature teams from outside Europe. The World Cup tournament is featured in full, and you can adjust which 24 teams this features, a particularly crucial feature for English and French fans, as their nations failed to qualify. For the first time in the series an on-screen referee is featured. The club team data has been updated to take into account transfers and kit changes since the previous version. Gameplay is much the same as previous editions, being viewed from above with small sprites and loose ball control.","International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/International Sensible Soccer - World Champions Limited Edition (Rev 1, NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_international-superstar-soccer","International Superstar Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-05-23","1995","1990s","Konami","Konami","Sports","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","International Superstar Soccer lets you choose from 26 national teams and dive into fast-paced football with realistic gameplay. Whether it's exhibition, international cup, penalty kicks, or training – the game offers multiple challenges. The scenario mode stands out, placing you in famous match situations where you're tasked with turning the game around. With mature player designs, back numbers, and smart AI, it's considered a landmark among 16-bit football games.","International Superstar Soccer (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","miximages/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","screenshots/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","backcovers/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png","marquees/snes/International Superstar Soccer (NA).png"
