"snes_iron-commando-koutetsu-no-senshi","Iron Commando - Koutetsu no Senshi","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-10","1995","1990s","Arcade Zone","Pack-In-Video","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Iron Commando is a side-scrolling beat-em-up not unlike that of Final Fight or Streets of Rage. Players take control of either the commando Jack or the kung-fu master Chang-Li as they work together to stop the terrorist group GHOST from obtaining a radioactive meteorite that fell from the sky and use it to create weapons of mass destruction. Weapons such as baseball bats, grenades and assault rifles are available for the player to use, though they do wear out quickly.","Iron Commando (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","miximages/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png","marquees/snes/Iron Commando (NA).png"
"snes_isozuri-ritou-hen","Isozuri - Ritou Hen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-19","1996","1990s","Pack In Video","Pack In Video","Hunting and Fishing","Action","1","1","1","80","4","Isozuri: Ritou Hen (""Rock Fishing: Island Edition"", where Isozuri specifically refers to standing on a rocky coastline while casting out to sea) is a fishing game exclusive to the Super Famicom. The player travels around an archipelago finding a place to start angling, catching different ocean fish depending on the location and the time of day.

