"snes_jikkyou-power-pro-wrestling-96-max-voltage","Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-09-13","1996","1990s","Diamond Head","Konami","Fighting","Fighting","1-4","1","4","80","4","Step up to the ring with Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling. As the name implies this is a wrestling game in which wrestlers from different leagues collide in grappling contests to determine who's the king of the hill.

Select your character with his unique stats and movesets, and go at it against any opponent from four fictional leagues with dozens of moves, submission holds and rope maneuvers in or out of the ring.

The game uses pre-rendered 2D sprites and features Vs, Tournament, and League play for up to four players. Also included is a career mode where you create a wrestler and control each aspect of his career up to his final victory in the inter-league tournament. And you can also configure matches to be standard, tag (with 4 or 6 wrestlers), submission or death-matches which adds such features as live wires and explosives to the ring.","Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","miximages/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","screenshots/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","titlescreens/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","3dboxes/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","backcovers/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png","marquees/snes/Jikkyou Power Pro Wrestling '96 - Max Voltage (English Translated by Phil).png"
"snes_jikkyou-powerful-pro-yakyuu-94","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-03-11","1994","1990s","Konami","Konami","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 is a baseball sim and the first in Konami's long-running Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu series, or simply Power Pro. It is the first of six Super Famicom games in the franchise. The game is reminiscent of Namco's Famista series, especially with the cartoonish super-deformed athletes. As well as the usual exhibition and pennant modes, the player can practice any position in the game (batting, pitching, fielding) with any team member.","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '94 (JP).png"
"snes_jikkyou-powerful-pro-yakyuu-96-kaimaku-ban","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-07-19","1996","1990s","Diamond Head","Konami","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 Kaimaku Han (""Live-Commentary Powerful Pro Baseball '96 Opener Edition"") is a baseball game from Pawapuro (back when they were still called Diamond Head) and Konami.

It fits between the core entries Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 3 and Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 4, which were released in the first quarters of 1996 and 1997 respectively, and largely based on the former's engine. Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 3 '97-Haru, also released in March of 1997, was another interstitial game that used the same engine as JPPY 3.

The game features updated rosters and details for the 1996 season of the Nippon Professional Baseball league. It carries over the large number of customizable game modes from the third game.","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu '96 - Kaimaku Ban (JP, Rev 1).png"
"snes_jikkyou-powerful-pro-yakyuu-basic-ban-98","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1998-03-19","1998","1990s","Diamond Head","Konami","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu Basic '98 (""Live Commentary Powerful Pro Baseball Basic '98"") is the last in Konami's Power Pro Yakyuu series to be released on the Super Famicom, where the series originated.

The game is another annual iteration on Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 3, first released in 1996, that saw regular roster updates until 1998. Those iterations also include '96 Kaimaku Han ('96 Opener Edition) and '97-Haru ('97 Spring), both reflecting the new rosters of those time periods. The '98 Basic version also strips out the game's trademark ""Success Mode"", where the player creates their own athlete and has them succeed in the Nippon Professional Baseball league.","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu - Basic Ban '98 (JP).png"
"snes_jikkyou-powerful-pro-yakyuu-2","Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-24","1995","1990s","Konami","Konami","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","ikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu 2 (""Play-by-play Powerful Pro Baseball 2"") is a baseball game for the Super Famicom and the second in Konami's Jikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu series, usually shortened to ""Power Pro"".

The player once again takes to the field with numerous real-life Japanese baseball teams albeit with spherical-domed super-deformed players. It comes with all the modes of the original, including training in any role on the field as well as the standard one-player exhibition, two-player exhibition, pennant mode and a ""watch mode"" where the player observes two CPU teams.

