"snes_kishin-douji-zenki-battle-raiden","Kishin Douji Zenki - Battle Raiden","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-08-04","1995","1990s","CAProduction","Hudson Soft","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Once already Chiaki and her reluctant demon servant Zenki have saved the world from the forces of darkness, but apparently once is never enough. Chiaki has a vision of five cloaked figures and knows that only she and Zenki can stop them. At once they set off to track down the demon leaders.

In Kishin Douji ZENKI: Battle Raiden the player takes the role of Zenki. At first, and occasionally through the game, Zenki will be in his powered down form where he can only punch, jump, and dash. After Chiaki recovers her bracelet, or regains her concentration, or whatever she needs to do at the time, she can transform Zenki into his powered up form. In this form Zenki deals more damage and has a much longer list of attacks that get added to as the game progresses, such as a pillar of energy, an electrified punch, and a dashing attack. By picking up scrolls Zenki can do a powerful Rudora attack to all enemies on screen, but this attack damages Zenki as well.","Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","miximages/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","screenshots/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","titlescreens/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","3dboxes/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","backcovers/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png","marquees/snes/Kishin Douji Zenki - Batoru Raiden (English Translated by Dynamic Designs).png"
"snes_knights-of-the-round","Knights of the Round","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Capcom","Capcom","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","In Knights of the Round, play the role of one of three knights from the Arthurian legends. The three characters are Sir Lancelot, Sir Percival, and of course King Arthur. 

The story tells of a man who pulled the mighty sword Excalibur from a rock which no one else could achieve. This feat signified that he should be king of the Britons and lead them to peace. The trouble is there is mass chaos in the land and the only way Arthur can stop it is to find the holy grail which has been hidden for over a thousand years. Aurthur is joined by Percival and Lancelot on his quest to find the grail.","Knights of the Round (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","miximages/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png","marquees/snes/Knights of the Round (NA).png"
"snes_kouryuu-densetsu-villgust-kieta-shoujo","Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-05-23","1992","1990s","Plex","Bandai","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","This game is based on the animé series Villgust. The main hero of the game is Shun, a teenager who lives in modern-day Japan. One day, when he was going back from school with his girlfriend Michiko, Shun noticed a strange red-eyed rabbit. When he tried to follow him, Shun suddenly found himself all alone in a forest clearing. He was immediately approached by a group of four adventurers who said they were members of a group called R.A.G.E. (Resistance Against God of Evil). Apparently, Shun was transported into a parallel medieval world, and an evil organization known as Vile was the one behind Michiko's kidnapping. Shun and his friends will now do anything to help Michiko and to destroy Vile!

This is a traditional console-style RPG. You travel on the world map, visit towns, buy equipment and items, descend into dungeons, and fight random enemies in turn-based combat viewed from a third-person ""over-the-shoulder"" perspective. The party can hold up to five characters. The characters level up in a standard way, and also get experience and new levels for their magical spells.","Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Kouryuu Densetsu Villgust - Kieta Shoujo (English Translated by Dynamic Designs, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_kouryuu-no-mimi","Kouryuu No Mimi","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-22","1995","1990s","Vap","Vap","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","70","3.5","Natsume Kiroemon, the 45th leader of the Natsume family, is due to inherit the Koryuu no Mimi, a tool which gives its bearer easy access to wealth and women. As a result of his father's death, he left the Italian monastery where he'd been training and rightfully took the name ""Natsume Kiroemon"" as well as the power of the Koryuu no Mimi. Upon his return to Japan, Natsume fell fatally in love with Kanako, one of the members of the rival Mina family. However, the evil hand of the Mina family attacked Natsume constantly and abducted Kanako. Now Natsume has unlocked the seal, making the Koryuu's power surge, and he's striking back at the Mina family. Both Koryuu and Kanako's fate are in the player's hands.","Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","miximages/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","screenshots/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","titlescreens/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","3dboxes/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","backcovers/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png","marquees/snes/Kouryuu no Mimi (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 2).png"
"snes_koushien-2","Koushien 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-06-26","1992","1990s","Affect","K. Amusement Leasing","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Koushien 2 is the second game in Affect's Koushien series of high school baseball sims, and the first to be released on the Super Famicom. As with its predecessor, players assume the role of a high school baseball team competing with others in Japan's Koushien stadium. It follows the standard ""behind the batter"" perspective of Bases Loaded/RBI Baseball. As with many early baseball games, the player moves all fielders simultaneously after a hit, rather than whichever one is closest to the ball.","Koushien 2 (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Koushien 2 (JP).png"
"snes_koushien-3","Koushien 3","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-29","1994","1990s","Magical Company","Magical Company","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Koushien 3 is the third of several Koushien baseball games. The game is focused on Japanese high school baseball: the title refers to the stadium in which the Japanese national high school baseball final takes place. The game uses the standard ""behind the batter"" perspective common to baseball games of this era.

Koushien 3 marks the first time Magical Company would publish a Koushien game, taking over from K Amusement Leasing. Its sequel Koushien 4 would be the last Koushien game for the Super Famicom system: the series moved to PlayStation shortly after.","Koushien 3 (JP).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Koushien 3 (JP).png"
"snes_krusty-s-super-fun-house","Krusty's Super Fun House","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-12-10","1992","1990s","Audiogenic Software","Acclaim Entertainment","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Krusty the Clown's Fun House has been overrun by rats. You must help him to herd the rats into trap machines to clear them out. In order to do so, Krusty must manipulate his environment to set up pathways so that the rats are headed in the right direction. Objects that Krusty move around include blocks, fans, and pipe pieces. The trap machines are operated by other recognizable Simpson's characters: Bart, Homer, Sideshow Mel, and Corporal Punishment.","Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Krusty's Super Fun House (NA, Rev 1).png"
