"snes_lupin-sansei-densetsu-no-hihou-o-oe","Lupin Sansei - Densetsu No Hihou O Oe!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-27","1994","1990s","SAS Sakata","Epoch","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","70","3.5","Lupin, Jigen, and Goemon are at their Manhattan hideout plotting their next caper, when suddenly a large masked man bursts in. The man is escorted by a woman who proceeds to tell Lupin and the others that Fujiko has been kidnapped and is being held prisoner at one of the skyscrapers downtown. In order to get her back they must find the fountain of youth. When the two leave, Lupin decides to go and rescue Fujiko himself and sets off to save her. When arrives he discovers that the building is crawling with police, all under the command of Zenigata... so Lupin must enter through the building's ventilation to find Fujiko.","Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","miximages/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png","marquees/snes/Lupin Sansei - Densetsu no Hihou o Oe! (JP).png"
"snes_m-a-c-s-basic-rifle-marksmanship","M.A.C.S. Basic Rifle Marksmanship","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Sculptured Software","Sculptured Software","Simulation","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","","","The Multi-Purpose Arcade Combat Simulator (or M.A.C.S.), was a shooting simulator developed for the U.S. Army as a cheap way to train shooting skills. It was a bit of a mystery until the rifle and and carts became available through Ebay. The rifle used for the M.A.C.S. is a replica of a Jäger AP 74 (an M16A2 clone). The light gun is far more accurate than the Super Scope and has the weight and feel of an authentic weapon. The gun includes a scope used for aiming, and the light sensor is in the barrel of the gun. The cord that connects to the controller port of the SNES comes out near the end of the barrel.","MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","miximages/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","screenshots/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","titlescreens/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","3dboxes/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","backcovers/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png","marquees/snes/MACS Basic Rifle Marksmanship (NA, Rev 1.1e).png"
"snes_madden-nfl-94","Madden NFL '94","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","High Score Productions","Electronic Arts","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-5","1","5","70","3.5","Madden NFL '94 is the third in the Madden series of football games for the SNES. It features 80 teams -- 28 teams from the 1993 season, 38 Super Bowl teams from 1966-1991, 12 All Star franchise teams since 1950, and two ""All-Madden"" teams: one for the 1993 season and one from a 20-year time span. You can play these teams in a regular exhibition game or sudden death overtime game, or take the 1993 teams through an entire season. You can also enter the playoffs with the 1993 teams, the Super Bowl champions, or the All Star franchise teams. Unlike many other sports games, saving a season is done by password rather than by storing the data into a saved game.","Madden NFL '94 (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Madden NFL '94 (NA).png"
