"snes_madden-nfl-97","Madden NFL 97","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-10-02","1996","1990s","EA Sports","EA Sports","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-5","1","5","80","4","Welcome to Madden NFL 97, the game that captures the excitement of a 30 yard touchdown pass, the strategy of a well executed scoring drive, and the atmosphere of a crisp autumn afternoon in the stadium. Madden NFL 97 delivers state of the art graphics and sound -- and with modem and network support, it's ready to put your competitive skills to the test.","Madden NFL '97 (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Madden NFL '97 (NA).png"
"snes_madden-nfl-98","Madden NFL 98","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1997-11-02","1997","1990s","Tiertex","Electronic Arts","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-5","1","5","80","4","Playcalling expert John Madden again licenses Electronic Arts' flagship football simulation. New features for 1998 include more advanced Quarterback functions such as the ability to play lob passes and adjust timing patterns, and more instinctive AI features to adjust as the match goes on. Squad features have also been advanced, with the opportunity to create plays and trade them.

Gameplay is much the same as the other editions, with the full season on offer as well as playoffs and the Superbowl. Everything is presented TV-style, with play-by-play analysis and reports. The contemporary NFL teams are joined by great squads of the past.","Madden NFL '98 (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Madden NFL '98 (NA).png"
"snes_madou-monogatari-hanamaru-daiyouchienji","Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchienji","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-12","1996","1990s","Compile","Tokuma Shoten Intermedia","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","The game is set in the same universe and shares characters and storyline with  Puyo Puyo puzzle games. Unlike Puyo Puyo, Mado Monogatari is a Japanese-style RPG. You play Arle, a five-year old apprentice magician. She is attending a special kindergarten, and it is time for the Final Exam. At the same time, Arle receives a mysterious letter that tells her that if she finds eight magical gems and takes them to the Wizard Mountain, she'll be granted one wish. Arle decides to search for the gems which are scattered all over the world, and to overcome all the obstacles with her great magic power!

The game features random enemy encounters and turn-based combat, which takes place on a platform (Arle to the left, the enemies to the right). You can't perform physical attacks at all, and your only way of harming enemies is through magic. During the game, you learn a variety of magic spells, which can be upgraded later. In battles you can't see your own and the enemies' hit points, and have to act according to your intuition.","Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Madou Monogatari - Hanamaru Daiyouchi Enji (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_magic-boy","Magic Boy","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-01","1994","1990s","JVC","Empire Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","Join Magic Boy as he attempts to become a master wizard, and he does this by shooting enemies, putting them in a bag, and throwing them away. He also must get through four areas: Sand Land, Wet World, Plastic Place, and Future Zone. There are also several power-ups that help him on his quest.","Magic Boy (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","miximages/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png","marquees/snes/Magic Boy (NA).png"
"snes_magic-sword","Magic Sword","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-03-18","1993","1990s","Capcom","Capcom","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","As the hero, you must climb up a monster-ridden tower to defeat Drokkmar, master of the Blackorb. To do this, you must defeat his army that stands in your way with whatever weapon you are carrying. Health is decreased by coming into contact with various monsters, attacks, traps, and the passage of time. It is increased by finding food. Every certain amount of points, a ""Food Fairy"" appears and drops off food as well.

Throughout your journey, you can smash open chests to find treasure and artifacts. Some of these artifacts can be recovered that alter gameplay, such as providing more damage or increased magical power. Also throughout your journey, you can collect keys, which are used to free imprisoned allies, who not only help you defeat monsters, but also leave you an item that will help you on your quest. Only one person can join you at a time.

As you progress through the tower, you will be granted new magical weapons after each boss you defeat. The weapons are affected by a ""magic bar"" that charges over time. When this bar is fully charged, the weapon has a powerful ranged attack, but when not charged only a close attack is produced. A magical staff will grant increased range attack ability. A magical blast may be generated by jumping and attacking, but doing this costs health.

There are multiple paths in the game, and two separate endings. Hidden doors can be used to skip levels when found - usually by attacking a wall or a particular spot.","Magic Sword (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","miximages/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png","marquees/snes/Magic Sword (NA).png"
"snes_magical-drop","Magical Drop","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-10-20","1995","1990s","Data East","Data East","Puzzle / Throw","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Magical Drop sometimes referred to by native Japanese users as MagiDro , is a series of puzzle games originally released in the arcade, and later primarily released for several platforms such as the Neo Geo, Super Famicom, Sega Saturn and Neo Geo Pocket Color developed by Data East. The games are notable for being extremely fast-paced.","Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","miximages/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","screenshots/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","titlescreens/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","3dboxes/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","backcovers/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png","marquees/snes/Magical Drop (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 0.95b).png"
"snes_magical-drop-2","Magical Drop 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-09-20","1996","1990s","Data East","Data East","Puzzle / Throw","Puzzle","1-5","1","5","80","4","In Magical Drop II, you control a clown that can grab and throw balloons. You have to match three balloons of the same colour or more vertically to pop them and clear the screen. You can hold multiple balloons of the same colour at once and cause consecutive collisions. There are special balloons that cannot be removed that easily and power-ups that clear entire rows or provide additional help.

Depending of the originating country, there are different game modes:

1. Survival: Play as long as you can - an endless flow of balloons appears at a rapidly increasing speed while you move up levels.

2. Puzzle: You have a limited time to clear a fixed set of balloons before time runs out.

3. VS Mode: Fight the CPU or a fellow player in a direct split-screen duel. Each character has specific item balloons during gameplay.","Magical Drop II (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","miximages/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png","marquees/snes/Magical Drop II (NA).png"
"snes_magical-pop-n","Magical Pop'n","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-03-10","1995","1990s","Polestar","Pack In Video","Platform","Platformer","1-5","1","5","80","4","The kingdom of Toaru prosperous and peaceful place that's famous for its magic.  Within Toaru castle lies the Magic Gem which legend says can give the person who holds it great magical powers.  Because of this, it is sealed inside the castle to prevent the gem from landing in the wrong hands. 

One night, a dark figure and his army of monsters invades the castle and steals the gem.  Armed with a sword and her magic powers, the Princess Toaru sets off to retrieve the gem and save the world.

Magical Pop'n let's you play a young, energetic little princess who is simply called...Princess.  The game starts off with Princess chasing after a floating bad guy off a balcony and into town. 

Princess has two type of weapons: her sword and  her magic powers. 

When using magic, Princess will consume star powers.  Different types of magic requires a different number of stars.  Stars can be collected throughout the game and you can also get stars after defeating a foe.  In the first stage you will only have access to Princess' magic beam powers which shoots small beams of laser at enemies.  Later, you will receive the ice, fire and other powers.

The sword can only be used to perform close range slashing against enemies. But it does not cost any stars.

In each stage, Princess will be confronted with a number of enemies that she must fight off to advance.  There are many mini-bosses and at the end of a stage, you will have to fight the main boss.

Princess' health is indicated by the number of hearts she has in her health meter.  There are various items that will help refill the meter: Candy refills half a heart, A slice of cake refills a whole heart and a birthday cake will refill the entire meter.

You will be taken to the game over screen if you lose all your lives.   But, no worries, there's an unlimited number of continues. There is no save feature in the game.","Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","2.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Magical Pop'n (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01 With FastROM Hack by Kandowontu, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_magna-braban-henreki-no-yusha","Magna Braban - Henreki No Yusha","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-18","1994","1990s","ASK Kodansha","ASK Kodansha","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","The Demon King and his monster armies have been attacking the human kingdoms in an effort to exterminate them all. One day a young boy named Alex is attacked by four monsters but is saved by a Knight of Anatea. Alex, the son of a shepard, grows up idolizing this knight and once the proper age, wishes to enroll in the Arena tournament, though his family forbids him. Entering the tournament Alex and two other warriors: Gina the Magician and Getz the Mercenary, all are defeated in the first round and sent to the Inn to recuperate. However during their absence, the Demon King plans a surprise attack on the Arena and kills everyone there. As the only surviving warriors from the tournament, Alex, Gina and Getz are mistakingly assumed to be strong enough to withstand monsters, and made knights by the King and given the mission of defeating the Demon King. They set out on an epic journey...

Magna Braban: Henreki no Yusha is a console-style RPG with party-based combat and random enemy encounters. The game's main view is an overhead map of a specific location, such as a town, where the characters move and can interact with NPCs. Upon leaving an area, the view changes to a larger overworld map showing locations of interest. The battles are viewed from an isometric perspective and the characters automatically engage and perform their actions. While the player does not directly control any of the characters, they can pause the battle at time and assign new strategies (such as melee, use long-ranged attacks or use Magic) to each character. Experience points and gold are awarded after each battle, the later of which can be used to purchase equipment and items.","Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","miximages/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","screenshots/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","titlescreens/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","3dboxes/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","backcovers/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png","marquees/snes/Magna Braban - Henreki no Yuusha (English Translated by KingMike's Translations, Rev 2 With Alt Font Patch by DaMarsMan).png"
"snes_mahou-kishi-rayearth","Mahou Kishi Rayearth","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-29","1995","1990s","Pandora Box","Tomy","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","A turn-based RPG that is based on the manga/anime of the same name, featuring three schoolgirls who are transported from modern day Tokyo to the magical world of Cephiro. The game loosely follows the plot of the manga and anime, wherein the heroines determine how Cephiro works and their role in rescuing the world's leader Princess Emeraude, who presently takes the vital role of Pillar, from the villainous Zagato.","Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","miximages/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","screenshots/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","titlescreens/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","3dboxes/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","backcovers/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png","marquees/snes/Mahou Kishi Rayearth (English Translated by RPGe, Rev 1.01 With Fixes by MTeam, Rev 1.02).png"
"snes_mahou-poi-poi-poitto","Mahou Poi Poi Poitto!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-08-05","1994","1990s","Metro 3D","Takara","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Mahou Poi Poi Poitto! (""Magic Poi Poi Poitto!"") is a puzzle game developed by Metro and published by TAKARA for the Arcade and SNES. It plays similarly to other match-3 games of the era, like Columns, in that the player has to line up three identical pieces horizontally, vertically or diagonally. Pieces fall in square clumps of four, sometimes including cloud pieces which immediately vanish, and very rarely including a sun icon that can remove all the icons of a single type.

The game features a competitive two-player mode and a one-player story mode. In the story mode, the player takes on a series of monsters. The monster intermittently casts spells at the player that randomly transforms blocks into ""enemy blocks"". By casting magic back at the monster, best done by creating chains and combos, the ground beneath them moves towards the ceiling. Once high enough, the monster is crushed and the player moves onto the next stage.","Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","miximages/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","screenshots/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","titlescreens/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","3dboxes/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","backcovers/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png","marquees/snes/Mahou Poipoi Poitto! (English Translated by KingMike's Translations).png"
"snes_majin-tensei","Majin Tensei","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-28","1994","1990s","Atlus","Atlus","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","70","3.5","Majin Tensei is the first game in the Majin Tensei series and was released for the Super Famicom. Majin Tensei and its successors put a turn-based strategy twist on the usual Megami Tensei gameplay formula.


In the late 1990s, ethnic battles around the world result in a large amount of deaths and a large portion of the world being closed off. Decades later, in 202X, a boy living in Neider Tokyo in the area D-03 suddenly receives a mysterious Demon Summoning Program on his COMP from someone called TAKEUCHI, with demons appearing immediately after. After fighting his way to a mysterious building, he finds a young woman in cryogenic sleep, who decides to join him. There are 3 possible endings: a bad ending, a normal ending, and the best ending.","Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","miximages/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","screenshots/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","titlescreens/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","3dboxes/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","backcovers/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png","marquees/snes/Majin Tensei (English Translated by DDSTranslation, Rev 4 With Alt Font Patch by Badnest).png"
"snes_majin-tensei-2-spiral-nemesis","Majin Tensei 2 - Spiral Nemesis","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-19","1995","1990s","Atlus","Atlus","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","The sequel to ""Majin Tensei"" is a strategy RPG that takes place in an alternate Tokyo of 1996. You control a group of three special agents whose task is to stop a demonic invasion from a different reality. You receive missions such as capturing enemy base, exterminating invaders, etc. After you complete a mission, you move to the next one in a linear fashion, without exploration. The gameplay consists of large strategic battles. You move on the battle field, trying to complete your mission and exterminate the demons on your way. Attacking (or being attacked by) a demon results in a short auto-battle sequence.

""Spiral Nemesis"" contains many classical Megaten elements, such as demon classification, Light/Dark and Law/Chaos alignment axis, etc.","Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","miximages/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","screenshots/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","titlescreens/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","3dboxes/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","backcovers/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png","marquees/snes/Majin Tensei II - Spiral Nemesis (English Translated by DDSTranslation).png"
"snes_majuu-ou","Majuu Ou","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-08-25","1995","1990s","KSS","KSS","Platform / Shooter Scrolling","Shooter","1","1","1","80","4","Abel's daughter has been kidnapped by his former friend, Bayer.  Bayer has sold his soul to the devil, and sacrificed Abel's wife, in an attempt to resurrect the King of Demons.  With no other choice, Abel vows to save his daughter, no matter what the cost - even if it is his own humanity...

Majyuuou is a side-scrolling platformer for the Super Nintendo, taking influences from Castlevania and Contra.  You play as Abel, intent on rescuing his daughter from the depths of Hell.  As you defeat certain bosses, they will drop large, color changing gems.  Pick up the gem, and you'll transform into either a red Harpy, a blue Dragon, or a green Lizard, depending on what color it is when you pick it up.  Each demon type has its own special attacks.","Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Majuu Ou (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_makeruna-makendou-2-kimero-youkai-souridaijin","Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-03-17","1995","1990s","Success","Datam Polystar","Fighting","Fighting","1","1","1","80","4","The Ghost Prime Minister is holding a fighting tournament, and 14-year-old Hikari Tsurugino, the second Mighty Makendo, must face off against all sort of strange apparitions. Characters from the first game make appearances, including Mai Tsurugino, Hikari's sister and the first Mighty Makendo.

Makeruna! Makendo 2 is a comical VS fighting game with an eclectic cast of characters including a soccer player, a zombie, a musclebound mer-man, and a giant robot. Bouts are best two-out-of-three, and each character has both a life bar and a ""Makendo"" meter, which lets each character perform a variety of special attacks. The game includes a story mode and a 2-player versus mode.","Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","miximages/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png","marquees/snes/Makeruna! Makendou 2 - Kimero! Youkai Souridaijin (JP).png"
"snes_manchester-united-championship-soccer","Manchester United Championship Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Krisalis Software","Krisalis Software","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","40","2","The game was released at the time when Manchester United was starting to dominate the English football scene. All the teams from the 1994?95 FA Premier League are represented. All-star teams and various European clubs that participated in the European competitions from the 1994/95 season are also included. During the gameplay the player can choose two type of views: top down and isometric view of the pitch.","Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Manchester United Championship Soccer (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_mario-is-missing","Mario Is Missing!","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-06-01","1993","1990s","The Software Toolworks","Nintendo","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","30","1.5","Bowser, the token bad guy from the Mario Bros. series, is up to no good again in this educational game designed to teach children geography. This time he's set up his headquarters in Antarctica and created portals to 25 famous cities around the world, so that his Koopas can wreak havoc in our own world. He's also kidnapped Mario, hence the title of this game. You play as Luigi who must foil Bowser's plans by entering through each of the portals, tracking down the Koopas who have stolen famous artifacts, and looking for clues about your location. Once you've set everything right and determined where you are, you call Yoshi on your Globulator so he can track you down. You need Yoshi's help to eat the Pokey (a cactus-like creature) that's guarding the return portal, and when Luigi returns he can close the portal forever.

By exploring these 25 cities, children can familiarize themselves with the landmarks and artifacts that each city has. When Luigi returns the stolen artifacts to the proper places he can even take photographs of them. There is also an add-on disk you can purchase that adds ten additional cities to the game (it originally retailed for $24.95).","Mario is Missing! (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mario is Missing! (NA).png"
"snes_mario-no-super-picross","Mario No Super Picross","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-14","1995","1990s","Jupiter","Nintendo","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","A sequel to Mario's Picross on the GameBoy, Mario's Super Picross features the same gameplay as its predecessor. The game is played slab of stone with a grid on it. Above of every column and next to every row are numbers that acts as clues as to where a filled square is located along that column or row. The point of the game is to find all the filled squares on the grid by using your hammer and chiseling out squares that you think are filled and marking those that aren't with X.

There are two different sets of puzzles available but you start off with only one, Mario's Picross, and when you completed the first level, Wario will pop in and offer you his set of puzzles. The difference between the two is that Mario's Picross have to be completed within a certain time. Every time you chisel out the wrong square, it will deduct time. If time runs out before you can solve the puzzle, it's game over. Wario's Picross are timed to see how long it will take you to complete it, but will not run out. The catch here is that you will not be notified of a wrong square.

Other features includes game-saves, hints and tutorials.","Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","miximages/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","screenshots/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","backcovers/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png","marquees/snes/Mario no Super Picross (English Translated by FCandChill and Kumori, Rev 1.5).png"
"snes_mario-to-wario","Mario To Wario","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-08-27","1993","1990s","Game Freak","Nintendo","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","40","2","This is the Spirit Forest. Within these woods lives a sprite, and those who meet it find happiness, or so the tale goes. One day, Mario came to the woods to confirm the legend. Peach and Yoshi should have been together with Luigi......but alas, the visage of Luigi was missing. Mario's group of three have separated to find lost little Luigi.

At once, the suspicious sound of an engine was in the air. I wonder what it could be? It was Wario riding his personal plane, the Bulldog, and it dropped a bucket from the sky.

""Whew, woosh!""

And suddenly, the bucket was a snug fit on Mario's head.

""Uwagh, I can't see in this thing!""

The sprite of the woods, Wanda, witnessed it. The petite pixie did not have the strength to remove the bucket on her own, but she desired to help somehow. Thus, Wanda sends Mario a signal with her magic wand, determined to reunite him with Luigi......","Mario to Wario (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","miximages/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png","marquees/snes/Mario to Wario (JP).png"
"snes_mario-s-early-years-fun-with-letters","Mario's Early Years : Fun with Letters","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-01","1994","1990s","The Software Toolworks","The Software Toolworks","Educational","Action","1","1","1","80","4","Mario's Early Years: Fun With Letters is a collection of letter-related activities for kids ages 3 to 6 hosted by Mario and Co. Playing with either Mario or Princess Toadstool, you select from 10 different activity ""worlds"" each filled with different activities that range from letter recognition to sentence fill-in, letter-sound recognition, vowel recognition, etc. Each activity can be played in either Discovery mode, where you are free to do what you wish, or in Learning mode, where Luigi guides you through the activities.

The game also includes a Parent's Information Center, which explains what each of the activities does and how to complement them. Options to configure the activities to each parent's wishes are also provided.","Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Letters (NA).png"
"snes_mario-s-early-years-fun-with-numbers","Mario's Early Years : Fun with Numbers","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-01","1994","1990s","The Software Toolworks","The Software Toolworks","Educational","Action","1","1","1","40","2","In FUN WITH NUMBERS, children are introduced to the basics of math by way of Shape, Number, Same and Different, Counting, Comparing, How Many, and Pattern Worlds.

Children simply guide Mario, selecting objects on the screen, which playfully illustrate numerical concepts. Moms and Dads get to interact and play, too. Mario invites them to join in the fun and observe their children as they become totally involved in the learning process. Through the MARIO?S EARLY YEARS Series children will discover the world around them by exploring the elements of that world. The MARIO'S EARLY YEARS Series covers a multitude of subjects, helping children to acquire valuable skills and develop a rich and active imagination.","Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mario's Early Years - Fun With Numbers (NA).png"
"snes_mario-s-early-years-preschool-fun","Mario's Early Years : Preschool Fun","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-01","1994","1990s","The Software Toolworks","Mindscape","Educational","Action","1","1","1","40","2","In PRESCHOOL FUN, children develop concepts through the exploration of shapes, colors, sounds, opposites, and numbers. With Mario?s help, your child learns to define and identify these subjects without pressure. Your child simply guides Mario, selecting objects on the screen which Mario bonks and bounces through, frequently affirming your child's correct choice. With Mario, Luigi, Princess Toadstool and all their friends as classmates, your child just may make the biggest stride since learning to walk.

