"snes_mario-s-time-machine","Mario's Time Machine","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","The Software Toolworks","The Software Toolworks","Educational","Action","1","1","1","60","3","Bowser is at it again!  He's using a time machine, called a Timulator, to loot historical artifacts from the past, in order to stock his museum.  He plans to destroy the time machine after, and therefore change the course of history forever.  It's up to Mario to stop Bowser and return all the stolen artifacts to their rightful place in history!","Mario's Time Machine (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mario's Time Machine (NA).png"
"snes_mark-davis-the-fishing-master","Mark Davis' The Fishing Master","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-04-02","1996","1990s","Natsume","Natsume","Fishing","Action","1","1","1","60","3","In Mark Davis' The Fishing Master, the player can take control of fishing legend Mark Davis and fish in five different lakes and even compete in a fishing tournament to win a trophy.

The gameplay is reminiscent of Super Black Bass.  The player picks a location to fish using an overhead map where the player is then taken to a behind the person perspective to cast their reel.  Once the player casts their line, the view will change to a split screen with the original view on the top with a underwater view on the bottom to view the bait and an approaching fish.

Each lake has a different criteria to meet such as a weight limit, time limit, etc., to advance to the next lake and ultimately compete in the major tournament.  Players can also assemble their own set of authentic fishing gear including rods, reels, bait and various equipment.  The game also boasts that the fish in the game act realistically to their real-life counterparts.","Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mark Davis' The Fishing Master (NA).png"
"snes_marko-s-magic-football","Marko's Magic Football","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-02-01","1995","1990s","Domark","Acclaim Entertainment","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Colonel Brown, the evil owner of a toy factory, has created a substance that can turn people and animals into mutant sludge monsters. When Marko's football comes in touch with the substance it gets magical powers, giving Marko the power to stop Colonel Brown.

Now Marko has to find his way through numerous platform levels filled with enemies and obstacles. Using his magic football, he can perform various moves and attacks. He can kill his enemies with different kicks, header shots or even bicycle kicks and also use his ball as a trampoline. 

The SNES version features two additional moves for Marko (the ability to balance on the ball and a different method of returning it to him), but they do not have a great impact on gameplay.","Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Marko's Magic Football (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_marvel-super-heroes-in-war-of-the-gems","Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1997-02-01","1997","1990s","Capcom","Capcom","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems is a side-scrolling platformer/beat 'em up based on the Infinity Gauntlet storyline from the comics.  Adam Warlock calls on the heroes to recover the 6 Infinity Gems before they are used for evil.

You may choose ones of five heroes: Spider-Man, Hulk, Captain America, Iron Man and Wolverine.  Each one has different stats and abilities.  (i.e. Spider-Man is agile. Hulk is strong, Iron Man can double-jump with his rocket boots, etc.)  Initially you can choose a training area in Avenger headquarters or four levels.  As you complete levels, most open up.  Each hero can be equipped with gems to boost their abilities in each section.  These must be obtained by finding them in the levels.

Gameplay is fairly similar to X-Men-Mutant Apocalypse.  Combat is all on a 2D plane.  Each hero has basic jumps and attacks and special moves that can be executed with button combinations like quarter-rolls.  Enemies include various villains from the Marvel Universe and evil doubles of various Marvel heroes.","Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","miximages/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png","marquees/snes/Marvel Super Heroes in War of the Gems (NA).png"
