"snes_power-rangers","Power Rangers","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-26","1995","1990s","Natsume","Bandai","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","80","4","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers is a side-scrolling beat 'em up game that lets you play as the famous rangers from the series. Their goal is simple: repel the hordes of the witch Rita Repulsa. The game has the unique feature of adapting its colors to match the ranger you are playing. Each hero has their own weapon, but using it gradually depletes their health. This means that in most cases, you have to resort to standard attacks to get through unscathed. The timing of your strikes is very important, as your opponents quickly reach your avatar and hit hard.","Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers (NA).png"
"snes_mighty-morphin-power-rangers-the-fighting-edition","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers : The Fighting Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Bandai","Natsume","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Fighting Edition is a game directly based on the world-known television series. In this game, you can choice among 8 playable characters: the Power Rangers' Zords (Thunder Megazord, Mega Tigerzord, Ninja Megazord, Shogun Megazord) or some of their known villains (Lipsyncher, Silver Horns, Goldar, Lord Zedd). The title offers 3 game modes: Story Mode (1-Player only), Fighting Mode (2-Player) and Trial Mode (a survival mode for 1-Player only).

During Story Mode, the goal is to defeat all the 4 Zords, the 4 villains up to Lord Zedd and last, but not least, Ivan Ooze. In this mode, you can opt by the Thunder Megazord (formed by the 5 original Rangers) or by the Mega Tigerzord (formed in conjunction with the White Ranger). The Fighting Mode is an traditional 2-Player head-to-head combat, where you can choose any of the 4 Zords or even the 4 villains. Trial Mode is a Endurance-like option, and the main goal is to win as many battles as possible using only 1 health bar (that will be partially replenished after each battle).

As well as many fighting games, you can take advantage of a Power Bar (here, it fills automatically): if you execute a Super Move when this bar is flashing, it will be cause more damage, besides increasing 1 level. Once you having reached its maximum status, it's possible to execute power-up versions of Special Moves or even unleash high-damage blows (Super Moves).","Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Fighting Edition (NA).png"
"snes_mighty-morphin-power-rangers-the-movie","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers : The Movie","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-06-23","1995","1990s","Natsume","Bandai","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","This game is loosely based off of the movie of the same name, where the player can take control of either the Yellow, Black, Pink, Blue, Red or White Ranger in a side-scrolling beat-em-up in an attempt to stop the evil Ivan Ooze who is trying to control the universe.

There are six different levels to play in each with their own standard obstacles and enemies, mid-level bosses and of course end bosses that range from Mordant, Lord Zedd to Ivan Ooze himself.  There are no weapons that can be used, instead the player must rely on kicks and punches to dispatch enemies and pick up health items left behind.

Additionally, the Yellow, Black, Pink Rangers are extremely fast and can jump into higher areas but are more weaker than Blue, Red, White Rangers who are much stronger, but lack the speed and jumping abilities of the other Rangers.  Players can refill their health by picking up heart icons and power icons to increase their morphing meter.  Once filled, the morphing meter will increase the Rangers power, attack capabilities, speed and jumping abilities.","Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers - The Movie (NA).png"
