Miracle Girls is based on the characters of the manga and anime of the same name. The player starts the game by picking either Tomomi or Mikage, although they both have the same abilities. Either can jump or toss candy, which will render enemies harmless for a few seconds as they eat it. Enemies incapacitated in this way can be used as platforms. Hidden in levels are bombs that fill the screen with candy, turning any onscreen enemies into heart rings, fruit that increase health, and doors that lead to a celestial slot machine that can reward additional lives. At the end of each level is a different challenge with a boss, such as a top-down squirt-gun fight or a game of matching cards.","Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Miracle Girls (English Translated by RPGOne, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_mlbpa-baseball","MLBPA Baseball","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-03-02","1994","1990s","Visual Concepts","EA Sports","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","The strategy of baseball is merged with a fast-paced arcade game in MLBPA Baseball from Electronic Arts. Details designed to appeal to the die-hard fan include: real players with statistics based on the 1993 season; a full 162 game season mode; stadium music; animated scoreboards; defensive alignments; cut-off plays; run-downs; and even the double switch. Features meant to appeal to the casual fan include: large colorful arcade graphics; one stadium with animated crowds; a simplified pitching interface allowing players to steer the ball; and a batting interface that relies on timing instead of aiming cursors. Secret power-up play modes await so step up to the plate and take some hacks! Season play can be continued using passwords provided at the end of each game.","MLBPA Baseball (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","miximages/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","screenshots/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","backcovers/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png","marquees/snes/MLBPA Baseball (NA).png"
