"snes_monopoly","Monopoly","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-06-01","1992","1990s","Sculptured Software","Parker Brothers","Board game","Board / Casual","1-8","1","8","70","3.5","This time, a Monopoly game on your computer, as good as it knows to be in your reality. Every move of yours can be in 3D animation, or off if you don't want to see animations. There can be up to 6 players at once, and it can be played over the Internet. Music is in midi format, and the sound quality is at the wav format. Roll, spin, and don't miss to give us a grin.","Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Monopoly (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_monstania","Monstania","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-09-27","1996","1990s","Bits Laboratory","Pack In Video","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-8","1","8","70","3.5","The hero of the game is Fron, a sixteen-year old boy who lives on the island of Monstania. One day, strolling in the forest, he notices a strange light. The light lead him to a clearing, and then suddenly disappeared. But Fron realized what was the meaning of that light - it was a fairy! Of course, everybody knew that fairies had been long extinct, but Fron never believed in that. All his life he wanted to meet a real fairy, and now, when the opportunity has come, he firmly decides to find her. His girlfriend Tia helps him on the dangerous journey, during which they meet a mysterious little girl named Chitta, and get involved in a grand adventure, that will ultimately lead them to the battle against the dark force that threatens the whole Monstania!

""Monstania"" has a somewhat unusual gameplay within the frames of console RPGs. You don't explore the world in the game: it is entirely linear and takes you to the next destination by itself (only at a few points you can choose where to go next by selecting an appropriate answer). Once within the location, you cannot leave it until you complete all your objectives there, which then take you to the next location. The objective is usually a large strategic battle. You navigate your party members on the battle field, attack with melee and long-ranged weapons, and use special technique which require action points. Unlike most other turn-based strategy games, an enemy makes a move immediately after you did the same with one of your characters, without waiting for the ""enemy turn"". The RPG element is not very significant: your characters level up automatically after each battle. There are also some puzzles to solve in certain locations.","Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","miximages/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","screenshots/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","titlescreens/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","3dboxes/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","backcovers/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png","marquees/snes/Monstania (English Translated by Aeon Genesis, Rev 1.03).png"
"snes_mortal-kombat","Mortal Kombat","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-10-28","1993","1990s","Midway","Acclaim Entertainment","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Five Hundred years ago, an ancient and well respected Shaolin fighting tournament, held every 50 years, was corrupted by an evil and elderly sorcerer by the name of Shang Tsung.  Shang was accompanied by Prince Goro, a warrior of the Shokan race (a four armed half-human/half-dragon). Knowing that if ten tournaments in a row were won by the Outworld champion, the Earth Realm would be conquered by evil and fall into darkness, Shang entered Goro in the tournament and had him defeat the great Kung Lao. Goro has been  reigning supreme as the undefeated fighting champion for five hundred years now. As the last tournament required draws near, Raiden, Thunder God and protector of the Earth Realm, enacts a plan to tip the scales in the humans favor, Seven fighters step into the arena on Shang Tsung's mysterious island: Shaolin warrior Liu Kang, Special Forces operative Sonya Blade, the mercenary thug Kano, fame-seeking actor Johnny Cage, the ice wielding Lin Kuei warrior Sub-Zero and his undead adversary Scorpion, and Raiden himself.

Mortal Kombat is a side-scrolling 1 on 1 fighting game. Fighting is set as one on one kombat, allowing each player to perform a variety of punches, kicks, and special moves in order to defeat their opponent.  When the opponent faces their second round loss, the winner can perform a finishing move called a ""Fatality"" on the loser.  The Fatality is a move unique to each fighter that graphically kills the loser in a blood-soaked finale.

Mortal Kombat began its life as a 2-player arcade title. It is notable for its use of digitized actors to represent the game's fighters, as well as its use of copious amounts of blood during gameplay.","Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Mortal Kombat (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_mortal-kombat-iii","Mortal Kombat III","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Sculptured Software","Acclaim Entertainment","Fighting / Versus","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","Shao Kahn has won. The Earthrealm is no more. In order to revive his Queen Sindel, the emperor Shao Kahn used the Outworld Tournament from Mortal Kombat 2 as a diversion while his Shadow Priests revive his fallen Queen on Earth. Once enacted, the dimensional bridge between the two realms connects, allowing Kahn's extermination squads to invade and destroy Earth, and enslave the population's souls.

A small team of Raiden's ""Chosen Warriors"" survives the attack: Mortal Kombat champion Liu Kang and his ally Kung Lao, Special Forces agents Sonya Blade and Jax, the shaman Nightwolf, the riot cop Stryker, the nomadic Kabal, and former Lin Kuei warrior Sub-Zero, who has gone rogue from his clan. Facing the warriors are the mercenary Kano, cyber-ninjas Smoke, Sektor and Cyrax, Sheeva, a female Shokan, the sorcerer Shang Tsung, and Queen Sindel herself.","Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Mortal Kombat 3 (NA).png"
"snes_mortal-kombat-ii","Mortal Kombat II","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-09","1994","1990s","Sculptured Software","Acclaim Entertainment","Fighting / Versus","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","The Mortal Kombat fighters, plus several new ones, return for a tournament held by the evil Shang Tsung of the Outworld. The action is one-on-one as before, and famed for its high level of violence and blood (other than the sanitised Nintendo version). There are 5 difficulty levels and optional credits, as well as the usual two player mode including same character duels.

To win the main tournament, the player must beat each of the other human players, before taking on Shang Tsung, Kintaro and finally Shao Kahn. Players have a range of punches and kicks available, as well as flying kicks, uppercuts, roundhouses, and the special moves, which vary for each player. These include throws, uppercuts, long-distance bullets, bicycle kicks and a teleport feature.","Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Mortal Kombat II (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_mortal-kombat","Mortal Kombat","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-10-28","1993","1990s","Midway","Acclaim Entertainment","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Five Hundred years ago, an ancient and well respected Shaolin fighting tournament, held every 50 years, was corrupted by an evil and elderly sorcerer by the name of Shang Tsung.  Shang was accompanied by Prince Goro, a warrior of the Shokan race (a four armed half-human/half-dragon). Knowing that if ten tournaments in a row were won by the Outworld champion, the Earth Realm would be conquered by evil and fall into darkness, Shang entered Goro in the tournament and had him defeat the great Kung Lao. Goro has been  reigning supreme as the undefeated fighting champion for five hundred years now. As the last tournament required draws near, Raiden, Thunder God and protector of the Earth Realm, enacts a plan to tip the scales in the humans favor, Seven fighters step into the arena on Shang Tsung's mysterious island: Shaolin warrior Liu Kang, Special Forces operative Sonya Blade, the mercenary thug Kano, fame-seeking actor Johnny Cage, the ice wielding Lin Kuei warrior Sub-Zero and his undead adversary Scorpion, and Raiden himself.

Mortal Kombat is a side-scrolling 1 on 1 fighting game. Fighting is set as one on one kombat, allowing each player to perform a variety of punches, kicks, and special moves in order to defeat their opponent.  When the opponent faces their second round loss, the winner can perform a finishing move called a ""Fatality"" on the loser.  The Fatality is a move unique to each fighter that graphically kills the loser in a blood-soaked finale.

Mortal Kombat began its life as a 2-player arcade title. It is notable for its use of digitized actors to represent the game's fighters, as well as its use of copious amounts of blood during gameplay.","Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).sfc","SFC","2.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","miximages/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","screenshots/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","titlescreens/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","3dboxes/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","backcovers/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png","marquees/snes/Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Gold 2000 (TW).png"
