"snes_operation-starfi5h","Operation Starfi5h","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Millennium Interactive","U.S. Gold","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Unlike the  first game of the series, that was a mission-based game, and the  second one, where your character had unique abilities such as observing the whole level and growing to unlimited height, ""James Pond 3"" is a standard jump and run platform game. Pond can run very quickly (by holding down the A button) through large levels, which often contain steep mountain sides and other tricky areas. Once again, he has to oppose the evil scientist Maybe and his minions.","Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Operation Starfi5h (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_operation-thunderbolt","Operation Thunderbolt","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-10-02","1994","1990s","Taito","Taito","Lightgun Shooter","Shooter","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Operation Thunderbolt is the exciting sequel to Operation Wolf. An airliner is hijacked by terrorists en-route from Paris to Boston, who threaten to kill all hostages on board if their mates aren't released from jail. Instead of reaching its destination, the airliner makes a landing in Kalubya, Africa, and all the hostages are hidden in various locations. The authorities have asked the hero from Operation Wolf to rescue the hostages, but only this time, the hero brings his friend along for the ride.

There are eight missions to complete in Operation Thunderbolt, and each one has you shooting down soldiers, choppers, and tanks. The gameplay varies every one or two missions. In some missions, you are driving a jeep or controlling a boat, while in others, you are walking while you're shooting. You have a limited supply of ammo, and a limited supply of rocket bombs, but you can always stock up by shooting down crates falling from the sky, or by killing a cat or dog that get in the line of fire. Also from crates, you can get special items like bulletproof vests, rocket bombs, and different weapons.

You also have a life bar to worry about. If you're shot at by soldiers, or if rocket bombs or grenades are thrown at you, you 'll lose energy, and once you're energy is depleted,  you lose one of your three lives. You can lose a lot of energy by killing hostages on purpose,  and you can't easily avoid killing them if you decide to use rocket bombs to wipe out enemies. The eighth mission, the mission that involves you fighting terrorists on a plane,  proves to be difficult because a woman in a blue dress stands up and gets in the line of fire, and you have to very careful when you're going to use rocket bombs.

There are two endings to this game, and which ending you can watch will depend on the number of hostages you've saved, and whether or not you shot the pilot instead of the mission eight boss.","Operation Thunderbolt (NA).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","miximages/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png","marquees/snes/Operation Thunderbolt (NA).png"
"snes_oscar","Oscar","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-12-01","1996","1990s","Flair Software","Flair Software","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Lights! Camera! Action! It's time to meet Oscar, the newest legend of the silver screen, ready to take Tinseltown by storm... once he's used his star-power to escape the theater he's trapped in, that is!

Star in the role of a lifetime as you help Oscar navigate 4 different levels full of fun and adventure in search of a way to escape the fantasy film world he's trapped in. Will our hero be able to turn in an award-winning performance and escape from the theater, or will he be stuck on-screen forever?","Oscar (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Oscar (NA).png","miximages/snes/Oscar (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Oscar (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Oscar (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Oscar (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Oscar (NA).png","marquees/snes/Oscar (NA).png"
