"snes_paperboy-2","Paperboy 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Tengen","Mindscape","Sports / Cycling","Sports","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","You're a paper boy. Get on your bicycle. Avoid obstacles on the road, such as dogs, cars, and basically everything you can imagine. Hell, some people shoot cannon balls at you! And you'd better be very sure to only throw papers at the right houses! (and at people, that's fun :)","Paperboy 2 (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Paperboy 2 (NA).png"
"snes_parlor-mini-pachinko-jikki-simulation-game","Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-04-26","1996","1990s","Telenet","Telenet","Casino","Board / Casual","1","1","1","80","4","Parlor! Mini: Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (""Jikki"" means ""machine"") is a pachinko game for the Super Famicom and the first in an off-shoot series based on Telenet Japan's Parlor! Parlor! series which intends to teach Super Famicom owners how to win big on real-life versions of the machines they feature. The Parlor! Mini series focuses on a smaller number of machines - typically two per game - and were sold for a budget price. Parlor! Mini was followed by seven sequels released throughout 1996, 1997 and 1998.

The first Parlor! Mini features a machine with an aquatic theme and another with an Asian dragon theme. Both have a pachi-slot component, where aiming pachinko balls for the device in the middle of the table would cause slots to spin. The player is free to practice on the machines with an infinite supply of pachinko balls, scrutinize the peg configurations for both and get tips and advice from the game to learn how to master their real-life equivalents.","Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Parlor! Mini - Pachinko Jikki Simulation Game (JP, Rev 1).png"
