"snes_power-rangers-zeo-battle-racers","Power Rangers Zeo : Battle Racers","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-09-01","1996","1990s","Natsume","Bandai","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","In this racing title based in the Zeo season of world-famous television series Power Rangers, players are allowed to select among the six Zeo Rangers (Pink, Yellow, Red, Blue, Green, Gold) or their enemies (King Mondo, Cog Soldier) to compete in a head-to-head circuit challenge along 16 race courses divided by 5 Tracks.

Each pilot has different attribute levels for Acceleration, Speed and Grip, providing a more balanced competition. Besides several obstacles and speed energizers scattered by the courses, players can attack opponents by firing Blasters (a la Super Mario Kart special items) at your adversaries; the limit is 5 Blasters per race except by Cog Soldier's infinite Blaster amount.

Along with 1-Player game modes (Race, Time Trial and VS CPU), the game also offers 2-Player split-screen gameplay through Race and 2P VS plus 3 alternative modalities: Point Race, where players must to race over objects to earn points; Bumper Chase, with the main objective to ram the opponent off the course; and Blaster Master, a Life Energy-based deathmatch.","Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","miximages/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png","marquees/snes/Power Rangers Zeo - Battle Racers (NA).png"
"snes_power-slide","Power Slide","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","The 3DO Company","The 3DO Company","Racing TPV","Racing","1","1","1","","","Power Slide is a cancelled game for the SNES and 3DO that had an amazing graphic for its time. The Super Nintendo version was going to be one of the few games to make use of the FX chip. It was being developed by Elite. Another racing game by the name Power Slide was eventually released for PC but it doesnt seem to be connected to this game in any way. The car handling physics in Power Slide were very advanced for the time, as were the visuals. Frame rate was less impressive unfortunately. A playable demo of Power Slide SNES does exist and it was leaked thanks to Eludevisibility! The in-game screens dont look anywhere as nice as the original tech demo tough. The game would have probably been like Dirt Racer, the other SNES racing game by Elite, released in 1994. Power Slide was basically a rally game, with real rally cars, Dirt Racer was a more arcade style game. The 3DO and PC versions of Power Slide were being developed by Maelstrom Games for Elite.","Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/Power Slide (Prototype - NTSC Conversion).png"
