"snes_seifuku-densetsu-pretty-fighter","Seifuku Densetsu Pretty Fighter","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-02","1994","1990s","Genki","Imagineer","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","60","3","8 beautiful fighters must compete against one another to prove that they are indeed the most beautiful warrior in the world. Do you have what it takes to defeat the challenger?","Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","miximages/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png","marquees/snes/Seifuku Densetsu - Pretty Fighter (JP).png"
"snes_seiken-densetsu-3","Seiken Densetsu 3","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-09-30","1995","1990s","Square","Squaresoft","Action RPG","RPG","1-3","1","3","90","4.5","Long ago, an era of peace was built upon eight Mana Stones that sealed away the world's ancient God-Beasts. Now, that peace is fading as rival kingdoms and dark powers move to claim this force for their own.
The story is defined by your choice of three heroes from a cast of six unique characters: Duran the swordsman, Angela the magician, Kevin the beastman, Charlotte the cleric, Hawkeye the thief, and Riesz the Amazon. The hero you select first determines which of three main storylines unfolds.
An action-oriented role-playing game, Seiken Densetsu 3 features a real-time 'Motion Battle' system. Characters evolve through a deep 'Class Change' system, where players choose a path of 'Light' or 'Dark' to unlock advanced classes with entirely new abilities, strengths, and spells.","Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","miximages/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","screenshots/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","titlescreens/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","3dboxes/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","backcovers/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png","marquees/snes/Seiken Densetsu 3 (English Translated by LNF Translations, Neill Corlett, and SoM2Freak, Rev 1.01).png"
"snes_sengoku-denshou","Sengoku Denshou","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-09-19","1993","1990s","Data East","Data East","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","A 2D side-scrolling beat 'em up, Sengoku casts you and a friend as two renegade fighters out to beat the crap out of the many assorted gangs that threaten the post-apocalyptic cities of the future. Unfortunately for them they also get caught in a time-warping scheme caused by the evil Nobunaga who attempts to invade the time period with mythical warriors and evil creatures from the Japanese sengoku period.

The game thus takes you from the city to a spirit-realm from time to time, in which you must fight all sorts of Japanese mythical figures, and release three haunted spirits that can aid you in your battle. Collecting orbs from defeated enemies allows you heal up, gain weapons and even energy attacks and also summon the warrior forms of the spirits you released, which change your character's form and give you a new collection of attacks and powers.","Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","miximages/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","screenshots/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","titlescreens/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","3dboxes/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","backcovers/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png","marquees/snes/Sengoku Denshou (English Translated by Vice Translations).png"
