"snes_spider-man-amp-x-men-arcade-s-revenge","Spider-Man &amp; X-Men : Arcade's Revenge","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-08-19","1993","1990s","Software Creations","Software Creations","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Spider-Man and members of the X-Men have teamed up in this side-scrolling action game to fight against Arcade, who has built a giant amusement park for the sole purpose of trapping and destroying the super-heroes. You first play as Spider-Man, who sees the X-Men get kidnapped by Arcade and follows them. Once you make it inside Arcade's park you can choose to play as Spider-Man, Cyclops, Storm, Gambit, or Wolverine, each of whom are trapped in a different part of Arcade's maze of deadly traps. You must navigate all five of them safely out, using their different skills and abilities while defeating baddies and bosses along the way.","Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","miximages/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png","marquees/snes/Spider-Man - X-Men - Arcade's Revenge (NA).png"
"snes_spindizzy-worlds","Spindizzy Worlds","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-11-01","1992","1990s","ASCII","ASCII","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","70","3.5","On it's most basic level, Spindizzy Worlds is, like its predecessor, similar to Marble Madness. Controlling GERALD, you must move through the isometrically viewed landscape (largely flick-screen on the ST). There are two skill levels; the harder one features more of the precarious ledges and falls of Spindizzy. Each one takes you to a different matrix of levels, which can be played in different orders and each consist of 10 screens, with a bonus level at the end.

You have limited energy, which can be recharged by collecting crystals. Fuel is limited, and is reduced by contact with hazards - generating a replacement GERALD takes time. There are many gates which are opened by running into spaces of the same colour. There are also aliens to avoid, and most movement is along thin slippery ledges with heavily inertia-based controls.","Spindizzy Worlds (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","miximages/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png","marquees/snes/Spindizzy Worlds (NA).png"
