"snes_super-bikkuriman","Super Bikkuriman","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-29","1993","1990s","Tom Create","BEC","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","60","3","Super Bikkuriman is a fighter game from BEC (Interbec) and Tom Create, based on a popular collectible sticker franchise. Specifically, the game is based on the 44 episode 1992-93 anime adaptation with the same name, and features most of its cast of characters in the roster. The game includes two modes: a single-player elimination tournament against increasingly difficult computer opponents, and a versus mode for up to two players.

In the single-player mode, the player can only choose from two characters: Phoenix and Tiki. The two characters fight almost identically. They fight through the other six characters from the versus mode and a ""clone fight"" against the character they did not select. Beating the game leads to the ending and a password (A, B, L, R, X, Y, Start) that allows players to select the same character as their opponent in versus mode.","Super Bikkuriman (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Bikkuriman (JP).png"
