"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling","Super Fire Pro Wrestling","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1991-12-20","1991","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","Fire Pro Wrestling has taken Japan by storm, and now it has come to the Super Famicom! 110 unique move are at your disposal, and this is the most realistic simulation of wrestling ever!","Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling (JP).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-queen-s-special","Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-06-30","1995","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Long before the WWE introduced the Divas wrestling matches, in Japan there was a more serious affair, where wrestling skill was more important than breast implants, and matches were ""real"" (as far as wrestling goes) instead of pillow-fighting or bra and panties fights.

In this game in the Fire Pro Series, the cast of the All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling promotion are available, all fighting to win the Red belt, the highest prize of the federation. It's also possible to fight in single matches, tournaments, Battle Royal and Elimination matches. The usual array of options in CAW is present, being possible to create 16 new Wrestlers.

Gameplay, as usual is the series, is dramatically different than in most western games. Each wrestler has a bunch of moves, ranked from weak to strong. While it's possible to connect any of them from open situations, while grappling only when the opponent is already beaten the most powerful moves can be successfully used.","Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling - Queen's Special (English Translated by Phil).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-2","Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-12-25","1992","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","The formula is the same, but the game has become much more powerful! More moves, more wrestlers, more mayhem! Up to four simultaneous players can now enjoy the greatest wrestling action on the Super Famicom!","Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling 2 (JP).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-3-easy-type","Super Fire Pro Wrestling 3 - Easy Type","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-04","1994","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-8","1","8","90","4.5","Super Fire Pro Wrestling 3 Final Bout was released in 1993. This is the first game ever created with contribution from Goichi Suda. Due to complaints about the game's difficulty, Human released ""Super Fire Pro Wrestling 3 Easy Type"". In this version there is no edit mode but all of the hidden wrestlers are unlocked.

Characters based on wrestling stars such as WWF's Hulk Hogan and WCW's Rick Rude are featured in the game along with Japanese professional wrestlers like Masahiro Chono. Each wrestler is ranked based on their attacking ability, defensive ability, and their running speed. An ""edit mode"" allows customized wrestlers to be created based on their wrestling type, the color of their skin, and a unique set of customized ring attire. A certain amount of points also have to be spent on developing certain attacks (and their respective defense against these attacks from opposing wrestlers). Digitized voices from the wrestlers and cheers from the audience members are included. Two of the buttons on the Super Famicom controller are used for strong blows while another button is used strictly for low blows. Sprites in the game actually show wrestlers in different sizes to each other (depending on height and weight). A battle royale mode permits four wrestlers to face off against each other simultaneously. There are 56 different wrestlers to control; with eight playable wrestling legends. Referees are available and can be chosen by the player; each referee has his own level of strictness and essentially determine how long the match will last. It is possible to perform up to 300 different professional wrestling moves in the game.","Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Easy Type (JP).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-3-final-bout","Super Fire Pro Wrestling 3 - Final Bout","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-28","1993","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-8","1","8","80","4","The action is once again presented in an isometric ring, and players must use timing-based button presses to effectively grapple and pin their opponents. The player can choose from a number of wrestlers, many of whom are from international circuits like the WWE and WCW, who are all homages to actual wrestlers under different names. The player could also make their own wrestler in the game's ""create-a-wrestler"" editor mode, a series staple.","Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling III - Final Bout (JP, Rev 1).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-special","Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-22","1994","1990s","Human Club","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","In this Special Fire Pro, you are a rookie wrestler working his way up through the ranks. During the journey, you fall in love with the sister of a wrestler named Akira Saeha. The road to the championship bout is a struggle, with loss after loss, both inside and outside of the ring, including you accidentally killing your best friend during a match.","Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling Special (Story Mode English Translated by BobSchneeder45, Boogal, and Iccanobif).png"
"snes_super-fire-pro-wrestling-x-premium","Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-03-29","1996","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Sports / Wrestling","Sports","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","In this final appearance of Fire Pro series on 16-bit consoles, the usual roster of over 150 wrestlers from several wresting promotions worldwide including several styles from Shoot or Pancrase to American and Lucha are joined by 80 Create-a-wrestler slots, plus secret wrestlers such as legends Gotch or Thesz or the roster of Blazing Tornado. While all fighters have fictional names, a lot of them are perfectly recognizable by their attire, stance and style. The CAW mode allows the player to create a wrestler from scratch, setting how they look (choosing face, size, clothing and setting colours) and fight, with several styles and stances available, as well as over 500 moves, each more suitable for certain styles and skills. To make them fight more realistically when controlled by the AI, the CAW mode also allows one to set move priorities.

Five game modes are available, including World Championship (single and tag), Battle Royale, 5-man Elimination Mode, League Battle and the One Night Dream Match. There are several referees available (each with their own quirks) and variant rules, from allowing fighting outside the ring without count-out (or disallowing it) to the disabling of disqualifications from illegal moves.","Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","miximages/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png","marquees/snes/Super Fire Pro Wrestling X Premium (English Translated by Brian).png"
"snes_super-fishing-big-fight","Super Fishing - Big Fight","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-16","1994","1990s","Geo Factory","Naxat Soft","Fishing","Action","1","1","1","70","3.5","Super Fishing: Big Fight is a fishing game released on the Super Famicom in 1994. It was developed by Geo Factory (their second Super Famicom game, after Super Jinsei Game) and published by Naxat Soft. The player, as an avid fisherman in a green backwards cap, is invited to participate in a multi-stage fishing contest that takes place across Japan.

The game uses a third-person behind-the-angler perspective, and the player can select a spot in each of the game's fishing areas and pick which direction to cast their line. There are different lures and bait that the player can use which all perform differently and attract different fish.

The game was followed in 1997 with a Sega Saturn sequel: Top Anglers: Super Fishing Big Fight 2.","Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Fishing Big Fight (JP).png"
"snes_super-formation-soccer-94-world-cup-edition","Super Formation Soccer 94 - World Cup Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-08-17","1994","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Super Formation Soccer 94 is a 1994 soccer game from Human Entertainment that was released exclusively on the Super Famicom. It is the third game in their Super Formation Soccer series. It is based on the 1994 World Cup event, held in the USA, and features the twenty four national teams that qualified that year. Japan, which did not qualify, replaces South Korea (which did) in the roster to appease the Japan-exclusive audience for the game.

The game features alternate modes as well as a World Cup Mode, and in these modes the player can select other non-qualifying teams like England, Uruguay, France and Denmark.

Super Formation Soccer 94 was rereleased as the updated Super Formation Soccer 94 World Cup Final Data in September the same year.","Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Edition (JP).png"
"snes_super-formation-soccer-94-world-cup-final-data","Super Formation Soccer 94 - World Cup Final Data","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-22","1994","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Super Formation Soccer 94: World Cup Final Data is an updated version of Super Formation Soccer 94: World Cup Edition, which was released merely 3 months later. It includes updated rosters and has minor improvements, such as the ability to view replays of fouls and goals.","Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","miximages/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png","marquees/snes/Super Formation Soccer '94 - World Cup Final Data (JP).png"
"snes_super-formation-soccer-95-della-serie-a","Super Formation Soccer 95 Della Serie A","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-03-31","1995","1990s","Human Entertainment","Human Entertainment","Sports","Sports","1-4","1","4","70","3.5","Super Formation Soccer 95: della Serie A is a soccer game from Human Entertainment and the fourth Super Nintendo game in their Formation Soccer series. It focuses entirely on Serie A, the highest division in the Italian Football League, and is licensed by the Italian Football League and Associazione Italiana Calciatori to use the real team and player names for the eighteen sides of the 1994-95 season of Serie A. It was released on the same day as another Serie A soccer game developed by a Japanese studio: Shijou Saikyou League Serie A: Ace Striker from TNN.

The game was released alongside two alternate versions:

- The Extra Package version which included a special booklet with stats and data on all 396 players in the Serie A league.
- A promotional version sponsored by UCC Xaqua, a soft drink endorsed by the Italian Football League and the footballer Roberto Baggio that consumers could win by entering a postcard competition. This particular edition had a very limited distribution.

The game uses sprite-scaling for its presentation, displaying the pitch from an angled vertical perspective in which the far side of the pitch is always visible, though becomes smaller or larger the closer the player is to the opposing goal. It also includes the player name across the bottom of the screen for whoever has possession of the ball at the time, making it easier to track what certain players are doing.","Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","miximages/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","screenshots/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","backcovers/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png","marquees/snes/Super Formation Soccer '95 - Della Serie A (JP - UCC Xaqua Version).png"
