"snes_super-turrican-2","Super Turrican 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-11-02","1995","1990s","Ocean","Ocean","Platform / Shooter Scrolling","Shooter","1","1","1","80","4","Super Turrican is back, and once again the USS Freedom Forces have to prevent the evil Machine from harming innocent civilizations.
This requires the player to jump and shoot his way through large levels filled with lots of enemies. To get rid of all the enemies, several different weapons can be used, most of which are already familiar to players from previous episodes: a Laser, a Spread-shot, and a(improved) Rebound. There is also the option to go into ""wheel-mode"" for a limited time to become invincible, lay mines and shoot rockets. The Flamethrower is new to the series as well as the Rope, which can be used to climb walls, cling to platforms or pick up out-of-reach items. Much like in side-scrolling shooters, you can now pick up homing missiles as secondary weapons. The biggest difference to previous Turrican-games however, is the fact that in Super Turrican 2 almost half of the levels are strictly linear and don't feature any large secret areas.","Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","miximages/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png","marquees/snes/Super Turrican 2 Special Edition (NA).png"
"snes_super-turrican-collection","Super Turrican Collection","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","2026-02-27","2026","2020s","Factor 5","Strictly Limited Games","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","","","Super Turrican Collection, or Super Turrican Director's Cut is a full-length version of Super Turrican, originally included digitally on the Analogue Super Nt console in 2018 and later as part of the Turrican Anthology compilation and as a standalone release in March 2022. This version restores most some content removed from the original version of the game, including one of the cut stages, and reorganizes some of the levels.","Super Turrican Collection (NA).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png","miximages/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png","","marquees/snes/Super Turrican Collection (NA).png"
