"snes_takeda-nobuhiro-no-super-league-soccer","Takeda Nobuhiro No Super League Soccer","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-25","1994","1990s","TOSE","Jaleco","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (æ­¦ç”°ä¿®å®ã®ã‚¹ãƒ¼ãƒ‘ãƒ¼ãƒªãƒ¼ã‚°ã‚µãƒƒã‚«ãƒ¼ Nobuhiro Takeda's Suparigusakka, ""Nobuhiro Takeda's Super League Soccer"") is a soccer simulation video game licensed/endorsed by Takeda Nobuhiro, published by Jaleco Entertainment for the Super Famicom console, which was released exclusively in Japan in 1994.

This game is a sequel to Takeda Nobuhiro no Super Cup Soccer. It features club teams based on the top division of Japan Professional Football League J. League Division 1 (though unlicensed) instead of national teams. While it kept largely the same structure of the original game, some new options were added.","Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","miximages/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png","marquees/snes/Takeda Nobuhiro no Super League Soccer (JP).png"
"snes_tales-of-phantasia","Tales Of Phantasia","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-15","1995","1990s","Wolf Team","Namco","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","In ""Tales of Phantasia"", you play a young boy named Cless, who lives together with his parents in a quiet village. It was a day like all the others when Cless decided to go hunting with his best friend Chester. Chasing a wild boar, Cless discovered a strange talking tree in the forest who was pleading him for help. But as soon as it stopped speaking, the two friends heard the sound of an alarm. They returned to the village and found it burnt down, and all its inhabitants murdered. Before Cless' mother died in his arms, she told him this terrible massacre had something to do with the pendant she and her husband gave Cless for his birthday... what connection could there be? Cless decides to visit his uncle who lives in another town, but he doesn't realize his journey will take him to much more remote places than that!","Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).sfc","SFC","6","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","miximages/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","screenshots/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","titlescreens/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","3dboxes/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","backcovers/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png","marquees/snes/Tales of Phantasia (English Translated and Alt Font Patch by DeJap, Rev 1.2 With Modern ROM Format Patch by Spinner 8 and Friends).png"
"snes_tarzan-lord-of-the-jungle","Tarzan : Lord of the Jungle","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","","","","Manley &amp; Associates","GameTek","Action / Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","","","The player controls Tarzan (based on the famous character created by Edgar Rice Burroughs for his novel Tarzan of the Apes) in six different missions set in Africa. These include curing the Great Ape's disease and saving his friends from the evil poachers. These poachers want to capture the wildlife and place them in their zoos. Weapons that can be utilized include: spears, knives, and arrows. Pitfalls and obstacles are to be avoided in order to collect the mandatory quest item. Under a strict time limit, players can swing on vines and swim vast bodies of water to cross various parts of stages.","Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","miximages/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","screenshots/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","titlescreens/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","3dboxes/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","backcovers/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png","marquees/snes/Tarzan - Lord of the Jungle (Prototype With Control Fix Patch by Rich Whitehouse).png"
"snes_taz-mania","Taz-Mania","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Visual Concepts","Sunsoft","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","80","4","This version of Taz-Mania is different from the side-scrolling versions by Sega, in this version the player controls Taz from a third-person perspective.  The goal of the game is to travel down the road, collecting Kiwi's before the timer runs out, avoiding obstacles along the way.  The Kiwi's will get harder to catch as the game goes on, jumping over Taz and actually outrunning him at times.

Some obstacles Taz faces are trees, telephone poles, tour buses, even pterodactyls who will bring Taz back at the beginning of the level, but also have to avoid characters such as Axl &amp; Bull, a pair of gators who try to capture Taz for the zoo, The She-Devil who is in love with Taz and if the player is caught by her, the game is instantly over and Wendal T. Wolf, who will jump on Taz's back and cover the screen with his hands making it hard to see.

You can avoid some obstacles by using Taz's tornado spin, but using the spin will cause Taz's health meter to drop, but it can be refilled by eating Kiwi's along with blue and red birds, bushrats and items thrown to Taz by Didgeri Dingo, but beware, he can also throw obstacles at Taz as well including T.N.T.  There is also a bonus stages after completing three levels in which you collect as many items you can in the allotted time to raise the score.","Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Taz-Mania (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_tecmo-secret-of-the-stars","Tecmo Secret of the Stars","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-07-01","1995","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-3","1","3","50","2.5","You are a young boy named Ray, who lives with his foster-father in a small country house on an island. But he can not enjoy his idyllic life for a long time. Ray is told about the evil wizard Homncruise (yes, that's the name) who plans to conquer the world. Defeating Homncruise won't be easy: first Ray must find the magic crest of his fallen father, and build a strong team of legendary warriors, named Aquitallion. Only then will he and his comrades be ready to face Homncruise and to save the world.

In this game you wander around the world map. visiting towns and dungeons, and fighting monsters in turn-based combat viewed from first-person perspective, much like in Dragon Quest games. You'll have two parties at your disposal, and will be able to switch between them at any time. One party is the Aquitallion, the ""main"" one, and the only one which can access plot-progressing areas. The other parties can be used for visiting dungeons and retrieving valuable items. At a certain point in the game, you'll also be able to build and to manage your own town.","Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Secret of the Stars (NA).png"
"snes_tecmo-super-baseball","Tecmo Super Baseball","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-09-01","1994","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Baseball","Sports","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","This is Tecmo's attempt at baseball after their Tecmo Bowl series. It has 700 authentic MLBPA players including Ken Griffey Jr., Tony Gwynn and Barry Bonds to name a few.  However, it does not feature an MLB license, so the cities nicknames and logos have been omitted, but all 28 teams with 1993 stats are still included.

The standard modes apply including Exhibition, All-Star and Season in which the player can choose either to play a full or reduced season.  The player can also choose to simulate games and watch them unfold or they also have the option to manage their team and watch the outcome of their decisions.  It also features a battery backup to allow saving of stats and games as well as two-player capabilities to allow friends to compete head-to-head.","Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Super Baseball (NA).png"
"snes_tecmo-super-bowl","Tecmo Super Bowl","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-01","1993","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Tecmo returns to the gridiron with this new version of Tecmo Super Bowl for 16-bit console systems. Play with real National Football League players and teams in this 2D, side-scrolling arcade game.  All of the features from the 8-bit game remain intact, with brand new ones added for even more electronic football fun!  

Additions include updated player rosters, options for weather effects (rain, snow), multiple season play (three regular season schedules available in all), adjustable game time length, and an offensive playbook that can be edited even during a game.","Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).sfc","SFC","1.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl (NA).png"
"snes_tecmo-super-bowl-ii-special-edition","Tecmo Super Bowl II : Special Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-02","1995","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","60","3","The follow up to the first 16-bit version of Tecmo Super Bowl. Includes the real NFL teams and players and the same basic gameplay as previous installments in the series.  There are also variety of new features and minor enhancements, such as slightly angled play perspective, larger player graphics, new movement animations, expanded playbooks, fake kicks/punts, audibles, and auto-scheduling based on your won-loss record from the previous year.","Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl II - Special Edition (NA).png"
"snes_tecmo-super-bowl-iii-final-edition","Tecmo Super Bowl III : Final Edition","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-10-01","1995","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","A late entry in what was once the premiere football simulation, TSB III has updated rosters and teams for the 1994-1995 season and is licensed by both the NFL and the Players group.  Features real NFLP players and photos, the real NFL schedule, and weekly standings.  You can change defensive and offensive formations, create your own Pro Bowl, fake punts and field goals, go for the two point conversion, and call audibles.  Updates to the game itself include new cinema screens, superstar mode, free agency system, improved graphics, larger field simulation, passing modes, and improved speech and music.  Horizontal scrolling.  Also features battery back-up.","Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Super Bowl III - Final Edition (NA).png"
"snes_tecmo-super-nba-basketball","Tecmo Super NBA Basketball","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-03-02","1993","1990s","Tecmo","Tecmo","Sports / Basketball","Sports","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","Tecmo Super NBA features real teams (all 27 contemporary teams) and a roster of real players (over 320).  One or two players can compete in regular, reduced, or short seasons, or play an exhibition game.   Though primarily horizontal scrolling, digitized speech and cinemas, along with a free throw point of view, add drama to the proceedings.  Besides the expected elements of basketball (substitutions, penalties, steals and blocks, time-outs, overtime), Super NBA gives you the chance to call offensive plays and to program win/loss records.  Has a battery to back-up season play.","Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tecmo Super NBA Basketball (NA).png"
"snes_teenage-mutant-hero-turtles-tournament-fighters","Teenage Mutant Hero Turtles : Tournament Fighters","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-01","1993","1990s","Konami","Konami","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","80","4","The game features the original 4 turtles from the previous games in the series, as well as other fighters.

The game is very much in the tradition of the Mortal Kombat or Street Fighter series, pitting you against opponents one at a time. Some fighters (besides the turtles) will be familiar, such as the Rat King, or even Shredder (now called ""Cyber-Shredder"" here).

Though even people familiar with the turtles will see differences in them. They can now, for example, do moves involving projectiles, such as ""fireballs"".

The game's modes include a story mode, where you can only pick one of the turtles and go on fighting opponents in order to rescue April and Splinter, and a tournament mode, where you fight only for the fame and money.","Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","miximages/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png","marquees/snes/Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles - Tournament Fighters (NA).png"
