"snes_tenchi-muyou-game-hen","Tenchi Muyou ! Game-hen","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-10-27","1995","1990s","TamTam","Banpresto","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Sasami is kidnapped by a mysterious little girl with magical powers, and Tenchi and his companions must travel to rescue her, battling monsters and other creatures on the way.

Tenchi Muyou! Game-Hen is a strategy game with RPG elements, based on the popular Japanese Tenchi Muyo! cartoon series. The game moves from battle to battle, with the plot being revealed through cutscenes between them. The player fights the computer on turns, controlling the individuals from a party of four. The party members are selected on a separate screen before each battle, and as the game progresses new characters become available.

During the skirmish, selecting the characters brings up a menu with three command options: move, attack or end turn. A fourth transform option becomes available later, after they reach a higher level. When moving or attacking, glowing tiles on the ground show the maximum range of the action. Performing either one costs action points, shown as eight regenerating green dots on the status window, alongside basic statistics like health, defense and attack levels. Characters level up automatically while on the battlefield, increasing their abilities and receiving more powerful attacks. Health powers are also accessed through the attack menu, recovering lost points to an ailing comrade within their range. Characters can transform to a more powerful version when they have the ability to do so, and all the eight green dots are still available. The transformed unit has more powerful attacks and a wider range of movement.

After the battle, a map screen appears where the player can save the game, and choose the next battle from one of the available paths. It is possible to revisit battlegrounds, to level up before tackling stronger enemies.","Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Tenchi Muyo! - Game Hen (English Translated by BorderLine and LNF, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_tengai-makyou-zero","Tengai Makyou Zero","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-12-22","1995","1990s","Red Company Corporation","Hudson Soft","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","In the feudal Japan-like world of Jipang, an evil prince releases the demon lord Ninigi, who in turn seals the gods of Jipang and suppresses the people of six kingdoms with his demon henchmen. After one of the henchmen attack his village and slay his grandfather, the main character, Higan, learns he is the legendary ""Fire Hero"" and must set off to save the kingdoms. Along the way, Higan meets several characters, such as Subaru, a fairy and Tenjin, a swordsman.","Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).sfc","SFC","7","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","miximages/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","screenshots/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","titlescreens/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","3dboxes/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","backcovers/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png","marquees/snes/Tengai Makyou Zero (English Translated by Tom, Rev 7).png"
"snes_tenshi-no-uta-shiroki-tsubasa-no-inori","Tenshi No Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa No Inori","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-07-29","1994","1990s","Telenet","Telenet","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","60","3","Reyard is a young man who lives in the town of Farell; his father is a skilled blacksmith, and the youngster hopes to follow the same career, enjoying a peaceful life. But everything changes when a wandering group of performers arrives in the town. Reyard meets Kurana, one of the artists, who was adopted by the leader of the troop, and is hoping to find her true parents. The two meet several times, and Reyard realizes that he has fallen in love. However, when Kurana tells him she will leave Farell soon, he is unable to express his feelings. Only when he hears that the duke of Bern is determined to marry Kurana, even against her will, Reyard understands that he has to do something...","Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","miximages/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","screenshots/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","titlescreens/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","3dboxes/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","backcovers/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png","marquees/snes/Tenshi no Uta - Shiroki Tsubasa no Inori (English Translated by Translation Corporation).png"
"snes_terminator-2-judgment-day","Terminator 2 : Judgment Day","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Bits Studios","LJN","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","The game consists of several actions parts linked together. All parts are different, each resembling typical games of the genre (for example: 1st level is like a side-view beat 'em up). Between each level a small cutscene from the movie is shown.","Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","miximages/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png","marquees/snes/Terminator 2 - Judgment Day (NA).png"
"snes_terranigma","Terranigma","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-12-19","1996","1990s","Quintet","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","Terranigma tells the story of Ark, a boy growing up in a remote village cut off from the outside world by lava. When he opens a forbidden door and releases a strange creature from a box, he disrupts the balance between two worlds and turns all villagers into stone. To save them, Ark must seek out five towers, uncover the secrets of both worlds, and confront dark forces. The game combines fast-paced combat with weapons and techniques such as dash and leap attacks, with RPG elements where Ark grows stronger after each quest. With its high level of detail, mix of action and RPG, and a branching story shaped by the player's choices, Terranigma stands out as a truly unique adventure.","Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","miximages/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","screenshots/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","titlescreens/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","3dboxes/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","backcovers/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png","marquees/snes/Terranigma (NTSC Conversion With 8x16 Font Patch).png"
"snes_tetris-amp-dr-mario","Tetris &amp; Dr. Mario","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-07-27","1995","1990s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","80","4","Two of the most popular puzzle games return, but now together in an exclusive compilation for SNES. The games have a slight graphical update when compared with the original Game Boy and NES games, but the gameplay remains totally faithful to the games released for both platforms.

In Tetris, the main objective is to pile blocks that will fall down continuously, in order to create a row or ""line"" without spaces. For this collection, the game comes with two bonus options: 2 PLAYER GAME (absent in the NES version) and VS. COM (absent in both versions), with 3 CPU opponents available, each one representing a difficulty level (EASY, MEDIUM, and HARD, respectively).

In Dr. Mario, the objective is to eliminate all the viruses contained in a big bottle. Dr. Mario (situated in the upper-right side of the screen) will throw capsules with 6 different color combinations (Red-Red, Red-Blue, Yellow-Yellow, Red-Yellow, Blue-Blue and Blue-Yellow) in order to line up at least four viruses or capsules of the same color horizontally or vertically and to make them disappear. In this compilation, the game comes with a bonus option: VS. COM, where you'll face the CPU players: Blue Virus (EASY), Yellow Virus (MEDIUM), and Red Virus (HARD).

For competitive players in both games, there is Mixed Match, where you and a friend can play Tetris and Dr. Mario like a tournament! Adjust the handicap levels, play time, music, and other settings to balance your different skills. The game order is: TETRIS B-TYPE (clear a certain amount of lines), DR. MARIO (disinfect a predetermined number of viruses) and TETRIS A-TYPE (clear lines until the time expires). At the end of the time limit, the player with the highest score is the winner.","Tetris &amp; Dr. Mario (NA).sfc","SFC","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
"snes_tetris-2","Tetris 2","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1995-01-01","1995","1990s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","80","4","Unlike the original Tetris, Tetris 2 has you clearing the field of blocks in a different way. Each play field starts with different colored dots (in this case black, gray and white), with one of each color flashing. The blocks are made up of the same three colors, and by matching blocks of the same color over the top or to the side of the dot will clear the dot and those blocks from the screen. If you clear a flashing dot, all the corresponding dots of the same color will be cleared. To complete the round just clear the dots, not the blocks themselves.","Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/snes/Tetris 2 (NA, Rev 1).png"
"snes_tetris-attack","Tetris Attack","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-11-28","1996","1990s","Intelligent Systems","Nintendo","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","80","4","Tetris Attack throws Yoshi's Island into turmoil – King Bowser has cast a dark spell, turning nearly all its inhabitants into mindless servants. Only Yoshi has escaped, and he must set out to rescue his friends and defeat Bowser. The game blends fast-paced puzzle action with colorful Yoshi's Island charm, as you swap blocks to create rows, trigger combos, and unleash massive garbage blocks on your opponents. Alongside the story mode, you'll find two-player battles, endless play, time trials, and tricky puzzles. Beneath its Western name lies the Japanese original Panel de Pon – now starring Yoshi and his vibrant island crew.","Tetris Attack (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","miximages/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png","marquees/snes/Tetris Attack (NA).png"
"snes_tetris-battle-gaiden","Tetris Battle Gaiden","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-12-24","1993","1990s","Bullet Proof Software","Bullet Proof Software","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","100","5","Tetris Battle Gaiden is a competitive puzzle-battle game, similar to games such as Puzzle Fighter or Puyo Puyo. One can play against a friend or the Computer in a story mode. There is also an included Rensa mode, which ensures a more hyperactive game due to increased gravity. The player can choose from a list of characters in the story mode, including a Dragon or a pumpkin named Halloween.","Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","miximages/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","screenshots/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","titlescreens/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","3dboxes/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","backcovers/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png","marquees/snes/Tetris Battle Gaiden (English Translated by DDSTranslation With Boss Selection Patch by Docrow, Rev 1.1).png"
"snes_tetsuwan-atom","Tetsuwan Atom","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-02-18","1994","1990s","Minato Giken","Zamuse","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Tetsuwan Atom is an action platforming game developed by Zamuse and published by Banpresto for the Super Famicom (SNES) platform. Tetsuwan Atom was only released in Japan. Tetsuwan Atom is the second video game to feature Astro Boy, the popular manga/anime character.The player takes control of Astro Boy. Astro Boy has a variety of attacks and moves to navigate through the levels. There are eight total levels in Astro Boy, most of which have an end boss that must be defeated to move on to the next level.","Tetsuwan Atom (JP).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","miximages/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","screenshots/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","titlescreens/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","3dboxes/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","backcovers/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png","marquees/snes/Tetsuwan Atom (JP).png"
"snes_the-7th-saga","The 7th Saga","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-09-01","1993","1990s","Produce","Enix","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Your character embarks on a quest to find the seven crystals that are hidden throughout the land of Ticondera. There are seven different characters to choose from, each with different beginning stats and specialties.

