"snes_the-addams-family-pugsley-s-scavenger-hunt","The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1992-01-01","1992","1990s","Ocean","Ocean","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","The Addams Family: Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt is a side-scrolling platformer based on the second animated TV series The Addams Family (1992). The player takes the role of Pugsley who gets challenged to a scavenger hunt by his sister Wednesday.  He has to retrieve six items which are of course hidden in six levels which can be accessed in any order. The gameplay follows the usual platforming standards: Pugsley moves from left to right while jumping a lot, avoiding enemies and sometimes solving switch puzzles. Pugsley can take three hits before dying but if he collects enough dollar symbols he can replenish his health.","The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","miximages/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","screenshots/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","backcovers/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png","marquees/snes/The Addams Family - Pugsley's Scavenger Hunt (NA).png"
"snes_the-adventures-of-batman-amp-robin","The Adventures of Batman &amp; Robin","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-11-01","1994","1990s","Konami","Konami","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","Konami's game based on the 90s animated series starring the Caped Crusader sends him against his most famous enemies in a platforming/beat'em'up title. Each level sends Batman against one particular villain. Most levels present Batman with a large number of henchmen to take out and environmental dangers to avoid on his way to one or more boss battles. Besides kicks, throws and punches, Batman can use a variety of equipment against the enemies. Always available are Batarangs and the grappling hook. Before each mission, Batman can also select additional equipment, like knockout gas spray, throwing stars, smoke bombs and plastic explosives, all with limited ammunition. Special equipment required for certain levels include a flashlight, gas mask and X-ray goggles. If some necessary equipment is missing, it is always possible to return to the Batcave to change the gear and then restart the current level. Many of the situations and environments of the levels are based on episodes from the series and the game's graphics emulate the animation and drawing style of the show.","The Adventures of Batman &amp; Robin (NA).sfc","SFC","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
"snes_the-adventures-of-dr-franken","The Adventures of Dr. Franken","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-01-01","1994","1990s","Motivetime","Elite Systems","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Franky and his girlfriend Bitsy are planning a vacation to New York. There's just one problem: Bitsy doesn't have a passport. Our protagonist comes up with a brilliant idea: He takes Bitsy apart and mails her to New York in different packages, where he will put her back together. Unfortunately for the couple, Bitsy has been lost in the mail. It is up to Franky to find her parts and put her back together.

The Adventures of Dr. Franken is a standard platformer where the player navigates platforms and avoids enemies. Touching too many enemies result in death. To defeat himself Franky has the ability to kick foes. The goal of every level is to find a package which is hidden in it. To reach it Franky also has to solve switch puzzles, There are overall 20 levels including four bonus levels.","The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","miximages/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","screenshots/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","backcovers/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png","marquees/snes/The Adventures of Dr. Franken (NA).png"
"snes_soccer-kid","Soccer Kid","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-06-01","1994","1990s","Yanoman Games","Krisalis Software","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Aliens attempting to steal the World Cup have crashed as they tried to flee, and the Cup has been broken, its pieces scattered around the globe. As Soccer Kid, you must retrieve it. During your journey you will visit Britain, Italy, Russia, Japan, and finally the States.

Soccer Kid is a platform game with some unique elements.  As the name implies, you have to kill your enemies with your ball. Football-style tricks of keeping the ball in the air and under control are especially useful - headers and overhead kicks can be played with practice. You gain access to the pieces by collecting 11 Player Cards across each world.

There is a saving feature that gives you the ability to save between each country (but not between individual levels).","The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).sfc","SFC","1.25","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","miximages/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","screenshots/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","backcovers/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png","marquees/snes/The Adventures of Kid Kleets (NA).png"
"snes_the-adventures-of-mighty-max","The Adventures of Mighty Max","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-09","1994","1990s","WJS Design","Ocean","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","80","4","The Adventures of Mighty Max is based on the TV cartoon Mighty Max which in turn is based on a series of toys.
Max is a kid who possesses a magic cap that allows you to travel across different world and to save people who get in trouble in other dimensions. But his archenemy, the demonic Skull Master, has recently locked all the portals Max was using for inter-dimensional travel. However, the Skull Master has kept some of the portals for himself, keeping there some of his destructive weapons. It's time to destroy those weapons and to stop Skull Master!

This is a platform game in which you control Max himself or one of his two side-kicks (that doesn't influence the gameplay). You travel through several different worlds. Your goal is to find Skull Master's weapons, which are scattered around the level, and to destroy them. The levels are timed, and there are also plenty of enemies who will disturb you on your way to the goal.","The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/The Adventures of Mighty Max (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_the-adventures-of-rocky-and-bullwinkle-and-friends","The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-06-02","1993","1990s","Imagineer","THQ Software","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","30","1.5","The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle is the video game adaptation of the 60's cartoon series staring Bullwinkle, a moose, and Rocky, a flying squirrel.  The game plays out much like an episode of the show.  The story begins at the dedication of the Frostbite Falls Rocky and Bullwinkle museum.  Unfortunately, the not-so-nice Boris and Natasha have disguised themselves as security guards for the museum and managed to steal some of the priceless artifacts.

Bullwinkle and Rocky must track down the stolen artifacts and return order to Frostbite Falls.  Most of the action is of the side-scrolling platformer variety, but along the way, you will get to play lots of mini-games involving characters from the show. During the platforming sections you can switch instantly between the two protagonists. Both play differently: Bullwinkle can throw bombs at enemies and Rocky can fly for short instances.","The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","miximages/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","screenshots/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","backcovers/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png","marquees/snes/The Adventures of Rocky and Bullwinkle and Friends (NA).png"
"snes_tintin-prisoners-of-the-sun","Tintin : Prisoners of the Sun","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-01","1996","1990s","Infogrames","Infogrames","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","90","4.5","The Adventures of Tintin: Prisoners of the Sun is based on the Belgian comic book of the same name. The basic plotline is the same: Professor Cuthbert Calculus gets kidnapped and the player, in the role of Tintin, needs to rescue him. The rest is more loosely adapted: in contrast to the comic, which is mostly based in Peru, this game offers many different locations all over the world.

The gameplay itself is a typical platforming action: Tintin walks through the levels while avoiding the enemies. Pretty much everyone, e.g. little girls and security guards, is out to hurt Tintin who has no means of defending himself. This means the most important aspect is learning enemy placements, their patterns and how to avoid them. But he has to hurry because of the time limit. Required for success is the usage of the two playing plains: from the player's perspective in the foreground and further towards the background. Tintin can switch between the two at any time.","The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","miximages/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","screenshots/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","titlescreens/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","3dboxes/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","backcovers/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png","marquees/snes/The Adventures of Tintin - Prisoners of the Sun (NTSC Conversion).png"
"snes_the-blues-brothers","The Blues Brothers","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Titus","Titus","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","40","2","Jukebox Adventure is the sequel to The Blues Brothers. Once again, the player has to choose a favourite Blues Brother and take him through different side-scrolling platform levels. He needs to collect records and use them as defence by throwing them towards enemies. There are also power-ups that can be gathered until the jukebox to progress to the next level is found.","The Blues Brothers (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","miximages/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","screenshots/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","backcovers/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png","marquees/snes/The Blues Brothers (NA).png"
"snes_the-brainies","The Brainies","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-12-01","1994","1990s","Titus Software","Titus","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","70","3.5","This puzzle game has 101 levels, in which you have to guide a varying number of Brainies of four different colors onto a spot that matches their color. You control a cross-hair, and press fire while over a Brainy to take or give up control of its motion. Running out of time costs you a life.

