"snes_time-trax","Time Trax","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1994-08-01","1994","1990s","Malibu Games","Malibu Games","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","60","3","Time Trax is based off of the 1993-94 sci-fi action series starring Dale Midkiff; you take the role of Darien Lambert, captain of the Fugitive Retrieval Section of Washington D.C. It is the year 2193 and your once high arrest record has started to decline sharply as routine trackdowns end in mysterious disappearances. It is discovered that noted MIT scientist Dr. Mordecai 'Mo' Sahmbi has been sending criminals back in time to 1993 using his invention the TRAX time machine, and has gone back himself. TRAX is captured by the police, and three guesses as to who is tasked with capturing the criminals and sending them back to 2193.

As Lambert, your primary targets in this game are neo-Nazi racist Sepp Dietrich and Sahmbi himself. You do have some equipment to help you: your supercomputer S.E.L.M.A. (Specified Encapsulated Limitless Memory Archive), disguised as an AT&amp;amp;T Mastercard and whose holographic persona resembles a British nanny, and the PPT (Pellet Projection Tube), a weapon capable of stunning a human from periods of a couple of minutes to a few hours and can fire pellets that render humans transportable to the future, disguised a keyless car alarm remote. Also, you have the ability to ""time stall"" (this slows the speed of images reaching your brain, allowing you to react quickly) and your Mosh-Ti (an Occidental improvement of martial arts) skills to rely on if the situation gets dire.

You'll run through the alleys of the future, through the Smithsonian (circa 1993), ride a motorcycle and jet-ski, battle criminals atop a construction site, and do so much more until you've finally captured the two fugitives.","Time Trax (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","miximages/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Time Trax (NA).png","marquees/snes/Time Trax (NA).png"
"snes_timecop","Timecop","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-01-01","1996","1990s","JVC","Cryo Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","40","2","Timecop continues the story of the time enforcement officer and sends you on a dangerous pursuit across multiple eras. The inventor of time travel has succumbed to megalomania, declared himself ruler of the universe and challenges you to a duel throughout history. From past settings to futuristic environments, you fight through numerous stages using punches, kicks and a firearm with limited ammunition. Traditional platform combat is mixed with vehicle sequences, culminating in a dramatic jetpack showdown over Los Angeles. The game stands out for its digitized characters, giving it a distinctive visual style – an action-driven time travel adventure blending close combat with science fiction spectacle.","Timecop (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Timecop (NA).png","miximages/snes/Timecop (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Timecop (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Timecop (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Timecop (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Timecop (NA).png","marquees/snes/Timecop (NA).png"
"snes_time-slip","Time Slip","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-11-02","1993","1990s","Sales Curve","Tokai Engineering","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","On the reptilian planet of Tirmat, scientists have discovered a rift in space and plan to use it to transport the planet's inhabitants before the planet is extinguished by sending their elite army through the rift and invade their closest neighbor...Earth.  However, to ensure their success they send their army into Earth's past in hopes of avoiding any modern weapons and increase their chances of saving their planet.  However, Earth has learned of their evil plot and has developed a experimental time portal and has sent their own one man army to stop them.

The player takes control of Dr. Vincent Gilgamesh who has acquired a massive arsenal including pistols, machine guns, rocket launchers and many more heavy weapons and must travel through various time periods including Medieval times, prehistoric times, Ancient Rome and Egypt and even the distant future.  The gameplay is similar to Contra where the player advances through the stages, shooting at various enemies and collecting power-ups and must also avoid various traps and pitfalls scattered throughout the levels.  There are also the standard bosses at the end of each stage.","Timeslip (NA).sfc","SFC","1","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","miximages/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Timeslip (NA).png","marquees/snes/Timeslip (NA).png"
