It includes 5 different types of sports - biathlon, alpine skiing (downhill, slalom, giant slalom and Super-G), ski jumping (90 m, 120 m), bobsleigh (2/4 men bob, 1/2 men luge) and skating (elimination, pursuit, time trial).  The events use 3D views","Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).sfc","SFC","2","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","miximages/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","screenshots/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","backcovers/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png","marquees/snes/Winter Olympic Games - Lillehammer '94 (NA).png"
"snes_wizardry-gaiden-4-taima-no-kodou","Wizardry Gaiden 4 - Taima No Kodou","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1996-09-20","1996","1990s","Access Games","ASCII","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","90","4.5","Wizardry Gaiden IV: Taima no Koudou (""Throb of the Demon's Heart"") is a turn-based dungeon crawler RPG for the Super Famicom. It is the fourth in a series of ""gaiden"" Wizardry games developed by Japanese studio Access and influenced heavily by Sir-Tech's core Wizardry series. The game was fan translated in late 2016.

Throb of the Demon's Heart is distinctive for the Wizardry series for adapting a lot of Japanese imagery and monsters in the familiar Wizardry format. This gives it a more home-grown feel among the Japanese-exclusive spin-offs, and heavily draws from Japanese folklore and religion.

It is the first Wizardry Gaiden to be released on a system other than the Nintendo Game Boy, and is also the last in the series. Many more Japanese Wizardry spin-off games would follow, however.","Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).sfc","SFC","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","miximages/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","screenshots/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","titlescreens/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","3dboxes/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","backcovers/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png","marquees/snes/Wizardry Gaiden IV - Taima no Kodou (English Translated by AgentOrange, DDS, Helly, and MrRichard999, Rev 1.02).png"
