"snes_striker","Striker","snes","Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) / Super Famicom","SNES","Nintendo","4. kynslóð (16-bit)","1993-01-01","1993","1990s","Rage Software","Elite Systems","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1-2","1","2","90","4.5","The first game in the long-running soccer series, which stood out from the crowd with a unique forced perspective 3D view rather than a simple overhead one. The players are drawn large and there is a large scanner to assist with long passing. However, the standard mode has the ball sticking closely to the feet, which makes mazy runs upfield a more useful strategy. There are 64 international teams on offer, with a European-style knock-out cup competition included. Many different formations and strategies are offered.","World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).sfc","SFC","0.5","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","miximages/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","screenshots/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","titlescreens/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","3dboxes/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","backcovers/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png","marquees/snes/World Soccer '94 - Road to Glory (NA).png"
