"n64_mario-golf","Mario Golf","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-09-14","1999","1990s","Camelot Software","Nintendo","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","Forget buying expensive golf gear--Mario brings the game to you. Mario Golf features four complete 18-hole courses, 11 golfers, and precise play control. Create your own golfer and build up his or her experience and skill levels by competing in various tournaments and head-to-head matches. The more you play, the stronger and more accurate your golfer becomes. There are many different modes of play in Mario Golf, including a wide variety of minigames designed to challenge even the most level-headed swingers.","Mario Golf (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","miximages/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png","marquees/n64/Mario Golf (NA).png"
"n64_mario-party","Mario Party","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-03-09","1999","1990s","Hudson Soft","Nintendo","Board game","Board / Casual","1-4","1","4","80","4","Mario has battled Bowser, saved the Mushroom Kingdom, and raced through countless adventures, but now it's time to party! In Mario Party, Nintendo brings the most exciting bash to the N64, where Mario and friends compete in a board game-style showdown packed with mini-games.
Players roll dice to move across themed boards, each filled with surprises and over fifty mini-games. Competitions range from free-for-all challenges to two-on-two and three-against-one battles, testing skills in racing, puzzles, and quick reflexes. Winning games earns coins and stars, determining the ultimate party champion.
Game boards feature animated elements, hazards, and special challenges. Mario, Luigi, Peach, Yoshi, Wario, Donkey Kong, and Bowser all join the fun, each with their own board. While Mario Party offers solo play, the real fun comes with friends, ensuring an unforgettable multiplayer experience full of laughter, strategy, and late-night excitement.","Mario Party (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","miximages/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Mario Party (NA).png","marquees/n64/Mario Party (NA).png"
"n64_mario-party-2","Mario Party 2","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","2000-10-13","2000","2000s","Hudson Soft","Nintendo","Board game","Board / Casual","1-4","1","4","80","4","Mario and a range of well known Nintendo characters, including Yoshi, Bowser, Luigi, and Wario return for some more party action. 

The second edition includes 5 new boards, each with a specific theme, such as Space Land, Western Land, Horror Land, and Mystery Land. Each board includes unique attributes in relation to the theme, but the main goal is the same: complete the board game over a certain amount of moves and be the player to have the most coins and/or stars at the end. 

The single player story mode allows one person and 3 CPU controlled players to play each board. Once you play a specific mini-game (64 in all), they become available to purchase using the coins you collected in your games to play anytime. Multiplayer allows 2 to 4 people to play the game.","Mario Party 2 (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","miximages/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png","marquees/n64/Mario Party 2 (NA).png"
"n64_mario-party-3","Mario Party 3","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","2001-11-16","2001","2000s","Hudson Soft","Nintendo","Board game","Board / Casual","1-4","1","4","80","4","The series continues with a set of 70 new mini-games.  Play in the new single-player Story mode, or bring in some friends for Party mode.  Four player games and a new two player mode are also available for play.

In Battle Royale mode (four player), you race around different boards to earn the most stars and coins.  At the end of each round, you face it off in one of the mini-games, which can be chicken chases, snowball fights, or various other competitions.

Duel mode allows play between just two people.  You still race around the board, but mini-games are only played when you land on a specific square.  Another play change is the addition of another character for your team, allowing tag team-style action in the game.

Story mode is essentially the same as a Battle Royale, except your opponents are played by the computer.","Mario Party 3 (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","miximages/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png","marquees/n64/Mario Party 3 (NA).png"
