"n64_neon-genesis-evangelion","Neon Genesis Evangelion","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-06-25","1999","1990s","BEC","Bandai","Fighting","Fighting","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Neon Genesis Evangelion is a game adaptation of Yoshiyuki Sadamoto’s manga of the same name which also got an anime release. It is the only Evangelion game that was released on N64. It covers the major battles from the entire Evangelion saga and features original footage from the anime. 

In Story Mode you take control of bio-mechanical mechas called Evas to fight against monstrous beings called Angels. To see every mission through, combo attacks (punches and kicks), blocking and grappling techniques are available at your disposal. Depending on the damage the Eva you control takes and if certain parameters are met during that time you will be given a time limit in which you must end the battle with the Angel. 

The Simulation Mode: almost plays like a shooter. It’s a 1st-person perspective mode where you must eliminate as many Angels as possible within the time limit. When the time limit ends you get a rank depending on how many enemies you destroyed and how many bullets you used.","Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","miximages/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","screenshots/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","titlescreens/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","3dboxes/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","backcovers/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png","marquees/n64/Neon Genesis Evangelion (JP).png"
"n64_nfl-blitz","NFL Blitz","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1997-09-09","1997","1990s","Midway","Midway","Sports / Football (American)","Sports","1-2","1","2","80","4","NFL Blitz gives the National Football League the same over-the-top treatment that Midway had used so effectively with NBA Jam. Features include exaggerated muscle-bound player models, ""turbo"" buttons, fast action, and some pretty wild rules changes (like 30 yards for a first down!). Blitz is nothing if not a unique football gaming experience.

