"n64_super-robot-spirits","Super Robot Spirits","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1998-07-17","1998","1990s","Vertex","Banpresto","Fighting / Versus","Fighting","1-2","1","2","50","2.5","Super Robot Spirits is a 3D fighting game developed and published by Banpresto for the Nintendo 64. Released exclusively in Japan on July 17, 1998, it is a spin-off of the Super Robot Wars series.

The game pits players in one-on-one battles featuring iconic mecha from various anime series, including Mobile Fighter G Gundam, Invincible Steel Man Daitarn 3, Aura Battler Dunbine, Chōdenji Machine Voltes V, Combat Mecha Xabungle, Dancouga – Super Beast Machine God, and Banpresto's original R-1 unit. Unlockable characters include the Master Gundam, Devil Gundam, and Judecca.

Gameplay is presented in a 2.5D style: characters and environments are rendered in 3D, but combat occurs on a 2D plane. Each mecha can punch, kick, block, and use weapons such as energy swords and turret guns. Players build up “spirit skills” during combat, which power devastating super attacks unique to each robot.","Super Robot Spirits (JP).z64","Z64","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","miximages/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","screenshots/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","titlescreens/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","3dboxes/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","backcovers/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png","marquees/n64/Super Robot Spirits (JP).png"
"n64_super-smash-bros","Super Smash Bros.","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-11-19","1999","1990s","HAL Laboratory","Nintendo","Fighting / Versus","Fighting","1-4","1","4","80","4","Super Smash Brothers takes familiar Nintendo characters such as Mario, Kirby and Donkey Kong, and puts them into battle! There are 8 fully-interactive landscapes, with one for each character and noticeable links to their games. Controls are analogue-based, with different moves executed depending on the direction and how firmly the stick is pressed. Items like baseball bats, Bob-ombs, and healing items drop into the arenas at random, aiding any nearby characters than can make use of them. The game uses a fixed viewpoint which scrolls, although characters are rendered in 3D.

The one-player mode has 14 stages to work through. Up to 4 human players can do battle at once, with team play as well as all-against-all action. Hidden characters are thrown in for good measure, as are bonus rounds, and a battle to the end with a giant hand (yeah, you read right!).

Playable characters include: Captain Falcon* (F-Zero), Donkey Kong, Fox (Star Fox), Kirby, Jigglypuff* (Pokémon), Link (Legend of Zelda), Luigi* (Mario), Mario, Ness* (Mother/EarthBound), Pikachu (Pokémon), Samus (Metroid) and Yoshi (Mario)

*character must be unlocked first","Super Smash Bros. (NA).z64","Z64","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","miximages/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png","marquees/n64/Super Smash Bros. (NA).png"
