"n64_turok-dinosaur-hunter","Turok : Dinosaur Hunter","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1997-03-04","1997","1990s","Iguana Entertainment","Acclaim Entertainment","Shooter / FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","90","4.5","Turok: Dinosaur Hunter is a first-person shooter with platforming and light puzzle-solving elements. Much of the game is set in outdoor environments, and requires the player to explore them by finding various paths, jumping, swimming, and climbing. The game's most notable enemies are dinosaurs of various sizes, though the levels also include human and demonic enemies, as well as wildlife. The player gradually gains access to thirteen weapons (plus the Chronoscepter, assembling which is the game's main objective); these include a knife, a bow, as well as high-tech firearms such as a rocket launcher and an atomic fusion cannon.","Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).z64","Z64","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","miximages/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","screenshots/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","titlescreens/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","3dboxes/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","backcovers/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png","marquees/n64/Turok - Dinosaur Hunter (NA, Rev 2).png"
