"n64_worms-armageddon","Worms Armageddon","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","2000-03-30","2000","2000s","Infogrames","Infogrames","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-4","1","4","80","4","Worms Armageddon expands on Worms 2 by improving quite a few facets of gameplay and including play over the Internet through Team 17's WORMNET. 

For those who've never played Worms, it's at heart similar to the old game Artillery, which you control an artillery piece. In essence, you give it a shot angle and shot power, and try to hit your enemy, despite wind effects and the enemy firing back at you. Worms puts you in command of a team of Worms, but not only can you move around the landscape, you can use many types of weapons to try to dispatch the enemy, from bazookas to mini-guns to exploding sheep. 

Everything is presented in a humorous cartoonish style, from the landscapes to the worms themselves and their cries of triumph or despair, depending on how you do.","Worms Armageddon (NA).z64","Z64","12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","miximages/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png","marquees/n64/Worms Armageddon (NA).png"
"n64_wwf-attitude","WWF Attitude","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-08-09","1999","1990s","Acclaim Entertainment","Acclaim Entertainment","Sports / Fighting","Sports","1-4","1","4","80","4","WWF Attitude was the third wrestling game by Acclaim for the Sony Playstation. It was also the second WWF 3D wrestling game for the system. This game was the followup to the commercial success WWF War Zone. At the time it was the wrestling game to have featured the most modes. The 20 or so game modes included specialty matches like royal rumble, survivor series, tornado matches and more. Also featured was a new career mode compared to that of WWF War Zone, realistic entrances and a first ever Create a PPV mode. The game featured over 40 of the then current WWF Superstars, including hidden ones. The Create A Wrestler feature was one of the most advanced of it's time.","WWF Attitude (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","miximages/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","screenshots/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","backcovers/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png","marquees/n64/WWF Attitude (NA).png"
"n64_wwf-no-mercy","WWF No Mercy","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","2000-12-15","2000","2000s","AKI Corporation","THQ","Sports / Fighting","Sports","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","The last wrestling title made by the team of THQ and AKI allows players to compete for 7 different WWF Titles with each belt getting its own unique story. Stories can be replayed, allowing players to defend their title in a storyline. Upon successful completion of a story mode, players will unlock the title they were competing for in Exhibition mode where titles can be won and defended as the players see fit.

A maximum of 4 players can compete in a range of modes, including caged and ladder contests and pay per view events. You can also create your own event and compete for WWF titles unlocked in Championship mode. Certain matches will take you outside the ring to 4 different backstage locations.","WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","miximages/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","screenshots/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","titlescreens/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","3dboxes/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","backcovers/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png","marquees/n64/WWF No Mercy (NA, Rev 1).png"
"n64_wwf-war-zone","WWF War Zone","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1998-08-21","1998","1990s","Iguana Entertainment","Acclaim Entertainment","Sports / Fighting","Sports","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","One of the first wrestling games for the Nintendo 64, and one of the many for the Playstation. The Playstation version has better, CD quality music, but has less features. One of the main attractions was that WWF's Steve Austin did a lot of voice acting for it, although the other wrestlers don't have nearly as much speech.

Features include custom player made wrestlers, as well as the real  wrestlers, many different game types (single player, multiplayer, royal rumbles, cage matches, etc.), but the career mode is where the action is, and you can build up your wrestlers strengths, and earn him belts.","WWF War Zone (NA).z64","Z64","12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","miximages/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","screenshots/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","backcovers/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png","marquees/n64/WWF War Zone (NA).png"
"n64_wwf-wrestlemania-2000","WWF WrestleMania 2000","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-10-12","1999","1990s","AKI Corporation","THQ","Sports / Fighting","Sports","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","Wrestlemania 2K features more than 50 real WWF stars as well as the option for 16 custom wrestlers. All the wrestlers come with their real-life theme music, entrance videos (made into slide shows) and entrance performances. A great improvement over the previous game is the ""road to Wrestlemania"" mode, an enhanced tournament where players can challenge for any number of belts and be challenged by other wrestlers in a 12 month journey that finally leads to Wrestlemania 2000 itself.","WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).z64","Z64","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","miximages/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","screenshots/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","backcovers/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png","marquees/n64/WWF WrestleMania 2000 (NA).png"
"n64_x-treme-roller","X'treme Roller","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","","","","Titus Software","Unknown","Sports / Extreme","Sports","1","1","1","","","This roller skating game, blending racing, acrobatics, and combat, immersed players in a near-future setting with manga-inspired characters. The goal was to cross the finish line first, performing spectacular tricks and battling rivals to impress the crowd. Successful performances earned credits to acquire new equipment. Each character had their own story and skating style, and mastering all the maneuvers was essential to defeating the final boss. The game featured around ten levels, each with different objectives: winning the race, chaining together tricks, or beating the clock.","X'treme Roller (Prototype).z64","Z64","24","true","true","true","false","true","true","true","false","covers/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).png","miximages/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).png","screenshots/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).jpg","","3dboxes/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).png","backcovers/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).png","marquees/n64/X'treme Roller (Prototype).png"
"n64_xena-warrior-princess","Xena : Warrior Princess","n64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo 64","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (64-bit)","1999-12-17","1999","1990s","Saffire","Titus","Fighting","Fighting","1-4","1","4","60","3","Xena shall choose the defenders of the world. We have seen them in the memories of her exploits. So come together, Earth's greatest heroes and villains. Choose your weapons wisely and let the battles begin! Just remember, each victory only brings you closer to challenging the embodiment of darkness... Despair himself! Each of Xena's 10 characters possess their own unique weapons, attitudes and fighting techniques. Exclusive multi-player feature includes a roster mode, plus team and single battles.","Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).z64","Z64","12","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","miximages/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","screenshots/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","titlescreens/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","3dboxes/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","backcovers/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png","marquees/n64/Xena - Warrior Princess - The Talisman of Fate (NA).png"
