"gbc_beyblade-fighting-tournament","Beyblade - Fighting Tournament","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-08-11","2000","2000s","Rokumendo","Hudson Soft","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","","","Beyblade Fighting Tournament was the second video game released. This game features some concepts and ideas that were later abandoned within the Beyblade franchise, though many ideas were continued on within the manga and anime.

The standard game play involves visiting locations and the player fights their way through tornements to advance to the next stage of the game. As each tornement was won, more parts and bit-beasts are made able to be bought from the games shop.
The player could only start with one of 4 arch-types, ""Dragoon"", ""Draciel"", ""Dranzer"" and ""Driger"". Intially by default the player could only choose Dragoons, although codes were released in magazines to acess the other arch-types.

Within each match, however, aside from the launch the player had virtually no control on the beyblade once it was in the arena, resulting in many matchses being won more based on luck and the beyblades strength then player skill.","Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).zip","ZIP","1.03","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","miximages/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","screenshots/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","titlescreens/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","3dboxes/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","backcovers/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png","marquees/gbc/Beyblade - Fighting Tournament (Japan).png"
"gbc_bibi-blocksberg-im-bann-der-hexenkugel","Bibi Blocksberg: Im Bann der Hexenkugel","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","","","","BVM Produktion","Kiddinx","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","70","3.5","Bibi Blocksberg is the star of a German children's radio play and TV series. She is an apprentice witch, living in the common world of today, who has to live through different adventures.

The story: During a witch meeting, a lightning bolt struck and broke a crystal ball in seven parts, causing the witches to go mad. Bibi Blocksberg now has find all the parts to put them together and to restore the witches' mental health.

The game is an action-adventure. The seven levels, each corresponding to one witch and one part of the crystal ball, are full of monsters which hurt Bibi when she touches them. The health can be restored by finding sweets hidden in the level. Apart of monsters, there are persons which help her. In each level there is a magical item, often reachable only after getting through a little ""game in game"", that expands Bibi's magical powers, for example the broom that allows her to fly. The magic has to be used sparsely, because it costs magical energy, which can be recharged by finding little pulsating dots. This magical item is needed to get to the witch of the level, which Bibi has to fight. If she wins, the witch gets back to normal, gives her a part of the crystal ball and Bibi can go the the next level.

There also is a password system that allows the player to jump to different situations in the game, so that one does not have to play it through in one session.","Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).zip","ZIP","0.31","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png","miximages/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png","screenshots/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png","titlescreens/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png","3dboxes/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png","","marquees/gbc/Bibi Blocksberg - Im Bann der Hexenkugel (Germany).png"
