"gbc_donald-duck-quack-attack","Donald Duck : Quack Attack","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-10-19","2000","2000s","Ubisoft","Disney Interactive","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","You play as Donald in this 3D platform action game. Donald's girlfriend, Daisy is a reporter for a television station in Duckberg. While doing a story on the secret temple of the terrible magician Merlock, Daisy is kidnapped. Now, it is up to Donald to get her back. Along the way he will have help from his nephews, Huey, Dewey, and Louie, and the inventor Gyro Gearloose. He will also have competition from Gladstone Gander, who is also trying to save Daisy. 

Game play alternates between side-scrolling running and jumping and 3D running and jumping. The side-scrolling levels play a lot like the Super Mario Bros. games. The 3D levels are more akin to the Crash Bandicoot series of games. All in all, there are 20 levels spread out through various areas.","Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).zip","ZIP","1.07","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","miximages/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","screenshots/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","titlescreens/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","3dboxes/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","backcovers/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","marquees/gbc/Donald Duck - Goin' Quackers (USA) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png"
"gbc_donkey-kong-country","Donkey Kong Country","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-11-04","2000","2000s","Rareware","Nintendo","Platform","Platformer","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","King K. Rool has stolen Donkey Kong's banana stash, and Donkey Kong needs your help to get them back. In search of K. Rool, the Kremling horde impedes your progress. Kremlings, crocodile-like creatures, include Kritters (they succumb to a simple jump on the head), Krushas (they are virtually indestructible), and others. There are also other enemies that block your path, such as beavers, snakes, vultures. Leading them are dastardly bosses, including Very Gnawty, Necky, Bumble B, and Dumb Drum, and they all bar the way with their own special blend of villainy.

Donkey Kong is joined by Diddy Kong: these two primates differ significantly. For example, Donkey Kong is generally stronger; he can destroy most enemies with a single jump and can lift barrels straight over his head to throw them farther. On the other hand, Diddy is faster and not as strong as Donkey; he can run really fast and do cartwheels. Diddy carries barrels in front of him, creating a shield against frontal attacks.

The game is split into different worlds, which are split into different levels. Each level contains bonus areas, where one can collect bananas, medallions, and lives. At the end of each world is a boss, which is usually a larger version of a minor enemy.","Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).zip","ZIP","1.18","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","miximages/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","screenshots/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","titlescreens/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","3dboxes/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","backcovers/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","marquees/gbc/Donkey Kong Country (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png"
