"gbc_gimmick-land","Gimmick Land","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-01-01","2001","2000s","AlphaDream","Unknown","Action RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","Gimmick Land : Tomato Atama no Himitsu is an unreleased RPG developed by AlphaDream that serves as the prototype to Tomato Adventure on the GBA. While the game was complete and fully playable, Nintendo asked AlphaDream to port the game to the GBA. The ROM was leaked online in September 2020 as a part of the ""Nintendo Gigaleak."" An unofficial English fan translation was released on August 3, 2022. 

The game takes place in the colorful world of Gimmick Land, where the inhabitants live surrounded by special objects called “gimmicks” – mysterious gadgets capable of producing magical effects and solving problems. The hero, a brave young boy, is swept up in an adventure when malevolent forces begin to disrupt the balance of the world. To save Gimmick Land, he must travel to various regions, meet strange characters, and collect different gimmicks. The hero will have to use his wits and strategy to stop this threat and restore peace to Gimmick Land.","Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).zip","ZIP","1.19","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png","miximages/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png","screenshots/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png","titlescreens/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png","3dboxes/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png","","marquees/gbc/Gimmick Land (Japan) (Proto).png"
"gbc_gobs-of-games","Gobs of Games","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-09-01","2000","2000s","2n Productions","The 3DO Company","Compilation","Compilation","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","GOBS OF GAMES brings many childhood games to the Game Boy Color. The 16 different games are broken into four categories: Paper games, Peg games, Puzzle games, and Board games. The Paper games include Hangman, Dot Boxes, Triangle Boxes, Share, Color Snakes, and Tic-Tac-Toe. Peg Game is a series of boards in which the goal is to remove all of the pegs by jumping over them. Scramble and Move It are Puzzle games, and the only Board game is Checkers. All of the games can be played solo, but some can also played against another person via a link cable. Try to relive your younger days with GOBS OF GAMES.","Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).zip","ZIP","0.33","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","miximages/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","screenshots/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","titlescreens/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","3dboxes/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","backcovers/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","marquees/gbc/Gobs of Games (USA) (En,Fr,De).png"
"gbc_godzilla-the-series","Godzilla : The Series","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-01-01","2000","2000s","Crawfish Interactive","Crave Entertainment","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","70","3.5","Godzilla: The Series is based off the TV show on Fox, which was in turn based off the 1998 film starring Matthew Broderick. In this game, the player takes control of the big guy himself as giant monsters from space have invaded Earth and are determined to destroy it. Unfortunately for both the aliens and Godzilla the military is out to destroy both, so Godzilla now has to fight off the military to throw back the alien menace.

