"gbc_heroes-of-might-and-magic-ii","Heroes of Might and Magic II","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-03-16","2001","2000s","KnowWonder Digital Mediaworks","The 3DO Company","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","70","3.5","Heroes of Might and Magic II is a fantasy strategy game that pits you against diabolical warlords in a struggle for territory and resources. Dangerous enemies and mystical creatures roam the land and await any hero who sets out to defeat them. At stake is the ultimate prize: control of the land and the royal throne. Support the villainous usurper and lead the armies of evil, or be loyal to the righteous prince and deliver the people from tyranny.","Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).zip","ZIP","0.48","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","miximages/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","screenshots/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","titlescreens/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","3dboxes/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","backcovers/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png","marquees/gbc/Heroes of Might and Magic II (USA) (En,Fr,De).png"
"gbc_hexcite-the-shapes-of-victory","Hexcite : The Shapes of Victory","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","1999-01-01","1999","1990s","Gu","Ubisoft","Puzzle","Puzzle","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Hexcite is a puzzle game played on a honeycomb-like playing field. In the center is a hexagon; six more hexagons make up the entire playing field. Because of the turn-based gameplay, two people can play using only one system. Two-player link mode is also supported.

Players begin by placing a geometric shape (triangle, hexagon, parallelogram, etc.) in the center hexagon.  The CPU or human opponent then places another shape adjacent (and touching completely on one side) to a previously played piece.  Players score bonus points for completing any full hexagon. Much of the strategy in this game is in tricking your opponent into letting you take a bonus. Bonuses are also scored for placing a piece so that two sides will contribute a score. The game is over when all pieces have been played, or if the remaining pieces cannot be played.  In that case points are subtracted for any remaining pieces, based on the complexity of the shape (twice as many points are subtracted for a hexagon compared to a triangle.)

In Japan, this game has seen several Windows versions, and even has been released as a board game.","Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).zip","ZIP","0.07","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png","miximages/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png","screenshots/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png","titlescreens/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png","3dboxes/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png","","marquees/gbc/Hexcite - The Shapes of Victory (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).png"
