"gbc_jeff-gordon-xs-racing","Jeff Gordon XS Racing","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","1999-11-11","1999","1990s","Natsume","ASC Games","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","","","You can experience the future of racing today with JEFF GORDON XS RACING. Choose from five different cars and race on seven different tracks. You can use the Time Trial mode to get the fastest lap time possible on an empty track. In the Championship mode, you will have to race through two seasons. The first season has you racing against five other cars, and you must finish in first place overall to gain access to the second season. In the second season you will face seven other competitors, including Jeff Gordon. Win the second season, and you can challenge Gordon to a one-on-one race on any track you choose. Should your friends want in on the action, they can join you via a link cable. Get behind the wheel of a futuristic racecar and take first place in JEFF GORDON XS RACING.","Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).zip","ZIP","0.09","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","miximages/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","screenshots/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","titlescreens/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","3dboxes/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","backcovers/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png","marquees/gbc/Jeff Gordon XS Racing (USA) (GB Compatible).png"
"gbc_jeremy-mcgrath-supercross-2000","Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-11-24","2000","2000s","M4","Acclaim Entertainment","Racing, Driving / Motorcycle","Racing","1","1","1","80","4","This to-go version of Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 is a top-down racing game, featuring two game modes (championship and arcade), 6 bikers and a variety of tracks in different scenarios.

Season mode features 3 championships, each with three stages composed of four races. The goal is to win all 9 gold medals by obtaining more points than the competition. Arcade mode is the same, except all championships and stages, as well as Jeremy McGrath, are unlocked from the start.
The difference between championships is the engine size - with larger (thus faster) bikes, the player has less time to react, and going head to head into the edge of the track can be a matter of a simple bump in 80cc to a spectacular flip into the stands in 250cc, also because it becomes a lot harder to do sharp turns in a limited space.

While it can be played as a straightforward racing game, by performing tricks the player can obtain some powerups - a bomb will knock down the next opponent, the arrow temporarily boosts bike stats and the shield allows the player to barge into one opponent, knocking him off his bike. There is one big catch - the skull and bones knock the player out of his bike, which can prove to be decisive in a close race.","Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).zip","ZIP","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","miximages/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png","marquees/gbc/Jeremy McGrath Supercross 2000 (USA, Europe).png"
