"gbc_matchbox-emergency-patrol","Matchbox Emergency Patrol","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-01-01","2001","2000s","Lucky Chicken Games","Mattel Electronics","Racing, Driving","Racing","1","1","1","90","4.5","A children's driving adventure game. Players will drive fire engines and police cars to protect the citizens of Matchbox city. The game is based in a city that has 5 distinctive parts connected by a freeway system.  As the player successfully completes missions they are promoted to new ranks as firemen and police and given larger areas of the city to be responsible for.  There are multiple mission types for each vehicle.  There are two separate control schemes designed to make the title playable for young children while still remaining challenging for older gamers.","Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).zip","ZIP","0.87","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","miximages/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png","marquees/gbc/Matchbox Emergency Patrol (USA, Europe).png"
"gbc_die-maus","Die Maus","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","1999-01-01","1999","1990s","Bit Managers","Infogrames","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","","","Die Maus is an action / puzzle game based on the German children's television show Die Sendung mit der Maus (The show with the mouse). You control both main characters of the show, the mouse and the elephant, in a search for the duck who has disappeared. The levels of the game are isometric puzzles. Both characters must reach the exit using and combining their different abilities. The mouse, for instance, is larger than the elephant, but the elephant is able to push heavy objects around. The game contains more than 150 puzzles in 5 different game worlds.","Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).zip","ZIP","0.15","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png","miximages/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png","screenshots/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png","titlescreens/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png","3dboxes/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png","","marquees/gbc/Maus, Die (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es).png"
