"gbc_road-champs-bxs-stunt-biking","Road Champs : BXS Stunt Biking","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-12-05","2000","2000s","HotGen","Activision","Sports / Cycling","Sports","1","1","1","60","3","Stunt biking makes an appearance on the Game Boy Color with ROAD CHAMPS BXS STUNT BIKING. When you start the game, you will have to progress through a 26-stage Training mode that teaches you how to perform all 50 moves in the game. After getting through training, you will be able take on a Single-Run, Career, or Tournament. The Single-Run mode allows you to work one course and master stringing tricks together, while Career mode has you compete in competitions to move from the amateur ranks to the world of the professionals. You can also compete in the Tournament mode to become the world champion. There are total of 64 unique levels spread throughout the game do you have what it takes to master ROAD CHAMPS BXS STUNT BIKING?","Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).zip","ZIP","0.22","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","miximages/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png","marquees/gbc/Road Champs - BXS Stunt Biking (USA, Europe).png"
"gbc_road-rash","Road Rash","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-12-15","2000","2000s","3d6 Games","Electronic Arts","Motorcycle race TPV","Racing","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Road Rash is an aggressive motorcycle racing game where the player assumes the role of a biker who takes part in a series of illegal races across the U.S.A. Starting at the back of the pack the objective is always to finish first on a linear course, overtaking the other bikers. This is achieved by driving very well or by playing it dirty, knocking opponents of their bikes using clubs, crowbars or your bare hands. The other racers fight back in a similar fashion and there are also hazards. All the races take place on the regular road with normal traffic (in both directions) and the cops, as well as occasional oil slicks and stray cows.

By winning races you can get promoted to a stronger division and earn cash with which you can buy a better bike. Whenever you're knocked off your bike or hit something you will have to run back to your bike and lose valuable time, plus your bike will suffer some damage. When the player crashes with cops nearby, it is possible to get busted and then you have to forfeit the race.

Like the whole Road Rash lineage, the game has arcade-like gameplay with no intention to be a motorcycle simulation. While the game has a two-player mode, this is not simultaneous.","Road Rash (USA, Europe).zip","ZIP","0.23","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","true","covers/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png","miximages/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png","","marquees/gbc/Road Rash (USA, Europe).png"
