"gbc_robot-wars-metal-mayhem","Robot Wars : Metal Mayhem","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-12-07","2000","2000s","Tiertex","BBC Multimedia","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1","1","1","","","Robot Wars: Metal Mayhem is the first video game based on the British game show Robot Wars. It was released exclusively for Game Boy Color on 7 December 2000.[1] It was the first of four games based on the show, with the first three selling over 250,000 copies.[2] The game was based on the third series of the show, and competitors such as its champion Chaos 2 feature in the game.

In the game, a competitor robot from the series, or a robot created by the player, is entered into combat against a robot controlled by the game. A bout finishes when one robot's health bar is fully depleted. In the Tournament Mode, the first robot to win two bouts advances. The game features the arena obstacles and House Robots of the series, and in other modes, a selection of mini-games based on the show's side events.","Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).zip","ZIP","0.41","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","miximages/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","screenshots/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","titlescreens/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","3dboxes/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","backcovers/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png","marquees/gbc/Robot Wars - Metal Mayhem (Europe) (En,Fr,De,It,Nl,Sv).png"
"gbc_rocket-power-gettin-air","Rocket Power : Gettin' Air","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-05-04","2001","2000s","Tiertex","THQ","Sports","Sports","1","1","1","60","3","They might be small, but that doesn't mean they can't enjoy extreme sports like the pros! The whole ROCKET POWER gang makes its way from the small screen adventures of their Nickelodeon program to the even smaller screen of the Game Boy Color. Such favorite characters as Otto, Reggie, Twister, and Sam are along for the adventure which, you can bet, will have plenty of extreme sports in it! There are 10 wild levels of action, which will have you snowboarding, surfing, skateboarding, and more. A comprehensive password system will help you pick up progress right where you left off, and the animation is lifted straight from the frames of the television program. If you perform well enough, you might even make the front page of Reggie's Zine, a publication dedicated to the thrills of alternative sports. Packed with action, cutscenes, and tons of funny stuff, this is one thrill ride you'll never want to get off of.","Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).zip","ZIP","0.3","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","miximages/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","screenshots/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","titlescreens/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","3dboxes/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","backcovers/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png","marquees/gbc/Rocket Power - Gettin' Air (USA, Europe).png"
"gbc_rocky-mountain-trophy-hunter","Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-09-06","2000","2000s","Xantera","Infogrames","Hunting","Action","1","1","1","","","If you've got a keen eye and a quick trigger finger, you might just have what it takes to become the next great hunter. Using a wide array of weaponry that ranges from rifles to bows to muzzleloaders, you'll search all sorts of scenery in pursuit of your prey. Journeying through the treacherous mountains of Colorado, deep into the expanses of Montana, and through the deserts of New Mexico, you'll have to keep your eyes peeled if you want to get the jump on these wily critters. There are plenty of animals out there, but each has realistic movements and behavior to evade your efforts. The big game creatures at large include deer, bighorn sheep, elk, and bears. Of course, you'll have access to the requisite calls, attractants, and cover scents, but don't expect any of these intelligent beasts to fall right into your traps. You'll have to use your brains, reflexes, instinct, and some basic perseverance to help bag you a trophy kill. In ROCKY MOUNTAIN TROPHY HUNTER, you won't have to worry about strapping a dead animal to your car roof!","Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).zip","ZIP","0.24","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","miximages/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","screenshots/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","titlescreens/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","3dboxes/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","backcovers/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png","marquees/gbc/Rocky Mountain Trophy Hunter (USA).png"
"gbc_rokumon-tengai-mon-colle-knight-gb","Rokumon Tengai Mon-colle-knight Gb","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-12-01","2000","2000s","Unknown","Kadokawa Shoten","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","","","In this RPG, players travel through four worlds in search of ""Monmon Items,"" which can be used to create combo attacks by cooperating with other monsters. Players can also play against each other using a communication cable.","Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).zip","ZIP","0.44","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","miximages/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","screenshots/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","titlescreens/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","3dboxes/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","backcovers/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png","marquees/gbc/Rokumon Tengai Mon-Colle-Knight GB (Japan).png"
"gbc_roland-garros-french-open","Roland Garros French Open","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-06-09","2000","2000s","Cryo Interactive","Carapace","Sports / Tennis","Sports","1","1","1","","","Roland Garros French Open is the only appearance of the franchise on the Game Boy Color. Less of a serious simulation of tennis than other versions, the handheld edition features cartoony 2D graphics and outrageous court locations.

All-in-all, the game includes eight different players and twelve different tournaments. Only five players and four tournaments can be selected from the start, the others are unlocked by winning events. The starting tournaments are realistic grand slam events: the Roland Garros French Open (the only one with a license), the English Open (i.e. Wimbledon), the US Championship and the Australian Cup, on clay, grass or turf. Winning them unlocks the more unusual locations: from street and beach tournaments to far-out events in the Antarctic or on the moon.

All events are single elimination, starting at the quarter finals. Matches follow original rules, and are seen from a standard perspective behind the controlled player. All characters (players, officials and fans) are drawn in a cartoony style with oversized heads. The controls allow for a variety of moves including backhand and forehand shots, volleys and lobs.","Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).zip","ZIP","0.33","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","miximages/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","screenshots/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","titlescreens/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","3dboxes/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","backcovers/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png","marquees/gbc/Roland Garros French Open (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It,Nl).png"
"gbc_ronaldo-v-football","Ronaldo V-Football","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-06-01","2001","2000s","Bit Managers","GT Interactive Software","Sports / Football (Soccer)","Sports","1","1","1","50","2.5","Based on the European hit, RONALDO-V FOOTBALL, this game is the pinnacle of soccer experiences for the Game Boy Color. Endorsed by international legend, Ronaldo Luis Nazario de Lima, RONALDO V-SOCCER brings Brazilian soccer traditions to the rest of the world. Boasting more than 100 real teams from around the globe, the game is set to an awesome Samba soundtrack and graced by colorful graphics. See how you fare over the course of an entire tournament in the comprehensive Simulation mode, or enjoy the rush of jumping right into things in Arcade mode. Either way, you're in for a highly realistic soccer experience with motion-capture animation and lifelike game physics. You can set up the rules and conditions any way you'd like, and you'll even have the ability to tailor your strategy to your opponent's style pulling from a complete playbook. Play alone, or compete against a friend.","Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).zip","ZIP","0.35","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png","miximages/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png","screenshots/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png","titlescreens/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png","3dboxes/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png","","marquees/gbc/Ronaldo V-Soccer (USA) (En,Fr,Es,Pt) (GB Compatible).png"
"gbc_roswell-conspiracies-aliens-myths-amp-legends","Roswell Conspiracies : Aliens, Myths &amp; Legends","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2001-01-01","2001","2000s","Crawfish Interactive","Red Storm Entertainment","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","60","3","Aliens have lived among mankind for centuries. However, man has known them as vampires, banshees, werewolves, and other mythical creatures. It is up to Global Alliance agent Nick Logan to stop these aliens from hunting humans and send them back to their home planets. Take control of Logan as he travels through 10 levels of action, spanning five exotic locations. In each level, Nick must master new technology to capture the aliens. If an alien tries to make a run for it, Logan can chase after it in a variety of vehicles, including a truck and a Humvee. In all of this action, he must avoid harming innocent human bystanders, who are unaware of the alien presence. Help Logan keep the aliens from feeding on humans in ROSWELL CONSPIRACIES: Aliens, Myths, &amp; Legends.","Roswell Conspiracies - Aliens, Myths &amp; Legends (USA) (En,Fr,De).zip","ZIP","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
