"gbc_tales-of-phantasia-narikiri-dungeon","Tales Of Phantasia - Narikiri Dungeon","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-11-10","2000","2000s","Namco","Namco","Japanese RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","Tales of Phantasia: Narikiri Dungeon (ãƒ†ã‚¤ãƒ«ã‚º ã‚ªãƒ– ãƒ•ã‚¡ãƒ³ã‚¿ã‚¸ã‚¢ ãªã‚Šãã‚Šãƒ€ãƒ³ã‚¸ãƒ§ãƒ³ Teiruzu Obu Fantajia Narikiri Danjon?) is a role-playing video game for the Game Boy Color released by Namco on November 10, 2000, selling 136,000 copies. Tales of Phantasia: Narikiri Dungeon's characteristic genre name is Dungeon RPG (ãƒ€ãƒ³ã‚¸ãƒ§ãƒ³RPG Danjon RPG?). It is the first sequel in the Tales series, which normally does not have connected storylines. The story begins 205 years after the beginning of Tales of Phantasia.

