"gbc_thunder-blast-man","Thunder Blast Man","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","","","","Sachen","Sachen","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","Thunder Blast Man (also known as Rocman X) is an unlicensed game created by Sachen, released on the Famicom and NES sometime in the 90's and also sometime later for the Game Boy Color. The NES and English Game Boy Color versions were released as Thunder Blast Man, the Chinese version of the GBC game released as Rockman X Gold, and one of the NES versions' label calls it Thunder Blaster Man.
The GBC version has similar graphics and levels, but has completely different music. Most of the graphics are taken from the Famicom version, including some unused enemy graphics. Also, the gameplay is changed to a more traditional Mega Man-styled game and there are no shops or additional weapons in the game. 
Two versions of this game exist: A ""Rocman X"" version featuring slightly edited Mega Man sprites and very slightly lower aim, and the more well-known ""Thunder Blast Man"" version, featuring the protagonist of the NES game. This version shares numerous similarities with Makon Soft games, particularly Rocman 8 and X4.","Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).zip","ZIP","0.08","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png","miximages/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png","screenshots/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png","titlescreens/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png","3dboxes/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png","","marquees/gbc/Thunder Blast Man (Europe) (Sachen) (Unl).png"
"gbc_thunderbirds","Thunderbirds","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-12-01","2000","2000s","Pukka Games","SCi Games","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","60","3","Join the Tracy Family in old-school gaming in 7 mini games accross the whole wide world.  Single player and story-driven, do YOU have what it takes to thwart the evil Hood?  This game allows players to control Thunderbirds vehicles 1-4, The mole and FAB1 in a variety of mini games.  TB1, a recon, and combat craft is a side scrolling mini-game involving bombing and shooting ground &amp; air targets while looking for people to resuce and collecting intel on the area.  TB2, the rescue craft is controlled from a top-down perspective and involves puzzle solving and exploration.  TB3, the space shuttle, is a vertical-scrolling, top-down, old school shooter and TB4, the submarine, is a collection and combat game played from a side-on perspective.  TB5, the Tracy Family Space Station is Brain often hangs out, updating the player with useful intel and story elements. The Mole is a subterranean digging machine and gameplay in this mode involves exploration, combat and collection - though on the surface it's reminiscent of DigDug.  FAB1, Lady Penelope's Rolls Royce is a time-based, top-down vertical scrolling driving game that captures the feeling of Chase HQ from the arcades of old.  Each mission involves different combinations of these craft and they occur in places as diverse as Egypt, Bermuda, Nepal, the Rainforests of South America and London.  The story reveals clues as to The Hood's intentions, but will you be able to piece them together before Brains?  You have 28 levels before the Game is up...","Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).zip","ZIP","0.65","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","miximages/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","screenshots/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","titlescreens/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","3dboxes/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","backcovers/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png","marquees/gbc/Thunderbirds (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It).png"
"gbc_tiger-woods-pga-tour-2000","Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000","gbc","Nintendo Game Boy Color","Game Boy Color","Nintendo","5. kynslóð (8-bit Handheld Color)","2000-01-01","2000","2000s","Xantera","THQ","Sports / Golf","Sports","1-4","1","4","","","This handheld version of Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 is the only game in the series to appear on the Game Boy Color. The game lets the player compete against six pros from the PGA Tour. There are four different modes of play: stroke, tournament, skins game and shoot out. Three courses exist: Summerlin, Sawgrass and Scottsdale. These are all official Tournament Players Club courses. Up to four players, either human or computer controlled, can play at any time.

When playing the player first get to see a top down view of the tee. He can here get information about wind and terrain and adjust his spin and cross hair. Once ready, the player has to use a power meter to take the shot. The player has to click it three times, first to start the backswing, then to end the backswing at the right strength and finally to strike the ball at the right time.","Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).zip","ZIP","0.69","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","miximages/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","screenshots/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","titlescreens/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","3dboxes/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","backcovers/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png","marquees/gbc/Tiger Woods PGA Tour 2000 (USA, Europe) (GB Compatible).png"
