"dreamcast_tomb-raider-chronicles","Tomb Raider : Chronicles","dreamcast","Sega Dreamcast","Dreamcast","Sega","6. kynslóð (128-bit)","2000-12-15","2000","2000s","Core Design","Eidos Interactive","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","80","4","A few days after the events described in Tomb Raider: The Last Revelation, Lara Croft is presumed dead. Her close friends begin to recollect her previous adventures, which occurred during different periods of her life. These include searching for the Philosopher's Stone in Rome; preventing the Spear of Destiny from falling into the hands of a ruthless gang leader; facing monsters on the Black Isle of Ireland as a child; and, finally, infiltrating a high-tech complex in pursuit of the Iris artefact. Like its predecessors, Tomb Raider: Chronicles is an action game with puzzle-solving and platforming elements. The gameplay is very similar to that of the previous games, with the addition of a few new skills. Lara can now walk on tightropes, swing on horizontal bars, and somersault forwards from a ledge while crouching. A grappling hook has been added to her inventory. The game also includes a level editor, allowing the player to create new stages for Lara to explore.","Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).chd","CHD","511.51","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","miximages/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","screenshots/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","titlescreens/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","3dboxes/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","backcovers/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png","marquees/dreamcast/Tomb Raider Chronicles (NA).png"
"dreamcast_tony-hawk-s-skateboarding","Tony Hawk's Skateboarding","dreamcast","Sega Dreamcast","Dreamcast","Sega","6. kynslóð (128-bit)","2000-06-29","2000","2000s","Treyarch","Crave Entertainment","Sports / Skateboard","Sports","1-2","1","2","100","5","Tony Hawk's Pro Skater, released as Tony Hawk's Skateboarding in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and parts of Europe, is a skateboarding video game developed by Neversoft. Published by Activision in 1999, it is the first entry in the Tony Hawk's series of video games. Development began after Tony Hawk's debut stint at the 1998 X-Games.

Pro Skater was originally released for the PlayStation on August 31, 1999, and was later ported to the Nintendo 64, Dreamcast, and N-Gage. It also received a Game Boy Color adaptation, and was released for Xbox in 2001 as part of the Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 2x collection. The game was met with critical acclaim from critics, who praised it for its innovative gameplay, level designs and control scheme. It was also commercially successful, selling rapidly upon its opening month. The game resulted in a successful franchise that has continued to be active, with the tenth installment and latest release, Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 5 released in October 2015.","Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).chd","CHD","370.13","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","miximages/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","screenshots/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","titlescreens/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","3dboxes/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","backcovers/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png","marquees/dreamcast/Tony Hawk's Pro Skater (NA).png"
