"gba_klonoa-heroes-densetsu-no-star-medal","Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu No Star Medal","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2002-12-13","2002","2000s","Namco","Namco","Role Playing Game","RPG","1","1","1","80","4","Klonoa Heroes: Densetsu no Star Medal is an action role-playing game developed and published by Namco and released in Japan in 2002. It is the first game in the Klonoa series to combine both standard action-gaming elements with role-playing features.
Taking a unique twist on the normal gameplay of the Klonoa handheld games, Klonoa Heroes instead relies on the player moving Klonoa, Guntz, or Pango across the screen from a top-down perspective, having them defeat enemies and earn experience points in the form of Dream Shards (small, crystal-like objects) and gold, which is used for currency, along the way. Klonoa once again utilizes his familiar weapon, the Wind Ring, but this time the ""wind bullet"" he can fire from it can be either blue or red. Guntz's handguns and Pango's bombs work the same way. Characters can acquire different weapons throughout the game. Likewise, each enemy in the game is given a color affinity of either blue or red, and Klonoa (or the other characters) can deal more damage to them by attacking with the same color.","Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).gba","GBA","32","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","miximages/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","screenshots/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","titlescreens/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","3dboxes/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","backcovers/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png","marquees/gba/Klonoa Heroes - Densetsu no Star Medal (English Translated, EEPROM Version).png"
"gba_lego-knights-kingdom","LEGO Knights Kingdom","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-10-04","2004","2000s","Razorback Developments","THQ","Action RPG","RPG","1-2","1","2","40","2","Become a hero knight and venture into the Citadel of Orlan on a quest to find the magical Shield of Ages. Lego Knights' Kingdom tests your combat skills against Vladek, the Dark Knight, and his fearsome army of Shadow Knights. Overcome your enemies, along with challenging puzzles and mini-quests. As one of five knights, you'll soon compete against Vladek himself in a grand tournament that will decide the fate of the Kingdom forever.","Knights' Kingdom (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","miximages/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png","marquees/gba/Knights' Kingdom (NA).png"
"gba_the-koala-brothers-outback-adventures","The Koala Brothers : Outback Adventures","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2006-02-03","2006","2000s","Sirius Games","The Game Factory","Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","60","3","You're never too young for adventure, at least when the Koala Brothers are involved! The Brothers and all their best buddies are waiting for new friends to join them on adventures through the beautiful Australian Outback. Preschoolers can play as all their favorite characters from the Koala Brothers TV show in 10 games packed with between 4 and 20 levels apiece. Kids learn how to handle the easy controls by using graphic-based instructions, so no reading is required! Players can help the brothers find George's lost mail, play tennis with Archie, hop around as Josie the Kangaroo, help Lolly run her ice cream truck, and more!","Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","miximages/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png","marquees/gba/Koala Brothers - Outback Adventures (NA).png"
"gba_konami-collector-s-series-arcade-classics","Konami Collector's Series : Arcade Classics","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2002-06-21","2002","2000s","Konami","Konami","Compilation","Compilation","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","Six Konami arcade classics arrive in Konami's Collectors Series: Arcade Advanced. For the first time in over ten years, play the original arcade version of the classic hit Frogger. Search the solar system, travel through time and space, and infiltrate enemy bases in Gyruss, Time Pilot, Rush 'n Attack, and Scramble. And test your martial arts skill in Yie Ar Kung Fu. With better graphics, levels, difficulty, and a multiplayer mode, Konami's compilation shows that its greatest games improve with age.","Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","miximages/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png","marquees/gba/Konami Collector's Series - Arcade Advanced (NA).png"
"gba_konami-krazy-racers","Konami Krazy Racers","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2001-06-11","2001","2000s","Konami","Konami","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-2","1","2","80","4","Konami Krazy Racers is a kart racing game with super deformed racers. It features famous Konami characters like Goemon (from Ganbare Goemon), Dracula (from Castlevania), and Vic Viper (from Gradius). There are 16 courses to race through, and you can collect coins to buy items. Gameplay is similar to that of Mario Kart.","Konami Krazy Racers (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","miximages/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png","marquees/gba/Konami Krazy Racers (NA).png"
"gba_kong-king-in-atlantis","Kong : King in Atlantis","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-10-25","2005","2000s","Skyworks Technologies","Majesco","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","10","0.5","Kong: King of Atlantis is based closely on the companion movie to Kong: The Animated Series, incorporating the plot of the video version in an action-packed, side-scrolling adventure.

When an ancient prophecy starts to come true, the sunken city of Atlantis begins to rise. The evil Queen Reptilla plans to trick Kong into becoming her King, using him as her slave to unite the warring clans of Atlantis for her own evil gains. In a race against time, Jason must convince Kong that Queen Reptilla is evil, in the hope that together they can save the islands of Kong and Atlantis and their inhabitants.","Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","miximages/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png","marquees/gba/Kong - King of Atlantis (NA).png"
"gba_king-kong-the-official-game-of-the-movie","King Kong : The Official Game of the Movie","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-11-21","2005","2000s","Ubisoft","Ubisoft","Action / Adventure","Adventure","1","1","1","60","3","Kong: The 8th Wonder of the World is an action/adventure video game developed by Ubisoft for the Nintendo Game Boy Advance. In Europe, it is known as King Kong: The Official Game of the Movie. Due to the limited technology the Game Boy Advance has, King Kong: The 8th Wonder of the World is very different from the home console versions of the game. In this game, players switch between various roles - one being the movie exhibition visiting Skull Island to do filming which comprises actress Ann Darrow, director Carl Denham and scriptwriter Jack Driscoll, and the 25 ft gorilla and king of Skull Island, King Kong. While the overhead human section focuses on puzzle-solving and adventuring elements, Kong sections are combat-oriented side-scrollers.","Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","miximages/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png","marquees/gba/Kong - The 8th Wonder of the World (NA).png"
