"gba_kurukuru-kururin","Kurukuru Kururin","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2001-03-21","2001","2000s","Eighting","Nintendo","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-4","1","4","80","4","Kuru Kuru Kururin is an innovative puzzle game in which the main character is inside a helicopter, and he must navigate himself through a maze in the least amount of time possible. Movements must be timed and precise, because if the helicopter's propeller hits a wall, 3 seconds is added to the timer. The protagonist's mission is to retrieve his brothers, who will join him after he finds them. He also finds many power-ups that will allow him to customize his helicopter's appearance.","Kurukuru Kururin (EU).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","miximages/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","screenshots/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","titlescreens/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","3dboxes/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","backcovers/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png","marquees/gba/Kurukuru Kururin (EU).png"
"gba_kururin-paradise","Kururin Paradise","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2002-12-06","2002","2000s","Eighting","Nintendo","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1-4","1","4","80","4","Kururin Paradise is the sequel to the GBA launch title, Kuru Kuru Kururin. In this game, Kururin and his family see an advertisement for the circus, which takes place at 6:00. Kururin's family arrive there on time, but Kururin is late, and when he gets there, everybody is missing! It's up to Kururin to search across the land for his missing family using his faithful helicopter, the Heririn. As in the first game, Kururin must navigate his way through fairly narrow mazes, trying not to hit the walls. Three consecutive hits, and the Heririn is destroyed, and you must start the stage again.

Paradise is vastly improved from the original game. It is now possible to find hidden keys in the levels, which open up locked doors, allowing for branched paths in the world map. Certain paths also lead to boss encounters, which take the form of an addictive mini-game including, but not limited to, lawn mowing, gathering stars, flying Kururin himself through clouds, and hopping across a path dodging helicopter blades. If you beat the boss, these mini-games are then added to your mini-game library, where you can play them against up to three friends using only one cart.

The game also features twelve toys built in that can be accessed by selecting one from a menu, then turning your GBA off, then on again. Most of them are fairly useless or incomprehensible in Japanese, but there are a couple of interesting ones, like the love tester, the musical note player, and the memory match game.","Kururin Paradise (English Translated).gba","GBA","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","miximages/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","screenshots/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","titlescreens/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","3dboxes/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","backcovers/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png","marquees/gba/Kururin Paradise (English Translated).png"
"gba_aigle-de-guerre-l","Aigle De Guerre, L'","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2001-03-21","2001","2000s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Strategy","Strategy / Sim","1-2","1","2","80","4","In the game's Story Mode, players play Napoleon Bonaparte who leads the revolutionary army into battle against the British. Set in the late 18th century, Napoleon's story is told in Fire Emblem fashion via strategic maps and character dialogue. However, the game takes many liberties with historical accuracy, such as Napoleon fighting man-eating ogres and abominable snowmen. The objectives for the missions vary slightly, but the basic idea is to send out units, defeat the enemy and take over the opponent's stronghold.","L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","miximages/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","screenshots/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","titlescreens/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","3dboxes/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","backcovers/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png","marquees/gba/L'Aigle de Guerre (English Translated).png"
