"gba_mario-kart-super-circuit","Mario Kart : Super Circuit","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2001-08-27","2001","2000s","Intelligent Systems","Nintendo","Racing, Driving","Racing","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","All your favourite kart-racing characters are back and ready to kick it into high gear! 20 brand-new tracks await on Game Boy Advance, loaded with classic power-ups and primed for the type of frenzied racing that only Mario Kart: Super Circuit can deliver. It's time to burn rubber in the Grand Prix, challenge your pals, race your own ghost, clash in battle mode and feel the power in the palm of your hand!","Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mario Kart - Super Circuit (NA).png"
"gba_mario-party-advance","Mario Party Advance","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-03-28","2005","2000s","A.I","Nintendo","Board game","Board / Casual","1-2","1","2","70","3.5","The first portable incarnation of the Mario Party series, Mario Party Advance shakes things up quite a bit on the GBA.  With the focus on the single-player, there are all kinds of single-player mini-games, one giant single-player board to traverse instead of multiple ones (Shroom City), and all kinds of different Gaddgets and gameplay modes to indulge in.

The main single-player experience involves traveling across ""Shroom City,"" which is a major departure from the standard set-up in past Mario Party titles.  You have the choice to be Mario, Luigi, Peach, or Yoshi, and depending on who you choose, you'll start at a different spot on the board, which is quite large.

You're given die rolls to navigate the board and, when you reach special sections of the map, complete special quests, which often involve helping residents of Shroom City and/or participating in special challenges.  Most quests involve collecting some sort of object elsewhere or a mini-game.  By completing these quests, you'll collect stars, which eventually allow for special boss bouts with Bowser, and you'll unlock mini-games and Gaddgets, which are simple, toy-like contraptions that you can play with.

The game ends when you complete your allotted number of turns, although additional turns and die rolls can be earned during the game by completing the ""Mushroom Challenges"" that occur rather often.  After completing your session, your rewards are saved, and you can play with your mini-games and Gaddgets in Play Mode.

There are also two additional modes available, ""Party Land,"" where you can play special duel mini-games with a friend, and ""Challenge Land,"" where you play through special modes that test your mini-game skills to earn coins, which can be used to purchase additional unlockables in a shop.

Finally, there is also a feature called the ""Bonus Board.""  You can play with a board that is included with the game using the GBA.  The GBA takes care of die rolls, mini-games, and end-of-the-game events.","Mario Party Advance (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mario Party Advance (NA).png"
"gba_super-mario-ball","Super Mario Ball","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-10-04","2004","2000s","Fuse Games","Nintendo","Pinball","Board / Casual","1","1","1","70","3.5","This is the standard ""Bowser has kidnapped the Princess, and Mario must rescue her"" story. In this case, the Princess is transformed into a ball and launched from a Super Mario 64-style cannon, which a pair of goombas aim directly at Bowser's Castle. Mario is also transformed into a ball and chases after her.

There are 5 levels, each consisting of a set of pinball tables. Each table has some exits (including the one below the flippers) that Mario can use to move to other tables. Also, each one holds a star, normally obtained by defeating all enemies on the table. Some exits require that Mario has a certain number of stars. To gain access to Bowser's castle, Mario must defeat the bosses of the first 4 levels, which gives him star keys. The game also features a ""Time Attack"" mode, which allows players to fight already defeated bosses again.","Mario Pinball Land (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mario Pinball Land (NA).png"
"gba_mario-power-tennis","Mario Power Tennis","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-11-18","2005","2000s","Camelot Software","Nintendo","Sports / Tennis","Sports","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","Players can test their backhand in this unique role-playing tennis adventure. Train hard at the Royal Tennis Academy to be a champion. Gain experience and improve your skills through lessons and tournaments, and rise to the top of the ranks. Play as Mario, Peach, Waluigi, or Donkey Kong in a slew of wild modes. Advance through the story and unlock even more characters, all with their own power moves. Beat Mario at his own game, then link up with a friend or three for even more frantic fun.","Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).gba","GBA","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mario Tennis - Power Tour (NA).png"
"gba_mario-vs-donkey-kong","Mario vs. Donkey Kong","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-05-24","2004","2000s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Puzzle","Puzzle","1","1","1","70","3.5","After years of apparent goodwill, Mario and Donkey Kong are at it again--this time, on Game Boy Advance. Donkey Kong has stolen all the Mini-Mario toys from the Mario Toy Co., and now it's up to Mario to hunt down his longtime nemesis and retrieve the pilfered goods. As Mario, you must race through challenging levels while finding keys and releasing Mini Marios before time runs out. Along the way, you'll master new moves that can help you overcome new puzzles.","Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).gba","GBA","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mario Vs. Donkey Kong (NA).png"
"gba_marvel-ultimate-alliance","Marvel : Ultimate Alliance","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2006-10-24","2006","2000s","Barking Lizards","Activision","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","50","2.5","The handheld version of Marvel Ultimate Alliance, like its console counterparts, has the player taking control over one of a selection of Marvel super-heroes and battling through locations and enemies from the Marvel universe. Selectable playable characters are: Spider-Man, Blade, Elektra, Thor, Wolverine, Captain America, Deadpool and Iceman. Ms. Marvel and Thing as also available as unlockable characters.

The game plays out something like Final Fight, where the player walks from left to right with the ability to move on the z-axis and punch and kick wave after wave of enemies including the occasional boss.

It has some unique elements added to the genre basics, however.  A meter controls the use of super powers, which can be upgraded as experience is gained. Players also have the ability to summon various Marvel heroes for quick support roles.  There are many items to find, both quest items, such as keys to unlock doors and weapons and equipment, like weapons and armor, to buff up the characters' abilties.","Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","miximages/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png","marquees/gba/Marvel - Ultimate Alliance (NA).png"
"gba_mary-kate-and-ashley-girls-night-out","Mary-Kate and Ashley : Girls Night Out","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2002-11-29","2002","2000s","Powerhead Games","Acclaim Entertainment","Music and Dancing","Action","1","1","1","40","2","These twins went from cute little toddlers on television to international fashion examples in a matter of just a few years, and they're ready to celebrate their success with a night on the town. Join the duo for an evening of clubbing and high style, dancing to the beats of techno, house, and disco music for the duration of the handheld gaming adventure. Just how does one go about dancing on a Game Boy Advance? Well, your fingers will represent your feet, as you try to master the correct combination of buttons and direction pad taps which isn't exactly as easy as it seems. Of course, you're nothing without the right clothes; choose your own shoes, shirts, pants, hairstyles, and accessories in this all-inclusive experience. One of your primary objectives will be to unlock all of the game's secret steps, songs, and clothes and that will take a combination of smarts and reflexes.","Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","miximages/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png","marquees/gba/Mary-Kate and Ashley - Girls Night Out (NA).png"
