"gba_ozzy-amp-drix","Ozzy &amp; Drix","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2003-12-16","2003","2000s","Raylight","Midway","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","50","2.5","A 2D platformer with 3D elements, Ozzy &amp; Drix is based on the hit cartoon series from the Kids' WB! which in turn is based on the movie Osmosis Jones. Join the gross-out adventures of a white blood cell ""cop,"" Ozzy, and his over-the-counter cold pill sidekick, Drix. Fans of the hit series will now be part of the action on Game Boy Advance. Whiz down a blood cell highway in the ""Cel Camino,"" provide protection from the dreaded ""Phlegm-alanche,"" face off against nemesis Spryman and Gluteus and more as Ozzy &amp; Drix live and play in their world inside teenage boy Hector Cruz.","Ozzy &amp; Drix (NA).gba","GBA","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
"gba_pac-man-collection","Pac-Man Collection","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2001-07-12","2001","2000s","Mass Media","Infogrames","Action / Labyrinth","Action","1","1","1","80","4","Four classic Pac-Man games are included in this collection from Namco:

1. Pac-Man: The original arcade classic, complete and un-cut. 
2. Pac-Mania: A conversion of the 1987 update to Pac-Man, which takes the elements of the original arcade game and puts it into an isometric view, as well as adding the ability to jump.
3. Pac-Man Arrangement: Never re-produced outside of the arcade, Arrangement again uses the elements of the original Pac-Man and adds a fifth ghost, who can change shape and size when combined with the other 4 ghosts, and make life harder for Pac-Man. New power-ups are also included, like the ability to dash quickly around the screen, warp points to get from one place to the other and new ways of catching ghosts.
Pac-Attack: Like Tetris before it, you must fit falling blocks together to complete a line to clear the screen. In this case, the falling tiles also have ghosts in them, and once the Pac-Man tile appears (a tile with the Pac-Man symbol), Pac-Man will eat all of the ghosts that are in his path until he gets to a dead end.","Pac-Man Collection (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","miximages/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png","marquees/gba/Pac-Man Collection (NA).png"
"gba_pac-man-pinball-advance","Pac-Man Pinball Advance","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-08-19","2005","2000s","Namco","Zoo Digital Publishing","Pinball","Board / Casual","1","1","1","80","4","It's Pac-Man meets Pinball!  PMPA merges classic Pac-Man action with pinball, reminiscent of Kirby's Pinball Land, letting the player choose from different table backgrounds, the goal of which is to advance through the tables, hitting certain parts to gain power-ups, even the ability to eat pellets and eat the ghost foes (Blinky, Inky, Pinky and Clyde) and rescue Pac-Mans friends, including Ms. Pac-Man as well.  There are also mini-games to be played such as a vertical shooter and classic Pac-Man mazes.","Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","miximages/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png","marquees/gba/Pac-Man Pinball Advance (NA).png"
"gba_pac-man-world","Pac-Man World","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-11-17","2004","2000s","Namco","Zoo Digital Publishing","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","100","5","Unlike most ""Pac-games,"" Pac-Man World is a platform-adventure in which the round, yellow hero progresses through over 20 levels of action. He still faces opposition, however, from ghostly nemeses like Inky, Blinky, Pinky, and Clyde. He must also run, jump, and swim his way past other malevolent creatures, such as skeletons, spiders, and killer fish. Thankfully, Pac-Man has a variety of attack methods. Excluding ghosts, most baddies are susceptible to projectile ""Pac-Dots,"" the ""Ultra Butt-Bounce"" (which also helps him jump higher), or the ""Rev Roll,"" a speed burst allowing Pac-Man to make lengthy jumps off ramps. When disposing of ghosts though, he must first ingest a good old-fashioned Power Pellet, then devour them before its effects wear off.","Pac-Man World (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","miximages/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png","marquees/gba/Pac-Man World (NA).png"
"gba_pac-man-world-2","Pac-Man World 2","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-08-19","2005","2000s","Full Fat","Zoo Digital Publishing","Platform","Platformer","1","1","1","70","3.5","Long ago, back in medieval times, an evil spirit known as Spooky had terrorized all of Pac-Land. In response to this, the great Wizard Pac created a potion that turned 5 ordinary fruit into the ""Golden Fruit."" A young knight called Sir Pac-alot fought and sealed Spooky underneath a large tree using the Golden Fruit, which were attached to the branches of the tree. In the present time late at night, Inky, Pinky, Blinky and Clyde sneak into the village and, in their mischief, pick the Golden Fruit off the tree in the center of town. Unfortunately, this has released Spooky from his prison. Spooky tells the ghosts to take the Golden Fruit and follow him if they wish to rid the land of the Pac-people forever. When Pac-Man awakes, he hears the news from Professor Pac about the Golden Fruit and Spooky, and sets off to defeat the ghosts and Spooky.","Pac-Man World 2 (NA).gba","GBA","4","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","miximages/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png","marquees/gba/Pac-Man World 2 (NA).png"
