"gba_puyo-pop-fever","Puyo Pop Fever","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2005-03-24","2005","2000s","Sonic Team","THQ","Puzzle / Fall","Puzzle","1","1","1","90","4.5","Puyo Pop Fever is a puzzle game of the falling-block variety, the goal of which is to clear your blocks (Puyos) by combining four or more of the same color, which will then vanish. This will produce Nuisance Puyos. These colorless Puyos will fall onto your opponents screen, thus blocking chains and combos they could create. These pesky Puyos can only be exterminated by removing neighboring Puyos.nnnnWhen an opponent sends Nuisance Puyos to your screen you can try to ""offset"" by clearing your own Puyos and limiting the number that would fall on your screen. This will also increase your Fever Meter. When this meter fills you will be given a set of prearranged Puyos with which you can wrack up giant combos and send tons of Nuisance Puyos to your opponent. When any player's field becomes so full that they can no longer drop Puyos they lose the game.","Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","miximages/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","screenshots/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","titlescreens/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","3dboxes/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","backcovers/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png","marquees/gba/Puyo Puyo Fever (English Translated).png"
"gba_pyuu-to-fuku-jaguar-byoo-to-deru-megane-kun","Pyuu To Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo To Deru! Megane-kun","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-04-29","2004","2000s","Konami","Konami","Action RPG","RPG","1","1","1","","","Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar is a Japanese gag manga series written and illustrated by Kyosuke Usuta. The story is about recorders, musicians, and their bizarre daily lives. It has a vague overall plot but is mainly episodic. This RPG's call to fame is its unique use (in the handheld arena, at least) of 3D glasses to create special stereoscopic effects. The game sports both basic platformer stages as well as 3/4 top-down areas. Features include seven different worlds, humorous action, and a flute meter.","Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png","miximages/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png","screenshots/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png","titlescreens/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png","3dboxes/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png","","marquees/gba/Pyuu to Fuku! Jaguar - Byoo to Deru! Megane-kun (JP).png"
