"gba_rhythm-tengoku","Rhythm Tengoku","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2006-08-03","2006","2000s","J.P. Room","Nintendo","Rhythm","Action","1","1","1","80","4","Rhythm Tengoku is a music game based around good timing and rhythm. The game has music supplied by the record production company J.P. ROOM, and is developed by the team responsible for Wario Ware.

As with Wario Ware, the game is actually a series of shorter games bundled into one package. Before each game starts, you are presented with a short tutorial that gets you ready and practice before you begin the real thing.

Players will punch in time with a karate expert as pots and rocks are thrown; pluck hairs off of an onion; march in time to an instructor; hit a baseball while the screen zooms in and out; shoot ghosts with arrows; chop demons as a samurai; and much more. At the end of each set of stages is a 'remix stage' - in this stage, sections of the previously played stages are combined and thrown at you at random, all while a single song plays.","Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).gba","GBA","16","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","false","covers/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","miximages/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","screenshots/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","titlescreens/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","3dboxes/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","backcovers/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png","marquees/gba/Rhythm Tengoku (English Translated, Rev 14).png"
"gba_river-city-ransom-ex","River City Ransom EX","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2004-05-26","2004","2000s","Million","Atlus","Beat'em Up","Beat 'em up","1","1","1","80","4","Kunio's greatest adventure with enhanced graphics and new gameplay!

Brothers Ryuichi and Ryuji arrive at the Reihou Academy, located near Nekketsu High. After a short amount of time, nearby schools have begun fallen under the control of Ryuichi and Ryuji, who rumor has it have dubbed themselves the Double Dragons.

Riki Samejima of Hanazono High has never seen eye to eye with Kunio, and in fact, they seem to always compete to be the best.

