"gba_shrek-prezessin","Shrek Prezessin","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","","","","Sintax","Unknown","Unknown","Unknown","1","1","1","","","Shrek Prezessin is well, you guessed it, another Digimon Adventure GBA reskin by Sintax. This feels like one of the stranger reskins by Sintax, but then again, they also did Harry Potter, Lord of the Rings and Spider-Man reskins as well, all being based off of movies. This mostly uses graphics from the Shrek GBA games, though the enemies &amp; bosses all seem to be taken elsewhere. I'm not sure if the backgrounds and tilesets are from the Shrek GBA games either, but I'm gonna guess that they probably are or aren't. Strangely, they actually bothered to change the spring sprite in this reskin, which is interesting since they didn't do that with Sonic 3 Fighter Sonic and so on. Also strangely, there is no English version of this reskin, since only Chinese and Russian versions of it exist. Anyways, this is probably where I'll stop doing longplays of Sintax GBA games, since they can get quite repetitive after a long time.","Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).gba","GBA","32","true","true","true","true","true","false","true","false","covers/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png","miximages/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png","screenshots/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png","titlescreens/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png","3dboxes/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png","","marquees/gba/Shiruike II - Yu Meiren (TW).png"
