"gba_wolfenstein-3d","Wolfenstein 3D","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2002-04-19","2002","2000s","Stalker Entertainment","Bam Entertainment","Shooter / FPV","Shooter","1","1","1","70","3.5","Under the Iron-fist grip of Nazi German Rule, the evil Dr. Schabbs is suspected of cultivating a project for building a mighty mutant Nazi German Army. Your mission, as William ""B.J."" Blazkowicz, is to steal the secret plans, make your escape and sabotage their evil plot. But captured in your attempt, you are hauled from Castle Hollehammer to the cells of Castle Wolfenstein - there to be questioned and await your certain execution. A lucky break gives you the chance to make your escape, only to find that Castle Wolfenstein is a maze of passages, bristling with trigger happy Nazi guards. Each level you break through brings you face to face with death. There's no time now to hold fire, it's kill or be killed . . .","Wolfenstein 3D (NA).gba","GBA","8","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","true","covers/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","miximages/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","screenshots/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","titlescreens/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","3dboxes/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","backcovers/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png","marquees/gba/Wolfenstein 3D (NA).png"
"gba_the-legend-of-zelda-a-link-to-the-past-amp-four-sw","The Legend of Zelda : A Link to the Past &amp; Four Sw","gba","Nintendo Game Boy Advance","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo","6. kynslóð (32-bit Handheld)","2003-03-28","2003","2000s","Nintendo","Nintendo","Role Playing Game","RPG","1-4","1","4","90","4.5","The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past &amp; Four Swords for Game Boy Advance is a remake of A Link to the Past coupled with an entirely new game, Four Swords. This two-in-one game was released shortly before The Wind Waker.

While A Link to the Past is largely a faithful port of the original, it does include an entirely new dungeon and a new quest as rewards for the player playing through the multiplayer-only Four Swords. Aside from these additions, it includes a number of smaller gameplay and dialogue changes, the latter of which are designed to correct a number of minor translation mistakes and inconsistencies with the original Japanese release and to unify the common terms used with the later games.","The Legend of Zelda - A Link to the Past &amp; Four Swords (NA).gba","GBA","0","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","false","","","","","","",""
